Esther	Est	19	9	32	And all things which are contained in the history of this book, which is called Esther.
Esther	Est	19	10	1	And king Assuerus made all the land, and all the islands of the sea tributary.
Esther	Est	19	10	2	And his strength and his empire, and the dignity and greatness wherewith he exalted Mardochai, are written in the books of the Medes, and of the Persians:
Esther	Est	19	10	3	And how Mardochai of the race of the Jews, was next after king Assuerus: and great among the Jews, and acceptable to the people of his brethren, seeking the good of his people, and speaking those things which were for the welfare of his seed.
Esther	Est	19	10	4	Then Mardochai said: God hath done these things.
Esther	Est	19	10	5	I remember a dream that I saw, which signified these same things: and nothing thereof hath failed.
Esther	Est	19	10	6	The little fountain which grew into a river, and was turned into a light, and into the sun, and abounded into many waters, is Esther, whom the king married, and made queen.
Esther	Est	19	10	7	But the two dragons are I and Aman.
Esther	Est	19	10	8	The nations that were assembled are they that endeavoured to destroy the name of the Jews.
Esther	Est	19	10	9	And my nation is Israel, who cried to the Lord, and the Lord saved his people: and he delivered us from all evils, and hath wrought great signs and wonders among the nations:
Esther	Est	19	10	10	And he commanded that there should be two lots, one of the people of God, and the other of all the nations.
Esther	Est	19	10	11	And both lots came to the day appointed already from that time before God to all nations:
Esther	Est	19	10	12	And the Lord remembered his people, and had mercy on his inheritance.
Esther	Est	19	10	13	And these days shall be observed in the month of Adar on the fourteenth, and fifteenth day of the same month. with all diligence, and joy of the people gathered into one assembly, throughout all the generations hereafter of the people of Israel.
Esther	Est	19	11	1	In the fourth year of the reign of Ptolemy and Cleopatra, Dositheus, who said he was a priest, and of the Levitical race, and Ptolemy his son brought this epistle of Phurim, which they said Lysimachus the son of Ptolemy had interpreted in Jerusalem.
Esther	Est	19	11	2	In the second year of the reign of Artaxerxes the great, in the first day of the month Nisan, Mardochai the son of Jair, the son of Semei, the son of Cis, of the tribe of Benjamin:
Esther	Est	19	11	3	A Jew who dwelt in the city of Susan, a great man and among the first of the king's court, had a dream.
Esther	Est	19	11	4	Now he was of the number of the captives, whom Nabuchodonosor king of Babylon had carried away from Jerusalem with Jechonias king of Juda:
Esther	Est	19	11	5	And this was his dream: Behold there were voices, and tumults, and thunders, and earthquakes, and a disturbance upon the earth.
Esther	Est	19	11	6	And behold two great dragons came forth ready to fight one against another.
Esther	Est	19	11	7	And at their cry all nations were stirred up to fight against the nation of the just.
Esther	Est	19	11	8	And that was a day of darkness and danger, of tribulation and distress, and great fear upon the earth.
Esther	Est	19	11	9	And the nation of the just was troubled fearing their own evils, and was prepared for death.
Esther	Est	19	11	10	And they cried to God: and as they were crying, a little fountain grew into a very great river, and abounded into many waters.
Esther	Est	19	11	11	The light and the sun rose up, and the humble were exalted, and they devoured the glorious.
Esther	Est	19	11	12	And when Mardochai had seen this, and arose out of his bed, he was thinking what God would do: and he kept it fixed in his mind, desirous to know what the dream should signify.
Esther	Est	19	12	1	And he abode at that time in the king's court with Bagatha and Thara the king's eunuchs, who were porters of the palace.
Esther	Est	19	12	2	And when he understood their designs, and had diligently searched into their projects, he learned that they went about to lay violent hands on king Artaxerxes, and he told the king thereof.
Esther	Est	19	12	3	Then the king had them both examined, and after they had confessed, commanded them to be put to death.
Esther	Est	19	12	4	But the king made a record of what was done: and Mardochai also committed the memory of the thing to writing.
Esther	Est	19	12	5	And the king commanded him, to abide in the court of the palace, and gave him presents for the information.
Esther	Est	19	12	6	But Aman the son of Amadathi the Bugite was in great honour with the king, and sought to hurt Mardochai and his people, because of the two eunuchs of the king who were put to death.
Esther	Est	19	13	1	And this was the copy of the letter: Artaxerxes the great king who reigneth from India to Ethiopia, to the princes and governors of the hundred and twenty-seven provinces, that are subject to his empire, greeting.
Esther	Est	19	13	2	Whereas I reigned over many nations, and had brought all the world under my dominion, I was not willing to abuse the greatness of my power, but to govern my subjects with clemency and lenity, that they might live quietly without any terror. and might enjoy peace, which is desired by all men.
Esther	Est	19	13	3	But when I asked my counsellors how this might be accomplished, one that excelled the rest in wisdom and fidelity, and was second after the king, Aman by name,
Esther	Est	19	13	4	Told me that there was a people scattered through the whole world, which used new laws, and acted against the customs of all nations, despised the commandments of kings, and violated by their opposition the concord of all nations.
Esther	Est	19	13	5	Wherefore having learned this, and seeing one nation in opposition to all mankind using perverse laws, and going against our commandments, and disturbing the peace and concord of the provinces subject to us,
Esther	Est	19	13	6	We have commanded that all whom Aman shall mark out, who is chief over all the provinces, and second after the king, and whom we honour as a father, shall be utterly destroyed by their enemies, with their wives and children, and that none shall have pity on them. on the fourteenth day of the twelfth month Adar of this present year:
Esther	Est	19	13	7	That these wicked men going down to hell in one day, may restore to our empire the peace which they had disturbed.
Esther	Est	19	13	8	But Mardochai besought the Lord, remembering all his works,
Esther	Est	19	13	9	And said: O Lord, Lord, almighty king, for all things are in thy power, and there is none that can resist thy will, if thou determine to save Israel.
Esther	Est	19	13	10	Thou hast made heaven and earth, and all things that are under the cope of heaven.
Esther	Est	19	13	11	Thou art Lord of all, and there is none that can resist thy majesty.
Esther	Est	19	13	12	Thou knowest all things, and thou knowest that it was not out of pride and contempt, or any desire of glory, that I refused to worship the proud Aman,
Esther	Est	19	13	13	(For I would willingly and readily for the salvation of Israel have kissed even the steps of his feet,)
Esther	Est	19	13	14	But I feared lest I should transfer the honour of my God to a man, and lest I should adore any one except my God.
Esther	Est	19	13	15	And now, O Lord, O king, O God of Abraham, have mercy on thy people, because our enemies resolve to destroy us, and extinguish thy inheritance.
Esther	Est	19	13	16	Despise not thy portion, which thou hast redeemed for thyself out of Egypt.
Esther	Est	19	13	17	Hear my supplication, and be merciful to thy lot and inheritance, and turn our mourning into joy, that we may live and praise thy name, O Lord, and shut not the mouths of them that sing to thee.
Esther	Est	19	13	18	And all Israel with like mind and supplication cried to the Lord, because they saw certain death hanging over their heads.
Esther	Est	19	14	1	Queen Esther also, fearing the danger that was at hand, had recourse to the Lord.
Esther	Est	19	14	2	And when she had laid away her royal apparel, she put on garments suitable for weeping and mourning: instead of divers precious ointments, she covered her head with ashes and dung, and she humbled her body with fasts: and all the places in which before she was accustomed to rejoice, she filled with her torn hair.
Esther	Est	19	14	3	And she prayed to the Lord the God of Israel, saying: O my Lord, who alone art our king, help me a desolate woman, and who have no other helper but thee.
Esther	Est	19	14	4	My danger is in my hands.
Esther	Est	19	14	5	I have heard of my father that thou, O Lord, didst take Israel from among all nations, and our fathers from all their predecessors, to possess them as an everlasting inheritance, and thou hast done to them as thou hast promised.
Esther	Est	19	14	6	We have sinned in thy sight, and therefore thou hast delivered us into the hands of our enemies:
Esther	Est	19	14	7	For we have worshipped their gods. Thou art just, O Lord.
Esther	Est	19	14	8	And now they are not content to oppress us with most hard bondage, but attributing the strength of their hands to the power of their idols,
Esther	Est	19	14	9	They design to change thy promises, and destroy thy inheritance, and shut the mouths of them that praise thee, and extinguish the glory of thy temple and altar,
Esther	Est	19	14	10	That they may open the mouths of Gentiles, and praise the strength of idols, and magnify for ever a carnal king.
Esther	Est	19	14	11	Give not, O Lord, thy sceptre to them that are not, lest they laugh at our ruin: but turn their counsel upon themselves, and destroy him that hath begun to rage against us.
Esther	Est	19	14	12	Remember, O Lord, and shew thyself to us in the time of our tribulation, and give me boldness, O Lord, king of gods, and of all power:
Esther	Est	19	14	13	Give me a well ordered speech in my mouth in the presence of the lion, and turn his heart to the hatred of our enemy, that both he himself may perish, and the rest that consent to him.
Esther	Est	19	14	14	But deliver us by thy hand, and help me, who have no other helper, but thee, O Lord, who hast the knowledge of all things.
Esther	Est	19	14	15	And thou knowest that I hate the glory of the wicked, and abhor the bed of the uncircumcised, and of every stranger.
Esther	Est	19	14	16	Thou knowest my necessity, that I abominate the sign of my pride and glory, which is upon my head in the days of my public appearance, and detest it as a menstruous rag, and wear it not in the days of my silence,
Esther	Est	19	14	17	And that I have not eaten at Aman's table, nor hath the king's banquet pleased me, and that I have not drunk the wine of the drink offerings:
Esther	Est	19	14	18	And that thy handmaid hath never rejoiced, since I was brought hither unto this day, but in thee, O Lord, the God of Abraham.
Esther	Est	19	14	19	O God, who art mighty above all, hear the voice of them, that have no other hope, and deliver us from the hand of the wicked, and deliver me from my fear.
Esther	Est	19	15	1	And he commanded her (no doubt but he was Mardochai) to go to the king, and petition for her people, and for her country.
Esther	Est	19	15	2	Remember, (said he,) the days of thy low estate, how thou wast brought up by my hand, because Aman the second after the king hath spoken against us unto death.
Esther	Est	19	15	3	And do thou call upon the Lord, and speak to the king for us, and deliver us from death.
Esther	Est	19	15	4	And on the third day she laid away the garments she wore, and put on her glorious apparel.
Esther	Est	19	15	5	And glittering in royal robes, after she had called upon God the ruler and Saviour of all, she took two maids with her,
Esther	Est	19	15	6	And upon one of them she leaned, as if for delicateness and overmuch tenderness she were not able to bear up her own body.
Esther	Est	19	15	7	And the other maid followed her lady, bearing up her train flowing on the ground.
Esther	Est	19	15	8	But she with a rosy colour in her face, and with gracious and bright eyes, hid a mind full of anguish, and exceeding great fear.
Esther	Est	19	15	9	So going in she passed through all the doors in order, and stood before the king, where he sat upon his royal throne, clothed with his royal robes, and glittering with gold, and precious stones, and he was terrible to behold.
Esther	Est	19	15	10	And when he had lifted up his countenance, and with burning eyes had shewn the wrath of his heart, the queen sunk down, and her colour turned pale, and she rested her weary head upon her handmaid.
Esther	Est	19	15	11	And God changed the king's spirit into mildness, and all in haste and in fear he leaped from his throne, and holding her up in his arms, till she came to herself, caressed her with these words:
Esther	Est	19	15	12	What is the matter, Esther? I am thy brother, fear not.
Esther	Est	19	15	13	Thou shalt not die: for this law is not made for thee, but for all others.
Esther	Est	19	15	14	Come near then, and touch the sceptre.
Esther	Est	19	15	15	And as she held her peace, he took the golden sceptre, and laid it upon her neck, and kissed her, and said: Why dost thou not speak to me?
Esther	Est	19	15	16	She answered: I saw thee, my lord, as an angel of God, and my heart was troubled for fear of thy majesty.
Esther	Est	19	15	17	For thou, my lord, art very admirable, and thy. face is full of graces.
Esther	Est	19	15	18	And while she was speaking, she fell down again, and was almost in a swoon.
Esther	Est	19	15	19	But the king was troubled, and all his servants comforted her.
Esther	Est	19	16	1	The great king Artaxerxes, from India to Ethiopia, to the governors and princes of a hundred and twenty-seven provinces, which obey our command, sendeth greeting.
Esther	Est	19	16	2	Many have abused unto pride the goodness of princes, and the honour that hath been bestowed upon them:
Esther	Est	19	16	3	And not only endeavour to oppress the king's subjects, but not bearing the glory that is given them, take in hand to practise also against them that gave it.
Esther	Est	19	16	4	Neither are they content not to return thanks for benefits received, and to violate in themselves the laws of humanity, but they think they can also escape the justice of God who seeth all things.
Esther	Est	19	16	5	And they break out into so great madness, as to endeavour to undermine by lies such as observe diligently the offices committed to them, and do all things in such manner as to be worthy of all men's praise,
Esther	Est	19	16	6	While with crafty fraud they deceive the ears of princes that are well meaning, and judge of others by their own nature.
Esther	Est	19	16	7	Now this is proved both from ancient histories, and by the things which are done daily, how the good designs of kings are depraved by the evil suggestions of certain men.
Esther	Est	19	16	8	Wherefore we must provide for the peace of all provinces.
Esther	Est	19	16	9	Neither must you think, if we command different things, that it cometh of the levity of our mind, but that we give sentence according to the quality and necessity of times, as the profit of the commonwealth requireth.
Esther	Est	19	16	10	Now that you may more plainly understand what we say, I Aman the son of Amadathi, a Macedonian both in mind and country, and having nothing of the Persian blood, but with his cruelty staining our goodness, was received being a stranger by us:
Esther	Est	19	16	11	And found our humanity so great towards him, that he was called our father, and was worshipped by all as the next man after the king:
Esther	Est	19	16	12	But he was so far puffed up with arrogancy, as to go about to deprive us of our kingdom and life.
Esther	Est	19	16	13	For with certain new and unheard of devices he hath sought the destruction of Mardochai, by whose fidelity and good services our life was saved, and of Esther the partner of our kingdom, with all their nation:
Esther	Est	19	16	14	Thinking that after they were slain, he might work treason against us left alone without friends, and might transfer the kingdom of the Persians to the Macedonians.
Esther	Est	19	16	15	But we have found that the Jews, who were by that most wicked man appointed to be slain, are in no fault at all, but contrariwise, use just laws,
Esther	Est	19	16	16	And are the children of the highest and the greatest, and the ever living God, by whose benefit the kingdom was given both to our fathers and to us, and is kept unto this day.
Esther	Est	19	16	17	Wherefore know ye that those letters which he sent in our name, are void and of no effect.
Esther	Est	19	16	18	For which crime both he himself that devised it, and all his kindred hang on gibbets, before the gates of this city Susan: not we, but God repaying him as he deserved.
Esther	Est	19	16	19	But this edict, which we now send, shall be published in all cities, that the Jews may freely follow their own laws.
Esther	Est	19	16	20	And you shall aid them that they may kill those who had prepared themselves to kill them, on the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, which is called Adar.
Esther	Est	19	16	21	For the almighty God hath turned this day of sadness and mourning into joy to them.
Esther	Est	19	16	22	Wherefore you shall also count this day among other festival days, and celebrate it with all joy, that it may be known also in times to come,
Esther	Est	19	16	23	That all they who faithfully obey the Persians, receive a worthy reward for their fidelity: but they that are traitors to their kingdom, are destroyed for their wickedness.
Esther	Est	19	16	24	And let every province and city, that will not be partaker of this solemnity, perish by the sword and by fire, and be destroyed in such manner as to be made unpassable, both to men and beasts, for an example of contempt, and disobedience.
Job	Job	20	1	1	There was a man in the land of Hus, whose name was Job, and that man was simple and upright, and fearing God, and avoiding evil.
Job	Job	20	1	2	And there were born to him seven sons and three daughters.
Job	Job	20	1	3	And his possession was seven thousand sheep, and three thousand camels, and five hundred yoke of oxen, and five hundred she asses, and a family exceeding great: and this man was great among all the people of the east.
Job	Job	20	1	4	And his sons went, and made a feast by houses every one in his day. And sending they called their three sisters to eat and drink with them.
Job	Job	20	1	5	And when the days of their feasting were gone about, Job sent to them, and sanctified them: and rising up early offered holocausts for every one of them. For he said: Lest perhaps my sons have sinned, and have blessed God in their hearts. So did Job all days.
Job	Job	20	1	6	Now on a certain day when the sons of God came to stand before the Lord, Satan also was present among them.
Job	Job	20	1	7	And the Lord said to him: Whence comest thou? And he answered and said: I have gone round about the earth, and walked through it.
Job	Job	20	1	8	And the Lord said to him: Hast thou considered my servant Job, that there is none like him in the earth, a simple and upright man, and fearing God, and avoiding evil?
Job	Job	20	1	9	And Satan answering, said: Doth Job fear God in vain?
Job	Job	20	1	10	Hast not thou made a fence for him, and his house, and all his substance round about, blessed the works of his hands, and his possession hath increased on the earth?
Job	Job	20	1	11	But stretch forth thy hand a little, and touch all that he hath, and see if he blesseth thee not to thy face.
Job	Job	20	1	12	Then the Lord said to Satan: Behold, all that he hath is in thy hand: only put not forth thy hand upon his person. And Satan went forth from the presence of the Lord.
Job	Job	20	1	13	Now upon a certain day when his sons and daughters were eating and drinking wine in the house of their eldest brother,
Job	Job	20	1	14	There came a messenger to Job, and said: The oxen were ploughing, and the asses feeding beside them,
Job	Job	20	1	15	And the Sabeans rushed in, and took all away, and slew the servants with the sword, and I alone have escaped to tell thee.
Job	Job	20	1	16	And while he was yet speaking, another came, and said: The fire of God fell from heaven, and striking the sheep and the servants, hath consumed them, and I alone have escaped to tell thee.
Job	Job	20	1	17	And while he also was yet speaking, there came another, and said: The Chaldeans made three troops, and have fallen upon the camels, and taken them, moreover they have slain the servants with the sword, and I alone have escaped to tell thee.
Job	Job	20	1	18	He was yet speaking, and behold another came in, and said: Thy sons and daughters were eating and drinking wine in the house of their elder brother:
Job	Job	20	1	19	A violent wind came on a sudden from the side of the desert, and shook the four corners of the house, and it fell upon thy children and they are dead, and I alone have escaped to tell thee.
Job	Job	20	1	20	Then Job rose up, and rent his garments, and having shaven his head fell down upon the ground and worshipped,
Job	Job	20	1	21	And said: Naked came I out of my mother's womb, and naked shall I return thither: the Lord gave, and the Lord hath taken away: as it hath pleased the Lord so is it done: blessed be the name of the Lord.
Job	Job	20	1	22	In all these things Job sinned not by his lips, nor spoke he any foolish thing against God.
Job	Job	20	2	1	And it came to pass, when on a certain day the sons of God came, and stood before the Lord, and Satan came among them, and stood in his sight,
Job	Job	20	2	2	That the Lord said to Satan: Whence comest thou? And he answered and said: I have gone round about the earth, and walked through it.
Job	Job	20	2	3	And the Lord said to Satan: Hast thou considered my servant Job, that there is none like him in the earth, a man simple, and upright, and fearing God, and avoiding evil, and still keeping his innocence? But thou hast moved me against him, that I should afflict him without cause.
Job	Job	20	2	4	And Satan answered, and said: Skin for skin, and all that a man hath he will give for his life:
Job	Job	20	2	5	But put forth thy hand, and touch his bone and his flesh, and then thou shalt see that he will bless thee to thy face.
Job	Job	20	2	6	And the Lord said to Satan: Behold he is in thy hand, but yet save his life.
Job	Job	20	2	7	So Satan went forth from the presence Of the Lord, and struck Job with a very grievous ulcer, from the sole of the foot even to the top of his head:
Job	Job	20	2	8	And he took a potsherd and scraped the corrupt matter, sitting on a dunghill.
Job	Job	20	2	9	And his wife said to him: Dost thou still continue in thy simplicity? bless God and die.
Job	Job	20	2	10	And he said to her: Thou hast spoken like one of the foolish women: if we have received good things at the hand of God, why should we not receive evil? In all these things Job did not sin with his lips.
Job	Job	20	2	11	Now when Job's three friends heard all the evil that had befallen him, they came every one from his own place, Alphas the Themanite, and Baldad the Suhite, and Sophar the Naamathite. For they had made an appointment to come together and visit him, and comfort him.
Job	Job	20	2	12	And when they had lifted up their eyes afar off, they knew him not, and crying out they wept, and rending their garments they sprinkled dust upon their heads towards heaven.
Job	Job	20	2	13	And they sat with him on the ground seven days and seven nights, and no man spoke to him a word: for they saw that his grief was very great.
Job	Job	20	3	1	After this Job opened his mouth, and cursed his day,
Job	Job	20	3	2	And he said:
Job	Job	20	3	3	Let the day perish wherein I was born, and the night in which it was said: A man child is conceived.
Job	Job	20	3	4	Let that day be turned into darkness, let not God regard it from above, and let not the light shine upon it.
Job	Job	20	3	5	Let darkness, and the shadow of death cover it, let a mist overspread it, and let it be wrapped up in bitterness.
Job	Job	20	3	6	Let a darksome whirlwind seize upon that night, let it not be counted in the days of the year, nor numbered in the months.
Job	Job	20	3	7	Let that night be solitary, and not worthy of praise.
Job	Job	20	3	8	Let them curse it who curse the day. who are ready to raise up a leviathan:
Job	Job	20	3	9	Let the stars be darkened with the mist thereof: let it expect light and not see it, nor the rising of the dawning of the day:
Job	Job	20	3	10	Because it shut not up the doors of the womb that bore me, nor took away evils from my eyes.
Job	Job	20	3	11	Why did I not die in the womb, why did I not perish when I came out of the belly?
Job	Job	20	3	12	Why received upon the knees? why suckled at the breasts?
Job	Job	20	3	13	For now I should have been asleep and still, and should have rest in my sleep.
Job	Job	20	3	14	With kings and consuls of the earth, who build themselves solitudes:
Job	Job	20	3	15	Or with princes, that possess gold, and All their houses with silver:
Job	Job	20	3	16	Or as a hidden untimely birth I should not be, or as they that being conceived have not seen the light.
Job	Job	20	3	17	There the wicked cease from tumult, and there the wearied in strength are at rest.
Job	Job	20	3	18	And they sometime bound together without disquiet, have not heard the voice of the oppressor.
Job	Job	20	3	19	The small and great are there, and the servant is free from his master.
Job	Job	20	3	20	Why is light given to him that is in misery, and life to them that are in bitterness of soul?
Job	Job	20	3	21	That look for death, and it cometh not, as they that dig for a treasure:
Job	Job	20	3	22	And they rejoice exceedingly when they have found the grave.
Job	Job	20	3	23	To a man whose way is hidden, and God hath surrounded him with darkness?
Job	Job	20	3	24	Before I eat I sigh: and as overflowing waters, so is my roaring:
Job	Job	20	3	25	For the fear which I feared hath come upon me: and that which I was afraid of, hath befallen me.
Job	Job	20	3	26	Have I not dissembled? have I not kept silence? have I not been quiet? and indignation is come upon me.
Job	Job	20	4	1	Then Eliphaz the Themanite answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	4	2	If we begin to speak to thee, perhaps thou wilt take it ill, but who can withhold the words he hath conceived?
Job	Job	20	4	3	Behold thou hast taught many, and thou hast strengthened the weary hands:
Job	Job	20	4	4	Thy words have confirmed them that were staggering, and thou hast strengthened the trembling knees:
Job	Job	20	4	5	But now the scourge is come upon thee, and thou faintest: it hath touched thee, and thou art troubled.
Job	Job	20	4	6	Where is thy fear, thy fortitude, thy patience, and the perfection of thy ways?
Job	Job	20	4	7	Remember, I pray thee, who ever perished being innocent? or when were the just destroyed?
Job	Job	20	4	8	On the contrary I have seen those who work iniquity, and sow sorrows, and reap them,
Job	Job	20	4	9	Perishing by the blast of God, and consumed by the spirit of his wrath.
Job	Job	20	4	10	The roaring of the lion, and the voice of the lioness, and the teeth of the whelps of lions are broken:
Job	Job	20	4	11	The tiger hath perished for want of prey, and the young lions are scattered abroad.
Job	Job	20	4	12	Now there was a word spoken to me in private, and my ears by stealth as it were received the veins of its whisper.
Job	Job	20	4	13	In the horror of a vision by night, when deep sleep is wont to hold men,
Job	Job	20	4	14	Fear seized upon me, and trembling, and all my bones were affrighted:
Job	Job	20	4	15	And when a spirit passed before me, the hair of my flesh stood up.
Job	Job	20	4	16	There stood one whose countenance I knew not, an image before my eyes, and I heard the voice as it were of a gentle wind:
Job	Job	20	4	17	Shall man be justified in comparison of God, or shall a man be more pure than his maker?
Job	Job	20	4	18	Behold they that serve him are not steadfast, and in his angels he found wickedness:
Job	Job	20	4	19	How much more shall they that dwell in houses of clay, who have an earthly foundation, be consumed as with the moth?
Job	Job	20	4	20	From morning till evening they shall be cut down: and because no one understandeth, they shall perish for ever.
Job	Job	20	4	21	And they that shall be left, shall be taken away from them: they shall die, and not in wisdom.
Job	Job	20	5	1	Call now if there be any that will answer thee, and turn to some of the saints.
Job	Job	20	5	2	Anger indeed killeth the foolish, and envy slayeth the little one.
Job	Job	20	5	3	I have seen a fool with a strong root, and I cursed his beauty immediately.
Job	Job	20	5	4	His children shall be far from safety, and shall be destroyed in the gate, and there shall be none to deliver them.
Job	Job	20	5	5	Whose harvest the hungry shall eat, and the armed man shall take him by violence, and the thirsty shall drink up his riches.
Job	Job	20	5	6	Nothing upon earth is done without a voice cause, and sorrow doth not spring out of the ground.
Job	Job	20	5	7	Man is born to labour and the bird to fly.
Job	Job	20	5	8	Wherefore I will pray to the Lord, and address my speech to God:
Job	Job	20	5	9	Who doth great things and unsearchable and wonderful things without number:
Job	Job	20	5	10	Who giveth rain upon the face of the earth, and watereth all things with waters:
Job	Job	20	5	11	Who setteth up the humble on high, and comforteth with health those that mourn.
Job	Job	20	5	12	Who bringeth to nought the designs of the malignant, so that their hands cannot accomplish what they had begun:
Job	Job	20	5	13	Who catcheth the wise in their craftiness, and disappointeth the counsel of the wicked:
Job	Job	20	5	14	They shall meet with darkness in the day, and grope at noonday as in the night.
Job	Job	20	5	15	But he shall save the needy from the sword of their mouth, and the poor from the hand of the violent.
Job	Job	20	5	16	And to the needy there shall be hope, but iniquity shall draw in her mouth.
Job	Job	20	5	17	Blessed is the man whom God correcteth: refuse not therefore the chastising of the lord:
Job	Job	20	5	18	For he woundeth, and cureth: he striketh, and his hands shall heal.
Job	Job	20	5	19	In six troubles he shall deliver thee, and in the seventh, evil shall not touch thee.
Job	Job	20	5	20	In famine he shall deliver thee from death: and in battle, from the hand of the sword.
Job	Job	20	5	21	Thou shalt be hidden from the scourge of the tongue: and thou shalt not fear calamity when it cometh.
Job	Job	20	5	22	In destruction and famine then shalt laugh: and thou shalt not be afraid of the beasts of the earth.
Job	Job	20	5	23	But thou shalt have a covenant with the stones of the lands, and the beasts of the earth shall be at peace with thee.
Job	Job	20	5	24	And thou shalt know that thy tabernacle is in peace, and visiting thy beauty thou shalt not sin.
Job	Job	20	5	25	Thou shalt know also that thy seed shall be multiplied, and thy offspring like the grass of the earth.
Job	Job	20	5	26	Thou shalt enter into the grave in abundance, as a heap of wheat is brought in its season.
Job	Job	20	5	27	Behold, this is even so, as we have searched out: which thou having heard, consider it thoroughly in thy mind.
Job	Job	20	6	1	But Job answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	6	2	O that my sins, whereby I have deserved wrath, and the calamity that I suffer, were weighed in a balance.
Job	Job	20	6	3	As the sand of the sea this would appear heavier: therefore my words are full of sorrow:
Job	Job	20	6	4	For the arrows of the Lord are in me, the rage whereof drinketh up my spirit, and the terrors of the Lord war against me.
Job	Job	20	6	5	Will the wild ass bray when he hath grass? or will the ox low when he standeth before a full manger?
Job	Job	20	6	6	Or can an unsavoury thing be eaten, that is not seasoned with salt? or can a man taste that which when tasted bringeth death?
Job	Job	20	6	7	The things which before my soul would not touch, now, through anguish are my meats.
Job	Job	20	6	8	Who will grant that my request may come: and that God may give me what I look for?
Job	Job	20	6	9	And that he that hath begun may destroy me, that he may let loose his hand, and cut me off?
Job	Job	20	6	10	And that this may be my comfort, that afflicting me with sorrow, he spare not, nor I contradict the words of the Holy One.
Job	Job	20	6	11	For what is my strength, that I can hold out? or what is my end that I should keep patience?
Job	Job	20	6	12	My strength is not the strength of stones, nor is my flesh of brass.
Job	Job	20	6	13	Behold there is no help for me in myself, and my familiar friends also are departed from me.
Job	Job	20	6	14	He that taketh away mercy from his friend, forsaketh the fear of the Lord.
Job	Job	20	6	15	My brethren have passed by me, as the torrent that passeth swiftly in the valleys.
Job	Job	20	6	16	They that fear the hoary frost, the snow shall fall upon them.
Job	Job	20	6	17	At the time when they shall be scattered they shall perish: and after it groweth hot they shall be melted out of their place.
Job	Job	20	6	18	The paths of their steps are entangled: they shall walk in vain, and shall perish.
Job	Job	20	6	19	Consider the paths of Thema, the ways of Saba, and wait a little while.
Job	Job	20	6	20	They are confounded, because I have hoped: they are come also even unto me, and are covered with shame.
Job	Job	20	6	21	Now you are come: and now seeing my affliction you are afraid.
Job	Job	20	6	22	Did I say: Bring to me, and give me of your substance?
Job	Job	20	6	23	Or deliver me from the hand of the enemy, and rescue me out of the hand of the mighty?
Job	Job	20	6	24	Teach me, and I will hold my peace: and if I have been ignorant in any thing, instruct me.
Job	Job	20	6	25	Why have you detracted the words of truth, whereas there is none of you that can reprove me?
Job	Job	20	6	26	You dress up speeches only to rebuke, and you utter words to the wind.
Job	Job	20	6	27	You rush in upon the fatherless, and you endeavour to overthrow your friend.
Job	Job	20	6	28	However finish what you have begun, give ear, and see whether I lie.
Job	Job	20	6	29	Answer, I beseech you, without contention: and speaking that which is just, judge ye.
Job	Job	20	6	30	And you shall not find iniquity in my tongue, neither shall folly sound in my mouth.
Job	Job	20	7	1	The life of man upon earth is a warfare, and his days are like the days of a hireling.
Job	Job	20	7	2	As a servant longeth for the shade, as the hireling looketh for the end of his work;
Job	Job	20	7	3	So I also have had empty months, and have numbered to myself wearisome nights.
Job	Job	20	7	4	If I lie down to sleep, I shall say: When shall I arise? and again I shall look for the evening, and shall be filled with sorrows even till darkness.
Job	Job	20	7	5	My flesh is clothed with rottenness and the filth of dust, my skin is withered and drawn together.
Job	Job	20	7	6	My days have passed more swiftly than the web is cut by the weaver, and are consumed without any hope.
Job	Job	20	7	7	Remember that my life is but wind, and my eyes shall not return to see good things.
Job	Job	20	7	8	Nor shall the sight of man behold me: thy eyes are upon me, and I shall be no more.
Job	Job	20	7	9	As a cloud is consumed, and passeth away: so he that shall go down to hell shall not come up.
Job	Job	20	7	10	Nor shall he return any more into his house, neither shall his place know him any more.
Job	Job	20	7	11	Wherefore I will not spare my mouth, I will speak in the affliction of my spirit: I will talk with the bitterness of my soul.
Job	Job	20	7	12	Am I a sea, or a whale, that thou hast enclosed me in a prison?
Job	Job	20	7	13	If I say: My bed shall comfort me, and I shall be relieved speaking with myself on my couch:
Job	Job	20	7	14	Thou wilt frighten me with dreams and terrify me with visions.
Job	Job	20	7	15	So that my soul rather chooseth hanging, and my bones death.
Job	Job	20	7	16	I have done with hope, I shall now live no longer: spare me, for my days are nothing.
Job	Job	20	7	17	What is a man that thou shouldst magnify him? or why dost thou set thy heart upon him?
Job	Job	20	7	18	Thou visitest him early in the morning, and thou provest him suddenly.
Job	Job	20	7	19	How long wilt thou not spare me, nor suffer me to swallow down my spittle?
Job	Job	20	7	20	I have sinned: what shall I do to thee, O keeper of men? why hast thou set me opposite to thee, and I am become burdensome to myself?
Job	Job	20	7	21	Why dost thou not remove my sin, and why dost thou not take away my iniquity? Behold now I shall sleep in the dust: and if thou seek me in the morning, I shall not be.
Job	Job	20	8	1	The Baldad the Suhite answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	8	2	How long wilt thou speak these things, and how long shall the words of thy mouth be like a strong wind?
Job	Job	20	8	3	Doth God pervert judgment, or doth the Almighty overthrow that which is just?
Job	Job	20	8	4	Although thy children have sinned against him, and he hath left them in the hand of their iniquity:
Job	Job	20	8	5	Yet if thou wilt arise early to God, and wilt beseech the Almighty:
Job	Job	20	8	6	If thou wilt walk clean and upright, he will presently awake onto thee, and will make the dwelling of thy justice peaceable:
Job	Job	20	8	7	Insomuch, that if thy former things were small, thy latter things would be multiplied exceedingly.
Job	Job	20	8	8	For inquire of the former generation, and search diligently into the memory of the fathers:
Job	Job	20	8	9	(For we are but of yesterday, and are ignorant that our days upon earth are but a shadow:)
Job	Job	20	8	10	And they shall teach thee: they shall speak to thee, and utter words out of their hearts.
Job	Job	20	8	11	Can the rush be green without moisture? or a sedge-bush grow without water?
Job	Job	20	8	12	When it is yet in flower, and is not plucked up with the hand, it withereth before all herbs.
Job	Job	20	8	13	Even so are the ways of all that forget God, and the hope of the hypocrite shall perish:
Job	Job	20	8	14	His folly shall not please him, and his trust shall be like the spider's web.
Job	Job	20	8	15	He shall lean upon his house, and it shall not stand: he shall prop it up, and it shall not rise:
Job	Job	20	8	16	He seemeth to have moisture before the sun cometh, and at his rising his blossom shall shoot forth.
Job	Job	20	8	17	His roots shall be thick upon a heap of stones, and among the stones he shall abide.
Job	Job	20	8	18	If one swallow him up out of his place, he shall deny him, and shall say: I know thee not.
Job	Job	20	8	19	For this is the joy of his way, that others may spring again out of the earth.
Job	Job	20	8	20	God will not cast away the simple, nor reach out his hand to the evildoer:
Job	Job	20	8	21	Until thy mouth be filled with laughter, and thy lips with rejoicing.
Job	Job	20	8	22	They that hate thee, shall be clothed with confusion: and the dwelling of the wicked shall not stand.
Job	Job	20	9	1	And Job answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	9	2	Indeed I know it is so, and that man cannot be justified compared with God.
Job	Job	20	9	3	If he will contend with him, he cannot answer him one for a thousand.
Job	Job	20	9	4	He is wise in heart, and mighty in strength: who hath resisted him, and hath had peace?
Job	Job	20	9	5	Who hath removed mountains, and they whom he overthrew in his wrath, knew it not.
Job	Job	20	9	6	Who shaketh the earth out of her place, and the pillars thereof tremble.
Job	Job	20	9	7	Who commandeth the sun and it riseth not: and shutteth up the stars as it were under a seal:
Job	Job	20	9	8	Who alone spreadeth out the heavens, and walketh upon the waves of the sea.
Job	Job	20	9	9	Who maketh Arcturus, and Orion, and Hyades, and the inner parts of the south.
Job	Job	20	9	10	Who doth things great and incomprehensible, and wonderful, of which there is no number.
Job	Job	20	9	11	If he come to me, I shall not see him: if he depart I shall not understand.
Job	Job	20	9	12	If he examine on a sudden, who shall answer him? or who can say: Why dost thou so?
Job	Job	20	9	13	God, whose wrath no man can resist, and under whom they stoop that bear up the world.
Job	Job	20	9	14	What am I then, that I should answer him, and have words with him?
Job	Job	20	9	15	I, who although I should have any just thing, would not answer, but would make supplication to my judge.
Job	Job	20	9	16	And if he should hear me when I call, I should not believe that he had heard my voice.
Job	Job	20	9	17	For he shall crush me in a whirlwind, and multiply my wounds even without cause.
Job	Job	20	9	18	He alloweth not my spirit to rest, and he filleth me with bitterness.
Job	Job	20	9	19	If strength be demanded, he is most strong: if equity of judgment, no man dare bear witness for me.
Job	Job	20	9	20	If I would justify myself, my own mouth shall condemn me: if I would shew myself innocent, he shall prove me wicked.
Job	Job	20	9	21	Although I should be simple, even this my soul shall be ignorant of, and I shall be weary of my life.
Job	Job	20	9	22	One thing there is that I have spoken, both the innocent and the wicked he consumeth.
Job	Job	20	9	23	If he scourge, let him kill at once, and not laugh at the pains of the innocent.
Job	Job	20	9	24	The earth is given into the hand of the wicked, he covereth the face of the judges thereof: and if it be not he, who is it then?
Job	Job	20	9	25	My days have been swifter than a post: they have fled away and have not seen good.
Job	Job	20	9	26	They have passed by as ships carrying fruits, as an eagle flying to the prey.
Job	Job	20	9	27	If I say: I will not speak so: I change my face, and am tormented with sorrow.
Job	Job	20	9	28	I feared all my works, knowing that thou didst not spare the offender.
Job	Job	20	9	29	But if so also I am wicked, why have I laboured in vain?
Job	Job	20	9	30	If I be washed as it were with snow waters, and my hands shall shine ever so clean:
Job	Job	20	9	31	Yet thou shalt plunge me in filth, and my garments shall abhor me,
Job	Job	20	9	32	For I shall not answer a man that is like myself: nor one that may be heard with me equally in judgment.
Job	Job	20	9	33	There is none that may be able to reprove both, and to put his hand between both.
Job	Job	20	9	34	Let him take his rod away from me, and let not his fear terrify me.
Job	Job	20	9	35	I will speak, and will not fear him: for I cannot answer while I am in fear.
Job	Job	20	10	1	My soul is weary of my life, I will let go my speech against myself, I will speak in the bitterness of my soul.
Job	Job	20	10	2	I will say to God: Do not condemn me: tell me why thou judgest me so.
Job	Job	20	10	3	Doth it seem good to thee that thou shouldst calumniate me, and oppress me, the work of thy own hands, and help the counsel of the wicked?
Job	Job	20	10	4	Hast thou eyes of flesh: or, shalt thou see as man seeth?
Job	Job	20	10	5	Are thy days as the days of man, and are thy years as the times of men:
Job	Job	20	10	6	That thou shouldst inquire after my iniquity, and search after my sin?
Job	Job	20	10	7	And shouldst know that I have done no wicked thing, whereas there is no man that can deliver out of thy hand.
Job	Job	20	10	8	Thy hands have made me, and fashioned me wholly round about, and dost thou thus cast me down headlong on a sudden?
Job	Job	20	10	9	Remember, I beseech thee, that thou hast made me as the clay, and thou wilt bring me into dust again.
Job	Job	20	10	10	Hast thou not milked me as milk, and curdled me like cheese?
Job	Job	20	10	11	Thou hast clothed me with skin and flesh: thou hast put me together with bones and sinews:
Job	Job	20	10	12	Thou hast granted me life and mercy, and thy visitation hath preserved my spirit.
Job	Job	20	10	13	Although thou conceal these things in thy heart, yet I know that thou rememberest all things.
Job	Job	20	10	14	If I have sinned and thou hast spared me for an hour: why dost thou not suffer me to be clean from my iniquity?
Job	Job	20	10	15	And if I be wicked, woe unto me: and if just, I shall not lift up my head, being filled with affliction and misery.
Job	Job	20	10	16	And for pride thou wilt take me as a lioness, and returning thou tormentest me wonderfully.
Job	Job	20	10	17	Thou renewest thy witnesses against me, and multipliest thy wrath upon me, and pains war against me.
Job	Job	20	10	18	Why didst thou bring me forth out of the womb: O that I had been consumed that eye might not see me!
Job	Job	20	10	19	I should have been as if I had not been, carried from the womb to the grave.
Job	Job	20	10	20	Shall not the fewness of my days be ended shortly? suffer me, therefore, that I may lament my sorrow a little:
Job	Job	20	10	21	Before I go, and return no more, to a land that is dark and covered with the mist of death:
Job	Job	20	10	22	A land of misery and darkness, where the shadow of death, and no order, but everlasting horror dwelleth.
Job	Job	20	11	1	Then Sophar the Naamathite answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	11	2	Shall not he that speaketh much, hear also? or shall a man full of talk be justified?
Job	Job	20	11	3	Shall men hold their peace to thee only? and when thou hast mocked others, shall no man confute thee?
Job	Job	20	11	4	For thou hast said: My word is pure, and I am clean in thy sight.
Job	Job	20	11	5	And I wish that God would speak with thee, and would open his lips to thee,
Job	Job	20	11	6	That he might shew thee the secrets of wisdom, and that his law is manifold, and thou mightest understand that he exacteth much less of thee, than thy iniquity deserveth.
Job	Job	20	11	7	Peradventure thou wilt comprehend the steps of God, and wilt find out the Almighty perfectly?
Job	Job	20	11	8	He is higher than heaven, and what wilt thou do? he is deeper than hell, and how wilt thou know?
Job	Job	20	11	9	The measure of him is longer than the earth, and broader than the sea.
Job	Job	20	11	10	If he shall overturn all things, or shall press them together, who shall contradict him?
Job	Job	20	11	11	For he knoweth the vanity of men, and when he seeth iniquity, doth he not consider it?
Job	Job	20	11	12	A vain man is lifted up into pride, and thinketh himself born free like a wild ass's colt.
Job	Job	20	11	13	But thou hast hardened thy heart, and hast spread thy hands to him.
Job	Job	20	11	14	If thou wilt put away from thee the iniquity that is in thy hand, and let not injustice remain in thy tabernacle:
Job	Job	20	11	15	Then mayst thou lift up thy face without spot, and thou shalt be steadfast, and shalt not fear.
Job	Job	20	11	16	Thou shalt also forget misery, and remember it only as waters that are passed away.
Job	Job	20	11	17	And brightness like that of the noonday, shall arise to thee at evening: and when thou shalt think thyself consumed, thou shalt rise as the day star.
Job	Job	20	11	18	And thou shalt have confidence, hope being set before thee, and being buried thou shalt sleep secure.
Job	Job	20	11	19	Thou shalt rest, and there shall be none to make thee afraid: and many shall entreat thy face.
Job	Job	20	11	20	But the eyes of the wicked shall decay, and the way to escape shall fail them, and their hope the abomination of the soul.
Job	Job	20	12	1	When Job answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	12	2	Are you then men alone, and shall wisdom die with you?
Job	Job	20	12	3	I also have a heart as well as you: for who is ignorant of these things, which you know?
Job	Job	20	12	4	He that is mocked by his friends as I, shall call upon God and he will hear him: for the simplicity of the just man is laughed to scorn.
Job	Job	20	12	5	The lamp despised in the thoughts of the rich, is ready for the time appointed.
Job	Job	20	12	6	The tabernacles of robbers abound, and they provoke God boldly; whereas it is he that hath given all into their hands:
Job	Job	20	12	7	But ask now the beasts, and they shall teach thee: and the birds of the air, and they shall tell thee.
Job	Job	20	12	8	Speak to the earth, and it shall answer thee: and the fishes of the sea shall tell.
Job	Job	20	12	9	Who is ignorant that the hand of the Lord hath made all these things?
Job	Job	20	12	10	In whose hand is the soul of every living thing, and the spirit of all flesh of man.
Job	Job	20	12	11	Doth not the ear discern words, and the palate of him that eateth, the taste?
Job	Job	20	12	12	In the ancient is wisdom, and in length of days prudence.
Job	Job	20	12	13	With him is wisdom and strength, he hath counsel and understanding.
Job	Job	20	12	14	If he pull down, there is no man that can build up: if he shut up a man, there is none that can open.
Job	Job	20	12	15	If he withhold the waters, all things shall be dried up: and if he send them out, they shall overturn the earth.
Job	Job	20	12	16	With him is strength and wisdom: he knoweth both the deceiver, and him that is deceived.
Job	Job	20	12	17	He bringeth counsellors to a foolish end, and judges to insensibility.
Job	Job	20	12	18	He looseth the belt of kings, and girdeth their loins with a cord.
Job	Job	20	12	19	He leadeth away priests without glory, and overthroweth nobles.
Job	Job	20	12	20	He changeth the speech of the true speakers, and taketh away the doctrine of the aged.
Job	Job	20	12	21	He poureth contempt upon princes, and relieveth them that were oppressed.
Job	Job	20	12	22	He discovereth deep things out of darkness, and bringeth up to light the shadow of death.
Job	Job	20	12	23	He multiplieth nations, and destroyeth them, and restoreth them again after they were overthrown.
Job	Job	20	12	24	He changeth the heart of the princes of the people of the earth, and deceiveth them that they walk in vain where there is no way.
Job	Job	20	12	25	They shall grope as in the dark, and not in the light, and he shall make them stagger like men that are drunk.
Job	Job	20	13	1	Behold my eye hath seen all these things, and my ear hath heard them, and I have understood them all.
Job	Job	20	13	2	According to your knowledge I also know: neither am I inferior to you.
Job	Job	20	13	3	But yet I will speak to the Almighty, and I desire to reason with God.
Job	Job	20	13	4	Having first shewn that you are forgers of lies, and maintainers of perverse opinions.
Job	Job	20	13	5	And I wish you would hold your peace, that you might be thought to be wise men.
Job	Job	20	13	6	Hear ye therefore my reproof, and attend to the judgment of my lips.
Job	Job	20	13	7	Hath God any need of your lie, that you should speak deceitfully for him?
Job	Job	20	13	8	Do you accept his person, and do you endeavour to judge for God?
Job	Job	20	13	9	Or shall it please him, from whom nothing can be concealed? or shall he be deceived as a man, with your deceitful dealings?
Job	Job	20	13	10	He shall reprove you, because in secret you accept his person.
Job	Job	20	13	11	As soon as he shall move himself, he shall trouble you: and his dread shall fall upon you.
Job	Job	20	13	12	Your remembrance shall be compared to ashes, and your necks shall be brought to clay.
Job	Job	20	13	13	Hold your peace a little while, that I may speak whatsoever my mind shall suggest to me.
Job	Job	20	13	14	Why do I tear my flesh with my teeth, and carry my soul in my hands?
Job	Job	20	13	15	Although he should kill me, I will trust in him: but yet I will reprove my ways in his sight.
Job	Job	20	13	16	And he shall be my saviour: for no hypocrite shall come before his presence.
Job	Job	20	13	17	Hear ye my speech, and receive with your ears hidden truths.
Job	Job	20	13	18	If I shall be judged, I know that I shall be found just.
Job	Job	20	13	19	Who is he that will plead against me? let him come: why am I consumed holding my peace?
Job	Job	20	13	20	Two things only do not to me, and then from thy face I shall not be hid:
Job	Job	20	13	21	Withdraw thy hand far from me, and let not thy dread terrify me.
Job	Job	20	13	22	Call me, and I will answer thee: or else I will speak, and do thou answer me.
Job	Job	20	13	23	How many are my iniquities and sins? make me know my crimes and offences.
Job	Job	20	13	24	Why hidest thou thy face, and thinkest me thy enemy?
Job	Job	20	13	25	Against a leaf, that is carried away with the wind, thou shewest thy power, and thou pursuest a dry straw.
Job	Job	20	13	26	For thou writest bitter things against me, and wilt consume me for the sins of my youth.
Job	Job	20	13	27	Thou hast put my feet in the stocks, and hast observed all my paths, and hast considered the steps of my feet:
Job	Job	20	13	28	Who am to be consumed as rottenness, and as a garment that is moth-eaten.
Job	Job	20	14	1	Man born of a woman, living for a short time, is filled with many miseries.
Job	Job	20	14	2	Who cometh forth like a flower, and is destroyed, and fleeth as a shadow, and never continueth in the same state.
Job	Job	20	14	3	And dost thou think it meet to open thy eyes upon such an one, and to bring him into judgment with thee?
Job	Job	20	14	4	Who can make him clean that is conceived of unclean seed? is it not thou who only art?
Job	Job	20	14	5	The days of man are short, and the number of his months is with thee: thou hast appointed his bounds which cannot be passed.
Job	Job	20	14	6	Depart a little from him, that he may rest, until his wished for day come, as that of the hireling.
Job	Job	20	14	7	A tree hath hope: if it be cut, it groweth green again, and the boughs thereof sprout.
Job	Job	20	14	8	If its root be old in the earth, and its stock be dead in the dust:
Job	Job	20	14	9	At the scent of water, it shall spring, and bring forth leaves, as when it was first planted.
Job	Job	20	14	10	But man when he shall be dead, and stripped and consumed, I pray you where is he?
Job	Job	20	14	11	As if the waters should depart out of the sea, and an emptied river should be dried up:
Job	Job	20	14	12	So man when he is fallen asleep shall not rise again; till the heavens be broken, he shall not awake, nor rise up out of his sleep.
Job	Job	20	14	13	Who will grant me this, that thou mayst protect me in hell, and hide me till thy wrath pass, and appoint me a time when thou wilt remember me?
Job	Job	20	14	14	Shall man that is dead, thinkest thou, live again? all the days in which I am now in warfare, I expect until my change come.
Job	Job	20	14	15	Thou shalt call me, and I will answer thee: to the work of thy hands thou shalt reach out thy right hand.
Job	Job	20	14	16	Thou indeed hast numbered my steps, but spare my sins.
Job	Job	20	14	17	Thou hast sealed up my offences as it were in a bag, but hast cured my iniquity.
Job	Job	20	14	18	A mountain falling cometh to nought, and a rock is removed out of its place.
Job	Job	20	14	19	Waters wear away the stones, and with inundation the ground by little and little is washed away: so in like manner thou shalt destroy man.
Job	Job	20	14	20	Thou hast strengthened him for a little while, that he may pass away for ever: thou shalt change his face, and shalt send him away.
Job	Job	20	14	21	Whether his children come to honour or dishonour, he shall not understand.
Job	Job	20	14	22	But yet his flesh, while he shall live, shall have pain, and his soul shall mourn over him.
Job	Job	20	15	1	And Eliphaz the Themanite, answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	15	2	Will a wise man answer as if he were speaking in the wind, and fill his stomach with burning heat?
Job	Job	20	15	3	Thou reprovest him by words, who is not equal to thee, and thou speakest that which is not good for thee.
Job	Job	20	15	4	As much as is in thee, thou hast made void fear, and hast taken away prayers from before God.
Job	Job	20	15	5	For thy iniquity hath taught thy mouth, and thou imitatest the tongue of blasphemers.
Job	Job	20	15	6	Thy own mouth shall condemn thee, and not I: and thy own lips shall answer thee.
Job	Job	20	15	7	Art thou the first man that was born, or wast thou made before the hills?
Job	Job	20	15	8	Hast thou heard God's counsel, and shall his wisdom be inferior to thee?
Job	Job	20	15	9	What knowest thou that we are ignorant of? what dost thou understand that we know not?
Job	Job	20	15	10	There are with us also aged and ancient men, much elder than thy fathers.
Job	Job	20	15	11	Is it a great matter that God should comfort thee? but thy wicked words hinder this.
Job	Job	20	15	12	Why doth thy heart elevate thee, and why dost thou stare with thy eyes, as if they were thinking great things?
Job	Job	20	15	13	Why doth thy spirit swell against God, to utter such words out of thy mouth?
Job	Job	20	15	14	What is man that he should be without spot, and he that is born of a woman that he should appear just?
Job	Job	20	15	15	Behold among his saints none is unchangeable, and the heavens are not pure in his sight.
Job	Job	20	15	16	How much more is man abominable, and unprofitable, who drinketh iniquity like water?
Job	Job	20	15	17	I will shew thee, hear me: and I will tell thee what I have seen.
Job	Job	20	15	18	Wise men confess and hide not their fathers.
Job	Job	20	15	19	To whom alone the earth was given, and no stranger hath passed among them.
Job	Job	20	15	20	The wicked man is proud all his days, and the number of the years of his tyranny is uncertain.
Job	Job	20	15	21	The sound of dread is always in his ears: and when there is peace, he always suspecteth treason.
Job	Job	20	15	22	He believeth not that he may return from darkness to light, looking round about for the sword on every side.
Job	Job	20	15	23	When he moveth himself to seek bread, he knoweth that the day of darkness is ready at his hand.
Job	Job	20	15	24	Tribulation shall terrify him, and distress shall surround him, as a king that is prepared for the battle.
Job	Job	20	15	25	For he hath stretched out his hand against God, and hath strengthened himself against the Almighty.
Job	Job	20	15	26	He hath run against him with his neck raised up, and is armed with a fat neck.
Job	Job	20	15	27	Fatness hath covered his face, and the fat hangeth down on his sides.
Job	Job	20	15	28	He hath dwelt in desolate cities, and in desert houses that are reduced into heaps.
Job	Job	20	15	29	He shall not be enriched, neither shall his substance continue, neither shall he push his root in the earth.
Job	Job	20	15	30	He shall not depart out of darkness: the flame shall dry up his branches, and he shall be taken away by the breath of his own mouth.
Job	Job	20	15	31	He shall not believe, being vainly deceived by error, that he may be redeemed with any price.
Job	Job	20	15	32	Before his days be full he shall perish: and his hands shall wither away.
Job	Job	20	15	33	He shall be blasted as a vine when its grapes are in the first flower, and as an olive tree that casteth its flower.
Job	Job	20	15	34	For the congregation of the hypocrite is barren, and fire shall devour their tabernacles, who love to take bribes.
Job	Job	20	15	35	He hath conceived sorrow, and hath brought forth iniquity, and his womb prepareth deceits.
Job	Job	20	16	1	Then Job answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	16	2	I have often heard such things as these: you are all troublesome comforters.
Job	Job	20	16	3	Shall windy words have no end? or is it any trouble to thee to speak?
Job	Job	20	16	4	I also could speak like you: and would God your soul were for my soul.
Job	Job	20	16	5	I would comfort you also with words, and would wag my head over you.
Job	Job	20	16	6	I would strengthen you with my mouth, and would move my lips, as sparing you.
Job	Job	20	16	7	But what shall I do? If I speak, my pain will not rest: and if I hold my peace, it will not depart from me.
Job	Job	20	16	8	But now my sorrow hath oppressed me, and all my limbs are brought to nothing.
Job	Job	20	16	9	My wrinkles bear witness against me, and a false speaker riseth up against my face, contradicting me.
Job	Job	20	16	10	He hath gathered together his fury against me, and threatening me he hath gnashed with his teeth upon me: my enemy hath beheld me with terrible eyes.
Job	Job	20	16	11	They have opened their mouths upon me, and reproaching me they have struck me on the cheek, they are filled with my pains.
Job	Job	20	16	12	God hath shut me up with the unjust man, and hath delivered me into the hands of the wicked.
Job	Job	20	16	13	I that was formerly so wealthy, am all on a sudden broken to pieces: he hath taken me by my neck, he hath broken me, and hath set me up to be his mark.
Job	Job	20	16	14	He hath compassed me round about with his lances, he hath wounded my loins, he hath not spared, and hath poured out my bowels on the earth.
Job	Job	20	16	15	He hath torn me with wound upon wound, he hath rushed in upon me like a giant.
Job	Job	20	16	16	I have sowed sackcloth upon my skin, and have covered my flesh with ashes.
Job	Job	20	16	17	My face is swollen with weeping, and my eyelids are dim.
Job	Job	20	16	18	These things have I suffered without the iniquity of my hand, when I offered pure prayers to God.
Job	Job	20	16	19	O earth, cover not thou my blood, neither let my cry find a hiding place in thee.
Job	Job	20	16	20	For behold my witness is in heaven, and he that knoweth my conscience is on high.
Job	Job	20	16	21	My friends are full of words: my eye poureth out tears to God.
Job	Job	20	16	22	And O that a man might so be judged with God, as the son of man is judged with his companion!
Job	Job	20	16	23	For behold short years pass away and I am walking in a path by which I shall not return.
Job	Job	20	17	1	My spirit shall be wasted, my days shall be shortened, and only the grave remaineth for me.
Job	Job	20	17	2	I have not sinned, and my eye abideth in bitterness.
Job	Job	20	17	3	Deliver me O Lord, and set me beside thee, and let any man's hand fight against me.
Job	Job	20	17	4	Thou hast set their heart far from understanding, therefore they shall not be exalted.
Job	Job	20	17	5	He promiseth a prey to his companions, and the eyes of his children shall fail.
Job	Job	20	17	6	He hath made me as it were a byword of the people, and I am an example before them.
Job	Job	20	17	7	My eye is dim through indignation, and my limbs are brought as it were to nothing.
Job	Job	20	17	8	The just shall be astonished at this, and the innocent shall be raised up against the hypocrite.
Job	Job	20	17	9	And the just man shall hold on his way, and he that hath clean hands shall be stronger and stronger.
Job	Job	20	17	10	Wherefore be you all converted, and come, and I shall not find among you any wise man.
Job	Job	20	17	11	My days have passed away, my thoughts are dissipated, tormenting my heart.
Job	Job	20	17	12	They have turned night into day, and after darkness I hope for light again.
Job	Job	20	17	13	If I wait hell is my house, and I have made my bed in darkness.
Job	Job	20	17	14	If I have said to rottenness: Thou art my father; to worms, my mother and my sister.
Job	Job	20	17	15	Where is now then my expectation, and who considereth my patience?
Job	Job	20	17	16	All that I have shall go down into the deepest pit: thinkest thou that there at least I shall have rest?
Job	Job	20	18	1	Then Baldad the Suhite answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	18	2	How long will you throw out words? understand first, and so let us speak.
Job	Job	20	18	3	Why are we reputed as beasts, and counted vile before you?
Job	Job	20	18	4	Thou that destroyest thy soul in thy fury, shall the earth be forsaken for thee, and shall rocks be removed out of their place?
Job	Job	20	18	5	Shall not the light of the wicked be extinguished, and the flame of his fire not shine?
Job	Job	20	18	6	The light shall be dark in his tabernacle, and the lamp that is over him, shall be put out.
Job	Job	20	18	7	The step of his strength shall be straitened, and his own counsel shall cast him down headlong.
Job	Job	20	18	8	For he hath thrust his feet into a net, and walketh in its meshes.
Job	Job	20	18	9	The sole of his foot shall be held in a snare, and thirst shall burn against him.
Job	Job	20	18	10	A gin is hidden for him in the earth, and his trap upon the path.
Job	Job	20	18	11	Fears shall terrify him on every side, and shall entangle his feet.
Job	Job	20	18	12	Let his strength be wasted with famine, and let hunger invade his ribs.
Job	Job	20	18	13	Let it devour the beauty of his skin, let the firstborn death consume his arms.
Job	Job	20	18	14	Let his confidence be rooted out of his tabernacle, and let destruction tread upon him like a king.
Job	Job	20	18	15	Let the companions of him that is not, dwell in his tabernacle, let brimstone be sprinkled in his tent.
Job	Job	20	18	16	Let his roots be dried up beneath, and his harvest destroyed above.
Job	Job	20	18	17	Let the memory of him perish from the earth and let not his name be renowned in the streets.
Job	Job	20	18	18	He shall drive him out of light into darkness, and shall remove him out of the world.
Job	Job	20	18	19	His seed shall not subsist, nor his offspring among his people, nor any remnants in his country.
Job	Job	20	18	20	They that come after him shall be astonished at his day, and horror shall fall upon them that went before.
Job	Job	20	18	21	These men are the tabernacles of the wicked, and this the place of him that knoweth not God.
Job	Job	20	19	1	Then Job answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	19	2	How long do you afflict my soul, and break me in pieces with words?
Job	Job	20	19	3	Behold, these ten times you confound me, and are not ashamed to oppress me.
Job	Job	20	19	4	For if I have been ignorant, my ignorance shall be with me.
Job	Job	20	19	5	But you have set yourselves up against me, and reprove me with my reproaches.
Job	Job	20	19	6	At least now understand, that God hath not afflicted me with an equal judgment, and compassed me with his scourges.
Job	Job	20	19	7	Behold I cry suffering violence, and no one will hear: I shall cry aloud, and there is none to judge.
Job	Job	20	19	8	He hath hedged in my path round about, and I cannot pass, and in my way he hath set darkness.
Job	Job	20	19	9	He hath stripped me of my glory, and hath taken the crown from my head.
Job	Job	20	19	10	He hath destroyed me on every side, and I am lost, and he hath taken away my hope, as from a tree that is plucked up.
Job	Job	20	19	11	His wrath is kindled against me, and he hath counted me as his enemy.
Job	Job	20	19	12	His troops have come together, and have made themselves a way by me, and have besieged my tabernacle round about.
Job	Job	20	19	13	He hath put my brethren far from me, and my acquaintance like strangers have departed from me.
Job	Job	20	19	14	My kinsmen have forsaken me, and they that knew me, have forgotten me.
Job	Job	20	19	15	They that dwelt in my house, and my maidservants have counted me a stranger, and I have been like an alien in their eyes.
Job	Job	20	19	16	I called my servant, and he gave me no answer, I entreated him with my own mouth.
Job	Job	20	19	17	My wife hath abhorred my breath, and I entreated the children of my womb.
Job	Job	20	19	18	Even fools despise me; and when I was gone from them, they spoke against me.
Job	Job	20	19	19	They that were sometime my counsellors, have abhorred me: and he whom I love most is turned against me.
Job	Job	20	19	20	The flesh being consumed. My bone hath cleaved to my skin, and nothing but lips are left about my teeth.
Job	Job	20	19	21	Have pity on me, have pity on me, at least you my friends, because the hand of the Lord hath touched me.
Job	Job	20	19	22	Why do you persecute me as God, and glut yourselves with my flesh?
Job	Job	20	19	23	Who will grant me that my words may be written? Who will grant me that they may be marked down in a book?
Job	Job	20	19	24	With an iron pen and in a plate of lead, or else be graven with an instrument in flint stone.
Job	Job	20	19	25	For I know that my Redeemer liveth, and in the last day I shall rise out of the earth.
Job	Job	20	19	26	And I shall be clothed again with my skin, and in my flesh I will see my God.
Job	Job	20	19	27	Whom I myself shall see, and my eyes shall behold, and not another: this my hope is laid up in my bosom.
Job	Job	20	19	28	Why then do you say now: Let us persecute him, and let us find occasion of word against him?
Job	Job	20	19	29	Flee then from the face of the sword, for the sword is the revenger of iniquities: and know ye that there is judgment.
Job	Job	20	20	1	Then Sophar the Naamathite answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	20	2	Therefore various thoughts succeed one another in me, and my mind is hurried away to different things.
Job	Job	20	20	3	The doctrine with which thou reprovest me, I will hear, and the spirit of my understanding shall answer for me.
Job	Job	20	20	4	This I know from the beginning, since man was placed upon the earth,
Job	Job	20	20	5	That the praise of the wicked is short, and the joy of the hypocrite but for a moment.
Job	Job	20	20	6	If his pride mount up even to heaven, and his head touch the clouds:
Job	Job	20	20	7	In the end he shall be destroyed like a dunghill, and they that has seen him shall say: Where is he?
Job	Job	20	20	8	As a dream that fleeth away he shall not be found, he shall pass as a vision of the night:
Job	Job	20	20	9	The eyes that had seen him, shall see him no more, neither shall his place any more behold him.
Job	Job	20	20	10	His children shall be oppressed with want, and his hands shall render him his sorrow.
Job	Job	20	20	11	His bones shall be filled with the vices of his youth, and they shall sleep with him in the dust.
Job	Job	20	20	12	For when evil shall be sweet in his mouth, he will hide it under his tongue.
Job	Job	20	20	13	He will spare it, and not leave it, and will hide it in his throat.
Job	Job	20	20	14	His bread in his belly shall be turned into the gall of asps within him.
Job	Job	20	20	15	The riches which he hath swallowed; he shall vomit up, and God shall draw them out of his belly.
Job	Job	20	20	16	He shall suck the head of asps, and the viper's tongue shall kill him.
Job	Job	20	20	17	(Let him not see the streams of the river, the brooks of honey and of butter.)
Job	Job	20	20	18	He shall be punished for all that he did, and yet shall not be consumed: according to the multitude of his devices so also shall he suffer.
Job	Job	20	20	19	Because he broke in and stripped the poor: he hath violently taken away a house which he did not build.
Job	Job	20	20	20	And yet his belly was not filled: and when he hath the things he coveted, he shall not be able to possess them.
Job	Job	20	20	21	There was nothing left of his meat, and therefore nothing shall continue of his goods:
Job	Job	20	20	22	When he shall be filled, he shall be straitened, he shall burn, and every sorrow shall fall upon him.
Job	Job	20	20	23	May his belly be filled, that God may send forth the wrath of his indignation upon him, and rain down his war upon him.
Job	Job	20	20	24	He shall flee from weapons of iron, and shall fall upon a bow of brass.
Job	Job	20	20	25	The sword is drawn out, and cometh forth from its scabbard, and glittereth in his bitterness: the terrible ones shall go and come upon him.
Job	Job	20	20	26	All darkness is hid in his secret places: a fire that is not kindled shall devour him, he shall be afflicted when left in his tabernacle.
Job	Job	20	20	27	The heavens shall reveal his iniquity, and the earth shall rise up against him.
Job	Job	20	20	28	The offspring of his house shall be exposed, he shall be pulled down in the day of God's wrath.
Job	Job	20	20	29	This is the portion of a wicked man from God, and the inheritance of his doings from the Lord.
Job	Job	20	21	1	Then Job answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	21	2	Hear, I beseech you, my words, and do penance.
Job	Job	20	21	3	Suffer me, and I will speak, and after, if you please, laugh at my words.
Job	Job	20	21	4	Is my debate against man, that I should not have just reason to be troubled?
Job	Job	20	21	5	Hearken to me and be astonished, and lay your finger on your mouth.
Job	Job	20	21	6	As for me, when I remember, I am afraid, and trembling taketh hold on my flesh.
Job	Job	20	21	7	Why then do the wicked live, are they advanced, and strengthened with riches?
Job	Job	20	21	8	Their seed continueth before them, a multitude of kinsmen, and of children's children in their sight.
Job	Job	20	21	9	Their houses are secure and peaceable, and the rod of God is not upon them.
Job	Job	20	21	10	Their cattle have conceived, and failed not: their cow has calved, and is not deprived of her fruit.
Job	Job	20	21	11	Their little ones go out like a flock, and their children dance and play.
Job	Job	20	21	12	They take the timbrel, and the harp, and rejoice at the sound of the organ.
Job	Job	20	21	13	They spend their days in wealth, and in a moment they go down to hell.
Job	Job	20	21	14	Who have said to God: Depart from us, we desire not the knowledge of thy ways.
Job	Job	20	21	15	Who is the Almighty, that we should serve him? and what doth it profit us if we pray to him?
Job	Job	20	21	16	Yet because their good things are not in their hand, may the counsel of the wicked be far from me.
Job	Job	20	21	17	How often shall the lamp of the wicked be put out, and a deluge come upon them, and he shall distribute the sorrows of his wrath?
Job	Job	20	21	18	They shall be as chaff before the face of the wind, and as ashes which the whirlwind scattereth.
Job	Job	20	21	19	God shall lay up the sorrow of the father for his children: and when he shall repay, then shall he know.
Job	Job	20	21	20	His eyes shall see his own destruction, and he shall drink of the wrath of the Almighty.
Job	Job	20	21	21	For what is it to him what befalleth his house after him: and if the number of his months be diminished by one half?
Job	Job	20	21	22	Shall any one teach God knowledge, who judgeth those that are high?
Job	Job	20	21	23	One man dieth strong, and hale, rich and happy.
Job	Job	20	21	24	His bowels are full of fat, and his bones are moistened with marrow.
Job	Job	20	21	25	But another dieth in bitterness of soul without any riches:
Job	Job	20	21	26	And yet they shall sleep together in the dust, and worms shall cover them.
Job	Job	20	21	27	Surely I know your thoughts, and your unjust judgments against me.
Job	Job	20	21	28	For you say: Where is the house of the prince? and where are the dwelling places of the wicked?
Job	Job	20	21	29	Ask any one of them that go by the way, and you shall perceive that he knoweth these same things.
Job	Job	20	21	30	Because the wicked man is reserved to the day of destruction, and he shall be brought to the day of wrath.
Job	Job	20	21	31	Who shall reprove his way to his face? and who shall repay him what he hath done?
Job	Job	20	21	32	He shall be brought to the graves, and shall watch in the heap of the dead.
Job	Job	20	21	33	He hath been acceptable to the gravel of Cocytus, and he shall draw every man after him, and there are innumerable before him.
Job	Job	20	21	34	How then do ye comfort me in vain, whereas your answer is shewn to be repugnant to truth?
Job	Job	20	22	1	Then Eliphaz the Themanite answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	22	2	Can man be compared with God, even though he were of perfect knowledge?
Job	Job	20	22	3	What doth it profit God if thou be just? or what dost thou give him if thy way be unspotted?
Job	Job	20	22	4	Shall he reprove thee for fear, and come with thee into judgment:
Job	Job	20	22	5	And not for thy manifold wickedness, and thy infinite iniquities?
Job	Job	20	22	6	For thou hast taken away the pledge of thy brethren without cause, and stripped the naked of their clothing.
Job	Job	20	22	7	Thou hast not given water to the weary, thou hast withdrawn bread from the hungry.
Job	Job	20	22	8	In the strength of thy arm thou didst possess the land, and being the most mighty thou holdest it.
Job	Job	20	22	9	Thou hast sent widows away empty, and the arms of the fatherless thou hast broken in pieces.
Job	Job	20	22	10	Therefore art thou surrounded with snares, and sudden fear troubleth thee.
Job	Job	20	22	11	And didst thou think that thou shouldst not see darkness, and that thou shouldst not be covered with the violence of overflowing waters?
Job	Job	20	22	12	Dost not thou think that God is higher than heaven, and is elevated above the height of the stars?
Job	Job	20	22	13	And thou sayst: What doth God know? and he judgeth as it were through a mist.
Job	Job	20	22	14	The clouds are his covert, and he doth not consider our things, and he walketh about the poles of heaven.
Job	Job	20	22	15	Dost thou desire to keep the path of ages, which wicked men have trodden?
Job	Job	20	22	16	Who were taken away before their time, and a flood hath overthrown their foundation.
Job	Job	20	22	17	Who said to God: Depart from us: and looked upon the Almighty as if he could do nothing:
Job	Job	20	22	18	Whereas he had filled their houses with good things: whose way of thinking be far from me.
Job	Job	20	22	19	The just shall see, and shall rejoice, and the innocent shall laugh them to scorn.
Job	Job	20	22	20	Is not their exaltation cut down, and hath not fire devoured the remnants of them?
Job	Job	20	22	21	Submit thyself then to him, and be at peace: and thereby thou shalt have the best fruits.
Job	Job	20	22	22	Receive the law of his mouth, and lay up his words in thy heart.
Job	Job	20	22	23	If thou wilt return to the Almighty, thou shalt be built up, and shalt put away iniquity far from thy tabernacle.
Job	Job	20	22	24	He shall give for earth flint, and for flint torrents of gold.
Job	Job	20	22	25	And the Almighty shall be against thy enemies, and silver shall be heaped together for thee.
Job	Job	20	22	26	Then shalt thou abound in delights in the Almighty, and shalt lift up thy face to God.
Job	Job	20	22	27	Thou shalt pray to him, and he will hear thee, and thou shalt pay vows.
Job	Job	20	22	28	Thou shalt decree a thing, and it shall come to thee, and light shall shine in thy ways.
Job	Job	20	22	29	For he that hath been humbled, shall be in glory: and he that shall bow down his eyes, he shall be saved.
Job	Job	20	22	30	The innocent shall be saved, and he shall be saved by the cleanness of his hands.
Job	Job	20	23	1	Then Job answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	23	2	Now also my words are in bitterness, and the hand of my scourge is more grievous than my mourning.
Job	Job	20	23	3	Who will grant me that I might know and find him, and come even to his throne?
Job	Job	20	23	4	I would set judgment before him, and would fill my mouth with complaints.
Job	Job	20	23	5	That I might know the words that he would answer me, and understand what he would say to me.
Job	Job	20	23	6	I would not that he should contend with me with much strength, nor overwhelm me with the weight of his greatness.
Job	Job	20	23	7	Let him propose equity against me, and let my judgment come to victory.
Job	Job	20	23	8	But if I go to the east, he appeareth not; if to the west, I shall not understand him.
Job	Job	20	23	9	If to the left hand, what shall I do? I shall not take hold on him: if I turn myself to the right hand, I shall not see him.
Job	Job	20	23	10	But he knoweth my way, and has tried me as gold that passeth through the fire:
Job	Job	20	23	11	My foot hath followed his steps, I have kept his way, and have not declined from it.
Job	Job	20	23	12	I have not departed from the commandments of his lips, and the words of his mouth I have hid in my bosom.
Job	Job	20	23	13	For he is alone, and no man can turn away his thought: and whatsoever his soul hath desired, that hath he done.
Job	Job	20	23	14	And when he shall have fulfilled his will in me, many other like things are also at hand with him.
Job	Job	20	23	15	And therefore I am troubled at his presence, and when I consider him I am made pensive with fear.
Job	Job	20	23	16	God hath softened my heart, and the Almighty hath troubled me.
Job	Job	20	23	17	For I have not perished because of the darkness that hangs over me, neither hath the mist covered my face.
Job	Job	20	24	1	Times are not hid from the Almighty: but they that know him, know not his days.
Job	Job	20	24	2	Some have removed landmarks, have taken away flocks by force, and fed them.
Job	Job	20	24	3	They have driven away the ass of the fatherless, and have taken away the widow's ox for a pledge.
Job	Job	20	24	4	They have overturned the way of the poor, and have oppressed together the meek of the earth.
Job	Job	20	24	5	Others like wild asses in the desert go forth to their work: by watching for a prey they get bread for their children.
Job	Job	20	24	6	They reap the field that is not their own, and gather the vintage of his vineyard whom by violence they have oppressed.
Job	Job	20	24	7	They send men away naked, taking away their clothes who have no covering in the cold:
Job	Job	20	24	8	Who are wet, with the showers of the mountains, and having no covering embrace the stones.
Job	Job	20	24	9	They have violently robbed the fatherless, and stripped the poor common people.
Job	Job	20	24	10	From the naked and them that go without clothing, and from the hungry they have taken away the ears of corn.
Job	Job	20	24	11	They have taken their rest at noon among the stores of them, who after having trodden the winepresses suffer thirst.
Job	Job	20	24	12	Out of the cities they have made men to groan, and the soul of the wounded hath cried out, and God doth not suffer it to pass unrevenged.
Job	Job	20	24	13	They have been rebellious to the light, they have not known his ways, neither have they returned by his paths.
Job	Job	20	24	14	The murderer riseth at the very break of day, he killeth the needy, and the poor man: but in the night he will be as a thief.
Job	Job	20	24	15	The eye of the adulterer observeth darkness, saying: No eye shall see me: and he will cover his face.
Job	Job	20	24	16	He diggeth through houses in the dark, as in the day they had appointed for themselves, and they have not known the light.
Job	Job	20	24	17	If the morning suddenly appear, it is to them the shadow of death: and they walk in darkness as if it were in light.
Job	Job	20	24	18	He is light upon the face of the water: cursed be his portion on the earth, let him not walk by the way of the vineyards.
Job	Job	20	24	19	Let him pass from the snow waters to excessive heat, and his sin even to hell.
Job	Job	20	24	20	Let mercy forget him: may worms be his sweetness: let him be remembered no more, but be broken in pieces as an unfruitful tree.
Job	Job	20	24	21	For he hath fed the barren that beareth not, and to the widow he hath done no good.
Job	Job	20	24	22	He hath pulled down the strong by his might: and when he standeth up, he shall not trust to his life.
Job	Job	20	24	23	God hath given him place for penance, and he abuseth it unto pride: but his eyes are upon his ways.
Job	Job	20	24	24	They are lifted up for a little while and shall not stand, and shall be brought down as all things, and shall be taken away, and as the tops of the ears of corn they shall be broken.
Job	Job	20	24	25	And if it be not so, who can convince me that I have lied, and set my words before God?
Job	Job	20	25	1	Then Baldad the Suhite answered, and I said:
Job	Job	20	25	2	Power and terror are with him, who maketh peace in his high places.
Job	Job	20	25	3	Is there any numbering of his soldiers? and upon whom shall not his light arise?
Job	Job	20	25	4	Can man be justified compared with God, or he that is born of a woman appear clean?
Job	Job	20	25	5	Behold even the moon doth not shine, and the stars are not pure in his sight.
Job	Job	20	25	6	How much less man that is rottenness and the son of man who is a worm?
Job	Job	20	26	1	Then Job answered, and said:
Job	Job	20	26	2	Whose helper art thou? is it of him that is weak? and dost thou hold up the arm of him that has no strength?
Job	Job	20	26	3	To whom hast thou given counsel? perhaps to him that hath no wisdom, and thou hast shewn thy very great prudence.
Job	Job	20	26	4	Whom hast thou desired to teach? was it not him that made life?
Job	Job	20	26	5	Behold the giants groan under the waters, and they that dwell with them.
Job	Job	20	26	6	Hell is naked before him, and there is no covering for destruction.
Job	Job	20	26	7	He stretched out the north over the empty space, and hangeth the earth upon nothing.
Job	Job	20	26	8	He bindeth up the waters in his clouds, so that they break not out and fall down together.
Job	Job	20	26	9	He withholdeth the face of his throne, and spreadeth his cloud over it.
Job	Job	20	26	10	He hath set bounds about the waters, till light and darkness come to an end.
Job	Job	20	26	11	The pillars of heaven tremble, and dread at his beck.
Job	Job	20	26	12	By his power the seas are suddenly gathered together, and his wisdom has struck the proud one.
Job	Job	20	26	13	His spirit hath adorned the heavens, and his obstetric hand brought forth the winding serpent.
Job	Job	20	26	14	Lo, these things are said in part of his ways: and seeing we have heard scarce a little drop of his word, who shall be able to behold the thunder of his greatness?
Job	Job	20	27	1	Job also added, taking up his parable, and said:
Job	Job	20	27	2	As God liveth, who hath taken away my judgment, and the Almighty, who hath brought my soul to bitterness,
Job	Job	20	27	3	As long as breath remaineth in me, and the spirit of God in my nostrils,
Job	Job	20	27	4	My lips shall not speak iniquity, neither shall my tongue contrive lying.
Job	Job	20	27	5	God forbid that I should judge you to be just: till I die I will not depart from my innocence.
Job	Job	20	27	6	My justification, which I have begun to hold, I will not forsake: for my heart doth not reprehend me in all my life.
Job	Job	20	27	7	Let my enemy be as the ungodly, and my adversary as the wicked one.
Job	Job	20	27	8	For what is the hope of the hypocrite if through covetousness he take by violence, and God deliver not his soul?
Job	Job	20	27	9	Will God hear his cry, when distress shall come upon him?
Job	Job	20	27	10	Or can he delight himself in the Almighty, and call upon God at all times?
Job	Job	20	27	11	I will teach you by the hand of God, what the Almighty hath, and I will not conceal it.
Job	Job	20	27	12	Behold you all know it, and why do you speak vain things without cause?
Job	Job	20	27	13	This is the portion of a wicked man with God, and the inheritance of the violent, which they shall receive of the Almighty.
Job	Job	20	27	14	If his sons be multiplied, they shall be for the sword, and his grandsons shall not be filled with bread.
Job	Job	20	27	15	They that shall remain of him, shall be buried in death, and his widows shall not weep.
Job	Job	20	27	16	If he shall heap together silver as earth, and prepare raiment as clay,
Job	Job	20	27	17	He shall prepare indeed, but the just man shall be clothed with it: and the innocent shall divide the silver.
Job	Job	20	27	18	He hath built his house as a moth, and as a keeper he hath made a booth.
Job	Job	20	27	19	The rich man when he shall sleep shall take away nothing with him: he shall open his eyes and find nothing.
Job	Job	20	27	20	Poverty like water shall take hold on him, a tempest shall oppress him in the night.
Job	Job	20	27	21	A burning wind shall take him up, and carry him away, and as a whirlwind shall snatch him from his place.
Job	Job	20	27	22	And he shall cast upon him, and shall not spare: out of his hand he would willingly flee.
Job	Job	20	27	23	He shall clasp his hands upon him, and shall hiss at him, beholding his place.
Job	Job	20	28	1	Silver hath beginnings of its veins, and gold hath a place wherein it is melted.
Job	Job	20	28	2	Iron is taken out of the earth, and stone melted with heat is turned into brass.
Job	Job	20	28	3	He hath set a time for darkness, and the end of all things he considereth, the stone also that is in the dark and the shadow of death.
Job	Job	20	28	4	The flood divideth from the people that are on their journey, those whom the food of the needy man hath forgotten, and who cannot be come at.
Job	Job	20	28	5	The land, out of which bread grew in its place, hath been overturned with fire.
Job	Job	20	28	6	The stones of it are the place of sapphires, and the clods of it are gold.
Job	Job	20	28	7	The bird hath not known the path, neither hath the eye of the vulture beheld it.
Job	Job	20	28	8	The children of the merchants have not trodden it, neither hath the lioness passed by it.
Job	Job	20	28	9	He hath stretched forth his hand to the flint, he hath overturned mountains from the roots.
Job	Job	20	28	10	In the rocks he hath cut out rivers, and his eye hath seen every precious thing.
Job	Job	20	28	11	The depths also of rivers he hath searched, and hidden things he hath brought forth to light.
Job	Job	20	28	12	But where is wisdom to be found, and where is the place of understanding?
Job	Job	20	28	13	Man knoweth not the price thereof, neither is it found in the land of them that live in delights.
Job	Job	20	28	14	The depth saith: It is not in me: and the sea saith: It is not with me.
Job	Job	20	28	15	The finest gold shall not purchase it, neither shall silver be weighed in exchange for it.
Job	Job	20	28	16	It shall not be compared with the dyed colours of India, or with the most precious stone sardonyx, or the sapphire.
Job	Job	20	28	17	Gold or crystal cannot equal it, neither shall any vessels of gold be changed for it.
Job	Job	20	28	18	High and eminent things shall not be mentioned in comparison of it: but wisdom is drawn out of secret places.
Job	Job	20	28	19	The topaz of Ethiopia shall not be equal to it, neither shall it be compared to the cleanest dyeing.
Job	Job	20	28	20	Whence then cometh wisdom? and where is the place of understanding?
Job	Job	20	28	21	It is hid from the eyes of all living. and the fowls of the air know it not.
Job	Job	20	28	22	Destruction and death have said: With our ears we have heard the fame thereof.
Job	Job	20	28	23	God understandeth the way of it, and he knoweth the place thereof.
Job	Job	20	28	24	For he beholdeth the ends of the world: and looketh on all things that are under heaven.
Job	Job	20	28	25	Who made a weight for the winds and weighed the waters by measure.
Job	Job	20	28	26	When he gave a law for the rain, and a way for the sounding storms.
Job	Job	20	28	27	Then he saw it, and declared, and prepared, and searched it.
Job	Job	20	28	28	And he said to man: Behold the fear of the Lord, that is wisdom: and to depart from evil, is understanding.
Job	Job	20	29	1	Job also added, taking up his parable, and said:
Job	Job	20	29	2	Who will grant me, that I might be according to the months past, according to the days in which God kept me?
Job	Job	20	29	3	When his lamp shined over my head, and I walked by his light in darkness?
Job	Job	20	29	4	As I was in the days of my youth, when God was secretly in my tabernacle?
Job	Job	20	29	5	When the Almighty was with me: and my servants round about me?
Job	Job	20	29	6	When I washed my feet with butter, and the rock poured me out rivers of oil?
Job	Job	20	29	7	When I went out to the gate of the city, and in the street they prepared me a chair?
Job	Job	20	29	8	The young men saw me, and hid themselves: and the old men rose up and stood.
Job	Job	20	29	9	The princes ceased to speak, and laid the finger on their mouth.
Job	Job	20	29	10	The rulers held their peace, and their tongue cleaved to their throat.
Job	Job	20	29	11	The ear that heard me blessed me, and the eye that saw me gave witness to me:
Job	Job	20	29	12	Because I had delivered the poor man that cried out; and the fatherless that had no helper.
Job	Job	20	29	13	The blessing of him that was ready to perish came upon me, and I comforted the heart of the widow.
Job	Job	20	29	14	I was clad with justice: and I clothed myself with my judgment, as with a robe and a diadem.
Job	Job	20	29	15	I was an eye to the blind, and a foot to the lame.
Job	Job	20	29	16	I was the father of the poor: and the cause which I knew not, I searched out most diligently.
Job	Job	20	29	17	I broke the jaws of the wicked man, and out of his teeth I took away the prey.
Job	Job	20	29	18	And I said: I shall die in my nest, and as a palm tree shall multiply my days.
Job	Job	20	29	19	My root is opened beside the waters, and dew shall continue in my harvest.
Job	Job	20	29	20	My glory shall always be renewed, and my bow in my hand shall be repaired.
Job	Job	20	29	21	They that heard me, waited for my sentence, and being attentive held their peace at my counsel.
Job	Job	20	29	22	To my words they durst add nothing, and my speech dropped upon them.
Job	Job	20	29	23	They waited for me as for rain, and they opened their mouth as for a latter shower.
Job	Job	20	29	24	If at any time I laughed on them, they believed not, and the light of my countenance fell not on earth.
Job	Job	20	29	25	If I had a mind to go to them, I sat first, and when I sat as a king, with his army standing about him, yet I was a comforter of them that mourned.
Job	Job	20	30	1	But now the younger in time scorn me, whose fathers I would not have set with the dogs of my flock:
Job	Job	20	30	2	The strength of whose hands was to me as nothing, and they were thought unworthy of life itself.
Job	Job	20	30	3	Barren with want and hunger, who gnawed in the wilderness, disfigured with calamity and misery.
Job	Job	20	30	4	And they ate grass, and barks of trees, and the root of junipers was their food.
Job	Job	20	30	5	Who snatched up these things out of the valleys, and when they had found any of them, they ran to them with a cry.
Job	Job	20	30	6	They dwelt in the desert places of torrents, and in caves of earth, or upon the gravel.
Job	Job	20	30	7	They pleased themselves among these kind of things, and counted it delightful to be under the briers.
Job	Job	20	30	8	The children of foolish and base men, and not appearing at all upon the earth.
Job	Job	20	30	9	Now I am turned into their song, and am become their byword.
Job	Job	20	30	10	They abhor me, and flee far from me, and are not afraid to spit in my face.
Job	Job	20	30	11	For he hath opened his quiver, and hath afflicted me, and hath put a bridle into my mouth.
Job	Job	20	30	12	At the right hand of my rising, my calamities forthwith arose: they have overthrown my feet, and have overwhelmed me with their paths as with waves.
Job	Job	20	30	13	They have destroyed my ways, they have lain in wait against me, and they have prevailed, and there was none to help.
Job	Job	20	30	14	They have rushed in upon me, as when a wall is broken, and a gate opened, and have rolled themselves down to my miseries.
Job	Job	20	30	15	I am brought to nothing: as a wind thou hast taken away my desire: and my prosperity hath passed away like a cloud.
Job	Job	20	30	16	And now my soul fadeth within myself, and the days of affliction possess me.
Job	Job	20	30	17	In the night my bone is pierced with sorrows: and they that feed upon me, do not sleep.
Job	Job	20	30	18	With the multitude of them my garment is consumed, and they have girded me about, as with the collar of my coat.
Job	Job	20	30	19	I am compared to dirt, and am likened to embers and ashes.
Job	Job	20	30	20	I cry to thee, and thou hearest me not: I stand up, and thou dost not regard me.
Job	Job	20	30	21	Thou art changed to be cruel toward me, and in the hardness of thy hand thou art against me.
Job	Job	20	30	22	Thou hast lifted me up, and set me as it were upon the wind, and thou hast mightily dashed me.
Job	Job	20	30	23	I know that thou wilt deliver me to death, where a house is appointed for every one that liveth.
Job	Job	20	30	24	But yet thou stretchest not forth thy hand to their consumption: and if they shall fall down thou wilt save.
Job	Job	20	30	25	I wept heretofore for him that was afflicted, and my soul had compassion on the poor.
Job	Job	20	30	26	I expected good things, and evils are come upon me: I waited for light, and darkness broke out.
Job	Job	20	30	27	My inner parts have boiled without any rest, the days of affliction have prevented me.
Job	Job	20	30	28	I went mourning without indignation; I rose up, and cried in the crowd.
Job	Job	20	30	29	I was the brother of dragons, and companion of ostriches.
Job	Job	20	30	30	My skin is become black upon me, and my bones are dried up with heat.
Job	Job	20	30	31	My harp is turned to mourning, and my organ into the voice of those that weep.
Job	Job	20	31	1	I made a covenant with my eyes, that I would not so much as think upon a virgin.
Job	Job	20	31	2	For what part should God from above have in me, and what inheritance the Almighty from on high?
Job	Job	20	31	3	Is not destruction to the wicked, and aversion to them that work iniquity?
Job	Job	20	31	4	Doth not he consider my ways, and number all my steps?
Job	Job	20	31	5	If I have walked in vanity, and my foot hath made haste to deceit:
Job	Job	20	31	6	Let him weigh me in a just balance, and let God know my simplicity.
Job	Job	20	31	7	If my step hath turned out of the way, and if my heart hath followed my eyes, and if a spot hath cleaved to my hands:
Job	Job	20	31	8	Then let me sow and let another eat: and let my offspring be rooted out.
Job	Job	20	31	9	If my heart hath been deceived upon a woman, and if I have laid wait at my friend's door:
Job	Job	20	31	10	Let my wife be the harlot of another, and let other men lie with her.
Job	Job	20	31	11	For this is a heinous crime, and a most grievous iniquity.
Job	Job	20	31	12	It is a fire that devoureth even to destruction, and rooteth up all things that spring.
Job	Job	20	31	13	If I have despised to abide judgment with my manservant, or my maidservant, when they had any controversy against me:
Job	Job	20	31	14	For what shall I do when God shall rise to judge? and when he shall examine, what shall I answer him?
Job	Job	20	31	15	Did not he that made me in the womb make him also: and did not one and the same form me in the womb?
Job	Job	20	31	16	If I have denied to the poor what they desired, and have made the eyes of the widow wait:
Job	Job	20	31	17	If I have eaten my morsel alone, and the fatherless hath not eaten thereof:
Job	Job	20	31	18	(For from my infancy mercy grew up with me: and it came out with me from my mother's womb:)
Job	Job	20	31	19	If I have despised him that was perishing for want of clothing, and the poor man that had no covering:
Job	Job	20	31	20	If his sides have not blessed me, and if he were not warmed with the fleece of my sheep:
Job	Job	20	31	21	If I have lifted up my hand against the fatherless, even when I saw myself superior in the gate:
Job	Job	20	31	22	Let my shoulder fall from its joint, and let my arm with its bones be broken.
Job	Job	20	31	23	For I have always feared God as waves swelling over me, and his weight I was not able to bear.
Job	Job	20	31	24	If I have thought gold my strength, and have said to fine gold: My confidence:
Job	Job	20	31	25	If I have rejoiced over my great riches, and because my hand had gotten much.
Job	Job	20	31	26	If I beheld the sun when it shined, and the moon going in brightness:
Job	Job	20	31	27	And my heart in secret hath rejoiced, and I have kissed my hand with my mouth:
Job	Job	20	31	28	Which is a very great iniquity, and a denial against the most high God.
Job	Job	20	31	29	If I have been glad at the downfall of him that hated me, and have rejoiced that evil had found him.
Job	Job	20	31	30	For I have not given my mouth to sin, by wishing a curse to his soul.
Job	Job	20	31	31	If the men of my tabernacle have not said: Who will give us of his flesh that we may be filled?
Job	Job	20	31	32	The stranger did not stay without, my door was open to the traveller.
Job	Job	20	31	33	If as a man I have hid my sin, and have concealed my iniquity in my bosom.
Job	Job	20	31	34	If I have been afraid at a very great multitude, and the contempt of kinsmen hath terrified me: and I have not rather held my peace, and not gone out of the door.
Job	Job	20	31	35	Who would grant me a hearer, that the Almighty may hear my desire; and that he himself that judgeth would write a book,
Job	Job	20	31	36	That I may carry it on my shoulder, and put it about me as a crown?
Job	Job	20	31	37	At every step of mine I would pronounce it, and offer it as to a prince.
Job	Job	20	31	38	If my land cry against me, and with it the furrows thereof mourn:
Job	Job	20	31	39	If I have eaten the fruits thereof without money, and have afflicted the soul of the tillers thereof:
Job	Job	20	31	40	Let thistles grow up to me instead of wheat, and thorns instead of barley.
Job	Job	20	32	1	So these three men ceased to answer Job, because he seemed just to himself.
Job	Job	20	32	2	And Eliu the son of Barachel the Buzite, of the kindred of Ram, was angry and was moved to indignation: now he was angry against Job, because he said he was just before God.
Job	Job	20	32	3	And he was angry with his friends because they had not found a reasonable answer, but only had condemned Job.
Job	Job	20	32	4	So Eliu waited while Job was speaking, because they were his elders that were speaking.
Job	Job	20	32	5	But when he saw that the three were not able to answer, he was exceedingly angry.
Job	Job	20	32	6	Then Eliu the son of Barachel the Buzite answered and said: I am younger in days, and you are more ancient; therefore hanging down my head, I was afraid to shew you my opinion.
Job	Job	20	32	7	For I hoped that greater age would speak, and that a multitude of years would teach wisdom.
Job	Job	20	32	8	But, as I see, there is a spirit in men, and the inspiration of the Almighty giveth understanding.
Job	Job	20	32	9	They that are aged are not the wise men, neither do the ancients understand judgment.
Job	Job	20	32	10	Therefore I will speak: Hearken to me, I also will shew you my wisdom.
Job	Job	20	32	11	For I have waited for your words, I have given ear to your wisdom, as long as you were disputing in words.
Job	Job	20	32	12	And as long as I thought you said some thing, I considered: but, as I see, there is none of you that can convince Job, and answer his words.
Job	Job	20	32	13	Lest you should say: We have found wisdom, God hath cast him down, not man.
Job	Job	20	32	14	He hath spoken nothing to me, and I will not answer him according to your words.
Job	Job	20	32	15	They were afraid, and answered no more, and they left off speaking.
Job	Job	20	32	16	Therefore because I have waited, and they have not spoken: they stood, and answered no more:
Job	Job	20	32	17	I also will answer my part, and will shew my knowledge.
Job	Job	20	32	18	For I am full of matter to speak of, and the spirit of my bowels straiteneth me.
Job	Job	20	32	19	Behold, my belly is as new wine which wanteth vent, which bursteth the new vessels.
Job	Job	20	32	20	I will speak and take breath a little: I will open my lips, and will answer.
Job	Job	20	32	21	I will not accept the person of man, and I will not level God with man.
Job	Job	20	32	22	For I know not how long I shall continue, and whether after a while my Maker may take me away.
Job	Job	20	33	1	Hear therefore, O Job, my speeches, and hearken to all my words.
Job	Job	20	33	2	Behold now I have opened my mouth, let my tongue speak within my jaws.
Job	Job	20	33	3	My words are from my upright heart, and my lips shall speak a pure sentence.
Job	Job	20	33	4	The spirit of God made me, and the breath of the Almighty gave me life.
Job	Job	20	33	5	If thou canst, answer me, and stand up against my face.
Job	Job	20	33	6	Behold God hath made me as well as thee, and of the same clay I also was formed.
Job	Job	20	33	7	But yet let not my wonder terrify thee, and let not my eloquence be burdensome to thee.
Job	Job	20	33	8	Now thou has said in my hearing, and I have heard the voice of thy words:
Job	Job	20	33	9	I am clean, and without sin: I am unspotted, and there is no iniquity in me.
Job	Job	20	33	10	Because he hath found complaints against me, therefore he hath counted me for his enemy.
Job	Job	20	33	11	He hath put my feet in the stocks, he hath observed all my paths.
Job	Job	20	33	12	Now this is the thing in which thou art not justified: I will answer thee, that God is greater than man.
Job	Job	20	33	13	Dost thou strive against him, because he hath not answered thee to all words?
Job	Job	20	33	14	God speaketh once, and repeateth not the selfsame thing the second time.
Job	Job	20	33	15	By a dream in a vision by night, when deep sleep falleth upon men, and they are sleeping in their beds:
Job	Job	20	33	16	Then he openeth the ears of men, and teaching instructeth them in what they are to learn.
Job	Job	20	33	17	That he may withdraw a man from the things he is doing, and may deliver him from pride.
Job	Job	20	33	18	Rescuing his soul from corruption: and his life from passing to the sword.
Job	Job	20	33	19	He rebuketh also by sorrow in the bed, and he maketh all his bones to wither.
Job	Job	20	33	20	Bread becometh abominable to him in his life, and to his soul the meat which before he desired.
Job	Job	20	33	21	His flesh shall be consumed away, and his bones that were covered shall be made bare.
Job	Job	20	33	22	His soul hath drawn near to corruption, and his life to the destroyers.
Job	Job	20	33	23	If there shall be an angel speaking for him, one among thousands, to declare man's uprightness,
Job	Job	20	33	24	He shall have mercy on him, and shall say: Deliver him, that he may not go down to corruption: I have found wherein I may be merciful to him.
Job	Job	20	33	25	His flesh is consumed with punishment, let him return to the days of his youth.
Job	Job	20	33	26	He shall pray to God, and he will be gracious to him: and he shall see his face with joy, and he will render to man his justice.
Job	Job	20	33	27	He shall look upon men, and shall say: I have sinned, and indeed I have offended, and I have not received what I have deserved.
Job	Job	20	33	28	He hath delivered his soul from going into destruction, that it may live and see the light.
Job	Job	20	33	29	Behold, all these things God worketh three times within every one.
Job	Job	20	33	30	That he may withdraw their souls from corruption, and enlighten them with the light of the living.
Job	Job	20	33	31	Attend, Job, and hearken to me: and hold thy peace, whilst I speak.
Job	Job	20	33	32	But if thou hast any thing to say, answer me, speak: for I would have thee to appear just.
Job	Job	20	33	33	And if thou have not, hear me: hold thy peace, and I will teach thee wisdom.
Job	Job	20	34	1	And Eliu continued his discourse, and said:
Job	Job	20	34	2	Hear ye, wise men, my words, and ye learned, hearken to me:
Job	Job	20	34	3	For the ear trieth words, and the mouth discerneth meats by the taste.
Job	Job	20	34	4	Let us choose to us judgment, and let us see among ourselves what is the best.
Job	Job	20	34	5	For Job hath said: I am just, and God hath overthrown my judgment.
Job	Job	20	34	6	For in judging me there is a lie: my arrow is violent without any sin.
Job	Job	20	34	7	What man is there like Job, who drinketh up scorning like water?
Job	Job	20	34	8	Who goeth in company with them that work iniquity, and walketh with wicked men?
Job	Job	20	34	9	For he hath said: Man shall not please God, although he run with him.
Job	Job	20	34	10	Therefore, ye men of understanding, hear me: far from god be wickedness, and iniquity from the Almighty.
Job	Job	20	34	11	For he will render to a man his work, and according to the ways of every one he will reward them.
Job	Job	20	34	12	For in very deed God will not condemn without cause, neither will the Almighty pervert judgment.
Job	Job	20	34	13	What other hath he appointed over the earth? or whom hath he set over the world which he made?
Job	Job	20	34	14	If he turn his heart to him, he shall draw his spirit and breath unto himself.
Job	Job	20	34	15	All flesh shall perish together, and man shall return into ashes.
Job	Job	20	34	16	If then thou hast understanding, hear what is said, and hearken to the voice of my words.
Job	Job	20	34	17	Can he be healed that loveth not judgment? and how dost thou so far condemn him that is just?
Job	Job	20	34	18	Who saith to the king: Thou art an apostate: who calleth rulers ungodly?
Job	Job	20	34	19	Who accepteth not the persons of princes: nor hath regarded the tyrant, when he contended against the poor man: for all are the work of his hands.
Job	Job	20	34	20	They shall suddenly die, and the people shall be troubled at midnight, and they shall pass, and take away the violent without hand.
Job	Job	20	34	21	For his eyes are upon the ways of men, and he considereth all their steps.
Job	Job	20	34	22	There is no darkness, and there is no shadow of death, where they may be hid who work iniquity.
Job	Job	20	34	23	For it is no longer in the power of man to enter into judgment with God.
Job	Job	20	34	24	He shall break in pieces many and innumerable, and shall make others to stand in their stead.
Job	Job	20	34	25	For he knoweth their works: and therefore he shall bring night on them, and they shall be destroyed.
Job	Job	20	34	26	He hath struck them, as being wicked, in open sight.
Job	Job	20	34	27	Who as it were on purpose have revolted from him, and would not understand all his ways:
Job	Job	20	34	28	So that they caused the cry of the needy to come to him, and he heard the voice of the poor.
Job	Job	20	34	29	For when he granteth peace, who is there that can condemn? When he hideth his countenance, who is there that can behold him, whether it regard nations, or all men?
Job	Job	20	34	30	Who maketh a man that is a hypocrite to reign for the sins of the people?
Job	Job	20	34	31	Seeing then I have spoken of God, I will not hinder thee in thy turn.
Job	Job	20	34	32	If I have erred, teach thou me: if I have spoken iniquity, I will add no more.
Job	Job	20	34	33	Doth God require it of thee, because it hath displeased thee? for thou begannest to speak, and not I: but if thou know any thing better, speak.
Job	Job	20	34	34	Let men of understanding speak to me, and let a wise man hearken to me.
Job	Job	20	34	35	But Job hath spoken foolishly, and his words sound not discipline.
Job	Job	20	34	36	My father, let Job be tried even to the end: cease not from the man of iniquity.
Job	Job	20	34	37	Because he addeth blasphemy upon his sins, let him be tied fast in the mean time amongst us: and then let him provoke God to judgment with his speeches.
Job	Job	20	35	1	Moreover Eliu spoke these words:
Job	Job	20	35	2	Doth thy thought seem right to thee, that thou shouldst say: I am more just than God?
Job	Job	20	35	3	For thou saidst: That which is right doth not please thee: or what will it profit thee if I sin?
Job	Job	20	35	4	Therefore I will answer thy words, and thy friends with thee.
Job	Job	20	35	5	Look up to heaven and see, and behold the sky, that it is higher than thee.
Job	Job	20	35	6	If thou sin, what shalt thou hurt him? and if thy iniquities be multiplied, what shalt thou do against him?
Job	Job	20	35	7	And if thou do justly, what shalt thou give him, or what shall he receive of thy hand?
Job	Job	20	35	8	Thy wickedness may hurt a man that is like thee: and thy justice may help the son of man.
Job	Job	20	35	9	By reason of the multitude of oppressions they shall cry out: and shall wail for the violence of the arm of tyrants.
Job	Job	20	35	10	And he hath not said: Where is God, who made me, who hath given songs in the night?
Job	Job	20	35	11	Who teacheth us more than the beasts of the earth, and instructeth us more than the fowls of the air.
Job	Job	20	35	12	There shall they cry, and he will not hear, because of the pride of evil men.
Job	Job	20	35	13	God therefore will not hear in vain, and the Almighty will look into the causes of every one.
Job	Job	20	35	14	Yea when thou shalt say: He considereth not: be judged before him, and expect him.
Job	Job	20	35	15	For he doth not now bring on his fury, neither doth he revenge wickedness exceedingly.
Job	Job	20	35	16	Therefore Job openeth his mouth in vain, and multiplieth words without knowledge.
Job	Job	20	36	1	Eliu also proceeded, and said:
Job	Job	20	36	2	Suffer me a little, and I will shew thee: for I have yet somewhat to speak in God's behalf.
Job	Job	20	36	3	I will repeat my knowledge from the beginning, and I will prove my Maker just.
Job	Job	20	36	4	For indeed my words are without a lie, and perfect knowledge shall be proved to thee.
Job	Job	20	36	5	God doth not cast away the mighty, whereas he himself also is mighty.
Job	Job	20	36	6	But he saveth not the wicked, and he giveth judgment to the poor.
Job	Job	20	36	7	He will not take away his eyes from the just, and he placeth kings on the throne for ever, and they are exalted.
Job	Job	20	36	8	And if they shall be in chains, and be bound with the cords of poverty:
Job	Job	20	36	9	He shall shew them their works, and their wicked deeds, because they have been violent.
Job	Job	20	36	10	He also shall open their ear, to correct them: and shall speak, that they may return from iniquity.
Job	Job	20	36	11	If they shall hear and observe, they shall accomplish their days in good, and their years in glory.
Job	Job	20	36	12	But if they hear not, they shall pass by the sword, and shall be consumed in folly.
Job	Job	20	36	13	Dissemblers and crafty men prove the wrath of God, neither shall they cry when they are bound.
Job	Job	20	36	14	Their soul shall die in a storm, and their life among the effeminate.
Job	Job	20	36	15	He shall deliver the poor out of his distress, and shall open his ear in affliction.
Job	Job	20	36	16	Therefore he shall set thee at large out of the narrow mouth, and which hath no foundation under it: and the rest of thy table shall be full of fatness.
Job	Job	20	36	17	Thy cause hath been judged as that of the wicked, cause and judgment thou shalt recover.
Job	Job	20	36	18	Therefore let not anger overcome thee to oppress any man: neither let multitude of gifts turn thee aside.
Job	Job	20	36	19	Lay down thy greatness without tribulation, and all the mighty of strength.
Job	Job	20	36	20	Prolong not the night that people may come up for them.
Job	Job	20	36	21	Beware thou turn not aside to iniquity: for this thou hast begun to follow after misery.
Job	Job	20	36	22	Behold, God is high in his strength, and none is like him among the lawgivers.
Job	Job	20	36	23	Who can search out his ways? or who can say to him: Thou has wrought iniquity?
Job	Job	20	36	24	Remember that thou knowest not his work, concerning which men have sung.
Job	Job	20	36	25	All men see him, every one beholdeth afar off.
Job	Job	20	36	26	Behold, God is great, exceeding our knowledge: the number of his years is inestimable.
Job	Job	20	36	27	He lifteth up the drops of rain, and poureth out showers like floods:
Job	Job	20	36	28	Which flow from the clouds that cover all above.
Job	Job	20	36	29	If he will spread out clouds as his tent,
Job	Job	20	36	30	And lighten with his light from above, he shall cover also the ends of the sea.
Job	Job	20	36	31	For by these he judgeth people, and giveth food to many mortals.
Job	Job	20	36	32	In his hands he hideth the light, and commandeth it to come again.
Job	Job	20	36	33	He sheweth his friend concerning it, that it is his possession, and that he may come up to it.
Job	Job	20	37	1	At this my heart trembleth, and is moved out of its place.
Job	Job	20	37	2	Hear ye attentively the terror of his voice, and the sound that cometh out of his mouth.
Job	Job	20	37	3	He beholdeth under all the heavens, and his light is upon the ends of the earth.
Job	Job	20	37	4	After it a noise shall roar, he shall thunder with the voice of his majesty, and shall not be found out, when his voice shall be heard.
Job	Job	20	37	5	God shall thunder wonderfully with his voice, he that doth great and unsearchable things.
Job	Job	20	37	6	He commandeth the snow to go down upon the earth, and the winter rain, and the shower of his strength.
Job	Job	20	37	7	He sealeth up the hand of all men, that every one may know his works.
Job	Job	20	37	8	Then the beast shall go into his covert, and shall abide in his den.
Job	Job	20	37	9	Out of the inner parts shall a tempest come, and cold out of the north.
Job	Job	20	37	10	When God bloweth there cometh frost, and again the waters are poured out abundantly.
Job	Job	20	37	11	Corn desireth clouds, and the clouds spread their light:
Job	Job	20	37	12	Which go round about, whithersoever the will of him that governeth them shall lead them, to whatsoever he shall command them upon the face of the whole earth:
Job	Job	20	37	13	Whether in one tribe, or in his own land, or in what place soever of his mercy he shall command them to be found.
Job	Job	20	37	14	Hearken to these things, Job: Stand, and consider the wondrous works of God.
Job	Job	20	37	15	Dost thou know when God commanded the rains, to shew his light of his clouds?
Job	Job	20	37	16	Knowest thou the great paths of the clouds, and the perfect knowledges?
Job	Job	20	37	17	Are not thy garments hot, when the south wind blows upon the earth?
Job	Job	20	37	18	Thou perhaps hast made the heavens with him, which are most strong, as if they were of molten brass.
Job	Job	20	37	19	shew us what we may say to him: for we are wrapped up in darkness.
Job	Job	20	37	20	Who shall tell him the things I speak? even if a man shall speak, he shall be swallowed up.
Job	Job	20	37	21	But now they see not the light: the air on a sudden shall be thickened into clouds, and the wind shall pass and drive them away.
Job	Job	20	37	22	Cold cometh out of the north, and to God praise with fear.
Job	Job	20	37	23	We cannot find him worthily: he is great in strength, and in judgment, and in justice, and he is ineffable.
Job	Job	20	37	24	Therefore men shall fear him, and all that seem to themselves to be wise, shall not dare to behold him.
Job	Job	20	38	1	Then the Lord answered Job out of a whirlwind, and said:
Job	Job	20	38	2	Who is this that wrappeth up sentences in unskillful words?
Job	Job	20	38	3	Gird up thy loins like a man: I will ask thee, and answer thou me.
Job	Job	20	38	4	Where wast thou when I laid up the foundations of the earth? tell me if thou hast understanding.
Job	Job	20	38	5	Who hath laid the measures thereof, if thou knowest? or who hath stretched the line upon it?
Job	Job	20	38	6	Upon what are its bases grounded? or who laid the corner stone thereof,
Job	Job	20	38	7	When the morning stars praised me together, and all the sons of God made a joyful melody?
Job	Job	20	38	8	Who shut up the sea with doors, when it broke forth as issuing out of the womb:
Job	Job	20	38	9	When I made a cloud the garment thereof, and wrapped it in a mist as in swaddling bands?
Job	Job	20	38	10	I set my bounds around it, and made it bars and doors:
Job	Job	20	38	11	And I said: Hitherto thou shalt come, and shalt go no further, and here thou shalt break thy swelling waves.
Job	Job	20	38	12	Didst thou since thy birth command the morning, and shew the dawning of the day its place?
Job	Job	20	38	13	And didst thou hold the extremities of the earth shaking them, and hast thou shaken the ungodly out of it?
Job	Job	20	38	14	The seal shall be restored as clay, and shall stand as a garment:
Job	Job	20	38	15	From the wicked their light shall be taken away, and the high arm shall be broken.
Job	Job	20	38	16	Hast thou entered into the depths of the sea, and walked in the lowest parts of the deep?
Job	Job	20	38	17	Have the gates of death been opened to thee, and hast thou seen the darksome doors?
Job	Job	20	38	18	Hast thou considered the breadth of the earth? tell me, if thou knowest all things?
Job	Job	20	38	19	Where is the way where light dwelleth, and where is the place of darkness:
Job	Job	20	38	20	That thou mayst bring every thing to its own bounds, and understand the paths of the house thereof.
Job	Job	20	38	21	Didst thou know then that thou shouldst be born? and didst thou know the number of thy days?
Job	Job	20	38	22	Hast thou entered into the storehouses of the snow, or has thou beheld the treasures of the hail:
Job	Job	20	38	23	Which I have prepared for the time of the enemy, against the day of battle and war?
Job	Job	20	38	24	By what way is the light spread, and heat divided upon the earth?
Job	Job	20	38	25	Who gave a course to violent showers, or a way for noisy thunder:
Job	Job	20	38	26	That it should rain on the earth without man in the wilderness, where no mortal dwelleth:
Job	Job	20	38	27	That it should fill the desert and desolate land, and should bring forth green grass?
Job	Job	20	38	28	Who is the father of rain? or who begot the drops of dew?
Job	Job	20	38	29	Out of whose womb came the ice; and the frost from heaven who hath gendered it?
Job	Job	20	38	30	The waters are hardened like a stone, and the surface of the deep is congealed.
Job	Job	20	38	31	Shalt thou be able to join together the shining stars the Pleiades, or canst thou stop the turning about of Arcturus?
Job	Job	20	38	32	Canst thou bring forth the day star in its time, and make the evening star to rise upon the children of the earth?
Job	Job	20	38	33	Dost thou know the order of heaven, and canst thou set down the reason thereof on the earth?
Job	Job	20	38	34	Canst thou lift up thy voice to the clouds, that an abundance of waters may cover thee?
Job	Job	20	38	35	Canst thou send lightnings, and will they go, and will they return and say to thee: Here we are?
Job	Job	20	38	36	Who hath put wisdom in the heart of man? or who gave the cock understanding?
Job	Job	20	38	37	Who can declare the order of the heavens, or who can make the harmony of heaven to sleep?
Job	Job	20	38	38	When was the dust poured on the earth, and the clods fastened together?
Job	Job	20	38	39	Wilt thou take the prey for the lioness, and satisfy the appetite of her whelps,
Job	Job	20	38	40	When they couch in the dens and lie in wait in holes?
Job	Job	20	38	41	Who provideth food for the raven, when her young ones cry to God, wandering about, because they have no meat?
Job	Job	20	39	1	Knowest thou the time when the wild goats bring forth among the rocks, or hast thou observed the hinds when they fawn?
Job	Job	20	39	2	Hast thou numbered the months of their conceiving, or knowest thou the time when they bring forth?
Job	Job	20	39	3	They bow themselves to bring forth young, and they cast them, and send forth roarings.
Job	Job	20	39	4	Their young are weaned and go to feed: they go forth, and return not to them.
Job	Job	20	39	5	Who hath sent out the wild ass free, and who hath loosed his bonds?
Job	Job	20	39	6	To whom I have given a house in the wilderness, and his dwellings in the barren land.
Job	Job	20	39	7	He scorneth the multitude of the city, he heareth not the cry of the driver.
Job	Job	20	39	8	He looketh round about the mountains of his pasture, and seeketh for every green thing.
Job	Job	20	39	9	Shall the rhinoceros be willing to serve thee, or will he stay at thy crib?
Job	Job	20	39	10	Canst thou bind the rhinoceros with thy thong to plough, or will he break the clods of the valleys after thee?
Job	Job	20	39	11	Wilt thou have confidence in his great strength, and leave thy labours to him?
Job	Job	20	39	12	Wilt thou trust him that he will render thee the seed, and gather it into thy barnfloor?
Job	Job	20	39	13	The wing of the ostrich is like the wings of the heron, and of the hawk.
Job	Job	20	39	14	When she leaveth her eggs on the earth, thou perhaps wilt warm them in the dust.
Job	Job	20	39	15	She forgetteth that the foot may tread upon them, or that the beasts of the field may break them.
Job	Job	20	39	16	She is hardened against her young ones, as though they were not hers, she hath laboured in vain, no fear constraining her.
Job	Job	20	39	17	For God hath deprived her of wisdom, neither hath he given her understanding.
Job	Job	20	39	18	When time shall be, she setteth up her wings on high: she scorneth the horse and his rider.
Job	Job	20	39	19	Wilt thou give strength to the horse, or clothe his neck with neighing?
Job	Job	20	39	20	Wilt thou lift him up like the locusts? the glory of his nostrils is terror.
Job	Job	20	39	21	He breaketh up the earth with his hoof, he pranceth boldly, he goeth forward to meet armed men.
Job	Job	20	39	22	He despiseth fear, he turneth not his back to the sword,
Job	Job	20	39	23	Above him shall the quiver rattle, the spear and shield shall glitter.
Job	Job	20	39	24	Chasing and raging he swalloweth the ground, neither doth he make account when the noise of the trumpet soundeth.
Job	Job	20	39	25	When he heareth the trumpet he saith: Ha, ha: he smelleth the battle afar off, the encouraging of the captains, and the shouting of the army.
Job	Job	20	39	26	Doth the hawk wax feathered by thy wisdom, spreading her wings to the south?
Job	Job	20	39	27	Will the eagle mount up at thy command, and make her nest in high places?
Job	Job	20	39	28	She abideth among the rocks, and dwelleth among cragged flints, and stony hills, where there is no access.
Job	Job	20	39	29	From thence she looketh for the prey, and her eyes behold afar off.
Job	Job	20	39	30	Her young ones shall suck up blood: and wheresoever the carcass shall be, she is immediately there.
Job	Job	20	39	31	And the Lord went on, and said to Job:
Job	Job	20	39	32	Shall he that contendeth with God be so easily silenced? surely he that reproveth God, ought to answer him.
Job	Job	20	39	33	Then Job answered the Lord, and said:
Job	Job	20	39	34	What can I answer, who hath spoken inconsiderately? I will lay my hand upon my mouth.
Job	Job	20	39	35	One thing I have spoken, which I wish I had not said: and another, to which I will add no more.
Job	Job	20	40	1	And the Lord answering Job out of the whirlwind, said:
Job	Job	20	40	2	Gird up thy loins like a man: I will ask thee, and do thou tell me.
Job	Job	20	40	3	Wilt thou make void my judgment: and condemn me, that thou mayst be justified?
Job	Job	20	40	4	And hast thou an arm like God, and canst thou thunder with a voice like him?
Job	Job	20	40	5	Clothe thyself with beauty, and set thyself up on high and be glorious, and put on goodly garments.
Job	Job	20	40	6	Scatter the proud in thy indignation, and behold every arrogant man, and humble him.
Job	Job	20	40	7	Look on all that are proud, and confound them, and crush the wicked in their place.
Job	Job	20	40	8	Hide them in the dust together, and plunge their faces into the pit.
Job	Job	20	40	9	Then I will confess that thy right hand is able to save thee.
Job	Job	20	40	10	Behold behemoth whom I made with thee, he eateth grass like an ox.
Job	Job	20	40	11	His strength is in his loins, and his force in the navel of his belly.
Job	Job	20	40	12	He setteth up his tail like a cedar, the sinews of his testicles are wrapped together.
Job	Job	20	40	13	His bones are like pipes of brass, his gristle like plates of iron.
Job	Job	20	40	14	He is the beginning of the ways of God, who made him, he will apply his sword.
Job	Job	20	40	15	To him the mountains bring forth grass: there all the beasts of the field shall play.
Job	Job	20	40	16	He sleepeth under the shadow, in the covert of the reed, and in moist places.
Job	Job	20	40	17	The shades cover his shadow, the willows of the brook shall compass him about.
Job	Job	20	40	18	Behold, he will drink up a river, and not wonder: and he trusteth that the Jordan may run into his mouth.
Job	Job	20	40	19	In his eyes as with a hook he shall take him, and bore through his nostrils with stakes.
Job	Job	20	40	20	Canst thou draw out the leviathan with a hook, or canst thou tie his tongue with a cord?
Job	Job	20	40	21	Canst thou put a ring in his nose, or bore through his jaw with a buckle?
Job	Job	20	40	22	Will he make many supplications to thee, or speak soft words to thee?
Job	Job	20	40	23	Will he make a covenant with thee, and wilt thou take him to be a servant for ever?
Job	Job	20	40	24	Shalt thou play with him as with a bird, or tie him up for thy handmaids?
Job	Job	20	40	25	Shall friends cut him in pieces, shall merchants divide him?
Job	Job	20	40	26	Wilt thou fill nets with his skin, and the cabins of fishes with his head?
Job	Job	20	40	27	Lay thy hand upon him: remember the battle, and speak no more.
Job	Job	20	40	28	Behold his hope shall fail him, and in the sight of all he shall be cast down.
Job	Job	20	41	1	I will not stir him up, like one that is cruel: for who can resist my countenance?
Job	Job	20	41	2	Who hath given me before that I should repay him? All things that are under heaven are mine.
Job	Job	20	41	3	I will not spare him, nor his mighty words, and framed to make supplication.
Job	Job	20	41	4	Who can discover the face of his garment? or who can go into the midst of his mouth?
Job	Job	20	41	5	Who can open the doors of his face? his teeth are terrible round about.
Job	Job	20	41	6	His body is like molten shields, shut close up with scales pressing upon one another.
Job	Job	20	41	7	One is joined to another, and not so much as any air can come between them:
Job	Job	20	41	8	They stick one to another and they hold one another fast, and shall not be separated.
Job	Job	20	41	9	His sneezing is like the shining of fire, and his eyes like the eyelids of the morning.
Job	Job	20	41	10	Out of his mouth go forth lamps, like torches of lighted fire.
Job	Job	20	41	11	Out of his nostrils goeth smoke, like that of a pot heated and boiling.
Job	Job	20	41	12	His breath kindleth coals, and a flame cometh forth out of his mouth.
Job	Job	20	41	13	In his neck strength shall dwell, and want goeth before his face.
Job	Job	20	41	14	The members of his flesh cleave one to another: he shall send lightnings against him, and they shall not be carried to another place.
Job	Job	20	41	15	His heart shall be as hard as a stone, and as firm as a smith's anvil.
Job	Job	20	41	16	When he shall raise him up, the angels shall fear, and being affrighted shall purify themselves.
Job	Job	20	41	17	When a sword shall lay at him, it shall not be able to hold, nor a spear, nor a breastplate.
Job	Job	20	41	18	For he shall esteem iron as straw, and brass as rotten wood.
Job	Job	20	41	19	The archer shall not put him to flight, the stones of the sling are to him like stubble.
Job	Job	20	41	20	As stubble will he esteem the hammer, and he will laugh him to scorn who shaketh the spear.
Job	Job	20	41	21	The beams of the sun shall be under him, and he shall strew gold under him like mire.
Job	Job	20	41	22	He shall make the deep sea to boil like a pot, and shall make it as when ointments boil.
Job	Job	20	41	23	A path shall shine after him, he shall esteem the deep as growing old.
Job	Job	20	41	24	There is no power upon earth that can be compared with him who was made to fear no one.
Job	Job	20	41	25	He beholdeth every high thing, he is king over all the children of pride.
Job	Job	20	42	1	Then Job answered the Lord, and said:
Job	Job	20	42	2	I know that thou canst do all things, and no thought is hid from thee.
Job	Job	20	42	3	Who is this that hideth counsel without knowledge? Therefore I have spoken unwisely, and things that above measure exceeded my knowledge.
Job	Job	20	42	4	Hear, and I will speak: I will ask thee, and do thou tell me.
Job	Job	20	42	5	With the hearing of the ear, I have heard thee, but now my eye seeth thee.
Job	Job	20	42	6	Therefore I reprehend myself, and do penance in dust and ashes.
Job	Job	20	42	7	And after the Lord had spoken these words to Job, he said to Eliphaz the Themanite: My wrath is kindled against thee, and against thy two friends, because you have not spoken the thing that is right before me, as my servant Job hath.
Job	Job	20	42	8	Take unto you therefore seven oxen, and seven rams, and go to my servant Job, and offer for yourselves a holocaust: and my servant Job shall pray for you: his face I will accept, that folly be not imputed to you: for you have not spoken right things before me, as my servant Job hath.
Job	Job	20	42	9	So Eliphaz the Themanite, and Baldad the Suhite, and Sophar the Naamathite went, and did as the Lord had spoken to them, and the Lord accepted the face of Job.
Job	Job	20	42	10	The Lord also was turned at the penance of Job, when he prayed for his friends. And the Lord gave Job twice as much as he had before.
Job	Job	20	42	11	And all his brethren came to him, and all his sisters, and all that knew him before, and they ate bread with him in his house: and bemoaned him, and comforted him upon all the evil that God had brought upon him. And every man gave him one ewe, and one earring of gold.
Job	Job	20	42	12	And the Lord blessed the latter end of Job more than his beginning. And he had fourteen thousand sheep, and six thousand camels, and a thousand yoke of oxen, and a thousand she asses.
Job	Job	20	42	13	And he had seven sons, and three daughters.
Job	Job	20	42	14	And he called the names of one Dies, and the name of the second Cassia, and the name of the third Cornustibil.
Job	Job	20	42	15	And there were not found in all the earth women so beautiful as the daughters of Job: and their father gave them inheritance among their brethren.
Job	Job	20	42	16	And Job lived after these things, a hundred and forty years, and he saw his children, and his children's children, unto the fourth generation, and he died an old man, and full of days.
Psalms	Ps	21	1	1	Blessed is the man who hath not walked in the counsel of the ungodly, nor stood in the way of sinners, nor sat in the chair of pestilence.
Psalms	Ps	21	1	2	But his will is in the law of the Lord, and on his law he shall meditate day and night.
Psalms	Ps	21	1	3	And he shall be like a tree which is planted near the running waters, which shall bring forth its fruit, in due season. And his leaf shall not fall off: and all whatsoever he shall do shall prosper.
Psalms	Ps	21	1	4	Not so the wicked, not so: but like the dust, which the wind driveth from the face of the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	1	5	Therefore the wicked shall not rise again in judgment: nor sinners in the council of the just.
Psalms	Ps	21	1	6	For the Lord knoweth the way of the just: and the way of the wicked shall perish.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	1	Why have the Gentiles raged, and the people devised vain things?
Psalms	Ps	21	2	2	The kings of the earth stood up, and the princes met together, against the Lord and against his Christ.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	3	Let us break their bonds asunder: and let us cast away their yoke from us.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	4	He that dwelleth in heaven shall laugh at them: and the Lord shall deride them.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	5	Then shall he speak to them in his anger, and trouble them in his rage.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	6	But I am appointed king by him over Sion his holy mountain, preaching his commandment.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	7	The Lord hath said to me: Thou art my son, this day have I begotten thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	8	Ask of me, and I will give thee the Gentiles for thy inheritance, and the utmost parts of the earth for thy possession.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	9	Thou shalt rule them with a rod of iron, and shalt break them in pieces like a potter's vessel.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	10	And now, O ye kings, understand: receive instruction, you that judge the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	11	Serve ye the Lord with fear: and rejoice unto him with trembling.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	12	Embrace discipline, lest at any time the Lord be angry, and you perish from the just way.
Psalms	Ps	21	2	13	When his wrath shall be kindled in a short time, blessed are all they that trust in him.
Psalms	Ps	21	3	1	[The psalm of David when he fled from the face of his son Absalom.]
Psalms	Ps	21	3	2	Why, O Lord, are they multiplied that afflict me? Many are they who rise up against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	3	3	Many say to my soul: There is no salvation for him in his God.
Psalms	Ps	21	3	4	But thou, O Lord art my protector, my glory, and the lifter up of my head.
Psalms	Ps	21	3	5	I have cried to the Lord with my voice: and he hath heard me from his holy hill.
Psalms	Ps	21	3	6	I have slept and taken my rest: and I have risen up, because the Lord hath protected me.
Psalms	Ps	21	3	7	I will not fear thousands of the people, surrounding me: arise, O Lord; save me, O my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	3	8	For thou hast struck all them who are my adversaries without cause: thou hast broken the teeth of sinners.
Psalms	Ps	21	3	9	Salvation is of the Lord: and thy blessing is upon thy people.
Psalms	Ps	21	4	1	[Unto the end, in verses. A psalm for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	4	2	When I called upon him, the God of my justice heard me: when I was in distress, thou hast enlarged me. Have mercy on me: and hear my prayer.
Psalms	Ps	21	4	3	O ye sons of men, how long will you be dull of heart? why do you love vanity, and seek after lying?
Psalms	Ps	21	4	4	Know ye also that the Lord hath made his holy one wonderful: the Lord will hear me when I shall cry unto him.
Psalms	Ps	21	4	5	Be angry, and sin not: the things you say in your hearts, be sorry for them upon your beds.
Psalms	Ps	21	4	6	Offer up the sacrifice of justice, and trust in the Lord: many say, Who sheweth us good things?
Psalms	Ps	21	4	7	The light of thy countenance O Lord, is signed upon us: thou hast given gladness in my heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	4	8	By the fruit of their corn, their wine and oil, they are multiplied.
Psalms	Ps	21	4	9	In peace in the selfsame I will sleep, and I will rest:
Psalms	Ps	21	4	10	For thou, O Lord, singularly hast settled me in hope.
Psalms	Ps	21	5	1	[Unto the end, for her that obtaineth the inheritance. A psalm of David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	5	2	Give ear, O Lord, to my words, understand my cry.
Psalms	Ps	21	5	3	Hearken to the voice of my prayer, O my King and my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	5	4	For to thee will I pray: O Lord, in the morning thou shalt hear my voice.
Psalms	Ps	21	5	5	In the morning I will stand before thee, and will see: because thou art not a God that willest iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	5	6	Neither shall the wicked dwell near thee: nor shall the unjust abide before thy eyes.
Psalms	Ps	21	5	7	Thou hatest all the workers of iniquity: Thou wilt destroy all that speak a lie. The bloody and the deceitful man the Lord will abhor.
Psalms	Ps	21	5	8	But as for me in the multitude of thy mercy, I will come into thy house; I will worship towards thy holy temple, in thy fear.
Psalms	Ps	21	5	9	Conduct me, O Lord, in thy justice: because of my enemies, direct my way in thy sight.
Psalms	Ps	21	5	10	For there is no truth in their mouth; their heart is vain.
Psalms	Ps	21	5	11	Their throat is an open sepulchre: they dealt deceitfully with their tongues: judge them, O God. Let them fall from their devices: according to the multitude of their wickedness cast them out: for they have provoked thee, O Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	5	12	But let all them be glad that hope in thee: they shall rejoice for ever, and thou shalt dwell in them. And all they that love thy name shall glory in thee:
Psalms	Ps	21	5	13	For thou wilt bless the just. O Lord, thou hast crowned us, as with a shield of thy good will.
Psalms	Ps	21	6	1	[Unto the end, in verses, a psalm for David, for the octave.]
Psalms	Ps	21	6	2	O Lord, rebuke me not in thy indignation, nor chastise me in thy wrath.
Psalms	Ps	21	6	3	Have mercy on me, O Lord, for I am weak: heal me, O Lord, for my bones are troubled.
Psalms	Ps	21	6	4	And my soul is troubled exceedingly: but thou, O Lord, how long?
Psalms	Ps	21	6	5	Turn to me, O Lord, and deliver my soul: O save me for thy mercy's sake.
Psalms	Ps	21	6	6	For there is no one in death, that is mindful of thee: and who shall confess to thee in hell?
Psalms	Ps	21	6	7	I have laboured in my groanings, every night I will wash my bed: I will water my couch with my tears.
Psalms	Ps	21	6	8	My eye is troubled through indignation: I have grown old amongst all my enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	6	9	Depart from me, all ye workers of iniquity: for the Lord hath heard the voice of my weeping.
Psalms	Ps	21	6	10	The Lord hath heard my supplication: the Lord hath received my prayer.
Psalms	Ps	21	6	11	Let all my enemies be ashamed, and be very much troubled: let them be turned back, and be ashamed very speedily.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	1	[The psalm of David which he sung to the Lord for the words of Chusi the son of Jemini.]
Psalms	Ps	21	7	2	O Lord my God, in thee have I put my trust: save me from all them that persecute me, and deliver me.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	3	Lest at any time he seize upon my soul like a lion, while there is no one to redeem me, nor to save.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	4	O Lord my God, if I have done this thing, if there be iniquity in my hands:
Psalms	Ps	21	7	5	If I have rendered to them that repaid me evils, let me deservedly fall empty before my enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	6	Let the enemy pursue my soul, and take it, and tread down my life on the earth, and bring down my glory to the dust.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	7	Rise up, O Lord, in thy anger: and be thou exalted in the borders of my enemies. And arise, O Lord my God, in the precept which thou hast commanded:
Psalms	Ps	21	7	8	And a congregation of people shall surround thee. And for their sakes return thou on high.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	9	The Lord judgeth the people. Judge me, O Lord, according to my justice, and according to my innocence in me.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	10	The wickedness of sinners shall be brought to nought: and thou shalt direct the just: the searcher of hearts and reins is God.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	11	Just is my help from the Lord: who saveth the upright of heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	12	God is a just judge, strong and patient: is he angry every day?
Psalms	Ps	21	7	13	Except you will be converted, he will brandish his sword: he hath bent his bow and made it ready.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	14	And in it he hath prepared the instruments of death, he hath made ready his arrows for them that burn.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	15	Behold he hath been in labour with injustice; he hath conceived sorrow, and brought forth iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	16	He hath opened a pit and dug it; and he is fallen into the hole he made.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	17	His sorrow shall be turned on his own head: and his iniquity shall come down upon his crown.
Psalms	Ps	21	7	18	I will give glory to the Lord according to his justice: and will sing to the name of the Lord the most high.
Psalms	Ps	21	8	1	[Unto the end, for the presses: a psalm of David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	8	2	O Lord our Lord, how admirable is thy name in the whole earth! For thy magnificence is elevated above the heavens.
Psalms	Ps	21	8	3	Out of the mouth of infants and of sucklings thou hast perfected praise, because of thy enemies, that thou mayst destroy the enemy and the avenger.
Psalms	Ps	21	8	4	For I will behold thy heavens, the works of thy fingers: the moon and the stars which thou hast founded.
Psalms	Ps	21	8	5	What is man that thou art mindful of him? or the son of man that thou visitest him?
Psalms	Ps	21	8	6	Thou hast made him a little less than the angels, thou hast crowned him with glory and honour:
Psalms	Ps	21	8	7	And hast set him over the works of thy hands.
Psalms	Ps	21	8	8	Thou hast subjected all things under his feet, all sheep and oxen: moreover the beasts also of the fields.
Psalms	Ps	21	8	9	The birds of the air, and the fishes of the sea, that pass through the paths of the sea.
Psalms	Ps	21	8	10	O Lord our Lord, how admirable is thy name in all the earth!
Psalms	Ps	21	9	1	[Unto the end, for the hidden things of the Son. A psalm for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	9	2	I will give praise to thee, O Lord, with my whole heart: I will relate all thy wonders.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	3	I will be glad and rejoice in thee: I will sing to thy name, O thou most high.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	4	When my enemy shall be turned back: they shall be weakened and perish before thy face.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	5	For thou hast maintained my judgment and my cause: thou hast sat on the throne, who judgest justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	6	Thou hast rebuked the Gentiles, and the wicked one hath perished: thou hast blotted out their name for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	7	The swords of the enemy have failed unto the end: and their cities thou hast destroyed. Their memory hath perished with a noise.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	8	But the Lord remaineth for ever. He hath prepared his throne in judgment:
Psalms	Ps	21	9	9	And he shall judge the world in equity, he shall judge the people in justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	10	And the Lord is become a refuge for the poor: a helper in due time in tribulation.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	11	And let them trust in thee who know thy name: for thou hast not forsaken them that seek thee, O Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	12	Sing ye to the Lord, who dwelleth in Sion: declare his ways among the Gentiles:
Psalms	Ps	21	9	13	For requiring their blood he hath remembered them: he hath not forgotten the cry of the poor.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	14	Have mercy on me, O Lord: see my humiliation which I suffer from my enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	15	Thou that liftest me up from the gates of death, that I may declare all thy praises in the gates of the daughter of Sion.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	16	I will rejoice in thy salvation: the Gentiles have stuck fast in the destruction which they have prepared. Their foot hath been taken in the very snare which they hid.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	17	The Lord shall be known when he executeth judgments: the sinner hath been caught in the works of his own hands.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	18	The wicked shall be turned into hell, all the nations that forget God.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	19	For the poor man shall not be forgotten to the end: the patience of the poor shall not perish for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	20	Arise, O Lord, let not man be strengthened: let the Gentiles be judged in thy sight.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	21	Appoint, O Lord, a lawgiver over them: that the Gentiles may know themselves to be but men.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	22	Why, O Lord, hast thou retired afar off? why dost thou slight us in our wants, in the time of trouble?
Psalms	Ps	21	9	23	Whilst the wicked man is proud, the poor is set on fire: they are caught in the counsels which they devise.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	24	For the sinner is praised in the desires of his soul: and the unjust man is blessed.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	25	The sinner hath provoked the Lord according to the multitude of his wrath he will not seek him:
Psalms	Ps	21	9	26	God is not before his eyes: his ways are filthy at all times. Thy judgments are removed from his sight: he shall rule over all his enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	27	For he hath said in his heart: I shall not be moved from generation to generation, and shall be without evil.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	28	His mouth is full of cursing, and of bitterness, and of deceit: under his tongue are labour and sorrow.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	29	He sitteth in ambush with the rich in private places, that he may kill the innocent.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	30	His eyes are upon the poor man: He lieth in wait in secret like a lion in his den. He lieth in ambush that he may catch the poor man: to catch the poor, whilst he draweth him to him.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	31	In his net he will bring him down, he will crouch and fall, when he shall have power over the poor.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	32	For he hath said in his heart: God hath forgotten, he hath turned away his face not to see to the end.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	33	Arise, O Lord God, let thy hand be exalted: forget not the poor.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	34	Wherefore hath the wicked provoked God? for he hath said in his heart: He will not require it.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	35	Thou seest it, for thou considerest labour and sorrow: that thou mayst deliver them into thy hands. To thee is the poor man left: thou wilt be a helper to the orphan.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	36	Break thou the arm of the sinner and of the malignant: his sin shall be sought, and shall not be found.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	37	The Lord shall reign to eternity, yea, for ever and ever: ye Gentiles shall perish from his land.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	38	The Lord hath heard the desire of the poor: thy ear hath heard the preparation of their heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	9	39	To judge for the fatherless and for the humble, that man may no more presume to magnify himself upon earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	10	1	[Unto the end. A psalm for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	10	2	In the Lord I put my trust: how then do you say to my soul: Get thee away from hence to the mountain like a sparrow?
Psalms	Ps	21	10	3	For, lo, the wicked have bent their bow; they have prepared their arrows in the quiver; to shoot in the dark the upright of heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	10	4	For they have destroyed the things which thou hast made: but what has the just man done?
Psalms	Ps	21	10	5	The Lord is in his holy temple, the Lord's throne is in heaven. His eyes look on the poor man: his eyelids examine the sons of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	10	6	The Lord trieth the just and the wicked: but he that loveth iniquity hateth his own soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	10	7	He shall rain snares upon sinners: fire and brimstone and storms of winds shall be the portion of their cup.
Psalms	Ps	21	10	8	For the Lord is just, and hath loved justice: his countenance hath beheld righteousness.
Psalms	Ps	21	11	1	[Unto the end; for the octave, a psalm for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	11	2	Save me, O Lord, for there is now no saint: truths are decayed from among the children of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	11	3	They have spoken vain things every one to his neighbour: with deceitful lips, and with a double heart have they spoken.
Psalms	Ps	21	11	4	May the Lord destroy all deceitful lips, and the tongue that speaketh proud things.
Psalms	Ps	21	11	5	Who have said: We will magnify our tongue; our lips are our own; who is Lord over us?
Psalms	Ps	21	11	6	By reason of the misery of the needy, and the groans of the poor, now will I arise, saith the Lord. I will set him in safety; I will deal confidently in his regard.
Psalms	Ps	21	11	7	The words of the Lord are pure words: as silver tried by the fire, purged from the earth refined seven times.
Psalms	Ps	21	11	8	Thou, O Lord, wilt preserve us: and keep us from this generation for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	11	9	The wicked walk round about: according to thy highness, thou hast multiplied the children of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	12	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for David.] How long, O Lord, wilt thou forget me unto the end? how long dost thou turn away thy face from me?
Psalms	Ps	21	12	2	How long shall I take counsels in my soul, sorrow in my heart all the day?
Psalms	Ps	21	12	3	How long shall my enemy be exalted over me?
Psalms	Ps	21	12	4	Consider, and hear me, O Lord my God. Enlighten my eyes that I never sleep in death:
Psalms	Ps	21	12	5	Lest at any time my enemy say: I have prevailed against him. They that trouble me will rejoice when I am moved:
Psalms	Ps	21	12	6	But I have trusted in thy mercy. My heart shall rejoice in thy salvation: I will sing to the Lord, who giveth me good things: yea I will sing to the name of the Lord the most high.
Psalms	Ps	21	13	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for David.] The fool hath said in his heart: There is no God, They are corrupt, and are become abominable in their ways: there is none that doth good, no not one.
Psalms	Ps	21	13	2	The Lord hath looked down from heaven upon the children of men, to see if there be any that understand and seek God.
Psalms	Ps	21	13	3	They are all gone aside, they are become unprofitable together: there is none that doth good, no not one. Their throat is an open sepulchre: with their tongues they acted deceitfully; the poison of asps is under their lips. Their mouth is full of cursing and bitterness; their feet are swift to shed blood. Destruction and unhappiness in their ways: and the way of peace they have not known: there is no fear of God before their eyes.
Psalms	Ps	21	13	4	Shall not all they know that work iniquity, who devour my people as they eat bread?
Psalms	Ps	21	13	5	They have not called upon the Lord: there have they trembled for fear, where there was no fear.
Psalms	Ps	21	13	6	For the Lord is in the just generation: you have confounded the counsel of the poor man, but the Lord is his hope.
Psalms	Ps	21	13	7	Who shall give out of Sion the salvation of Israel? when the Lord shall have turned away the captivity of his people, Jacob shall rejoice and Israel shall be glad.
Psalms	Ps	21	14	1	[A psalm of David.] Lord, who shall dwell in thy tabernacle? or who shall rest in thy holy hill?
Psalms	Ps	21	14	2	He that walketh without blemish, and worketh justice:
Psalms	Ps	21	14	3	He that speaketh truth in his heart, who hath not used deceit in his tongue: Nor hath done evil to his neighbour: nor taken up a reproach against his neighbours.
Psalms	Ps	21	14	4	In his sight the malignant is brought to nothing: but he glorifieth them that fear the Lord. He that sweareth to his neighbour, and deceiveth not;
Psalms	Ps	21	14	5	He that hath not put out his money to usury, nor taken bribes against the innocent: He that doth these things shall not be moved for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	15	1	[The inscription of a title to David himself.] Preserve me, O Lord, for I have put my trust in thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	15	2	I have said to the Lord, thou art my God, for thou hast no need of my goods.
Psalms	Ps	21	15	3	To the saints, who are in his land, he hath made wonderful all my desires in them.
Psalms	Ps	21	15	4	Their infirmities were multiplied: afterwards they made haste. I will not gather together their meetings for blood offerings: nor will I be mindful of their names by my lips.
Psalms	Ps	21	15	5	The Lord is the portion of my inheritance and of my cup: it is thou that wilt restore my inheritance to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	15	6	The lines are fallen unto me in goodly places: for my inheritance is goodly to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	15	7	I will bless the Lord, who hath given me understanding: moreover my reins also have corrected me even till night.
Psalms	Ps	21	15	8	I set the Lord always in my sight: for he is at my right hand, that I be not moved.
Psalms	Ps	21	15	9	Therefore my heart hath been glad, and my tongue hath rejoiced: moreover my flesh also shall rest in hope.
Psalms	Ps	21	15	10	Because thou wilt not leave my soul in hell; nor wilt thou give thy holy one to see corruption.
Psalms	Ps	21	15	11	Thou hast made known to me the ways of life, thou shalt fill me with joy with thy countenance: at thy right hand are delights even to the end.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	1	[The prayer of David.] Hear, O Lord, my justice: attend to my supplication. Give ear unto my prayer, which proceedeth not from deceitful lips.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	2	Let my judgment come forth from thy countenance: let thy eyes behold the things that are equitable.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	3	Thou hast proved my heart, and visited it by night, thou hast tried me by fire: and iniquity hath not been found in me.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	4	That my mouth may not speak the works of men: for the sake of the words of thy lips, I have kept hard ways.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	5	Perfect thou my goings in thy paths: that my footsteps be not moved.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	6	I have cried to thee, for thou, O God, hast heard me: O incline thy ear unto me, and hear my words.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	7	shew forth thy wonderful mercies; thou who savest them that trust in thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	8	From them that resist thy right hand keep me, as the apple of thy eye. Protect me under the shadow of thy wings.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	9	From the face of the wicked who have afflicted me. My enemies have surrounded my soul:
Psalms	Ps	21	16	10	They have shut up their fat: their mouth hath spoken proudly.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	11	They have cast me forth and now they have surrounded me: they have set their eyes bowing down to the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	12	They have taken me, as a lion prepared for the prey; and as a young lion dwelling in secret places.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	13	Arise, O Lord, disappoint him and supplant him; deliver my soul from the wicked one: thy sword
Psalms	Ps	21	16	14	From the enemies of thy hand. O Lord, divide them from the few of the earth in their life: their belly is filled from thy hidden stores. They are full of children: and they have left to their little ones the rest of their substance.
Psalms	Ps	21	16	15	But as for me, I will appear before thy sight in justice: I shall be satisfied when thy glory shall appear.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	1	[Unto the end, for David the servant of the Lord, who spoke to the Lord the words of this canticle, in the day that the Lord delivered him from the hands of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul.]
Psalms	Ps	21	17	2	I will love thee, O Lord, my strength:
Psalms	Ps	21	17	3	The Lord is my firmament, my refuge, and my deliverer. My God is my helper, and in him will I put my trust. My protector and the horn of my salvation, and my support.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	4	Praising I will call upon the Lord: and I shall be saved from my enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	5	The sorrows of death surrounded me: and the torrents of iniquity troubled me.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	6	The sorrows of hell encompassed me: and the snares of death prevented me.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	7	In my affliction I called upon the Lord, and I cried to my God: And he heard my voice from his holy temple: and my cry before him came into his ears.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	8	The earth shook and trembled: the foundations of the mountains were troubled and were moved, because he was angry with them.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	9	There went up a smoke in his wrath: and a fire flamed from his face: coals were kindled by it.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	10	He bowed the heavens, and came down: and darkness was under his feet.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	11	And he ascended upon the cherubim, and he flew; he flew upon the wings of the winds.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	12	And he made darkness his covert, his pavilion round about him: dark waters in the clouds of the air.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	13	At the brightness that was before him the clouds passed, hail and coals of fire.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	14	And the Lord thundered from heaven, and the highest gave his voice: hail and coals of fire.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	15	And he sent forth his arrows, and he scattered them: he multiplied lightnings, and troubled them.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	16	Then the fountains of waters appeared, and the foundations of the world were discovered: At thy rebuke, O Lord, at the blast of the spirit of thy wrath.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	17	He sent from on high, and took me: and received me out of many waters.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	18	He delivered me from my strongest enemies, and from them that hated me: for they were too strong for me.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	19	They prevented me in the day of my affliction: and the Lord became my protector.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	20	And he brought me forth into a large place: he saved me, because he was well pleased with me.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	21	And the Lord will reward me according to my justice; and will repay me according to the cleanness of my hands:
Psalms	Ps	21	17	22	Because I have kept the ways of the Lord; and have not done wickedly against my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	23	For till his judgments are in my sight: and his justices I have not put away from me.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	24	And I shall be spotless with him: and shall keep myself from my iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	25	And the Lord will reward me according to my justice; and according to the cleanness of my hands before his eyes.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	26	With the holy, thou wilt be holy; and with the innocent man thou wilt be innocent.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	27	And with the elect thou wilt be elect: and with the perverse thou wilt be perverted.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	28	For thou wilt save the humble people; but wilt bring down the eyes of the proud.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	29	For thou lightest my lamp, O Lord: O my God enlighten my darkness.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	30	For by thee I shall be delivered from temptation; and through my God I shall go over a wall.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	31	As for my God, his way is undefiled: the words of the Lord are fire tried: he is the protector of all that trust in him.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	32	For who is God but the Lord? or who is God but our God?
Psalms	Ps	21	17	33	God who hath girt me with strength; and made my way blameless.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	34	Who hath made my feet like the feet of harts: and who setteth me upon high places.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	35	Who teacheth my hands to war: and thou hast made my arms like a brazen bow.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	36	And thou hast given me the protection of thy salvation: and thy right hand hath held me up: And thy discipline hath corrected me unto the end: and thy discipline, the same shall teach me.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	37	Thou hast enlarged my steps under me; and my feet are not weakened.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	38	I will pursue after my enemies, and overtake them: and I will not turn again till they are consumed.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	39	I will break them, and they shall not be able to stand: they shall fall under my feet.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	40	And thou hast girded me with strength unto battle; and hast subdued under me them that rose up against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	41	And thou hast made my enemies turn their back upon me, and hast destroyed them that hated me.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	42	They cried, but there was none to save them, to the Lord: but he heard them not.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	43	And I shall beat them as small as the dust before the wind; I shall bring them to nought, like the dirt in the streets.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	44	Thou wilt deliver me from the contradictions of the people: thou wilt make me head of the Gentiles.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	45	A people, which I knew not, hath served me: at the hearing of the ear they have obeyed me.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	46	The children that are strangers have lied to me, strange children have faded away, and have halted from their paths.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	47	The Lord liveth, and blessed be my God, and let the God of my salvation be exalted:
Psalms	Ps	21	17	48	O God, who avengest me, and subduest the people under me, my deliverer from my enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	49	And thou wilt lift me up above them that rise up against me: from the unjust man thou wilt deliver me.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	50	Therefore will I give glory to thee, O Lord, among the nations, and I will sing a psalm to thy name.
Psalms	Ps	21	17	51	Giving great deliverance to his king, and shewing mercy to David his anointed: and to his seed for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	1	[Unto the end. A psalm for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	18	2	The heavens shew forth the glory of God, and the firmament declareth the work of his hands.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	3	Day to day uttereth speech, and night to night sheweth knowledge.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	4	There are no speeches nor languages, where their voices are not heard.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	5	Their sound hath gone forth into all the earth: and their words unto the ends of the world.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	6	He hath set his tabernacle in the sun: and he, as a bridegroom coming out of his bride chamber, Hath rejoiced as a giant to run the way:
Psalms	Ps	21	18	7	His going out is from the end of heaven, And his circuit even to the end thereof: and there is no one that can hide himself from his heat.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	8	The law of the Lord is unspotted, converting souls: the testimony of the Lord is faithful, giving wisdom to little ones.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	9	The justices of the Lord are right, rejoicing hearts: the commandment of the Lord is lightsome, enlightening the eyes.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	10	The fear of the Lord is holy, enduring for ever and ever: the judgments of the Lord are true, justified in themselves.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	11	More to be desired than gold and many precious stones: and sweeter than honey and the honeycomb.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	12	For thy servant keepeth them, and in keeping them there is a great reward.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	13	Who can understand sins? from my secret ones cleanse me, O Lord:
Psalms	Ps	21	18	14	And from those of others spare thy servant. If they shall have no dominion over me, then shall I be without spot: and I shall be cleansed from the greatest sin.
Psalms	Ps	21	18	15	And the words of my mouth shall be such as may please: and the meditation of my heart always in thy sight. O Lord, my helper, and my redeemer.
Psalms	Ps	21	19	1	[Unto the end. A psalm for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	19	2	May the Lord hear thee in the day of tribulation: may the name of the God of Jacob protect thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	19	3	May he send thee help from the sanctuary: and defend thee out of Sion.
Psalms	Ps	21	19	4	May he be mindful of all thy sacrifices: and may thy whole burnt offering be made fat.
Psalms	Ps	21	19	5	May he give thee according to thy own heart; and confirm all thy counsels.
Psalms	Ps	21	19	6	We will rejoice in thy salvation; and in the name of our God we shall be exalted.
Psalms	Ps	21	19	7	The Lord fulfill all thy petitions: now have I known that the Lord hath saved his anointed. He will hear him from his holy heaven: the salvation of his right hand is in powers.
Psalms	Ps	21	19	8	Some trust in chariots, and some in horses: but we will call upon the name of the Lord our God.
Psalms	Ps	21	19	9	They are bound, and have fallen; but we are risen, and are set upright. O Lord, save the king: and hear us in the day that we shall call upon thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	1	[Unto the end. A psalm for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	20	2	In thy strength, O Lord, the king shall joy; and in thy salvation he shall rejoice exceedingly.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	3	Thou hast given him his heart's desire: and hast not withholden from him the will of his lips.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	4	For thou hast prevented him with blessings of sweetness: thou hast set on his head a crown of precious stones.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	5	He asked life of thee: and thou hast given him length of days for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	6	His glory is great in thy salvation: glory and great beauty shalt thou lay upon him.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	7	For thou shalt give him to be a blessing for ever and ever: thou shalt make him joyful in gladness with thy countenance.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	8	For the king hopeth in the Lord: and through the mercy of the most High he shall not be moved.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	9	Let thy hand be found by all thy enemies: let thy right hand find out all them that hate thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	10	Thou shalt make them as an oven of fire, in the time of thy anger: the Lord shall trouble them in his wrath, and fire shall devour them.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	11	Their fruit shalt thou destroy from the earth: and their seed from among the children of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	12	For they have intended evils against thee: they have devised counsels which they have not been able to establish.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	13	For thou shalt make them turn their back: in thy remnants thou shalt prepare their face.
Psalms	Ps	21	20	14	Be thou exalted, O Lord, in thy own strength: we will sing and praise thy power.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	1	[Unto the end, for the morning protection, a psalm for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	21	2	O God my God, look upon me: why hast thou forsaken me? Far from my salvation are the words of my sins.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	3	O my God, I shall cry by day, and thou wilt not hear: and by night, and it shall not be reputed as folly in me.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	4	But thou dwellest in the holy place, the praise of Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	5	In thee have our fathers hoped: they have hoped, and thou hast delivered them.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	6	They cried to thee, and they were saved: they trusted in thee, and were not confounded.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	7	But I am a worm, and no man: the reproach of men, and the outcast of the people.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	8	All they that saw me have laughed me to scorn: they have spoken with the lips, and wagged the head.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	9	He hoped in the Lord, let him deliver him: let him save him, seeing he delighteth in him.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	10	For thou art he that hast drawn me out of the womb: my hope from the breasts of my mother.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	11	I was cast upon thee from the womb. From my mother's womb thou art my God,
Psalms	Ps	21	21	12	Depart not from me. For tribulation is very near: for there is none to help me.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	13	Many calves have surrounded me: fat bulls have besieged me.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	14	They have opened their mouths against me, as a lion ravening and roaring.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	15	I am poured out like water; and all my bones are scattered. My heart is become like wax melting in the midst of my bowels.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	16	My strength is dried up like a potsherd, and my tongue hath cleaved to my jaws: and thou hast brought me down into the dust of death.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	17	For many dogs have encompassed me: the council of the malignant hath besieged me. They have dug my hands and feet.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	18	They have numbered all my bones. And they have looked and stared upon me.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	19	They parted my garments amongst them; and upon my vesture they cast lots.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	20	But thou, O Lord, remove not thy help to a distance from me; look towards my defence.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	21	Deliver, O God, my soul from the sword: my only one from the hand of the dog.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	22	Save me from the lion's mouth; and my lowness from the horns of the unicorns.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	23	I will declare thy name to my brethren: in the midst of the church will I praise thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	24	Ye that fear the Lord, praise him: all ye the seed of Jacob, glorify him.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	25	Let all the seed of Israel fear him: because he hath not slighted nor despised the supplication of the poor man. Neither hath he turned away his face from me: and when I cried to him he heard me.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	26	With thee is my praise in a great church: I will pay my vows in the sight of them that fear him.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	27	The poor shall eat and shall be filled: and they shall praise the Lord that seek him: their hearts shall live for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	28	All the ends of the earth shall remember, and shall be converted to the Lord: And all the kindreds of the Gentiles shall adore in his sight.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	29	For the kingdom is the Lord's; and he shall have dominion over the nations.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	30	All the fat ones of the earth have eaten and have adored: all they that go down to the earth shall fall before him.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	31	And to him my soul shall live: and my seed shall serve him.
Psalms	Ps	21	21	32	There shall be declared to the Lord a generation to come: and the heavens shall shew forth his justice to a people that shall be born, which the Lord hath made.
Psalms	Ps	21	22	1	[A psalm for David.] The Lord ruleth me: and I shall want nothing.
Psalms	Ps	21	22	2	He hath set me in a place of pasture. He hath brought me up, on the water of refreshment:
Psalms	Ps	21	22	3	He hath converted my soul. He hath led me on the paths of justice, for his own name's sake.
Psalms	Ps	21	22	4	For though I should walk in the midst of the shadow of death, I will fear no evils, for thou art with me. Thy rod and thy staff, they have comforted me.
Psalms	Ps	21	22	5	Thou hast prepared a table before me against them that afflict me. Thou hast anointed my head with oil; and my chalice which inebriateth me, how goodly is it!
Psalms	Ps	21	22	6	And thy mercy will follow me all the days of my life. And that I may dwell in the house of the Lord unto length of days.
Psalms	Ps	21	23	1	[On the first day of the week, a psalm for David.] The earth is the Lord's and the fulness thereof: the world, and all they that dwell therein.
Psalms	Ps	21	23	2	For he hath founded it upon the seas; and hath prepared it upon the rivers.
Psalms	Ps	21	23	3	Who shall ascend into the mountain of the Lord: or who shall stand in his holy place?
Psalms	Ps	21	23	4	The innocent in hands, and clean of heart, who hath not taken his soul in vain, nor sworn deceitfully to his neighbour.
Psalms	Ps	21	23	5	He shall receive a blessing from the Lord, and mercy from God his Saviour.
Psalms	Ps	21	23	6	This is the generation of them that seek him, of them that seek the face of the God of Jacob.
Psalms	Ps	21	23	7	Lift up your gates, O ye princes, and be ye lifted up, O eternal gates: and the King of Glory shall enter in.
Psalms	Ps	21	23	8	Who is this King of Glory? the Lord who is strong and mighty: the Lord mighty in battle.
Psalms	Ps	21	23	9	Lift up your gates, O ye princes, and be ye lifted up, O eternal gates: and the King of Glory shall enter in.
Psalms	Ps	21	23	10	Who is this King of Glory? the Lord of hosts, he is the King of Glory.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for David.] To thee, O Lord, have I lifted up my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	2	In thee, O my God, I put my trust; let me not be ashamed.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	3	Neither let my enemies laugh at me: for none of them that wait on thee shall be confounded.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	4	Let all them be confounded that act unjust things without cause. Shew, O Lord, thy ways to me, and teach me thy paths.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	5	Direct me in thy truth, and teach me; for thou art God my Saviour; and on thee have I waited all the day long.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	6	Remember, O Lord, thy bowels of compassion; and thy mercies that are from the beginning of the world.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	7	The sins of my youth and my ignorances do not remember. According to thy mercy remember thou me: for thy goodness' sake, O Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	8	The Lord is sweet and righteous: therefore he will give a law to sinners in the way.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	9	He will guide the mild in judgment: he will teach the meek his ways.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	10	All the ways of the Lord are mercy and truth, to them that seek after his covenant and his testimonies.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	11	For thy name's sake, O Lord, thou wilt pardon my sin: for it is great.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	12	Who is the man that feareth the Lord? He hath appointed him a law in the way he hath chosen.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	13	His soul shall dwell in good things: and his seed shall inherit the land.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	14	The Lord is a firmament to them that fear him: and his covenant shall be made manifest to them.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	15	My eyes are ever towards the Lord: for he shall pluck my feet out of the snare.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	16	Look thou upon me, and have mercy on me; for I am alone and poor.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	17	The troubles of my heart are multiplied: deliver me from my necessities.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	18	See my abjection and my labour; and forgive me all my sins.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	19	Consider my enemies for they are multiplied, and have hated me with an unjust hatred.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	20	Keep thou my soul, and deliver me: I shall not be ashamed, for I have hoped in thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	21	The innocent and the upright have adhered to me: because I have waited on thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	24	22	Deliver Israel, O God, from all his tribulations.
Psalms	Ps	21	25	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for David.] Judge me, O Lord, for I have walked in my innocence: and I have put my trust in the Lord, and shall not be weakened.
Psalms	Ps	21	25	2	Prove me, O Lord, and try me; burn my reins and my heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	25	3	For thy mercy is before my eyes; and I am well pleased with thy truth.
Psalms	Ps	21	25	4	I have not sat with the council of vanity: neither will I go in with the doers of unjust things.
Psalms	Ps	21	25	5	I have hated the assembly of the malignant; and with the wicked I will not sit.
Psalms	Ps	21	25	6	I will wash my hands among the innocent; and will compass thy altar, O Lord:
Psalms	Ps	21	25	7	That I may hear the voice of thy praise: and tell of all thy wondrous works.
Psalms	Ps	21	25	8	I have loved, O Lord, the beauty of thy house; and the place where thy glory dwelleth.
Psalms	Ps	21	25	9	Take not away my soul, O God, with the wicked: nor my life with bloody men:
Psalms	Ps	21	25	10	In whose hands are iniquities: their right hand is filled with gifts.
Psalms	Ps	21	25	11	But as for me, I have walked in my innocence: redeem me, and have mercy on me.
Psalms	Ps	21	25	12	My foot hath stood in the direct way: in the churches I will bless thee, O Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	1	[The psalm of David before he was anointed.] The Lord is my light and my salvation, whom shall I fear? The Lord is the protector of my life: of whom shall I be afraid?
Psalms	Ps	21	26	2	Whilst the wicked draw near against me, to eat my flesh. My enemies that trouble me, have themselves been weakened, and have fallen.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	3	If armies in camp should stand together against me, my heart shall not fear. If a battle should rise up against me, in this will I be confident.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	4	One thing I have asked of the Lord, this will I seek after; that I may dwell in the house of the Lord all the days of my life. That I may see the delight of the Lord, and may visit his temple.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	5	For he hath hidden me in his tabernacle; in the day of evils, he hath protected me in the secret place of his tabernacle.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	6	He hath exalted me upon a rock: and now he hath lifted up my head above my enemies. I have gone round, and have offered up in his tabernacle a sacrifice of jubilation: I will sing, and recite a psalm to the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	7	Hear, O Lord, my voice, with which I have cried to thee: have mercy on me and hear me.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	8	My heart hath said to thee: My face hath sought thee: thy face, O Lord, will I still seek.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	9	Turn not away thy face from me; decline not in thy wrath from thy servant. Be thou my helper, forsake me not; do not thou despise me, O God my Saviour.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	10	For my father and my mother have left me: but the Lord hath taken me up.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	11	Set me, O Lord, a law in thy way, and guide me in the right path, because of my enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	12	Deliver me not over to the will of them that trouble me; for unjust witnesses have risen up against me; and iniquity hath lied to itself.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	13	I believe to see the good things of the Lord in the land of the living.
Psalms	Ps	21	26	14	Expect the Lord, do manfully, and let thy heart take courage, and wait thou for the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	27	1	[A psalm for David himself.] Unto thee will I cry, O Lord: O my God, be not thou silent to me: lest thou be silent to me, I become like them that go down into the pit.
Psalms	Ps	21	27	2	Hear, O Lord, the voice of my supplication, when I pray to thee; when I lift up my hands to thy holy temple.
Psalms	Ps	21	27	3	Draw me not away together with the wicked; and with the workers of iniquity destroy me not: Who speak peace with their neighbour, but evils are in their hearts.
Psalms	Ps	21	27	4	Give them according to their works, and according to the wickedness of their inventions. According to the works of their hands give thou to them: render to them their reward.
Psalms	Ps	21	27	5	Because they have not understood the works of the Lord, and the operations of his hands: thou shalt destroy them, and shalt not build them up.
Psalms	Ps	21	27	6	Blessed be the Lord, for he hath heard the voice of my supplication.
Psalms	Ps	21	27	7	The Lord is my helper and my protector: in him hath my heart confided, and I have been helped. And my flesh hath flourished again, and with my will I will give praise to him.
Psalms	Ps	21	27	8	The Lord is the strength of his people, and the protector of the salvation of his anointed.
Psalms	Ps	21	27	9	Save, O Lord, thy people, and bless thy inheritance: and rule them and exalt them for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	28	1	[A psalm for David, at the finishing of the tabernacle.] Bring to the Lord, O ye children of God: bring to the Lord the offspring of rams.
Psalms	Ps	21	28	2	Bring to the Lord glory and honour: bring to the Lord glory to his name: adore ye the Lord in his holy court.
Psalms	Ps	21	28	3	The voice of the Lord is upon the waters; the God of majesty hath thundered, The Lord is upon many waters.
Psalms	Ps	21	28	4	The voice of the Lord is in power; the voice of the Lord in magnificence.
Psalms	Ps	21	28	5	The voice of the Lord breaketh the cedars: yea, the Lord shall break the cedars of Libanus.
Psalms	Ps	21	28	6	And shall reduce them to pieces, as a calf of Libanus, and as the beloved son of unicorns.
Psalms	Ps	21	28	7	The voice of the Lord divideth the flame of fire:
Psalms	Ps	21	28	8	The voice of the Lord shaketh the desert: and the Lord shall shake the desert of Cades.
Psalms	Ps	21	28	9	The voice of the Lord prepareth the stags: and he will discover the thick woods: and in his temple all shall speak his glory.
Psalms	Ps	21	28	10	The Lord maketh the flood to dwell: and the Lord shall sit king for ever. The Lord will give strength to his people: the Lord will bless his people with peace.
Psalms	Ps	21	29	1	[A psalm of a canticle, at the dedication of David's house.]
Psalms	Ps	21	29	2	I will extol thee, O Lord, for thou hast upheld me: and hast not made my enemies to rejoice over me.
Psalms	Ps	21	29	3	O Lord my God, I have cried to thee, and thou hast healed me.
Psalms	Ps	21	29	4	Thou hast brought forth, O Lord, my soul from hell: thou hast saved me from them that go down into the pit.
Psalms	Ps	21	29	5	Sing to the Lord, O ye his saints: and give praise to the memory of his holiness.
Psalms	Ps	21	29	6	For wrath is in his indignation; and life in his good will. In the evening weeping shall have place, and in the morning gladness.
Psalms	Ps	21	29	7	And in my abundance I said: I shall never be moved.
Psalms	Ps	21	29	8	O Lord, in thy favour, thou gavest strength to my beauty. Thou turnedst away thy face from me, and I became troubled.
Psalms	Ps	21	29	9	To thee, O Lord, will I cry: and I will make supplication to my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	29	10	What profit is there in my blood, whilst I go down to corruption? Shall dust confess to thee, or declare thy truth?
Psalms	Ps	21	29	11	The Lord hath heard, and hath had mercy on me: the Lord became my helper.
Psalms	Ps	21	29	12	Thou hast turned for me my mourning into joy: thou hast cut my sackcloth, and hast compassed me with gladness:
Psalms	Ps	21	29	13	To the end that my glory may sing to thee, and I may not regret: O Lord my God, I will give praise to thee for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for David, in an ecstasy.]
Psalms	Ps	21	30	2	In thee, O Lord, have I hoped, let me never be confounded: deliver me in thy justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	3	Bow down thy ear to me: make haste to deliver me. Be thou unto me a God, a protector, and a house of refuge, to save me.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	4	For thou art my strength and my refuge; and for thy name's sake thou wilt lead me, and nourish me.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	5	Thou wilt bring me out of this snare, which they have hidden for me: for thou art my protector.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	6	Into thy hands I commend my spirit: thou hast redeemed me, O Lord, the God of truth.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	7	Thou hast hated them that regard vanities, to no purpose. But I have hoped in the Lord:
Psalms	Ps	21	30	8	I will be glad and rejoice in thy mercy. For thou hast regarded my humility, thou hast saved my soul out of distresses.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	9	And thou hast not shut me up in the hands of the enemy: thou hast set my feet in a spacious place.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	10	Have mercy on me, O Lord, for I am afflicted: my eye is troubled with wrath, my soul, and my belly:
Psalms	Ps	21	30	11	For my life is wasted with grief: and my years in sighs. My strength is weakened through poverty and my bones are disturbed.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	12	I am become a reproach among all my enemies, and very much to my neighbours; and a fear to my acquaintance. They that saw me without fled from me.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	13	I am forgotten as one dead from the heart. I am become as a vessel that is destroyed.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	14	For I have heard the blame of many that dwell round about. While they assembled together against me, they consulted to take away my life.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	15	But I have put my trust in thee, O Lord: I said: Thou art my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	16	My lots are in thy hands. Deliver me out of the hands of my enemies; and from them that persecute me.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	17	Make thy face to shine upon thy servant; save me in thy mercy.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	18	Let me not be confounded, O Lord, for I have called upon thee. Let the wicked be ashamed, and be brought down to hell.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	19	Let deceitful lips be made dumb. Which speak iniquity against the just, with pride and abuse.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	20	O how great is the multitude of thy sweetness, O Lord, which thou hast hidden for them that fear thee! Which thou hast wrought for them that hope in thee, in the sight of the sons of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	21	Thou shalt hide them in the secret of thy face, from the disturbance of men. Thou shalt protect them in thy tabernacle from the contradiction of tongues.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	22	Blessed be the Lord, for he hath shewn his wonderful mercy to me in a fortified city.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	23	But I said in the excess of my mind: I am cast away from before thy eyes. Therefore thou hast heard the voice of my prayer, when I cried to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	24	O love the Lord, all ye his saints: for the Lord will require truth, and will repay them abundantly that act proudly.
Psalms	Ps	21	30	25	Do ye manfully, and let your heart be strengthened, all ye that hope in the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	31	1	[To David himself, understanding.] Blessed are they whose iniquities are forgiven, and whose sins are covered.
Psalms	Ps	21	31	2	Blessed is the man to whom the Lord hath not imputed sin, and in whose spirit there is no guile.
Psalms	Ps	21	31	3	Because I was silent my bones grew old; whilst I cried out all the day long.
Psalms	Ps	21	31	4	For day and night thy hand was heavy upon me: I am turned in my anguish, whilst the thorn is fastened.
Psalms	Ps	21	31	5	I have acknowledged my sin to thee, and my injustice I have not concealed. I said I will confess against myself my injustice to the Lord: and thou hast forgiven the wickedness of my sin.
Psalms	Ps	21	31	6	For this shall every one that is holy pray to thee in a seasonable time. And yet in a flood of many waters, they shall not come nigh unto him.
Psalms	Ps	21	31	7	Thou art my refuge from the trouble which hath encompassed me: my joy, deliver me from them that surround me.
Psalms	Ps	21	31	8	I will give thee understanding, and I will instruct thee in this way, in which thou shalt go: I will fix my eyes upon thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	31	9	Do not become like the horse and the mule, who have no understanding. With bit and bridle bind fast their jaws, who come not near unto thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	31	10	Many are the scourges of the sinner, but mercy shall encompass him that hopeth in the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	31	11	Be glad in the Lord, and rejoice, ye just, and glory, all ye right of heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	1	[A psalm for David.] Rejoice in the Lord, O ye just: praise becometh the upright.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	2	Give praise to the Lord on the harp; sing to him with the psaltery, the instrument of ten strings.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	3	Sing to him a new canticle, sing well unto him with a loud noise.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	4	For the word of the Lord is right, and all his works are done with faithfulness.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	5	He loveth mercy and judgment; the earth is full of the mercy of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	6	By the word of the Lord the heavens were established; and all the power of them by the spirit of his mouth:
Psalms	Ps	21	32	7	Gathering together the waters of the sea, as in a vessel; laying up the depths in storehouses.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	8	Let all the earth fear the Lord, and let all the inhabitants of the world be in awe of him.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	9	For he spoke and they were made: he commanded and they were created.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	10	The Lord bringeth to naught the counsels of nations; and he rejecteth the devices of people, and casteth away the counsels of princes.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	11	But the counsel of the Lord standeth for ever: the thoughts of his heart to all generations.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	12	Blessed is the nation whose God is the Lord: the people whom he hath chosen for his inheritance.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	13	The Lord hath looked from heaven: he hath beheld all the sons of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	14	From his habitation which he hath prepared, he hath looked upon all that dwell on the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	15	He who hath made the hearts of every one of them: who understandeth all their works.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	16	The king is not saved by a great army: nor shall the giant be saved by his own great strength.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	17	Vain is the horse for safety: neither shall he be saved by the abundance of his strength.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	18	Behold the eyes of the Lord are on them that fear him: and on them that hope in his mercy.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	19	To deliver their souls from death; and feed them in famine.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	20	Our soul waiteth for the Lord: for he is our helper and protector.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	21	For in him our heart shall rejoice: and in his holy name we have trusted.
Psalms	Ps	21	32	22	Let thy mercy, O Lord, be upon us, as we have hoped in thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	1	[For David, when he changed his countenance before Achimelech, who dismissed him, and he went his way.]
Psalms	Ps	21	33	2	I will bless the Lord at all times, his praise shall be always in my mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	3	In the Lord shall my soul be praised: let the meek hear and rejoice.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	4	O magnify the Lord with me; and let us extol his name together.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	5	I sought the Lord, and he heard me; and he delivered me from all my troubles.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	6	Come ye to him and be enlightened: and your faces shall not be confounded.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	7	This poor man cried, and the Lord heard him: and saved him out of all his troubles.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	8	The angel of the Lord shall encamp round about them that fear him: and shall deliver them.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	9	O taste, and see that the Lord is sweet: blessed is the man that hopeth in him.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	10	Fear the Lord, all ye his saints: for there is no want to them that fear him.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	11	The rich have wanted, and have suffered hunger: but they that seek the Lord shall not be deprived of any good.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	12	Come, children, hearken to me: I will teach you the fear of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	13	Who is the man that desireth life: who loveth to see good days?
Psalms	Ps	21	33	14	Keep thy tongue from evil, and thy lips from speaking guile.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	15	Turn away from evil and do good: seek after peace and pursue it.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	16	The eyes of the Lord are upon the just: and his ears unto their prayers.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	17	But the countenance of the Lord is against them that do evil things: to cut off the remembrance of them from the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	18	The just cried, and the Lord heard them: and delivered them out of all their troubles.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	19	The Lord is nigh unto them that are of a contrite heart: and he will save the humble of spirit.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	20	Many are the afflictions of the just; but out of them all will the Lord deliver them.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	21	The Lord keepeth all their bones, not one of them shall be broken.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	22	The death of the wicked is very evil: and they that hate the just shall be guilty.
Psalms	Ps	21	33	23	The Lord will redeem the souls of his servants: and none of them that trust in him shall offend.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	1	[For David himself.] Judge thou, O Lord, them that wrong me: overthrow them that fight against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	2	Take hold of arms and shield: and rise up to help me.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	3	Bring out the sword, and shut up the way against them that persecute me: say to my soul: I am thy salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	4	Let them be confounded and ashamed that seek after my soul. Let them be turned back and be confounded that devise against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	5	Let them become as dust before the wind: and let the angel of the Lord straiten them.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	6	Let their way become dark and slippery; and let the angel of the Lord pursue them.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	7	For without cause they have hidden their net for me unto destruction: without cause they have upbraided my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	8	Let the snare which he knoweth not come upon him: and let the net which he hath hidden catch him: and into that very snare let them fall.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	9	But my soul shall rejoice in the Lord; and shall be delighted in his salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	10	All my bones shall say: Lord, who is like to thee? Who deliverest the poor from the hand of them that are stronger than he; the needy and the poor from them that strip him.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	11	Unjust witnesses rising up have asked me things I knew not.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	12	They repaid me evil for good: to the depriving me of my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	13	But as for me, when they were troublesome to me, I was clothed with haircloth. I humbled my soul with fasting; and my prayer shall be turned into my bosom.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	14	As a neighbour and as an own brother, so did I please: as one mourning and sorrowful so was I humbled.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	15	But they rejoiced against me, and came together: scourges were gathered together upon me, and I knew not.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	16	They were separated, and repented not: they tempted me, they scoffed at me with scorn: they gnashed upon me with their teeth.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	17	Lord, when wilt thou look upon me? rescue thou my soul from their malice: my only one from the lions.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	18	I will give thanks to thee in a great church; I will praise thee in a strong people.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	19	Let not them that are my enemies wrongfully rejoice over me: who have hated me without cause, and wink with the eyes.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	20	For they spoke indeed peaceably to me; and speaking in the anger of the earth they devised guile.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	21	And they opened their mouth wide against me; they said: Well done, well done, our eyes have seen it.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	22	Thou hast seen, O Lord, be not thou silent: O Lord, depart not from me.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	23	Arise, and be attentive to my judgment: to my cause, my God, and my Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	24	Judge me, O Lord my God according to thy justice, and let them not rejoice over me.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	25	Let them not say in their hearts: It is well, it is well, to our mind: neither let them say: We have swallowed him up.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	26	Let them blush: and be ashamed together, who rejoice at my evils. Let them be clothed with confusion and shame, who speak great things against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	27	Let them rejoice and be glad, who are well pleased with my justice, and let them say always: The Lord be magnified, who delights in the peace of his servant.
Psalms	Ps	21	34	28	And my tongue shall meditate thy justice, thy praise all the day long.
Psalms	Ps	21	35	1	[Unto the end, for the servant of God, David himself.]
Psalms	Ps	21	35	2	The unjust hath said within himself, that he would sin: there is no fear of God before his eyes.
Psalms	Ps	21	35	3	For in his sight he hath done deceitfully, that his iniquity may be found unto hatred.
Psalms	Ps	21	35	4	The words of his mouth are iniquity and guile: he would not understand that he might do well.
Psalms	Ps	21	35	5	He hath devised iniquity on his bed, he hath set himself on every way that is not good: but evil he hath not hated.
Psalms	Ps	21	35	6	O Lord, thy mercy is in heaven, and thy truth reacheth, even to the clouds.
Psalms	Ps	21	35	7	Thy justice is as the mountains of God, thy judgments are a great deep. Men and beasts thou wilt preserve, O Lord:
Psalms	Ps	21	35	8	O how hast thou multiplied thy mercy, O God! But the children of men shall put their trust under the covert of thy wings.
Psalms	Ps	21	35	9	They shall be inebriated with the plenty of thy house; and thou shalt make them drink of the torrent of thy pleasure.
Psalms	Ps	21	35	10	For with thee is the fountain of life; and in thy light we shall see light.
Psalms	Ps	21	35	11	Extend thy mercy to them that know thee, and thy justice to them that are right in heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	35	12	Let not the foot of pride come to me, and let not the hand of the sinner move me.
Psalms	Ps	21	35	13	There the workers of iniquity are fallen, they are cast out, and could not stand.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	1	[A psalm for David himself.] Be not emulous of evildoers; nor envy them that work iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	2	For they shall shortly wither away as grass, and as the green herbs shall quickly fall.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	3	Trust in the Lord, and do good, and dwell in the land, and thou shalt be fed with its riches.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	4	Delight in the Lord, and he will give thee the requests of thy heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	5	Commit thy way to the Lord, and trust in him, and he will do it.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	6	And he will bring forth thy justice as the light, and thy judgment as the noonday.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	7	Be subject to the Lord and pray to him Envy not the man who prospereth in his way; the man who doth unjust things.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	8	Cease from anger, and leave rage; have no emulation to do evil.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	9	For the evildoers shall be cut off: but they that wait upon the Lord shall inherit the land.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	10	For yet a little while, and the wicked shall not be: and thou shalt seek his place, and shalt not find it.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	11	But the meek shall inherit the land, and shall delight in abundance of peace.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	12	The sinner shall watch the just man: and shall gnash upon him with his teeth.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	13	But the Lord shall laugh at him: for he foreseeth that his day shall come.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	14	The wicked have drawn out the sword: they have bent their bow. To cast down the poor and needy, to kill the upright of heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	15	Let their sword enter into their own hearts, and let their bow be broken.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	16	Better is a little to the just, than the great riches of the wicked.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	17	For the arms of the wicked shall be broken in pieces; but the Lord strengtheneth the just.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	18	The Lord knoweth the days of undefiled; and their inheritance shall be for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	19	They shall not be confounded in the evil time; and in the days of famine they shall be filled:
Psalms	Ps	21	36	20	Because the wicked shall perish. And the enemies of the Lord, presently after they shall be honoured and exalted, shall come to nothing and vanish like smoke.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	21	The sinner shall borrow, and not pay again; but the just sheweth mercy and shall give.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	22	For such as bless him shall inherit the land: but such as curse him shall perish.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	23	With the Lord shall the steps of a man be directed, and he shall like well his way.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	24	When he shall fall he shall not be bruised, for the Lord putteth his hand under him.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	25	I have been young, and now am old; and I have not seen the just forsaken, nor his seed seeking bread.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	26	He sheweth mercy, and lendeth all the day long; and his seed shall be in blessing.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	27	Decline from evil and do good, and dwell for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	28	For the Lord loveth judgment, and will not forsake his saints: they shall be preserved for ever. The unjust shall be punished, and the seed of the wicked shall perish.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	29	But the just shall inherit the land, and shall dwell therein for evermore.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	30	The mouth of the just shall meditate wisdom: and his tongue shall speak judgment.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	31	The law of his God is in his heart, and his steps shall not be supplanted.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	32	The wicked watcheth the just man, and seeketh to put him to death,
Psalms	Ps	21	36	33	But the Lord will not leave him in his hands; nor condemn him when he shall be judged.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	34	Expect the Lord and keep his way: and he will exalt thee to inherit the land: when the sinners shall perish thou shalt see.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	35	I have seen the wicked highly exalted, and lifted up like the cedars of Libanus.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	36	And I passed by, and lo, he was not: and I sought him and his place was not found.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	37	Keep innocence, and behold justice: for there are remnants for the peaceable man.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	38	But the unjust shall be destroyed together: the remnants of the wicked shall perish.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	39	But the salvation of the just is from the Lord, and he is their protector in the time of trouble.
Psalms	Ps	21	36	40	And the Lord will help them and deliver them: and he will rescue them from the wicked, and save them, because they have hoped in him.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	1	[A psalm for David, for a remembrance of the sabbath.]
Psalms	Ps	21	37	2	Rebuke me not, O Lord, in thy indignation; nor chastise me in thy wrath.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	3	For thy arrows are fastened in me: and thy hand hath been strong upon me.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	4	There is no health in my flesh, because of thy wrath: there is no peace for my bones, because of my sins.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	5	For my iniquities are gone over my head: and as a heavy burden are become heavy upon me.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	6	My sores are putrified and corrupted, because of my foolishness.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	7	I am become miserable, and am bowed down even to the end: I walked sorrowful all the day long.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	8	For my loins are filled with illusions; and there is no health in my flesh.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	9	I am afflicted and humbled exceedingly: I roared with the groaning of my heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	10	Lord, all my desire is before thee, and my groaning is not hidden from thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	11	My heart is troubled, my strength hath left me, and the light of my eyes itself is not with me.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	12	My friends and my neighbours have drawn near, and stood against me. And they that were near me stood afar off:
Psalms	Ps	21	37	13	And they that sought my soul used violence. And they that sought evils to me spoke vain things, and studied deceits all the day long.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	14	But I, as a deaf man, heard not: and as a dumb man not opening his mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	15	And I became as a man that heareth not: and that hath no reproofs in his mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	16	For in thee, O Lord, have I hoped: thou wilt hear me, O Lord my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	17	For I said: Lest at any time my enemies rejoice over me: and whilst my feet are moved, they speak great things against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	18	For I am ready for scourges: and my sorrow is continually before me.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	19	For I will declare my iniquity: and I will think for my sin.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	20	But my enemies live, and are stronger than I: and they that hate me wrongfully are multiplied.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	21	They that render evil for good, have detracted me, because I followed goodness.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	22	Forsake me not, O Lord my God: do not thou depart from me.
Psalms	Ps	21	37	23	Attend unto my help, O Lord, the God of my salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	1	[Unto the end, for Idithun himself, a canticle of David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	38	2	I said: I will take heed to my ways: that I sin not with my tongue. I have set guard to my mouth, when the sinner stood against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	3	I was dumb, and was humbled, and kept silence from good things: and my sorrow was renewed.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	4	My heart grew hot within me: and in my meditation a fire shall flame out.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	5	I spoke with my tongue: O Lord, make me know my end. And what is the number of my days: that I may know what is wanting to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	6	Behold thou hast made my days measurable: and my substance is as nothing before thee. And indeed all things are vanity: every man living.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	7	Surely man passeth as an image: yea, and he is disquieted in vain. He storeth up: and he knoweth not for whom he shall gather these things.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	8	And now what is my hope? is it not the Lord? and my substance is with thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	9	Deliver thou me from all my iniquities: thou hast made me a reproach to the fool.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	10	I was dumb, and I opened not my mouth, because thou hast done it.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	11	Remove thy scourges from me. The strength of thy hand hath made me faint in rebukes:
Psalms	Ps	21	38	12	Thou hast corrected man for iniquity. And thou hast made his soul to waste away like a spider: surely in vain is any man disquieted.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	13	Hear my prayer, O Lord, and my supplication: give ear to my tears. Be not silent: for I am a stranger with thee, and a sojourner as all my fathers were.
Psalms	Ps	21	38	14	O forgive me, that I may be refreshed, before I go hence, and be no more.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for David himself.]
Psalms	Ps	21	39	2	With expectation I have waited for the Lord, and he was attentive to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	3	And he heard my prayers, and brought me out of the pit of misery and the mire of dregs. And he set my feet upon a rock, and directed my steps.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	4	And he put a new canticle into my mouth, a song to our God. Many shall see, and shall fear: and they shall hope in the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	5	Blessed is the man whose trust is in the name of the Lord; and who hath not had regard to vanities, and lying follies.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	6	Thou hast multiplied thy wonderful works, O Lord my God: and in thy thoughts there is no one like to thee. I have declared and I have spoken they are multiplied above number.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	7	Sacrifice and oblation thou didst not desire; but thou hast pierced ears for me. Burnt offering and sin offering thou didst not require:
Psalms	Ps	21	39	8	Then said I, Behold I come. In the head of the book it is written of me
Psalms	Ps	21	39	9	That I should do thy will: O my God, I have desired it, and thy law in the midst of my heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	10	I have declared thy justice in a great church, lo, I will not restrain my lips: O Lord, thou knowest it.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	11	I have not hid thy justice within my heart: I have declared thy truth and thy salvation. I have not concealed thy mercy and thy truth from a great council.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	12	Withhold not thou, O Lord, thy tender mercies from me: thy mercy and thy truth have always upheld me.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	13	For evils without number have surrounded me; my iniquities have overtaken me, and I was not able to see. They are multiplied above the hairs of my head: and my heart hath forsaken me.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	14	Be pleased, O Lord, to deliver me, look down, O Lord, to help me.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	15	Let them be confounded and ashamed together, that seek after my soul to take it away. Let them be turned backward and be ashamed that desire evils to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	16	Let them immediately bear their confusion, that say to me: Tis well, tis well.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	17	Let all that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee: and let such as love thy salvation say always: The Lord be magnified.
Psalms	Ps	21	39	18	But I am a beggar and poor: the Lord is careful for me. Thou art my helper and my protector: O my God, be not slack.
Psalms	Ps	21	40	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for David himself.]
Psalms	Ps	21	40	2	Blessed is he that understandeth concerning the needy and the poor: the Lord will deliver him in the evil day.
Psalms	Ps	21	40	3	The Lord preserve him and give him life, and make him blessed upon the earth: and deliver him not up to the will of his enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	40	4	The Lord help him on his bed of sorrow: thou hast turned all his couch in his sickness.
Psalms	Ps	21	40	5	I said: O Lord, be thou merciful to me: heal my soul, for I have sinned against thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	40	6	My enemies have spoken evils against me: when shall he die and his name perish?
Psalms	Ps	21	40	7	And if he came in to see me, he spoke vain things: his heart gathered together iniquity to itself. He went out and spoke to the same purpose.
Psalms	Ps	21	40	8	All my enemies whispered together against me: they devised evils to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	40	9	They determined against me an unjust word: shall he that sleepeth rise again no more?
Psalms	Ps	21	40	10	For even the man of peace, in whom I trusted, who ate my bread, hath greatly supplanted me.
Psalms	Ps	21	40	11	But thou, O Lord, have mercy on me, and raise me up again: and I will requite them.
Psalms	Ps	21	40	12	By this I know, that thou hast had a good will for me: because my enemy shall not rejoice over me.
Psalms	Ps	21	40	13	But thou hast upheld me by reason of my innocence: and hast established me in thy sight for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	40	14	Blessed be the Lord the God of Israel from eternity to eternity. So be it. So be it.
Psalms	Ps	21	41	1	[Unto the end, understanding for the sons of Core.]
Psalms	Ps	21	41	2	As the hart panteth after the fountains of water; so my soul panteth after thee, O God.
Psalms	Ps	21	41	3	My soul hath thirsted after the strong living God; when shall I come and appear before the face of God?
Psalms	Ps	21	41	4	My tears have been my bread day and night, whilst it is said to me daily: Where is thy God?
Psalms	Ps	21	41	5	These things I remembered, and poured out my soul in me: for I shall go over into the place of the wonderful tabernacle, even to the house of God: With the voice of joy and praise; the noise of one feasting.
Psalms	Ps	21	41	6	Why art thou sad, O my soul? and why dost thou trouble me? Hope in God, for I will still give praise to him: the salvation of my countenance,
Psalms	Ps	21	41	7	And my God. My soul is troubled within myself: therefore will I remember thee from the land of Jordan and Hermoniim, from the little hill.
Psalms	Ps	21	41	8	Deep calleth on deep, at the noise of thy flood-gates. All thy heights and thy billows have passed over me.
Psalms	Ps	21	41	9	In the daytime the Lord hath commanded his mercy; and a canticle to him in the night. With me is prayer to the God of my life.
Psalms	Ps	21	41	10	I will say to God: Thou art my support. Why hast thou forgotten me? and why go I mourning, whilst my enemy afflicteth me?
Psalms	Ps	21	41	11	Whilst my bones are broken, my enemies who trouble me have reproached me; Whilst they say to me day by day: Where is thy God?
Psalms	Ps	21	41	12	Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why dost thou disquiet me? Hope thou in God, for I will still give praise to him: the salvation of my countenance, and my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	42	1	[A psalm for David.] Judge me, O God, and distinguish my cause from the nation that is not holy: deliver me from the unjust and deceitful man.
Psalms	Ps	21	42	2	For thou art God my strength: why hast thou cast me off? and why do I go sorrowful whilst the enemy afflicteth me?
Psalms	Ps	21	42	3	Send forth thy light and thy truth: they have conducted me, and brought me unto thy holy hill, and into thy tabernacles.
Psalms	Ps	21	42	4	And I will go in to the altar of God: to God who giveth joy to my youth.
Psalms	Ps	21	42	5	To thee, O God my God, I will give praise upon the harp: why art thou sad, O my soul? and why dost thou disquiet me?
Psalms	Ps	21	42	6	Hope in God, for I will still give praise to him: the salvation of my countenance, and my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	1	[Unto the end, for the sons of Core, to give understanding.]
Psalms	Ps	21	43	2	We have heard, O God, with our ears: our fathers have declared to us, The work, thou hast wrought in their days, and in the days of old.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	3	Thy hand destroyed the Gentiles, and thou plantedst them: thou didst afflict the people and cast them out.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	4	For they got not the possession of the land by their own sword: neither did their own arm save them. But thy right hand and thy arm, and the light of thy countenance: because thou wast pleased with them.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	5	Thou art thyself my king and my God, who commandest the saving of Jacob.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	6	Through thee we will push down our enemies with the horn: and through thy name we will despise them that rise up against us.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	7	For I will not trust in my bow: neither shall my sword save me.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	8	But thou hast saved us from them that afflict us: and hast put them to shame that hate us.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	9	In God shall we glory all the day long: and in thy name we will give praise for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	10	But now thou hast cast us off, and put us to shame: and thou, O God, wilt not go out with our armies.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	11	Thou hast made us turn our back to our enemies: and they that hated us plundered for themselves.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	12	Thou hast given us up like sheep to be eaten: thou hast scattered us among the nations.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	13	Thou hast sold thy people for no price: and there was no reckoning in the exchange of them.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	14	Thou hast made us a reproach to our neighbours, a scoff and derision to them that are round about us.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	15	Thou hast made us a byword among the Gentiles: a shaking of the head among the people.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	16	All the day long my shame is before me: and the confusion of my face hath covered me,
Psalms	Ps	21	43	17	At the voice of him that reproacheth and detracteth me: at the face of the enemy and persecutor.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	18	All these things have come upon us, yet we have not forgotten thee: and we have not done wickedly in thy covenant.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	19	And our heart hath not turned back: neither hast thou turned aside our steps from thy way.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	20	For thou hast humbled us in the place of affliction: and the shadow of death hath covered us.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	21	If we have forgotten the name of our God, and if we have spread forth our hands to a strange god:
Psalms	Ps	21	43	22	Shall not God search out these things: for he knoweth the secrets of the heart. Because for thy sake we are killed all the day long: we are counted as sheep for the slaughter.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	23	Arise, why sleepest thou, O Lord? arise, and cast us not off to the end.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	24	Why turnest thou thy face away? and forgettest our want and our trouble?
Psalms	Ps	21	43	25	For our soul is humbled down to the dust: our belly cleaveth to the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	43	26	Arise, O Lord, help us and redeem us for thy name's sake.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	1	[Unto the end, for them that shall be changed, for the sons of Core, for understanding. A canticle for the Beloved.]
Psalms	Ps	21	44	2	My heart hath uttered a good word: I speak my works to the king; My tongue is the pen of a scrivener that writeth swiftly.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	3	Thou art beautiful above the sons of men: grace is poured abroad in thy lips; therefore hath God blessed thee for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	4	Gird thy sword upon thy thigh, O thou most mighty.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	5	With thy comeliness and thy beauty set out, proceed prosperously, and reign. Because of truth and meekness and justice: and thy right hand shall conduct thee wonderfully.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	6	Thy arrows are sharp: under thee shall people fall, into the hearts of the king's enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	7	Thy throne, O God, is for ever and ever: the sceptre of thy kingdom is a sceptre of uprightness.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	8	Thou hast loved justice, and hated iniquity: therefore God, thy God, hath anointed thee with the oil of gladness above thy fellows.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	9	Myrrh and stacte and cassia perfume thy garments, from the ivory houses: out of which
Psalms	Ps	21	44	10	The daughters of kings have delighted thee in thy glory. The queen stood on thy right hand, in gilded clothing; surrounded with variety.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	11	Hearken, O daughter, and see, and incline thy ear: and forget thy people and thy father's house.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	12	And the king shall greatly desire thy beauty; for he is the Lord thy God, and him they shall adore.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	13	And the daughters of Tyre with gifts, yea, all the rich among the people, shall entreat thy countenance.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	14	All the glory of the king's daughter is within in golden borders,
Psalms	Ps	21	44	15	Clothed round about with varieties. After her shall virgins be brought to the king: her neighbours shall be brought to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	16	They shall be brought with gladness and rejoicing: they shall be brought into the temple of the king.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	17	Instead of thy fathers, sons are born to thee: thou shalt make them princes over all the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	44	18	They shall remember thy name throughout all generations. Therefore shall people praise thee for ever; yea, for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	45	1	[Unto the end, for the sons of Core, for the hidden.]
Psalms	Ps	21	45	2	Our God is our refuge and strength: a helper in troubles, which have found us exceedingly.
Psalms	Ps	21	45	3	Therefore we will not fear, when the earth shall be troubled; and the mountains shall be removed into the heart of the sea.
Psalms	Ps	21	45	4	Their waters roared and were troubled: the mountains were troubled with his strength.
Psalms	Ps	21	45	5	The stream of the river maketh the city of God joyful: the most High hath sanctified his own tabernacle.
Psalms	Ps	21	45	6	God is in the midst thereof, it shall not be moved: God will help it in the morning early.
Psalms	Ps	21	45	7	Nations were troubled, and kingdoms were bowed down: he uttered his voice, the earth trembled.
Psalms	Ps	21	45	8	The Lord of armies is with us: the God of Jacob is our protector.
Psalms	Ps	21	45	9	Come and behold ye the works of the Lord: what wonders he hath done upon earth,
Psalms	Ps	21	45	10	Making wars to cease even to the end of the earth. He shall destroy the bow, and break the weapons: and the shield he shall burn in the fire.
Psalms	Ps	21	45	11	Be still and see that I am God; I will be exalted among the nations, and I will be exalted in the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	45	12	The Lord of armies is with us: the God of Jacob is our protector.
Psalms	Ps	21	46	1	[Unto the end, for the sons of Core.]
Psalms	Ps	21	46	2	O clap your hands, all ye nations: shout unto God with the voice of Joy,
Psalms	Ps	21	46	3	For the Lord is high, terrible: a great king over all the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	46	4	He hath subdued the people under us; and the nations under our feet.
Psalms	Ps	21	46	5	He hath chosen for us his inheritance the beauty of Jacob which he hath loved.
Psalms	Ps	21	46	6	God is ascended with jubilee, and the Lord with the sound of trumpet.
Psalms	Ps	21	46	7	Sing praises to our God, sing ye: sing praises to our king, sing ye.
Psalms	Ps	21	46	8	For God is the king of all the earth: sing ye wisely.
Psalms	Ps	21	46	9	God shall reign over the nations: God sitteth on his holy throne.
Psalms	Ps	21	46	10	The princes of the people are gathered together, with the God of Abraham: for the strong gods of the earth are exceedingly exalted.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	1	[A psalm of a canticle, for the sons of Core, on the second day of the week.]
Psalms	Ps	21	47	2	Great is the Lord, and exceedingly to be praised in the city of our God, in his holy mountain.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	3	With the joy of the whole earth is mount Sion founded, on the sides of the north, the city of the great king.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	4	In her houses shall God be known, when he shall protect her.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	5	For behold the kings of the earth assembled themselves: they gathered together.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	6	So they saw, and they wondered, they were troubled, they were moved:
Psalms	Ps	21	47	7	Trembling took hold of them. There were pains as of a woman in labour.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	8	With a vehement wind thou shalt break in pieces the ships of Tharsis.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	9	As we have heard, so have we seen, in the city of the Lord of hosts, in the city of our God: God hath founded it for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	10	We have received thy mercy, O God, in the midst of thy temple.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	11	According to thy name, O God, so also is thy praise unto the ends of the earth: thy right hand is full of justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	12	Let mount Sion rejoice, and the daughters of Juda be glad; because of thy judgments, O Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	13	Surround Sion, and encompass her: tell ye in her towers.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	14	Set your hearts on her strength; and distribute her houses, that ye may relate it in another generation.
Psalms	Ps	21	47	15	For this is God, our God unto eternity, and for ever and ever: he shall rule us for evermore.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for the sons of Core.]
Psalms	Ps	21	48	2	Hear these things, all ye nations: give ear, all ye inhabitants of the world.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	3	All you that are earthborn, and you sons of men: both rich and poor together.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	4	My mouth shall speak wisdom: and the meditation of my heart understanding.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	5	I will incline my ear to a parable; I will open my proposition on the psaltery.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	6	Why shall I fear in the evil day? the iniquity of my heel shall encompass me.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	7	They that trust in their own strength, and glory in the multitude of their riches,
Psalms	Ps	21	48	8	No brother can redeem, nor shall man redeem: he shall not give to God his ransom,
Psalms	Ps	21	48	9	Nor the price of the redemption of his soul: and shall labour for ever,
Psalms	Ps	21	48	10	And shall still live unto the end.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	11	He shall not see destruction, when he shall see the wise dying: the senseless and the fool shall perish together: And they shall leave their riches to strangers:
Psalms	Ps	21	48	12	And their sepulchres shall be their houses for ever. Their dwelling places to all generations: they have called their lands by their names.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	13	And man when he was in honour did not understand; he is compared to senseless beasts, and is become like to them.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	14	This way of theirs is a stumblingblock to them: and afterwards they shall delight in their mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	15	They are laid in hell like sheep: death shall feed upon them. And the just shall have dominion over them in the morning; and their help shall decay in hell from their glory.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	16	But God will redeem my soul from the hand of hell, when he shall receive me.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	17	Be not thou afraid, when a man shall be made rich, and when the glory of his house shall be increased.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	18	For when he shall die he shall take nothing away; nor shall his glory descend with him.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	19	For in his lifetime his soul will be blessed: and he will praise thee when thou shalt do well to him.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	20	He shall go in to the generations of his fathers: and he shall never see light.
Psalms	Ps	21	48	21	Man when he was in honour did not understand: he hath been compared to senseless beasts, and made like to them.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	1	[A psalm for Asaph.] The God of gods, the Lord hath spoken: and he hath called the earth. From the rising of the sun, to the going down thereof:
Psalms	Ps	21	49	2	Out of Sion the loveliness of his beauty.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	3	God shall come manifestly: our God shall come, and shall not keep silence. A fire shall burn before him: and a mighty tempest shall be round about him.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	4	He shall call heaven from above, and the earth, to judge his people.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	5	Gather ye together his saints to him: who set his covenant before sacrifices.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	6	And the heavens shall declare his justice: for God is judge.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	7	Hear, O my people, and I will speak: O Israel, and I will testify to thee: I am God, thy God.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	8	I will not reprove thee for thy sacrifices: and thy burnt offerings are always in my sight.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	9	I will not take calves out of thy house: nor he goats out of thy flocks.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	10	For all the beasts of the woods are mine: the cattle on the hills, and the oxen.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	11	I know all the fowls of the air: and with me is the beauty of the field.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	12	If I should be hungry, I would not tell thee: for the world is mine, and the fulness thereof.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	13	Shall I eat the flesh of bullocks? or shall I drink the blood of goats?
Psalms	Ps	21	49	14	Offer to God the sacrifice of praise: and pay thy vows to the most High.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	15	And call upon me in the day of trouble: I will deliver thee, and thou shalt glorify me.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	16	But to the sinner God hath said: Why dost thou declare my justices, and take my covenant in thy mouth?
Psalms	Ps	21	49	17	Seeing thou hast hated discipline: and hast cast my words behind thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	18	If thou didst see a thief thou didst run with him: and with adulterers thou hast been a partaker.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	19	Thy mouth hath abounded with evil, and thy tongue framed deceits.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	20	Sitting thou didst speak against thy brother, and didst lay a scandal against thy mother's son:
Psalms	Ps	21	49	21	These things hast thou done, and I was silent. Thou thoughtest unjustly that I should be like to thee: but I will reprove thee, and set before thy face.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	22	Understand these things, you that forget God; lest he snatch you away, and there be none to deliver you.
Psalms	Ps	21	49	23	The sacrifice of praise shall glorify me: and there is the way by which I will shew him the salvation of God.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	1	[Unto the end, a psalm of David,
Psalms	Ps	21	50	2	When Nathan the prophet came to him after he had sinned with Bethsabee.]
Psalms	Ps	21	50	3	Have mercy on me, O God, according to thy great mercy. And according to the multitude of thy tender mercies blot out my iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	4	Wash me yet more from my iniquity, and cleanse me from my sin.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	5	For I know my iniquity, and my sin is always before me.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	6	To thee only have I sinned, and have done evil before thee: that thou mayst be justified in thy words and mayst overcome when thou art judged.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	7	For behold I was conceived in iniquities; and in sins did my mother conceive me.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	8	For behold thou hast loved truth: the uncertain and hidden things of thy wisdom thou hast made manifest to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	9	Thou shalt sprinkle me with hyssop, and I shall be cleansed: thou shalt wash me, and I shall be made whiter than snow.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	10	To my hearing thou shalt give joy and gladness: and the bones that have been humbled shall rejoice.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	11	Turn away thy face from my sins, and blot out all my iniquities.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	12	Create a clean heart in me, O God: and renew a right spirit within my bowels.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	13	Cast me not away from thy face; and take not thy holy spirit from me.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	14	Restore unto me the joy of thy salvation, and strengthen me with a perfect spirit.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	15	I will teach the unjust thy ways: and the wicked shall be converted to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	16	Deliver me from blood, O God, thou God of my salvation: and my tongue shall extol thy justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	17	O Lord, thou wilt open my lips: and my mouth shall declare thy praise.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	18	For if thou hadst desired sacrifice, I would indeed have given it: with burnt offerings thou wilt not be delighted.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	19	A sacrifice to God is an afflicted spirit: a contrite and humbled heart, O God, thou wilt not despise.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	20	Deal favourably, O Lord, in thy good will with Sion; that the walls of Jerusalem may be built up.
Psalms	Ps	21	50	21	Then shalt thou accept the sacrifice of justice, oblations and whole burnt offerings: then shall they lay calves upon thy altar.
Psalms	Ps	21	51	1	[Unto the end, understanding for David,
Psalms	Ps	21	51	2	When Doeg the Edomite came and told Saul David went to the house of Achimelech.]
Psalms	Ps	21	51	3	Why dost thou glory in malice, thou that art mighty in iniquity?
Psalms	Ps	21	51	4	All the day long thy tongue hath devised injustice: as a sharp razor, thou hast wrought deceit.
Psalms	Ps	21	51	5	Thou hast loved malice more than goodness: and iniquity rather than to speak righteousness.
Psalms	Ps	21	51	6	Thou hast loved all the words of ruin, O deceitful tongue.
Psalms	Ps	21	51	7	Therefore will God destroy thee for ever: he will pluck thee out, and remove thee from thy dwelling place: and thy root out of the land of the living.
Psalms	Ps	21	51	8	The just shall see and fear, and shall laugh at him, and say:
Psalms	Ps	21	51	9	Behold the man that made not God his helper: But trusted in the abundance of his riches: and prevailed in his vanity.
Psalms	Ps	21	51	10	But I, as a fruitful olive tree in the house of God, have hoped in the mercy of God for ever, yea for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	51	11	I will praise thee for ever, because thou hast done it: and I will wait on thy name, for it is good in the sight of thy saints.
Psalms	Ps	21	52	1	[Unto the end, for Maeleth, understandings to David.] The fool said in his heart: There is no God.
Psalms	Ps	21	52	2	They are corrupted, and become abominable in iniquities: there is none that doth good.
Psalms	Ps	21	52	3	God looked down from heaven on the children of men: to see if there were any that did understand, or did seek God.
Psalms	Ps	21	52	4	All have gone aside, they are become unprofitable together, there is none that doth good, no not one.
Psalms	Ps	21	52	5	Shall not all the workers of iniquity know, who eat up my people as they eat bread?
Psalms	Ps	21	52	6	They have not called upon God: there have they trembled for fear, where there was no fear. For God hath scattered the bones of them that please men: they have been confounded, because God hath despised them.
Psalms	Ps	21	52	7	Who will give out of Sion the salvation of Israel? when God shall bring back the captivity of his people, Jacob shall rejoice, and Israel shall be glad.
Psalms	Ps	21	53	1	[Unto the end, In verses, understanding for David.
Psalms	Ps	21	53	2	When the men of Ziph had come and said to Saul: Is not David hidden with us?]
Psalms	Ps	21	53	3	Save me, O God, by thy name, and judge me in thy strength.
Psalms	Ps	21	53	4	O God, hear my prayer: give ear to the words of my mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	53	5	For strangers have risen up against me; and the mighty have sought after my soul: and they have not set God before their eyes.
Psalms	Ps	21	53	6	For behold God is my helper: and the Lord is the protector of my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	53	7	Turn back the evils upon my enemies; and cut them off in thy truth.
Psalms	Ps	21	53	8	I will freely sacrifice to thee, and will give praise, O God, to thy name: because it is good:
Psalms	Ps	21	53	9	For thou hast delivered me out of all trouble: and my eye hath looked down upon my enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	1	[Unto the end, in verses, understanding for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	54	2	Hear, O God, my prayer, and despise not my supplication:
Psalms	Ps	21	54	3	Be attentive to me and hear me. I am grieved in my exercise; and am troubled,
Psalms	Ps	21	54	4	At the voice of the enemy, and at the tribulation of the sinner. For they have cast iniquities upon me: and in wrath they were troublesome to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	5	My heart is troubled within me: and the fear of death is fallen upon me.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	6	Fear and trembling are come upon me: and darkness hath covered me.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	7	And I said: Who will give me wings like a dove, and I will fly and be at rest?
Psalms	Ps	21	54	8	Lo, I have gone far off flying away; and I abode in the wilderness.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	9	I waited for him that hath saved me from pusillanimity of spirit, and a storm.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	10	Cast down, O Lord, and divide their tongues; for I have seen iniquity and contradiction in the city.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	11	Day and night shall iniquity surround it upon its walls: and in the midst thereof are labour,
Psalms	Ps	21	54	12	And injustice. And usury and deceit have not departed from its streets.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	13	For if my enemy had reviled me, I would verily have borne with it. And if he that hated me had spoken great things against me, I would perhaps have hidden myself from him.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	14	But thou a man of one mind, my guide, and my familiar,
Psalms	Ps	21	54	15	Who didst take sweetmeats together with me: in the house of God we walked with consent.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	16	Let death come upon them, and let them go down alive into hell. For there is wickedness in their dwellings: in the midst of them.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	17	But I have cried to God: and the Lord will save me.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	18	Evening and morning, and at noon I will speak and declare: and he shall hear my voice.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	19	He shall redeem my soul in peace from them that draw near to me: for among many they were with me.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	20	God shall hear, and the Eternal shall humble them. For there is no change with them, and they have not feared God:
Psalms	Ps	21	54	21	He hath stretched forth his hand to repay. They have defiled his covenant,
Psalms	Ps	21	54	22	They are divided by the wrath Of his countenance, and his heart hath drawn near. His words are smoother than oil, and the same are darts.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	23	Cast thy care upon the Lord, and he shall sustain thee: he shall not suffer the just to waver for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	54	24	But thou, O God, shalt bring them down into the pit of destruction. Bloody and deceitful men shall not live out half their days; but I will trust in thee, O Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	55	1	[Unto the end, for a people that is removed at a distance from the sanctuary for David, for an inscription of a title (or pillar) when the Philistines held him in Geth.]
Psalms	Ps	21	55	2	Have mercy on me, O God, for man hath trodden me under foot; all the day long he hath afflicted me fighting against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	55	3	My enemies have trodden on me all the day long; for they are many that make war against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	55	4	From the height of the day I shall fear: but I will trust in thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	55	5	In God I will praise my words, in God I have put my trust: I will not fear what flesh can do against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	55	6	All the day long they detested my words: all their thoughts were against me unto evil.
Psalms	Ps	21	55	7	They will dwell and hide themselves: they will watch my heel. As they have waited for my soul,
Psalms	Ps	21	55	8	For nothing shalt thou save them: in thy anger thou shalt break the people in pieces, O God,
Psalms	Ps	21	55	9	I have declared to thee my life: thou hast set my tears in thy sight, As also in thy promise.
Psalms	Ps	21	55	10	Then shall my enemies be turned back. In what day soever I shall call upon thee, behold I know thou art my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	55	11	In God will I praise the word, in the Lord will I praise his speech. In God have I hoped, I will not fear what man can do to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	55	12	In me, O God, are vows to thee, which I will pay, praises to thee:
Psalms	Ps	21	55	13	Because thou hast delivered my soul from death, my feet from falling: that I may please in the sight of God, in the light of the living.
Psalms	Ps	21	56	1	[Unto the end, destroy not, for David, for an inscription of a title, when he fled from Saul into the cave.]
Psalms	Ps	21	56	2	Have mercy on me, O God, have mercy on me: for my soul trusteth in thee. And in the shadow of thy wings will I hope, until iniquity pass away.
Psalms	Ps	21	56	3	I will cry to God the most High; to God who hath done good to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	56	4	He hath sent from heaven and delivered me: he hath made them a reproach that trod upon me. God hath sent his mercy and his truth,
Psalms	Ps	21	56	5	And he hath delivered my soul from the midst of the young lions. I slept troubled. The sons of men, whose teeth are weapons and arrows, and their tongue a sharp sword.
Psalms	Ps	21	56	6	Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens, and thy glory above all the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	56	7	They prepared a snare for my feet; and they bowed down my soul. They dug a pit before my face, and they are fallen into it.
Psalms	Ps	21	56	8	My heart is ready, O God, my heart is ready: I will Sing, and rehearse a psalm.
Psalms	Ps	21	56	9	Arise, O my glory, arise psaltery and harp: I will arise early.
Psalms	Ps	21	56	10	I will give praise to thee, O Lord, among the people: I will sing a psalm to thee among the nations.
Psalms	Ps	21	56	11	For thy mercy is magnified even to the heavens: and thy truth unto the clouds.
Psalms	Ps	21	56	12	Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens: and thy glory above all the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	57	1	[Unto the end, destroy not, for David, for an inscription of a title.]
Psalms	Ps	21	57	2	If in very deed you speak justice: judge right things, ye sons of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	57	3	For in your heart you work iniquity: your hands forge injustice in the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	57	4	The wicked are alienated from the womb; they have gone astray from the womb: they have spoken false things.
Psalms	Ps	21	57	5	Their madness is according to the likeness of a serpent: like the deaf asp that stoppeth her ears:
Psalms	Ps	21	57	6	Which will not hear the voice of the charmers; nor of the wizard that charmeth wisely.
Psalms	Ps	21	57	7	God shall break in pieces their teeth in their mouth: the Lord shall break the grinders of the lions.
Psalms	Ps	21	57	8	They shall come to nothing, like water running down; he hath bent his bow till they be weakened.
Psalms	Ps	21	57	9	Like wax that melteth they shall be taken away: fire hath fallen on them, and they shall not see the sun.
Psalms	Ps	21	57	10	Before your thorns could know the brier; he swalloweth them up, as alive, in his wrath.
Psalms	Ps	21	57	11	The just shall rejoice when he shall see the revenge: he shall wash his hands in the blood of the sinner.
Psalms	Ps	21	57	12	And man shall say: If indeed there be fruit to the just: there is indeed a God that judgeth them on the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	1	[Unto the end, destroy not, for David for an inscription of It title, when Saul sent and watched his house to kill him.]
Psalms	Ps	21	58	2	Deliver me from my enemies, O my God; and defend me from them that rise up against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	3	Deliver me from them that work iniquity, and save me from bloody men.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	4	For behold they have caught my soul: the mighty have rushed in upon me:
Psalms	Ps	21	58	5	Neither is it my iniquity, nor my sin, O Lord: without iniquity have I run, and directed my steps.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	6	Rise up thou to meet me, and behold: even thou, O Lord, the God of hosts, the God of Israel. Attend to visit all the nations: have no mercy on all them that work iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	7	They shall return at evening, and shall suffer hunger like dogs: and shall go round about the city.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	8	Behold they shall speak with their mouth, and a sword is in their lips: for who, say they, hath heard us?
Psalms	Ps	21	58	9	But thou, O Lord, shalt laugh at them: thou shalt bring all the nations to nothing.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	10	I will keep my strength to thee: for thou art my protector:
Psalms	Ps	21	58	11	My God, his mercy shall prevent me.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	12	God shall let me see over my enemies: slay them not, lest at any time my people forget. Scatter them by thy power; and bring them down, O Lord, my protector:
Psalms	Ps	21	58	13	For the sin of their mouth, and the word of their lips: and let them be taken in their pride. And for their cursing and lying they shall be talked of,
Psalms	Ps	21	58	14	When they are consumed: when they are consumed by thy wrath, and they shall be no more. And they shall know that God will rule Jacob, and all the ends of the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	15	They shall return at evening and shall suffer hunger like dogs: and shall go round about the city.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	16	They shall be scattered abroad to eat, and shall murmur if they be not filled.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	17	But I will sing thy strength: and will extol thy mercy in the morning. For thou art become my support, and my refuge, in the day of my trouble.
Psalms	Ps	21	58	18	Unto thee, O my helper, will I sing, for thou art God my defence: my God my mercy.
Psalms	Ps	21	59	1	[Unto the end, for them that shall be changed, for the inscription of a title, to David himself, for doctrine,
Psalms	Ps	21	59	2	When he set fire to Mesopotamia of Syria and Sobal and Joab returned and slew of Edom, in the vale of the saltpits, twelve thousand men.]
Psalms	Ps	21	59	3	O God, thou hast cast us off, and hast destroyed us; thou hast been angry, and hast had mercy on us.
Psalms	Ps	21	59	4	Thou hast moved the earth, and hast troubled it: heal thou the breaches thereof, for it has been moved.
Psalms	Ps	21	59	5	Thou hast shewn thy people hard things; thou hast made us drink wine of sorrow.
Psalms	Ps	21	59	6	Thou hast given a warning to them that fear thee: that they may flee from before the bow: That thy beloved may be delivered.
Psalms	Ps	21	59	7	Save me with thy right hand, and hear me.
Psalms	Ps	21	59	8	God hath spoken in his holy place: I will rejoice, and I will divide Sichem; and will mete out the vale of tabernacles.
Psalms	Ps	21	59	9	Galaad is mine, and Manasses is mine: and Ephraim is the strength of my head. Juda is my king:
Psalms	Ps	21	59	10	Moab is the pot of my hope. Into Edom will I stretch out my shoe: to me the foreigners are made subject.
Psalms	Ps	21	59	11	Who will bring me into the strong city? who will lead me into Edom?
Psalms	Ps	21	59	12	Wilt not thou, O God, who hast cast us off? and wilt not thou, O God, go out with our armies?
Psalms	Ps	21	59	13	Give us help from trouble: for vain is the salvation of man.
Psalms	Ps	21	59	14	Through God we shall do mightily: and he shall bring to nothing them that afflict us.
Psalms	Ps	21	60	1	[Unto the end, in hymns, for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	60	2	Hear, O God, my supplication: be attentive to my prayer,
Psalms	Ps	21	60	3	To thee have I cried from the ends of the earth: when my heart was in anguish, thou hast exalted me on a rock. Thou hast conducted me;
Psalms	Ps	21	60	4	For thou hast been my hope; a tower of strength against the face of the enemy.
Psalms	Ps	21	60	5	In thy tabernacle I shall dwell for ever: I shall be protected under the covert of thy wings.
Psalms	Ps	21	60	6	For thou, my God, hast heard my prayer: thou hast given an inheritance to them that fear thy name.
Psalms	Ps	21	60	7	Thou wilt add days to the days of the king: his years even to generation and generation.
Psalms	Ps	21	60	8	He abideth for ever in the sight of God: his mercy and truth who shall search?
Psalms	Ps	21	60	9	So will I sing a psalm to thy name for ever and ever: that I may pay my vows from day to day.
Psalms	Ps	21	61	1	[Unto the end, for Idithun, a psalm of David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	61	2	Shall not my soul be subject to God? for from him is my salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	61	3	For he is my God and my saviour: he is my protector, I shall be moved no more.
Psalms	Ps	21	61	4	How long do you rush in upon a man? you all kill, as if you were thrusting down a leaning wall, and a tottering fence.
Psalms	Ps	21	61	5	But they have thought to cast away my price; I ran in thirst: they blessed with their mouth, but cursed with their heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	61	6	But be thou, O my soul, subject to God: for from him is my patience.
Psalms	Ps	21	61	7	For he is my God and my saviour: he is my helper, I shall not be moved.
Psalms	Ps	21	61	8	In God is my salvation and my glory: he is the God of my help, and my hope is in God.
Psalms	Ps	21	61	9	Trust in him, all ye congregation of people: pour out your hearts before him. God is our helper for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	61	10	But vain are the sons of men, the sons of men are liars in the balances: that by vanity they may together deceive.
Psalms	Ps	21	61	11	Trust not in iniquity, and cover not robberies: if riches abound, set not your heart upon them.
Psalms	Ps	21	61	12	God hath spoken once, these two things have I heard, that power belongeth to God,
Psalms	Ps	21	61	13	And mercy to thee, O Lord; for thou wilt render to every man according to his works.
Psalms	Ps	21	62	1	[A psalm of David when he was in the desert of Edom.]
Psalms	Ps	21	62	2	O God, my God, to thee do I watch at break of day. For thee my soul hath thirsted; for thee my flesh, O how many ways!
Psalms	Ps	21	62	3	In a desert land, and where there is no way, and no water: so in the sanctuary have I come before thee, to see thy power and thy glory.
Psalms	Ps	21	62	4	For thy mercy is better than lives: thee my lips shall praise.
Psalms	Ps	21	62	5	Thus will I bless thee all my life long: and in thy name I will lift up my hands.
Psalms	Ps	21	62	6	Let my soul be filled as with marrow and fatness: and my mouth shall praise thee with joyful lips.
Psalms	Ps	21	62	7	If I have remembered thee upon my bed, I will meditate on thee in the morning:
Psalms	Ps	21	62	8	Because thou hast been my helper. And I will rejoice under the covert of thy wings:
Psalms	Ps	21	62	9	My soul hath stuck close to thee: thy right hand hath received me.
Psalms	Ps	21	62	10	But they have sought my soul in vain, they shall go into the lower parts of the earth:
Psalms	Ps	21	62	11	They shall be delivered into the hands of the sword, they shall be the portions of foxes.
Psalms	Ps	21	62	12	But the king shall rejoice in God, all they shall be praised that swear by him: because the mouth is stopped of them that speak wicked things.
Psalms	Ps	21	63	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	63	2	Hear, O God, my prayer, when I make supplication to thee: deliver my soul from the fear of the enemy.
Psalms	Ps	21	63	3	Thou hast protected me from the assembly of the malignant; from the multitude of the workers of iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	63	4	For they have whetted their tongues like a sword; they have bent their bow a bitter thing,
Psalms	Ps	21	63	5	To shoot in secret the undefiled.
Psalms	Ps	21	63	6	They will shoot at him on a sudden, and will not fear: they are resolute in wickedness. They have talked of hiding snares; they have said: Who shall see them?
Psalms	Ps	21	63	7	They have searched after iniquities: they have failed in their search. Man shall come to a deep heart:
Psalms	Ps	21	63	8	And God shall be exalted. The arrows of children are their wounds:
Psalms	Ps	21	63	9	And their tongues against them are made weak. All that saw them were troubled;
Psalms	Ps	21	63	10	And every man was afraid. And they declared the works of God: and understood his doings.
Psalms	Ps	21	63	11	The just shall rejoice in the Lord, and shall hope in him: and all the upright in heart shall be praised.
Psalms	Ps	21	64	1	[To the end, a psalm of David. The canticle of Jeremias and Ezechiel to the people of the captivity, when they began to go out.]
Psalms	Ps	21	64	2	A Hymn, O God, becometh thee in Sion: and a vow shall be paid to thee in Jerusalem.
Psalms	Ps	21	64	3	O hear my prayer: all flesh shall come to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	64	4	The words of the wicked have prevailed over us: and thou wilt pardon our transgressions.
Psalms	Ps	21	64	5	Blessed is he whom thou hast chosen and taken to thee: he shall dwell in thy courts. We shall be filled with the good things of thy house; holy is thy temple,
Psalms	Ps	21	64	6	Wonderful in justice. Hear us, O God our saviour, who art the hope of all the ends of the earth, and in the sea afar off.
Psalms	Ps	21	64	7	Thou who preparest the mountains by thy strength, being girded with power:
Psalms	Ps	21	64	8	Who troublest the depth of the sea, the noise of its waves. The Gentiles shall be troubled,
Psalms	Ps	21	64	9	And they that dwell in the uttermost borders shall be afraid at thy signs: thou shalt make the outgoings of the morning and of the evening to be joyful.
Psalms	Ps	21	64	10	Thou hast visited the earth, and hast plentifully watered it; thou hast many ways enriched it. The river of God is filled with water, thou hast prepared their food: for so is its preparation.
Psalms	Ps	21	64	11	Fill up plentifully the streams thereof, multiply its fruits; it shall spring up and rejoice in its showers.
Psalms	Ps	21	64	12	Thou shalt bless the crown of the year of thy goodness: and thy fields shall be filled with plenty.
Psalms	Ps	21	64	13	The beautiful places of the wilderness shall grow fat: and the hills shall be girded about with joy,
Psalms	Ps	21	64	14	The rams of the flock are clothed, and the vales shall abound with corn: they shall shout, yea they shall sing a hymn.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	1	[Unto the end, a canticle of a psalm of the resurrection.] Shout with joy to God, all the earth,
Psalms	Ps	21	65	2	Sing ye a psalm to his name; give glory to his praise.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	3	Say unto God, How terrible are thy works, O Lord! in the multitude of thy strength thy enemies shall lie to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	4	Let all the earth adore thee, and sing to thee: let it sing a psalm to thy name.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	5	Come and see the works of God; who is terrible in his counsels over the sons of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	6	Who turneth the sea into dry land, in the river they shall pass on foot: there shall we rejoice in him.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	7	Who by his power ruleth for ever: his eyes behold the nations; let not them that provoke him be exalted in themselves.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	8	O bless our God, ye Gentiles: and make the voice of his praise to be heard.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	9	Who hath set my soul to live: and hath not suffered my feet to be moved:
Psalms	Ps	21	65	10	For thou, O God, hast proved us: thou hast tried us by fire, as silver is tried.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	11	Thou hast brought us into a net, thou hast laid afflictions on our back:
Psalms	Ps	21	65	12	Thou hast set men over our heads. We have passed through fire and water, and thou hast brought us out into a refreshment.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	13	I will go into thy house with burnt offerings: I will pay thee my vows,
Psalms	Ps	21	65	14	Which my lips have uttered, And my mouth hath spoken, when I was in trouble.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	15	I will offer up to thee holocausts full of marrow, with burnt offerings of rams: I will offer to thee bullocks with goats.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	16	Come and hear, all ye that fear God, and I will tell you what great things he hath done for my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	17	I cried to him with my mouth: and I extolled him with my tongue.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	18	If I have looked at iniquity in my heart, the Lord will not hear me.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	19	Therefore hath God heard me, and hath attended to the voice of my supplication.
Psalms	Ps	21	65	20	Blessed be God, who hath not turned away my prayer, nor his mercy from me.
Psalms	Ps	21	66	1	[Unto the end, in, hymns, a psalm of a canticle for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	66	2	May God have mercy on us, and bless us: may he cause the light of his countenance to shine upon us, and may he have mercy on us.
Psalms	Ps	21	66	3	That we may know thy way upon earth: thy salvation in all nations.
Psalms	Ps	21	66	4	Let people confess to thee, O God: let all people give praise to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	66	5	Let the nations be glad and rejoice: for thou judgest the people with justice, and directest the nations upon earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	66	6	Let the people, O God, confess to thee: let all the people give praise to thee:
Psalms	Ps	21	66	7	The earth hath yielded her fruit. May God, our God bless us,
Psalms	Ps	21	66	8	May God bless us: and all the ends of the earth fear him.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	1	[Unto the end, a psalm of a canticle for David himself.]
Psalms	Ps	21	67	2	Let God arise, and let his enemies be scattered: and let them that hate him flee from before his face.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	3	As smoke vanisheth, so let them vanish away: as wax melteth before the fire, so let the wicked perish at the presence of God.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	4	And let the just feast, and rejoice before God: and be delighted with gladness.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	5	Sing ye to God, sing a psalm to his name, make a way for him who ascendeth upon the west: the Lord is his name. Rejoice ye before him: but the wicked shall be troubled at his presence,
Psalms	Ps	21	67	6	Who is the father of orphans, and the judge of widows. God in his holy place:
Psalms	Ps	21	67	7	God who maketh men of one manner to dwell in a house: Who bringeth out them that were bound in strength; in like manner them that provoke, that dwell in sepulchres.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	8	O God, when thou didst go forth in the sight of thy people, when thou didst pass through the desert:
Psalms	Ps	21	67	9	The earth was moved, and the heavens dropped at the presence of the God of Sina, at the presence of the God of Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	10	Thou shalt set aside for thy inheritance a free rain, O God: and it was weakened, but thou hast made it perfect.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	11	In it shall thy animals dwell; in thy sweetness, O God, thou hast provided for the poor.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	12	The Lord shall give the word to them that preach good tidings with great power.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	13	The king of powers is of the beloved, of the beloved; and the beauty of the house shall divide spoils.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	14	If you sleep among the midst of lots, you shall be as the wings of a dove covered with silver, and the hinder parts of her back with the paleness of gold.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	15	When he that is in heaven appointeth kings over her, they shall be whited with snow in Selmon.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	16	The mountain of God is a fat mountain. A curdled mountain, a fat mountain.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	17	Why suspect, ye curdled mountains? A mountain in which God is well pleased to dwell: for there the Lord shall dwell unto the end.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	18	The chariot of God is attended by ten thousands; thousands of them that rejoice: the Lord is among them in Sina, in the holy place.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	19	Thou hast ascended on high, thou hast led captivity captive; thou hast received gifts in men. Yea for those also that do not believe, the dwelling of the Lord God.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	20	Blessed be the Lord day by day: the God of our salvation will make our journey prosperous to us.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	21	Our God is the God of salvation: and of the Lord, of the Lord are the issues from death.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	22	But God shall break the heads of his enemies: the hairy crown of them that walk on in their sins.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	23	The Lord said: I will turn them from Basan, I will turn them into the depth of the sea:
Psalms	Ps	21	67	24	That thy foot may be dipped in the blood of thy enemies; the tongue of thy dogs be red with the same.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	25	They have seen thy goings, O God, the goings of my God: of my king who is in his sanctuary.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	26	Princes went before joined with singers, in the midst of young damsels playing on timbrels.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	27	In the churches bless ye God the Lord, from the fountains of Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	28	There is Benjamin a youth, in ecstasy of mind. The princes of Juda are their leaders: the princes of Zabulon, the princes of Nephthali.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	29	Command thy strength, O God: confirm, O God, what thou hast wrought in us.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	30	From thy temple in Jerusalem, kings shall offer presents to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	31	Rebuke the wild beasts of the reeds, the congregation of bulls with the kine of the people; who seek to exclude them who are tried with silver. Scatter thou the nations that delight in wars:
Psalms	Ps	21	67	32	Ambassadors shall come out of Egypt: Ethiopia shall soon stretch out her hands to God.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	33	Sing to God, ye kingdoms of the earth: sing ye to the Lord: Sing ye to God,
Psalms	Ps	21	67	34	Who mounteth above the heaven of heavens, to the east. Behold he will give to his voice the voice of power:
Psalms	Ps	21	67	35	Give ye glory to God for Israel, his magnificence, and his power is in the clouds.
Psalms	Ps	21	67	36	God is wonderful in his saints: the God of Israel is he who will give power and strength to his people. Blessed be God.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	1	[Unto the end, for them that shall be changed; for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	68	2	Save me, O God: for the waters are come in even unto my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	3	I stick fast in the mire of the deep: and there is no sure standing. I am come into the depth of the sea: and a tempest hath overwhelmed me.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	4	I have laboured with crying; my jaws are become hoarse: my eyes have failed, whilst I hope in my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	5	They are multiplied above the hairs of my head, who hate me without cause. My enemies are grown strong who have wrongfully persecuted me: then did I pay that which I took not away.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	6	O God, thou knowest my foolishness; and my offences are not hidden from thee:
Psalms	Ps	21	68	7	Let not them be ashamed for me, who look for thee, O Lord, the Lord of hosts. Let them not be confounded on my account, who seek thee, O God of Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	8	Because for thy sake I have borne reproach; shame hath covered my face.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	9	I am become a stranger to my brethren, and an alien to the sons of my mother.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	10	For the zeal of thy house hath eaten me up: and the reproaches of them that reproached thee are fallen upon me.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	11	And I covered my soul in fasting: and it was made a reproach to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	12	And I made haircloth my garment: and I became a byword to them.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	13	They that sat in the gate spoke against me: and they that drank wine made me their song.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	14	But as for me, my prayer is to thee, O Lord; for the time of thy good pleasure, O God. In the multitude of thy mercy hear me, in the truth of thy salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	15	Draw me out of the mire, that I may not stick fast: deliver me from them that hate me, and out of the deep waters.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	16	Let not the tempest of water drown me, nor the deep swallow me up: and let not the pit shut her mouth upon me.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	17	Hear me, O Lord, for thy mercy is kind; look upon me according to the multitude of thy tender mercies.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	18	And turn not away thy face from thy servant: for I am in trouble, hear me speedily.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	19	Attend to my soul, and deliver it: save me because of my enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	20	Thou knowest my reproach, and my confusion, and my shame.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	21	In thy sight are all they that afflict me; my heart hath expected reproach and misery. And I looked for one that would grieve together with me, but there was none: and for one that would comfort me, and I found none.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	22	And they gave me gall for my food, and in my thirst they gave me vinegar to drink.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	23	Let their table become as a snare before them, and a recompense, and a stumblingblock.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	24	Let their eyes be darkened that they see not; and their back bend thou down always.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	25	Pour out thy indignation upon them: and let thy wrathful anger take hold of them.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	26	Let their habitation be made desolate: and let there be none to dwell in their tabernacles.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	27	Because they have persecuted him whom thou hast smitten; and they have added to the grief of my wounds.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	28	Add thou iniquity upon their iniquity: and let them not come into thy justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	29	Let them be blotted out of the book of the living; and with the just let them not be written.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	30	But I am poor and sorrowful: thy salvation, O God, hath set me up.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	31	I will praise the name of God with a canticle: and I will magnify him with praise.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	32	And it shall please God better than a young calf, that bringeth forth horns and hoofs.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	33	Let the poor see and rejoice: seek ye God, and your soul shall live.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	34	For the Lord hath heard the poor: and hath not despised his prisoners.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	35	Let the heavens and the earth praise him; the sea, and every thing that creepeth therein.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	36	For God will save Sion, and the cities of Juda shall be built up. And they shall dwell there, and acquire it by inheritance.
Psalms	Ps	21	68	37	And the seed of his servants shall possess it; and they that love his name shall dwell therein.
Psalms	Ps	21	69	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for David, to bring to remembrance that the Lord saved him.]
Psalms	Ps	21	69	2	O God, come to my assistance; O Lord, make haste to help me.
Psalms	Ps	21	69	3	Let them be confounded and ashamed that seek my soul:
Psalms	Ps	21	69	4	Let them be turned backward, and blush for shame that desire evils to me: Let them be presently turned away blushing for shame that say to me: Tis well, tis well.
Psalms	Ps	21	69	5	Let all that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee; and let such as love thy salvation say always: The Lord be magnified.
Psalms	Ps	21	69	6	But I am needy and poor; O God, help me. Thou art my helper and my deliverer: O Lord, make no delay.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	1	[A psalm for David. Of the sons of Jonadab, and the former captives.] In thee, O Lord, I have hoped, let me never be put to confusion:
Psalms	Ps	21	70	2	Deliver me in thy justice, and rescue me. Incline thy ear unto me, and save me.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	3	Be thou unto me a God, a protector, and a place of strength: that thou mayst make me safe. For thou art my firmament and my refuge.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	4	Deliver me, O my God, out of the hand of the sinner, and out of the hand of the transgressor of the law and of the unjust.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	5	For thou art my patience, O Lord: my hope, O Lord, from my youth;
Psalms	Ps	21	70	6	By thee have I been confirmed from the womb: from my mother's womb thou art my protector. Of thee shall I continually sing:
Psalms	Ps	21	70	7	I am become unto many as a wonder, but thou art a strong helper.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	8	Let my mouth be filled with praise, that I may sing thy glory; thy greatness all the day long.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	9	Cast me not off in the time of old age: when my strength shall fail, do not thou forsake me.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	10	For my enemies have spoken against me; and they that watched my soul have consulted together,
Psalms	Ps	21	70	11	Saying: God hath forsaken him: pursue and take him, for there is none to deliver him.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	12	O God, be not thou far from me: O my God, make haste to my help.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	13	Let them be confounded and come to nothing that detract my soul; let them be covered with confusion and shame that seek my hurt.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	14	But I will always hope; and will add to all thy praise.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	15	My mouth shall shew forth thy justice; thy salvation all the day long. Because I have not known learning,
Psalms	Ps	21	70	16	I will enter into the powers of the Lord: O Lord, I will be mindful of thy justice alone.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	17	Thou hast taught me, O God, from my youth: and till now I will declare thy wonderful works.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	18	And unto old age and grey hairs: O God, forsake me not, Until I shew forth thy arm to all the generation that is to come: Thy power,
Psalms	Ps	21	70	19	And thy justice, O God, even to the highest great things thou hast done: O God, who is like to thee?
Psalms	Ps	21	70	20	How great troubles hast thou shewn me, many and grievous: and turning thou hast brought me to life, and hast brought me back again from the depths of the earth:
Psalms	Ps	21	70	21	Thou hast multiplied thy magnificence; and turning to me thou hast comforted me.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	22	For I will also confess to thee thy truth with the instruments of psaltery: O God, I will sing to thee with the harp, thou holy one of Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	23	My lips shall greatly rejoice, when I shall sing to thee; and my soul which thou hast redeemed.
Psalms	Ps	21	70	24	Yea and my tongue shall meditate on thy justice all the day; when they shall be confounded and put to shame that seek evils to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	1	[A psalm on Solomon.]
Psalms	Ps	21	71	2	Give to the king thy judgment, O God: and to the king's son thy justice: To judge thy people with justice, and thy poor with judgment.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	3	Let the mountains receive peace for the people: and the hills justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	4	He shall judge the poor of the people, and he shall save the children of the poor: and he shall humble the oppressor.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	5	And he shall continue with the sun, and before the moon, throughout all generations.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	6	He shall come down like rain upon the fleece; and as showers falling gently upon the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	7	In his days shall justice spring up, and abundance of peace, till the moon be taken away.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	8	And he shall rule from sea to sea, and from the river unto the ends of the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	9	Before him the Ethiopians shall fall down: and his enemies shall lick the ground.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	10	The kings of Tharsis and the islands shall offer presents: the kings of the Arabians and of Saba shall bring gifts:
Psalms	Ps	21	71	11	And all kings of the earth shall adore him: all nations shall serve him.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	12	For he shall deliver the poor from the mighty: and the needy that had no helper.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	13	He shall spare the poor and needy: and he shall save the souls of the poor.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	14	He shall redeem their souls from usuries and iniquity: and their names shall be honourable in his sight.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	15	And he shall live, and to him shall be given of the gold of Arabia, for him they shall always adore: they shall bless him all the day.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	16	And there shall be a firmament on the earth on the tops of mountains, above Libanus shall the fruit thereof be exalted: and they of the city shall flourish like the grass of the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	17	Let his name be blessed for evermore: his name continueth before the sun. And in him shall all the tribes of the earth be blessed: all nations shall magnify him.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	18	Blessed be the Lord, the God of Israel, who alone doth wonderful things.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	19	And blessed be the name of his majesty for ever: and the whole earth shall be filled with his majesty. So be it. So be it.
Psalms	Ps	21	71	20	The praises of David, the son of Jesse, are ended.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	1	[A psalm for Asaph.] How good is God to Israel, to them that are of a right heart!
Psalms	Ps	21	72	2	But my feet were almost moved; my steps had well nigh slipped.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	3	Because I had a zeal on occasion of the wicked, seeing the prosperity of sinners.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	4	For there is no regard to their death, nor is there strength in their stripes.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	5	They are not in the labour of men: neither shall they be scourged like other men.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	6	Therefore pride hath held them fast: they are covered with their iniquity and their wickedness.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	7	Their iniquity hath come forth, as it were from fatness: they have passed into the affection of the heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	8	They have thought and spoken wickedness: they have spoken iniquity on high.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	9	They have set their mouth against heaven: and their tongue hath passed through the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	10	Therefore will my people return here and full days shall be found in them.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	11	And they said: How doth God know? and is there knowledge in the most High?
Psalms	Ps	21	72	12	Behold these are sinners; and yet abounding in the world they have obtained riches.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	13	And I said: Then have I in vain justified my heart, and washed my hands among the innocent.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	14	And I have been scourged all the day; and my chastisement hath been in the mornings.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	15	If I said: I will speak thus; behold I should condemn the generation of thy children.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	16	I studied that I might know this thing, it is a labour in my sight:
Psalms	Ps	21	72	17	Until I go into the sanctuary of God, and understand concerning their last ends.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	18	But indeed for deceits thou hast put it to them: when they were lifted up thou hast cast them down.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	19	How are they brought to desolation? they have suddenly ceased to be: they have perished by reason of their iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	20	As the dream of them that awake, O Lord; so in thy city thou shalt bring their image to nothing.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	21	For my heart hath been inflamed, and my reins have been changed:
Psalms	Ps	21	72	22	And I am brought to nothing, and I knew not.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	23	I am become as a beast before thee: and I am always with thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	24	Thou hast held me by my right hand; and by thy will thou hast conducted me, and with thy glory thou hast received me.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	25	For what have I in heaven? and besides thee what do I desire upon earth?
Psalms	Ps	21	72	26	For thee my flesh and my heart hath fainted away: thou art the God of my heart, and the God that is my portion for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	27	For behold they that go far from thee shall perish: thou hast destroyed all them that are disloyal to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	72	28	But it is good for me to adhere to my God, to put my hope in the Lord God: That I may declare all thy praises, in the gates of the daughter of Sion.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	1	[Understanding for Asaph.] O God, why hast thou cast us off unto the end: why is thy wrath enkindled against the sheep of thy pasture?
Psalms	Ps	21	73	2	Remember thy congregation, which thou hast possessed from the beginning. The sceptre of thy inheritance which thou hast redeemed: mount Sion in which thou hast dwelt.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	3	Lift up thy hands against their pride unto the end; see what things the enemy hath done wickedly in the sanctuary.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	4	And they that hate thee have made their boasts, in the midst of thy solemnity. They have set up their ensigns for signs,
Psalms	Ps	21	73	5	And they knew not both in the going out and on the highest top. As with axes in a wood of trees,
Psalms	Ps	21	73	6	They have cut down at once the gates thereof, with axe and hatchet they have brought it down.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	7	They have set fire to thy sanctuary: they have defiled the dwelling place of thy name on the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	8	They said in their heart, the whole kindred of them together: Let us abolish all the festival days of God from the land.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	9	Our signs we have not seen, there is now no prophet: and he will know us no more.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	10	How long, O God, shall the enemy reproach: is the adversary to provoke thy name for ever?
Psalms	Ps	21	73	11	Why dost thou turn away thy hand: and thy right hand out of the midst of thy bosom for ever?
Psalms	Ps	21	73	12	But God is our king before ages: he hath wrought salvation in the midst of the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	13	Thou by thy strength didst make the sea firm: thou didst crush the heads of the dragons in the waters.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	14	Thou hast broken the heads of the dragon: thou hast given him to be meat for the people of the Ethiopians.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	15	Thou hast broken up the fountains and the torrents: thou hast dried up the Ethan rivers.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	16	Thine is the day, and thine is the night: thou hast made the morning light and the sun.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	17	Thou hast made all the borders of the earth: the summer and the spring were formed by thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	18	Remember this, the enemy hath reproached the Lord: and a foolish people hath provoked thy name.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	19	Deliver not up to beasts the souls that confess to thee: and forget not to the end the souls of thy poor.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	20	Have regard to thy covenant: for they that are the obscure of the earth have been filled with dwellings of iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	21	Let not the humble be turned away with confusion: the poor and needy shall praise thy name.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	22	Arise, O God, judge thy own cause: remember thy reproaches with which the foolish man hath reproached thee all the day.
Psalms	Ps	21	73	23	Forget not the voices of thy enemies: the pride of them that hate thee ascendeth continually.
Psalms	Ps	21	74	1	[Unto the end, corrupt not, a psalm of a canticle for Asaph.]
Psalms	Ps	21	74	2	We will praise thee, O God: we will praise, and we will call upon thy name. We will relate thy wondrous works:
Psalms	Ps	21	74	3	When I shall take a time, I will judge justices.
Psalms	Ps	21	74	4	The earth is melted, and all that dwell therein: I have established the pillars thereof.
Psalms	Ps	21	74	5	I said to the wicked: Do not act wickedly: and to the sinners: Lift not up the horn.
Psalms	Ps	21	74	6	Lift not up your horn on high: speak not iniquity against God.
Psalms	Ps	21	74	7	For neither from the east, nor from the west, nor from the desert hills:
Psalms	Ps	21	74	8	For God is the judge. One he putteth down, and another he lifteth up:
Psalms	Ps	21	74	9	For in the hand of the Lord there is a cup of strong wine full of mixture. And he hath poured it out from this to that: but the dregs thereof are not emptied: all the sinners of the earth shall drink.
Psalms	Ps	21	74	10	But I will declare for ever: I will sing to the God of Jacob.
Psalms	Ps	21	74	11	And I will break all the horns of sinners: but the horns of the just shall be exalted.
Psalms	Ps	21	75	1	[Unto the end, in praises, a psalm for Asaph: a canticle to the Assyrians.]
Psalms	Ps	21	75	2	In Judea God is known: his name is great in Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	75	3	And his place is in peace: and his abode in Sion:
Psalms	Ps	21	75	4	There hath he broken the powers of bows, the shield, the sword, and the battle.
Psalms	Ps	21	75	5	Thou enlightenest wonderfully from the everlasting hills.
Psalms	Ps	21	75	6	All the foolish of heart were troubled. They have slept their sleep; and all the men of riches have found nothing in their hands.
Psalms	Ps	21	75	7	At thy rebuke, O God of Jacob, they have all slumbered that mounted on horseback.
Psalms	Ps	21	75	8	Thou art terrible, and who shall resist thee? from that time thy wrath.
Psalms	Ps	21	75	9	Thou hast caused judgment to be heard from heaven: the earth trembled and was still,
Psalms	Ps	21	75	10	When God arose in judgment, to save all the meek of the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	75	11	For the thought of man shall give praise to thee: and the remainders of the thought shall keep holiday to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	75	12	Vow ye, and pay to the Lord your God: all you that are round about him bring presents. To him that is terrible,
Psalms	Ps	21	75	13	Even to him who taketh away the spirit of princes: to the terrible with the kings of the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	1	[Unto the end, for Idithun, a psalm of Asaph.]
Psalms	Ps	21	76	2	I cried to the Lord with my voice; to God with my voice, and he gave ear to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	3	In the day of my trouble I sought God, with my hands lifted up to him in the night, and I was not deceived. My soul refused to be comforted:
Psalms	Ps	21	76	4	I remembered God, and was delighted, and was exercised, and my spirit swooned away.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	5	My eyes prevented the watches: I was troubled, and I spoke not.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	6	I thought upon the days of old: and I had in my mind the eternal years.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	7	And I meditated in the night with my own heart: and I was exercised and I swept my spirit.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	8	Will God then cast off for ever? or will he never be more favourable again?
Psalms	Ps	21	76	9	Or will he cut off his mercy for ever, from generation to generation?
Psalms	Ps	21	76	10	Or will God forget to shew mercy? or will he in his anger shut up his mercies?
Psalms	Ps	21	76	11	And I said, Now have I begun: this is the change of the right hand of the most High.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	12	I remembered the works of the Lord: for I will be mindful of thy wonders from the beginning.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	13	And I will meditate on all thy works: and will be employed in thy inventions.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	14	Thy way, O God, is in the holy place: who is the great God like our God?
Psalms	Ps	21	76	15	Thou art the God that dost wonders. Thou hast made thy power known among the nations:
Psalms	Ps	21	76	16	With thy arm thou hast redeemed thy people the children of Jacob and of Joseph.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	17	The waters saw thee, O God, the waters saw thee: and they were afraid, and the depths were troubled.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	18	Great was the noise of the waters: the clouds sent out a sound. For thy arrows pass:
Psalms	Ps	21	76	19	The voice of thy thunder in a wheel. Thy lightnings enlightened the world: the earth shook and trembled.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	20	Thy way is in the sea, and thy paths in many waters: and thy footsteps shall not be known.
Psalms	Ps	21	76	21	Thou hast conducted thy people like sheep, by the hand of Moses and Aaron.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	1	[Understanding for Asaph.] Attend, O my people, to my law: incline your ears to the words of my mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	2	I will open my mouth in parables: I will utter propositions from the beginning.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	3	How great things have we heard and known, and our fathers have told us.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	4	They have not been hidden from their children, in another generation. Declaring the praises of the Lord, and his powers, and his wonders which he hath done.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	5	And he set up a testimony in Jacob: and made a law in Israel. How great things he commanded our fathers, that they should make the same known to their children:
Psalms	Ps	21	77	6	That another generation might know them. The children that should be born and should rise up, and declare them to their children.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	7	That they may put their hope in God and may not forget the works of God: and may seek his commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	8	That they may not become like their fathers, a perverse and exasperating generation. A generation that set not their heart aright: and whose spirit was not faithful to God.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	9	The sons of Ephraim who bend and shoot with the bow: they have turned back in the day of battle.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	10	They kept not the covenant of God: and in his law they would not walk.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	11	And they forgot his benefits, and his wonders that he had shewn them.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	12	Wonderful things did he do in the sight of their fathers, in the land of Egypt, in the field of Tanis.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	13	He divided the sea and brought them through: and he made the waters to stand as in a vessel.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	14	And he conducted them with a cloud by day: and all the night with a light of fire.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	15	He struck the rock in the wilderness: and gave them to drink, as out of the great deep.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	16	He brought forth water out of the rock: and made streams run down as rivers.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	17	And they added yet more sin against him: they provoked the most High to wrath in the place without water.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	18	And they tempted God in their hearts, by asking meat for their desires.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	19	And they spoke ill of God: they said: Can God furnish a table in the wilderness?
Psalms	Ps	21	77	20	Because he struck the rock, and the waters gushed out, and the streams overflowed. Can he also give bread, or provide a table for his people?
Psalms	Ps	21	77	21	Therefore the Lord heard, and was angry: and a fire was kindled against Jacob, and wrath came up against Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	22	Because they believed not in God: and trusted not in his salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	23	And he had commanded the clouds from above, and had opened the doors of heaven.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	24	And had rained down manna upon them to eat, and had given them the bread of heaven.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	25	Man ate the bread of angels: he sent them provisions in abundance.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	26	He removed the south wind from heaven: and by his power brought in the southwest wind.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	27	And he rained upon them flesh as dust: and feathered fowls like as the sand of the sea.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	28	And they fell in the midst of their camp, round about their pavilions.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	29	So they did eat, and were filled exceedingly, and he gave them their desire:
Psalms	Ps	21	77	30	They were not defrauded of that which they craved. As yet their meat was in their mouth:
Psalms	Ps	21	77	31	And the wrath of God came upon them. And he slew the fat ones amongst them, and brought down the chosen men of Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	32	In all these things they sinned still: and they believed not for his wondrous works.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	33	And their days were consumed in vanity, and their years in haste.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	34	When he slew them, then they sought him: and they returned, and came to him early in the morning.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	35	And they remembered that God was their helper: and the most high God their redeemer.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	36	And they loved him with their mouth: and with their tongue they lied unto him:
Psalms	Ps	21	77	37	But their heart was not right with him: nor were they counted faithful in his covenant.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	38	But he is merciful, and will forgive their sins: and will not destroy them. And many a time did he turn away his anger: and did not kindle all his wrath.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	39	And he remembered that they are flesh: a wind that goeth and returneth not.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	40	How often did they provoke him in the desert: and move him to wrath in the place without water?
Psalms	Ps	21	77	41	And they turned back and tempted God: and grieved the holy one of Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	42	They remembered not his hand, in the day that he redeemed them from the hand of him that afflicted them:
Psalms	Ps	21	77	43	How he wrought his signs in Egypt, and his wonders in the field of Tanis.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	44	And he turned their rivers into blood, and their showers that they might not drink.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	45	He sent amongst them divers sores of flies, which devoured them: and frogs which destroyed them.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	46	And he gave up their fruits to the blast, and their labours to the locust.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	47	And he destroyed their vineyards with hail, and their mulberry trees with hoarfrost.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	48	And he gave up their cattle to the hail, and their stock to the fire.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	49	And he sent upon them the wrath of his indignation: indignation and wrath and trouble, which he sent by evil angels.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	50	He made a way for a path to his anger: he spared not their souls from death, and their cattle he shut up in death.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	51	And he killed all the firstborn in the land of Egypt: the firstfruits of all their labour in the tabernacles of Cham.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	52	And he took away his own people as sheep: and guided them in the wilderness like a flock.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	53	And he brought them out in hope, and they feared not: and the sea overwhelmed their enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	54	And he brought them into the mountain of his sanctuary: the mountain which his right hand had purchased. And he cast out the Gentiles before them: and by lot divided to them their land by a line of distribution.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	55	And he made the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tabernacles.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	56	Yet they tempted, and provoked the most high God: and they kept not his testimonies.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	57	And they turned away, and kept not the covenant: even like their fathers they were turned aside as a crooked bow.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	58	They provoked him to anger on their hills: and moved him to jealousy with their graven things.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	59	God heard, and despised them, and he reduced Israel exceedingly as it were to nothing.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	60	And he put away the tabernacle of Silo, his tabernacle where he dwelt among men.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	61	And he delivered their strength into captivity: and their beauty into the hands of the enemy.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	62	And he shut up his people under the sword: and he despised his inheritance.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	63	Fire consumed their young men: and their maidens were not lamented.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	64	Their priests fell by the sword: and their widows did not mourn.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	65	And the Lord was awaked as one out of sleep, and like a mighty man that hath been surfeited with wine.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	66	And he smote his enemies on the hinder parts: he put them to an everlasting reproach.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	67	And he rejected the tabernacle of Joseph: and chose not the tribe of Ephraim:
Psalms	Ps	21	77	68	But he chose the tribe of Juda, mount Sion which he loved.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	69	And he built his sanctuary as of unicorns, in the land which he founded for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	70	And he chose his servant David, and took him from the flocks of sheep: he brought him from following the ewes great with young,
Psalms	Ps	21	77	71	To feed Jacob his servant, and Israel his inheritance.
Psalms	Ps	21	77	72	And he fed them in the innocence of his heart: and conducted them by the skillfulness of his hands.
Psalms	Ps	21	78	1	[A psalm for Asaph.] O God, the heathens are come into thy inheritance, they have defiled thy holy temple: they have made Jerusalem as a place to keep fruit.
Psalms	Ps	21	78	2	They have given the dead bodies of thy servants to be meat for the fowls of the air: the flesh of thy saints for the beasts of the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	78	3	They have poured out their blood as water, round about Jerusalem and there was none to bury them.
Psalms	Ps	21	78	4	We are become a reproach to our neighbours: a scorn and derision to them that are round about us.
Psalms	Ps	21	78	5	How long, O Lord, wilt thou be angry for ever: shall thy zeal be kindled like a fire?
Psalms	Ps	21	78	6	Pour out thy wrath upon the nations that have not known thee: and upon the kingdoms that have not called upon thy name.
Psalms	Ps	21	78	7	Because they have devoured Jacob; and have laid waste his place.
Psalms	Ps	21	78	8	Remember not our former iniquities: let thy mercies speedily prevent us, for we are become exceeding poor.
Psalms	Ps	21	78	9	Help us, O God, our saviour: and for the glory of thy name, O Lord, deliver us: and forgive us our sins for thy name's sake:
Psalms	Ps	21	78	10	Lest they should say among the Gentiles: Where is their God? And let him be made known among the nations before our eyes, By the revenging the blood of thy servants, which hath been shed:
Psalms	Ps	21	78	11	Let the sighing of the prisoners come in before thee. According to the greatness of thy arm, take possession of the children of them that have been put to death.
Psalms	Ps	21	78	12	And render to our neighbours sevenfold in their bosom: the reproach wherewith they have reproached thee, O Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	78	13	But we thy people, and the sheep of thy pasture, will give thanks to thee for ever. We will shew forth thy praise, unto generation and generation.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	1	[Unto the end, for them that shall be changed, a testimony for Asaph, a psalm.]
Psalms	Ps	21	79	2	Give ear, O thou that rulest Israel: thou that leadest Joseph like a sheep. Thou that sittest upon the cherubims, shine forth
Psalms	Ps	21	79	3	Before Ephraim, Benjamin, and Manasses. Stir up thy might, and come to save us.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	4	Convert us, O God: and shew us thy face, and we shall be saved.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	5	O Lord God of hosts, how long wilt thou be angry against the prayer of thy servant?
Psalms	Ps	21	79	6	How long wilt thou feed us with the bread of tears: and give us for our drink tears in measure?
Psalms	Ps	21	79	7	Thou hast made us to be a contradiction to our neighbours: and our enemies have scoffed at us.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	8	O God of hosts, convert us: and shew thy face, and we shall be saved.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	9	Thou hast brought a vineyard out of Egypt: thou hast cast out the Gentiles and planted it.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	10	Thou wast the guide of its journey in its sight: thou plantedst the roots thereof, and it filled the land.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	11	The shadow of it covered the hills: and the branches thereof the cedars of God.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	12	It stretched forth its branches unto the sea, and its boughs unto the river.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	13	Why hast thou broken down the hedge thereof, so that all they who pass by the way do pluck it?
Psalms	Ps	21	79	14	The boar out of the wood hath laid it waste: and a singular wild beast hath devoured it.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	15	Turn again, O God of hosts, look down from heaven, and see, and visit this vineyard:
Psalms	Ps	21	79	16	And perfect the same which thy right hand hath planted: and upon the son of man whom thou hast confirmed for thyself.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	17	Things set on fire and dug down shall perish at the rebuke of thy countenance.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	18	Let thy hand be upon the man of thy right hand: and upon the son of man whom thou hast confirmed for thyself.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	19	And we depart not from thee, thou shalt quicken us: and we will call upon thy name.
Psalms	Ps	21	79	20	O Lord God of hosts, convert us: and shew thy face, and we shall be saved.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	1	[Unto the end, for the winepresses, a psalm for Asaph himself.]
Psalms	Ps	21	80	2	Rejoice to God our helper: sing aloud to the God of Jacob.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	3	Take a psalm, and bring hither the timbrel: the pleasant psaltery with the harp.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	4	Blow up the trumpet on the new moon, on the noted day of your solemnity.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	5	For it is a commandment in Israel, and a judgment to the God of Jacob.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	6	He ordained it for a testimony in Joseph, when he came out of the land of Egypt: he heard a tongue which he knew not.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	7	He removed his back from the burdens: his hands had served in baskets.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	8	Thou calledst upon me in affliction, and I delivered thee: I heard thee in the secret place of tempest: I proved thee at the waters of contradiction.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	9	Hear, O my people, and I will testify to thee: O Israel, if thou wilt hearken to me,
Psalms	Ps	21	80	10	There shall be no new god in thee: neither shalt thou adore a strange god.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	11	For I am the Lord thy God, who brought thee out of the land of Egypt: open thy mouth wide, and I will fill it.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	12	But my people heard not my voice: and Israel hearkened not to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	13	So I let them go according to the desires of their heart: they shall walk in their own inventions.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	14	If my people had heard me: if Israel had walked in my ways:
Psalms	Ps	21	80	15	I should soon have humbled their enemies, and laid my hand on them that troubled them.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	16	The enemies of the Lord have lied to him: and their time shall be for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	80	17	And he fed them with the fat of wheat, and filled them with honey out of the rock.
Psalms	Ps	21	81	1	[A psalm for Asaph.] God hath stood in the congregation of gods: and being in the midst of them he judgeth gods.
Psalms	Ps	21	81	2	How long will you judge unjustly: and accept the persons of the wicked?
Psalms	Ps	21	81	3	Judge for the needy and fatherless: do justice to the humble and the poor.
Psalms	Ps	21	81	4	Rescue the poor; and deliver the needy out of the hand of the sinner.
Psalms	Ps	21	81	5	They have not known nor understood: they walk on in darkness: all the foundations of the earth shall be moved.
Psalms	Ps	21	81	6	I have said: You are gods and all of you the sons of the most High.
Psalms	Ps	21	81	7	But you like men shall die: and shall fall like one of the princes.
Psalms	Ps	21	81	8	Arise, O God, judge thou the earth: for thou shalt inherit among all the nations.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	1	[A canticle of a psalm for Asaph.]
Psalms	Ps	21	82	2	O God, who shall be like to thee? hold not thy peace, neither be thou still, O God.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	3	For lo, thy enemies have made a noise: and they that hate thee have lifted up the head.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	4	They have taken a malicious counsel against thy people, and have consulted against thy saints.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	5	They have said: Come and let us destroy them, so that they be not a nation: and let the name of Israel be remembered no more.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	6	For they have contrived with one consent: they have made a covenant together against thee,
Psalms	Ps	21	82	7	The tabernacles of the Edomites, and the Ismahelites: Moab, and the Agarens,
Psalms	Ps	21	82	8	Gebal, and Ammon and Amalec: the Philistines, with the inhabitants of Tyre.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	9	Yea, and the Assyrian also is joined with them: they are come to the aid of the sons of Lot.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	10	Do to them as thou didst to Madian and to Sisara: as to Jabin at the brook of Cisson.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	11	Who perished at Endor: and became as dung for the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	12	Make their princes like Oreb, and Zeb, and Zebee, and Salmana. All their princes,
Psalms	Ps	21	82	13	Who have said: Let us possess the sanctuary of God for an inheritance.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	14	O my God, make them like a wheel; and as stubble before the wind.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	15	As fire which burneth the wood: and as a flame burning mountains:
Psalms	Ps	21	82	16	So shalt thou pursue them with thy tempest: and shalt trouble them in thy wrath.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	17	Fill their faces with shame; and they shall seek thy name, O Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	18	Let them be ashamed and troubled for ever and ever: and let them be confounded and perish.
Psalms	Ps	21	82	19	And let them know that the Lord is thy name: thou alone art the most High over all the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	83	1	[Unto the end, for the winepresses, a psalm for the sons of Core.]
Psalms	Ps	21	83	2	How lovely are thy tabernacles, O Lord of hosts!
Psalms	Ps	21	83	3	My soul longeth and fainteth for the courts of the Lord. My heart and my flesh have rejoiced in the living God.
Psalms	Ps	21	83	4	For the sparrow hath found herself a house, and the turtle a nest for herself where she may lay her young ones: Thy altars, O Lord of hosts, my king and my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	83	5	Blessed are they that dwell in thy house, O Lord: they shall praise thee for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	83	6	Blessed is the man whose help is from thee: in his heart he hath disposed to ascend by steps,
Psalms	Ps	21	83	7	In the vale of tears, in the place which he hath set.
Psalms	Ps	21	83	8	For the lawgiver shall give a blessing, they shall go from virtue to virtue: the God of gods shall be seen in Sion.
Psalms	Ps	21	83	9	O Lord God of hosts, hear my prayer: give ear, O God of Jacob.
Psalms	Ps	21	83	10	Behold, O God our protector: and look on the face of thy Christ.
Psalms	Ps	21	83	11	For better is one day in thy courts above thousands. I have chosen to be an abject in the house of my God, rather than to dwell in the tabernacles of sinners.
Psalms	Ps	21	83	12	For God loveth mercy and truth: the Lord will give grace and glory.
Psalms	Ps	21	83	13	He will not deprive of good things them that walk in innocence: O Lord of hosts, blessed is the man that trusteth in thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	1	[Unto the end, for the sons of Core, a psalm.]
Psalms	Ps	21	84	2	Lord, thou hast blessed thy land: thou hast turned away the captivity of Jacob.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	3	Thou hast forgiven the iniquity of thy people: thou hast covered all their sins.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	4	Thou hast mitigated all thy anger: thou hast turned away from the wrath of thy indignation.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	5	Convert us, O God our saviour: and turn off thy anger from us.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	6	Wilt thou be angry with us for ever: or wilt thou extend thy wrath from generation to generation?
Psalms	Ps	21	84	7	Thou wilt turn, O God, and bring us to life: and thy people shall rejoice in thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	8	Shew us, O Lord, thy mercy; and grant us thy salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	9	I will hear what the Lord God will speak in me: for he will speak peace unto his people: And unto his saints: and unto them that are converted to the heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	10	Surely his salvation is near to them that fear him: that glory may dwell in our land.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	11	Mercy and truth have met each other: justice and peace have kissed.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	12	Truth is sprung out of the earth: and justice hath looked down from heaven.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	13	For the Lord will give goodness: and our earth shall yield her fruit.
Psalms	Ps	21	84	14	Justice shall walk before him: and shall set his steps in the way.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	1	[A prayer for David himself.] Incline thy ear, O Lord, and hear me: for I am needy and poor.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	2	Preserve my soul, for I am holy: save thy servant, O my God, that trusteth in thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	3	Have mercy on me, O Lord, for I have cried to thee all the day.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	4	Give joy to the soul of thy servant, for to thee, O Lord, I have lifted up my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	5	For thou, O Lord, art sweet and mild: and plenteous in mercy to all that call upon thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	6	Give ear, O Lord, to my prayer: and attend to the voice of my petition.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	7	I have called upon thee in the day of my trouble: because thou hast heard me.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	8	There is none among the gods like unto thee, O Lord: and there is none according to thy works.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	9	All the nations thou hast made shall come and adore before thee, O Lord: and they shall glorify thy name.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	10	For thou art great and dost wonderful things: thou art God alone.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	11	Conduct me, O Lord, in thy way, and I will walk in thy truth: let my heart rejoice that it may fear thy name.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	12	I will praise thee, O Lord my God: with my whole heart, and I will glorify thy name for ever:
Psalms	Ps	21	85	13	For thy mercy is great towards me: and thou hast delivered my soul out of the lower hell.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	14	O God, the wicked are risen up against me, and the assembly of the mighty have sought my soul: and they have not set thee before their eyes.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	15	And thou, O Lord, art a God of compassion, and merciful, patient, and of much mercy, and true.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	16	O look upon me, and have mercy on me: give thy command to thy servant, and save the son of thy handmaid.
Psalms	Ps	21	85	17	Shew me a token for good: that they who hate me may see, and be confounded, because thou, O Lord, hast helped me and hast comforted me.
Psalms	Ps	21	86	1	[For the sons of Core, a psalm of a canticle.] The foundations thereof are in the holy mountains:
Psalms	Ps	21	86	2	The Lord loveth the gates of Sion above all the tabernacles of Jacob.
Psalms	Ps	21	86	3	Glorious things are said of thee, O city of God.
Psalms	Ps	21	86	4	I will be mindful of Rahab and of Babylon knowing me. Behold the foreigners, and Tyre, and the people of the Ethiopians, these were there.
Psalms	Ps	21	86	5	Shall not Sion say: This man and that man is born in her? and the Highest himself hath founded her.
Psalms	Ps	21	86	6	The Lord shall tell in his writings of peoples and of princes, of them that have been in her.
Psalms	Ps	21	86	7	The dwelling in thee is as it were of all rejoicing.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	1	[A canticle of a psalm for the sons of Core: unto the end, for Maheleth, to answer understanding of Eman the Ezrahite.]
Psalms	Ps	21	87	2	O Lord, the God of my salvation: I have cried in the day, and in the night before thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	3	Let my prayer come in before thee: incline thy ear to my petition.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	4	For my soul is filled with evils: and my life hath drawn nigh to hell.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	5	I am counted among them that go down to the pit: I am become as a man without help,
Psalms	Ps	21	87	6	Free among the dead. Like the slain sleeping in the sepulchres, whom thou rememberest no more: and they are cast off from thy hand.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	7	They have laid me in the lower pit: in the dark places, and in the shadow of death.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	8	Thy wrath is strong over me: and all thy waves thou hast brought in upon me.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	9	Thou hast put away my acquaintance far from me: they have set me an abomination to themselves. I was delivered up, and came not forth:
Psalms	Ps	21	87	10	My eyes languished through poverty. All the day I cried to thee, O Lord: I stretched out my hands to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	11	Wilt thou shew wonders to the dead? or shall physicians raise to life, and give praise to thee?
Psalms	Ps	21	87	12	Shall any one in the sepulchre declare thy mercy: and thy truth in destruction?
Psalms	Ps	21	87	13	Shall thy wonders be known in the dark; and thy justice in the land of forgetfulness?
Psalms	Ps	21	87	14	But I, O Lord, have cried to thee: and in the morning my prayer shall prevent thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	15	Lord, why castest thou off my prayer: why turnest thou away thy face from me?
Psalms	Ps	21	87	16	I am poor, and in labours from my youth: and being exalted have been humbled and troubled.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	17	Thy wrath hath come upon me: and thy terrors have troubled me.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	18	They have come round about me like water all the day: they have compassed me about together.
Psalms	Ps	21	87	19	Friend and neighbour thou hast put far from me: and my acquaintance, because of misery.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	1	[Of understanding, for Ethan the Ezrahite.]
Psalms	Ps	21	88	2	The mercies of the Lord I will sing for ever. I will shew forth thy truth with my mouth to generation and generation.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	3	For thou hast said: Mercy shall be built up for ever in the heavens: thy truth shall be prepared in them.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	4	I have made a covenant with my elect: I have sworn to David my servant:
Psalms	Ps	21	88	5	Thy seed will I settle for ever. And I will build up thy throne unto generation and generation.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	6	The heavens shall confess thy wonders, O Lord: and thy truth in the church of the saints.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	7	For who in the clouds can be compared to the Lord: or who among the sons of God shall be like to God?
Psalms	Ps	21	88	8	God, who is glorified in the assembly of the saints: great and terrible above all them that are about him.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	9	O Lord God of hosts, who is like to thee? thou art mighty, O Lord, and thy truth is round about thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	10	Thou rulest the power of the sea: and appeasest the motion of the waves thereof.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	11	Thou hast humbled the proud one, as one that is slain: with the arm of thy strength thou hast scattered thy enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	12	Thine are the heavens, and thine is the earth: the world and the fulness thereof thou hast founded:
Psalms	Ps	21	88	13	The north and the sea thou hast created. Thabor and Hermon shall rejoice in thy name:
Psalms	Ps	21	88	14	Thy arm is with might. Let thy hand be strengthened, and thy right hand exalted:
Psalms	Ps	21	88	15	Justice and judgment are the preparation of thy throne. Mercy and truth shall go before thy face:
Psalms	Ps	21	88	16	Blessed is the people that knoweth jubilation. They shall walk, O Lord, in the light of thy countenance:
Psalms	Ps	21	88	17	And in thy name they shall rejoice all the day, and in thy justice they shall be exalted.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	18	For thou art the glory of their strength: and in thy good pleasure shall our horn be exalted.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	19	For our protection is of the Lord, and of our king the holy one of Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	20	Then thou spokest in a vision to thy saints, and saidst: I have laid help upon one that is mighty, and have exalted one chosen out of my people.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	21	I have found David my servant: with my holy oil I have anointed him.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	22	For my hand shall help him: and my arm shall strengthen him.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	23	The enemy shall have no advantage over him: nor the son of iniquity have power to hurt him.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	24	And I will cut down his enemies before his face; and them that hate him I will put to flight.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	25	And my truth and my mercy shall be with him: and in my name shall his horn be exalted.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	26	And I will set his hand in the sea; and his right hand in the rivers.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	27	He shall cry out to me: Thou art my father: my God, and the support of my salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	28	And I will make him my firstborn, high above the kings of the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	29	I will keep my mercy for him for ever: and my covenant faithful to him.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	30	And I will make his seed to endure for evermore: and his throne as the days of heaven.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	31	And if his children forsake my law, and walk not in my judgments:
Psalms	Ps	21	88	32	If they profane my justices: and keep not my commandments:
Psalms	Ps	21	88	33	I will visit their iniquities with a rod: and their sins with stripes.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	34	But my mercy I will not take away from him: nor will I suffer my truth to fail.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	35	Neither will I profane my covenant: and the words that proceed from my mouth I will not make void.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	36	Once have I sworn by my holiness: I will not lie unto David:
Psalms	Ps	21	88	37	His seed shall endure for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	38	And his throne as the sun before me: and as the moon perfect for ever, and a faithful witness in heaven.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	39	But thou hast rejected and despised: thou hast been angry with thy anointed.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	40	Thou hast overthrown the covenant of thy servant: thou hast profaned his sanctuary on the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	41	Thou hast broken down all his hedges: thou hast made his strength fear.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	42	All that pass by the way have robbed him: he is become a reproach to his neighbours.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	43	Thou hast set up the right hand of them that oppress him: thou hast made all his enemies to rejoice.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	44	Thou hast turned away the help of his sword; and hast not assisted him in battle.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	45	Thou hast made his purification to cease: and thou hast cast his throne down to the ground.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	46	Thou hast shortened the days of his time: thou hast covered him with confusion.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	47	How long, O Lord, turnest thou away unto the end? shall thy anger burn like fire?
Psalms	Ps	21	88	48	Remember what my substance is for hast thou made all the children of men in vain?
Psalms	Ps	21	88	49	Who is the man that shall live, and not see death: that shall deliver his soul from the hand of hell?
Psalms	Ps	21	88	50	Lord, where are thy ancient mercies, according to what thou didst swear to David in thy truth?
Psalms	Ps	21	88	51	Be mindful, O Lord, of the reproach of thy servants (which I have held in my bosom) of many nations:
Psalms	Ps	21	88	52	Wherewith thy enemies have reproached, O Lord; wherewith they have reproached the change of thy anointed.
Psalms	Ps	21	88	53	Blessed be the Lord for evermore. So be it. So be it.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	1	[A prayer of Moses the man of God.] Lord, thou hast been our refuge from generation to generation.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	2	Before the mountains were made, or the earth and the world was formed; from eternity and to eternity thou art God.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	3	Turn not man away to be brought low: and thou hast said: Be converted, O ye sons of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	4	For a thousand years in thy sight are as yesterday, which is past. And as a watch in the night,
Psalms	Ps	21	89	5	Things that are counted nothing, shall their years be.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	6	In the morning man shall grow up like grass; in the morning he shall flourish and pass away: in the evening he shall fall, grow dry, and wither.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	7	For in thy wrath we have fainted away: and are troubled in thy indignation.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	8	Thou hast set our iniquities before thy eyes: our life in the light of thy countenance.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	9	For all our days are spent; and in thy wrath we have fainted away. Our years shall be considered as a spider:
Psalms	Ps	21	89	10	The days of our years in them are threescore and ten years. But if in the strong they be fourscore years: and what is more of them is labour and sorrow. For mildness is come upon us: and we shall be corrected.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	11	Who knoweth the power of thy anger, and for thy fear
Psalms	Ps	21	89	12	Can number thy wrath? So make thy right hand known: and men learned in heart, in wisdom.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	13	Return, O Lord, how long? and be entreated in favour of thy servants.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	14	We are filled in the morning with thy mercy: and we have rejoiced, and are delighted all our days.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	15	We have rejoiced for the days in which thou hast humbled us: for the years in which we have seen evils.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	16	Look upon thy servants and upon their works: and direct their children.
Psalms	Ps	21	89	17	And let the brightness of the Lord our God be upon us: and direct thou the works of our hands over us; yea, the work of our hands do thou direct.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	1	[The praise of a canticle for David.] He that dwelleth in the aid of the most High, shall abide under the protection of the God of Jacob.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	2	He shall say to the Lord: Thou art my protector, and my refuge: my God, in him will I trust.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	3	For he hath delivered me from the snare of the hunters: and from the sharp word.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	4	He will overshadow thee with his shoulders: and under his wings thou shalt trust.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	5	His truth shall compass thee with a shield: thou shalt not be afraid of the terror of the night.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	6	Of the arrow that flieth in the day, of the business that walketh about in the dark: of invasion, or of the noonday devil.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	7	A thousand shall fall at thy side, and ten thousand at thy right hand: but it shall not come nigh thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	8	But thou shalt consider with thy eyes: and shalt see the reward of the wicked.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	9	Because thou, O Lord, art my hope: thou hast made the most High thy refuge.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	10	There shall no evil come to thee: nor shall the scourge come near thy dwelling.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	11	For he hath given his angels charge over thee; to keep thee in all thy ways.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	12	In their hands they shall bear thee up: lest thou dash thy foot against a stone.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	13	Thou shalt walk upon the asp and the basilisk: and thou shalt trample under foot the lion and the dragon.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	14	Because he hoped in me I will deliver him: I will protect him because he hath known my name.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	15	He shall cry to me, and I will hear him: I am with him in tribulation, I will deliver him, and I will glorify him.
Psalms	Ps	21	90	16	I will fill him with length of days; and I will shew him my salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	1	[A psalm of a canticle on the sabbath day.]
Psalms	Ps	21	91	2	It is good to give praise to the Lord: and to sing to thy name, O most High.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	3	To shew forth thy mercy in the morning, and thy truth in the night:
Psalms	Ps	21	91	4	Upon an instrument of ten strings, upon the psaltery: with a canticle upon the harp.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	5	For thou hast given me, O Lord, a delight in thy doings: and in the works of thy hands I shall rejoice.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	6	O Lord, how great are thy works! thy thoughts are exceeding deep.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	7	The senseless man shall not know: nor will the fool understand these things.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	8	When the wicked shall spring up as grass: and all the workers of iniquity shall appear: That they may perish for ever and ever:
Psalms	Ps	21	91	9	But thou, O Lord, art most high for evermore.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	10	For behold thy enemies, O Lord, for behold thy enemies shall perish: and all the workers of iniquity shall be scattered.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	11	But my horn shall be exalted like that of the unicorn: and my old age in plentiful mercy.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	12	My eye also hath looked down upon my enemies: and my ear shall hear of the downfall of the malignant that rise up against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	13	The just shall flourish like the palm tree: he shall grow up like the cedar of Libanus.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	14	They that are planted in the house of the Lord shall flourish in the courts of the house of our God.
Psalms	Ps	21	91	15	They shall still increase in a fruitful old age: and shall be well treated,
Psalms	Ps	21	91	16	That they may shew, That the Lord our God is righteous, and there is no iniquity in him.
Psalms	Ps	21	92	1	The Lord hath reigned, he is clothed with beauty: the Lord is clothed with strength, and hath girded himself. For he hath established the world which shall not be moved.
Psalms	Ps	21	92	2	Thy throne is prepared from of old: thou art from everlasting.
Psalms	Ps	21	92	3	The floods have lifted up, O Lord: the floods have lifted up their voice. The floods have lifted up their waves,
Psalms	Ps	21	92	4	With the noise of many waters. Wonderful are the surges of the sea: wonderful is the Lord on high.
Psalms	Ps	21	92	5	Thy testimonies are become exceedingly credible: holiness becometh thy house, O Lord, unto length of days.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	1	The Lord is the God to whom revenge belongeth: the God of revenge hath acted freely.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	2	Lift up thyself, thou that judgest the earth: render a reward to the proud.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	3	How long shall sinners, O Lord: how long shall sinners glory?
Psalms	Ps	21	93	4	Shall they utter, and speak iniquity: shall all speak who work injustice?
Psalms	Ps	21	93	5	Thy people, O Lord, they have brought low: and they have afflicted thy inheritance.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	6	They have slain the widow and the stranger: and they have murdered the fatherless.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	7	And they have said: The Lord shall not see: neither shall the God of Jacob understand.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	8	Understand, ye senseless among the people: and, you fools, be wise at last.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	9	He that planted the ear, shall he not hear? or he that formed the eye, doth he not consider?
Psalms	Ps	21	93	10	He that chastiseth nations, shall he not rebuke: he that teacheth man knowledge?
Psalms	Ps	21	93	11	The Lord knoweth the thoughts of men, that they are vain.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	12	Blessed is the man whom thou shalt instruct, O Lord: and shalt teach him out of thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	13	That thou mayst give him rest from the evil days: till a pit be dug for the wicked.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	14	For the Lord will not cast off his people: neither will he forsake his own inheritance.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	15	Until justice be turned into judgment: and they that are near it are all the upright in heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	16	Who shall rise up for me against the evildoers? or who shall stand with me against the workers of iniquity?
Psalms	Ps	21	93	17	Unless the Lord had been my helper, my soul had almost dwelt in hell.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	18	If I said: My foot is moved: thy mercy, O Lord, assisted me.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	19	According to the multitude of my sorrows in my heart, thy comforts have given joy to my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	20	Doth the seat of iniquity stick to thee, who framest labour in commandment?
Psalms	Ps	21	93	21	They will hunt after the soul of the just, and will condemn innocent blood.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	22	But the Lord is my refuge: and my God the help of my hope.
Psalms	Ps	21	93	23	And he will render them their iniquity: and in their malice he will destroy them: the Lord our God will destroy them.
Psalms	Ps	21	94	1	Come let us praise the Lord with joy: let us joyfully sing to God our saviour.
Psalms	Ps	21	94	2	Let us come before his presence with thanksgiving; and make a joyful noise to him with psalms.
Psalms	Ps	21	94	3	For the Lord is a great God, and a great King above all gods.
Psalms	Ps	21	94	4	For in his hand are all the ends of the earth: and the heights of the mountains are his.
Psalms	Ps	21	94	5	For the sea is his, and he made it: and his hands formed the dry land.
Psalms	Ps	21	94	6	Come let us adore and fall down: and weep before the Lord that made us.
Psalms	Ps	21	94	7	For he is the Lord our God: and we are the people of his pasture and the sheep of his hand.
Psalms	Ps	21	94	8	Today if you shall hear his voice, harden not your hearts:
Psalms	Ps	21	94	9	As in the provocation, according to the day of temptation in the wilderness: where your fathers tempted me, they proved me, and saw my works.
Psalms	Ps	21	94	10	Forty years long was I offended with that generation, and I said: These always err in heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	94	11	And these men have not known my ways: so I swore in my wrath that they shall not enter into my rest.
Psalms	Ps	21	95	1	[A canticle for David himself, when the house was built after the captivity.] Sing ye to the Lord a new canticle: sing to the Lord, all the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	95	2	Sing ye to the Lord and bless his name: shew forth his salvation from day to day.
Psalms	Ps	21	95	3	Declare his glory among the Gentiles: his wonders among all people.
Psalms	Ps	21	95	4	For the Lord is great, and exceedingly to be praised: he is to be feared above all gods.
Psalms	Ps	21	95	5	For all the gods of the Gentiles are devils: but the Lord made the heavens.
Psalms	Ps	21	95	6	Praise and beauty are before him: holiness and majesty in his sanctuary.
Psalms	Ps	21	95	7	Bring ye to the Lord, O ye kindreds of the Gentiles, bring ye to the Lord glory and honour:
Psalms	Ps	21	95	8	Bring to the Lord glory unto his name. Bring up sacrifices, and come into his courts:
Psalms	Ps	21	95	9	Adore ye the Lord in his holy court. Let all the earth be moved at his presence.
Psalms	Ps	21	95	10	Say ye among the Gentiles, the Lord hath reigned. For he hath corrected the world, which shall not be moved: he will judge the people with justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	95	11	Let the heavens rejoice, and let the earth be glad, let the sea be moved, and the fulness thereof:
Psalms	Ps	21	95	12	The fields and all things that are in them shall be joyful. Then shall all the trees of the woods rejoice
Psalms	Ps	21	95	13	Before the face of the Lord, because he cometh: because he cometh to judge the earth. He shall judge the world with justice, and the people with his truth.
Psalms	Ps	21	96	1	[For the same David, when his land was restored again to him.] The Lord hath reigned, let the earth rejoice: let many islands be glad.
Psalms	Ps	21	96	2	Clouds and darkness are round about him: justice and judgment are the establishment of his throne.
Psalms	Ps	21	96	3	A fire shall go before him, and shall burn his enemies round about.
Psalms	Ps	21	96	4	His lightnings have shone forth to the world: the earth saw and trembled.
Psalms	Ps	21	96	5	The mountains melted like wax, at the presence of the Lord: at the presence of the Lord of all the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	96	6	The heavens declared his justice: and all people saw his glory.
Psalms	Ps	21	96	7	Let them be all confounded that adore graven things, and that glory in their idols. Adore him, all you his angels:
Psalms	Ps	21	96	8	Sion heard, and was glad. And the daughters of Juda rejoiced, because of thy judgments, O Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	96	9	For thou art the most high Lord over all the earth: thou art exalted exceedingly above all gods.
Psalms	Ps	21	96	10	You that love the Lord, hate evil: the Lord preserveth the souls of his saints, he will deliver them out of the hand of the sinner.
Psalms	Ps	21	96	11	Light is risen to the just, and joy to the right of heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	96	12	Rejoice, ye just, in the Lord: and give praise to the remembrance of his holiness.
Psalms	Ps	21	97	1	[A psalm for David himself.] Sing ye to the Lord a new canticle: because he hath done wonderful things. His right hand hath wrought for him salvation, and his arm is holy.
Psalms	Ps	21	97	2	The Lord hath made known his salvation: he hath revealed his justice in the sight of the Gentiles.
Psalms	Ps	21	97	3	He hath remembered his mercy and his truth toward the house of Israel. All the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God.
Psalms	Ps	21	97	4	Sing joyfully to God, all the earth; make melody, rejoice and sing.
Psalms	Ps	21	97	5	Sing praise to the Lord on the harp, on the harp, and with the voice of a psalm:
Psalms	Ps	21	97	6	With long trumpets, and sound of cornet. Make a joyful noise before the Lord our king:
Psalms	Ps	21	97	7	Let the sea be moved and the fulness thereof: the world and they that dwell therein.
Psalms	Ps	21	97	8	The rivers shall clap their hands, the mountains shall rejoice together
Psalms	Ps	21	97	9	At the presence of the Lord: because he cometh to judge the earth. He shall judge the world with justice, and the people with equity.
Psalms	Ps	21	98	1	[A psalm for David himself.] The Lord hath reigned, let the people be angry: he that sitteth on the cherubims: let the earth be moved.
Psalms	Ps	21	98	2	The Lord is great in Sion, and high above all people.
Psalms	Ps	21	98	3	Let them give praise to thy great name: for it is terrible and holy:
Psalms	Ps	21	98	4	And the king's honour loveth judgment. Thou hast prepared directions: thou hast done judgment and justice in Jacob.
Psalms	Ps	21	98	5	Exalt ye the Lord our God, and adore his footstool, for it is holy.
Psalms	Ps	21	98	6	Moses and Aaron among his priests: and Samuel among them that call upon his name. They called upon the Lord, and he heard them:
Psalms	Ps	21	98	7	He spoke to them in the pillar of the cloud. They kept his testimonies, and the commandment which he gave them.
Psalms	Ps	21	98	8	Thou didst hear them, O Lord our God: thou wast a merciful God to them, and taking vengeance on all their inventions.
Psalms	Ps	21	98	9	Exalt ye the Lord our God, and adore at his holy mountain: for the Lord our God is holy.
Psalms	Ps	21	99	1	[A psalm of praise.]
Psalms	Ps	21	99	2	Sing joyfully to God, all the earth: serve ye the Lord with gladness. Come in before his presence with exceeding great joy.
Psalms	Ps	21	99	3	Know ye that the Lord he is God: he made us, and not we ourselves. We are his people and the sheep of his pasture.
Psalms	Ps	21	99	4	Go ye into his gates with praise, into his courts with hymns: and give glory to him. Praise ye his name:
Psalms	Ps	21	99	5	For the Lord is sweet, his mercy endureth for ever, and his truth to generation and generation.
Psalms	Ps	21	100	1	[A psalm for David himself.] Mercy and judgment I will sing to thee, O Lord: I will sing,
Psalms	Ps	21	100	2	And I will understand in the unspotted way, when thou shalt come to me. I walked in the innocence of my heart, in the midst of my house.
Psalms	Ps	21	100	3	I did not set before my eyes any unjust thing: I hated the workers of iniquities.
Psalms	Ps	21	100	4	The perverse heart did not cleave to me: and the malignant, that turned aside from me, I would not know.
Psalms	Ps	21	100	5	The man that in private detracted his neighbour, him did I persecute. With him that had a proud eye, and an unsatiable heart, I would not eat.
Psalms	Ps	21	100	6	My eyes were upon the faithful of the earth, to sit with me: the man that walked in the perfect way, he served me.
Psalms	Ps	21	100	7	He that worketh pride shall not dwell in the midst of my house: he that speaketh unjust things did not prosper before my eyes.
Psalms	Ps	21	100	8	In the morning I put to death all the wicked of the land: that I might cut off all the workers of iniquity from the city of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	1	[The prayer of the poor man, when he was anxious, and poured out his supplication before the Lord.]
Psalms	Ps	21	101	2	Hear, O Lord, my prayer: and let my cry come to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	3	Turn not away thy face from me: in the day when I am in trouble, incline thy ear to me. In what day soever I shall call upon thee, hear me speedily.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	4	For my days are vanished like smoke: and my bones are grown dry like fuel for the fire.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	5	I am smitten as grass, and my heart is withered: because I forgot to eat my bread.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	6	Through the voice of my groaning, my bone hath cleaved to my flesh.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	7	I am become like to a pelican of the wilderness: I am like a night raven in the house.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	8	I have watched, and am become as a sparrow all alone on the housetop.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	9	All the day long my enemies reproached me: and they that praised me did swear against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	10	For I did eat ashes like bread, and mingled my drink with weeping.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	11	Because of thy anger and indignation: for having lifted me up thou hast thrown me down.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	12	My days have declined like a shadow, and I am withered like grass.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	13	But thou, O Lord, endurest for ever: and thy memorial to all generations.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	14	Thou shalt arise and have mercy on Sion: for it is time to have mercy on it, for the time is come.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	15	For the stones thereof have pleased thy servants: and they shall have pity on the earth thereof.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	16	And the Gentiles shall fear thy name, O Lord, and all the kings of the earth thy glory.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	17	For the Lord hath built up Sion: and he shall be seen in his glory.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	18	He hath had regard to the prayer of the humble: and he hath not despised their petition.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	19	Let these things be written unto another generation: and the people that shall be created shall praise the Lord:
Psalms	Ps	21	101	20	Because he hath looked forth from his high sanctuary: from heaven the Lord hath looked upon the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	21	That he might hear the groans of them that are in fetters: that he might release the children of the slain:
Psalms	Ps	21	101	22	That they may declare the name of the Lord in Sion: and his praise in Jerusalem;
Psalms	Ps	21	101	23	When the people assemble together, and kings, to serve the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	24	He answered him in the way of his strength: Declare unto me the fewness of my days.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	25	Call me not away in the midst of my days: thy years are unto generation and generation.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	26	In the beginning, O Lord, thou foundedst the earth: and the heavens are the works of thy hands.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	27	They shall perish but thou remainest: and all of them shall grow old like a garment: And as a vesture thou shalt change them, and they shall be changed.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	28	But thou art always the selfsame, and thy years shall not fail.
Psalms	Ps	21	101	29	The children of thy servants shall continue: and their seed shall be directed for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	1	[For David himself.] Bless the Lord, O my soul: and let all that is within me bless his holy name.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	2	Bless the Lord, O my soul, and never forget all he hath done for thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	3	Who forgiveth all thy iniquities: who healeth all thy diseases.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	4	Who redeemeth thy life from destruction: who crowneth thee with mercy and compassion.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	5	Who satisfieth thy desire with good things: thy youth shall be renewed like the eagle's.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	6	The Lord doth mercies, and judgment for all that suffer wrong.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	7	He hath made his ways known to Moses: his wills to the children of Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	8	The Lord is compassionate and merciful: longsuffering and plenteous in mercy.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	9	He will not always be angry: nor will he threaten for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	10	He hath not dealt with us according to our sins: nor rewarded us according to our iniquities.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	11	For according to the height of the heaven above the earth: he hath strengthened his mercy towards them that fear him.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	12	As far as the east is from the west, so far hath he removed our iniquities from us.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	13	As a father hath compassion on his children, so hath the Lord compassion on them that fear him:
Psalms	Ps	21	102	14	For he knoweth our frame. He remembereth that we are dust:
Psalms	Ps	21	102	15	Man's days are as grass, as the flower of the field so shall he flourish.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	16	For the spirit shall pass in him, and he shall not be: and he shall know his place no more.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	17	But the mercy of the Lord is from eternity and unto eternity upon them that fear him: And his justice unto children's children,
Psalms	Ps	21	102	18	To such as keep his covenant, And are mindful of his commandments to do them.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	19	The Lord hath prepared his throne in heaven: and his kingdom shall rule over all.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	20	Bless the Lord, all ye his angels: you that are mighty in strength, and execute his word, hearkening to the voice of his orders.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	21	Bless the Lord, all ye his hosts: you ministers of his that do his will.
Psalms	Ps	21	102	22	Bless the Lord, all his works: in every place of his dominion, O my soul, bless thou the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	1	[For David himself.] Bless the Lord, O my soul: O Lord my God, thou art exceedingly great. Thou hast put on praise and beauty:
Psalms	Ps	21	103	2	And art clothed with light as with a garment. Who stretchest out the heaven like a pavilion:
Psalms	Ps	21	103	3	Who coverest the higher rooms thereof with water. Who makest the clouds thy chariot: who walkest upon the wings of the winds.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	4	Who makest thy angels spirits: and thy ministers a burning fire.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	5	Who hast founded the earth upon its own bases: it shall not be moved for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	6	The deep like a garment is its clothing: above the mountains shall the waters stand.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	7	At thy rebuke they shall flee: at the voice of thy thunder they shall fear.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	8	The mountains ascend, and the plains descend into the place which thou hast founded for them.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	9	Thou hast set a bound which they shall not pass over; neither shall they return to cover the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	10	Thou sendest forth springs in the vales: between the midst of the hills the waters shall pass.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	11	All the beasts of the field shall drink: the wild asses shall expect in their thirst.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	12	Over them the birds of the air shall dwell: from the midst of the rocks they shall give forth their voices.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	13	Thou waterest the hills from thy upper rooms: the earth shall be filled with the fruit of thy works:
Psalms	Ps	21	103	14	Bringing forth grass for cattle, and herb for the service of men. That thou mayst bring bread out of the earth:
Psalms	Ps	21	103	15	And that wine may cheer the heart of man. That he may make the face cheerful with oil: and that bread may strengthen man's heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	16	The trees of the field shall be filled, and the cedars of Libanus which he hath planted:
Psalms	Ps	21	103	17	There the sparrows shall make their nests. The highest of them is the house of the heron.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	18	The high hills are a refuge for the harts, the rock for the irchins.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	19	He hath made the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	20	Thou hast appointed darkness, and it is night: in it shall all the beasts of the woods go about:
Psalms	Ps	21	103	21	The young lions roaring after their prey, and seeking their meat from God.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	22	The sun ariseth, and they are gathered together: and they shall lie down in their dens.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	23	Man shall go forth to his work, and to his labour until the evening.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	24	How great are thy works, O Lord? thou hast made all things in wisdom: the earth is filled with thy riches.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	25	So is this great sea, which stretcheth wide its arms: there are creeping things without number: Creatures little and great.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	26	There the ships shall go. This sea dragon which thou hast formed to play therein.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	27	All expect of thee that thou give them food in season.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	28	What thou givest to them they shall gather up: when thou openest thy hand, they shall all be filled with good.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	29	But if thou turnest away thy face, they shall be troubled: thou shalt take away their breath, and they shall fail, and shall return to their dust.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	30	Thou shalt send forth thy spirit, and they shall be created: and thou shalt renew the face of the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	31	May the glory of the Lord endure for ever: the Lord shall rejoice in his works.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	32	He looketh upon the earth, and maketh it tremble: he toucheth the mountains, and they smoke.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	33	I will sing to the Lord as long as I live: I will sing praise to my God while I have my being.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	34	Let my speech be acceptable to him: but I will take delight in the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	103	35	Let sinners be consumed out of the earth, and the unjust, so that they be no more: O my soul, bless thou the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	1	[Alleluia.] Give glory to the Lord, and call upon his name: declare his deeds among the Gentiles.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	2	Sing to him, yea sing praises to him: relate all his wondrous works.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	3	Glory ye in his holy name: let the heart of them rejoice that seek the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	4	Seek ye the Lord, and be strengthened: seek his face evermore.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	5	Remember his marvellous works which he hath done; his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	6	O ye seed of Abraham his servant; ye sons of Jacob his chosen.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	7	He is the Lord our God: his judgments are in all the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	8	He hath remembered his covenant for ever: the word which he commanded to a thousand generations.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	9	Which he made to Abraham; and his oath to Isaac:
Psalms	Ps	21	104	10	And he appointed the same to Jacob for a law, and to Israel for an everlasting testament:
Psalms	Ps	21	104	11	Saying: To thee will I give the land of Chanaan, the lot of your inheritance.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	12	When they were but a small number: yea very few, and sojourners therein:
Psalms	Ps	21	104	13	And they passed from nation to nation, and from one kingdom to another people.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	14	He suffered no man to hurt them: and he reproved kings for their sakes.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	15	Touch ye not my anointed: and do no evil to my prophets.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	16	And he called a famine upon the land: and he broke in pieces all the support of bread.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	17	He sent a man before them: Joseph, who was sold for a slave.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	18	They humbled his feet in fetters: the iron pierced his soul,
Psalms	Ps	21	104	19	Until his word came. The word of the Lord inflamed him.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	20	The king sent, and he released him: the ruler of the people, and he set him at liberty.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	21	He made him master of his house, and ruler of all his possession.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	22	That he might instruct his princes as himself, and teach his ancients wisdom.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	23	And Israel went into Egypt: and Jacob was a sojourner in the land of Cham.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	24	And he increased his people exceedingly: and strengthened them over their enemies,
Psalms	Ps	21	104	25	He turned their heart to hate his people: and to deal deceitfully with his servants.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	26	He sent Moses his servant: Aaron the man whom he had chosen.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	27	He gave them power to shew his signs, and his wonders in the land of Cham.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	28	He sent darkness, and made it obscure: and grieved not his words.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	29	He turned their waters into blood, and destroyed their fish.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	30	Their land brought forth frogs, in the inner chambers of their kings.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	31	He spoke, and there came divers sorts of flies and sciniphs in all their coasts.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	32	He gave them hail for rain, a burning fire in the land.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	33	And he destroyed their vineyards and their fig trees: and he broke in pieces the trees of their coasts.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	34	He spoke, and the locust came, and the bruchus, of which there was no number.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	35	And they devoured all the grass in their land, and consumed all the fruit of their ground.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	36	And he slew all the firstborn in their land: the firstfruits of all their labour.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	37	And he brought them out with silver and gold: and there was not among their tribes one that was feeble.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	38	Egypt was glad when they departed: for the fear of them lay upon them.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	39	He spread a cloud for their protection, and fire to give them light in the night.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	40	They asked, and the quail came: and he filled them with the bread of heaven.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	41	He opened the rock, and waters flowed: rivers ran down in the dry land.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	42	Because he remembered his holy word, which he had spoken to his servant Abraham.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	43	And he brought forth his people with joy, and his chosen with gladness.
Psalms	Ps	21	104	44	And he gave them the lands of the Gentiles: and they possessed the labours of the people:
Psalms	Ps	21	104	45	That they might observe his justifications, and seek after his law.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	1	[Alleluia.] Give glory to the Lord, for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	2	Who shall declare the powers of the Lord? who shall set forth all his praises?
Psalms	Ps	21	105	3	Blessed are they that keep judgment, and do justice at all times.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	4	Remember us, O Lord, in the favour of thy people: visit us with thy salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	5	That we may see the good of thy chosen, that we may rejoice in the joy of thy nation: that thou mayst be praised with thy inheritance.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	6	We have sinned with our fathers: we have acted unjustly, we have wrought iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	7	Our fathers understood not thy wonders in Egypt: they remembered not the multitude of thy mercies: And they provoked to wrath going up to the sea, even the Red Sea.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	8	And he saved them for his own name's sake: that he might make his power known.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	9	And he rebuked the Red Sea, and it was dried up: and he led them through the depths, as in a wilderness.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	10	And he saved them from the hand of them that hated them: and he redeemed them from the hand of the enemy.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	11	And the water covered them that afflicted them: there was not one of them left.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	12	And they believed his words: and they sang his praises.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	13	They had quickly done, they forgot his works: and they waited not for his counsels.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	14	And they coveted their desire in the desert: and they tempted God in the place without water.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	15	And he gave them their request: and sent fulness into their souls.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	16	And they provoked Moses in the camp, Aaron the holy one of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	17	The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan: and covered the congregation of Abiron.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	18	And a fire was kindled in their congregation: the flame burned the wicked.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	19	They made also a calf in Horeb: and they adored the graven thing.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	20	And they changed their glory into the likeness of a calf that eateth grass.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	21	They forgot God, who saved them, who had done great things in Egypt,
Psalms	Ps	21	105	22	Wondrous works in the land of Cham: terrible things in the Red Sea.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	23	And he said that he would destroy them: had not Moses his chosen stood before him in the breach: To turn away his wrath, lest he should destroy them.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	24	And they set at nought the desirable land. They believed not his word,
Psalms	Ps	21	105	25	And they murmured in their tents: they hearkened not to the voice of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	26	And he lifted up his hand over them: to overthrow them in the desert;
Psalms	Ps	21	105	27	And to cast down their seed among the nations, and to scatter them in the countries.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	28	They also were initiated to Beelphegor: and ate the sacrifices of the dead.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	29	And they provoked him with their inventions: and destruction was multiplied among them.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	30	Then Phinees stood up, and pacified him: and the slaughter ceased.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	31	And it was reputed to him unto justice, to generation and generation for evermore.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	32	They provoked him also at the waters of contradiction: and Moses was afflicted for their sakes:
Psalms	Ps	21	105	33	Because they exasperated his spirit. And he distinguished with his lips.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	34	They did not destroy the nations of which the Lord spoke unto them.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	35	And they were mingled among the heathens, and learned their works:
Psalms	Ps	21	105	36	And served their idols, and it became a stumblingblock to them.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	37	And they sacrificed their sons, and their daughters to devils.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	38	And they shed innocent blood: the blood of their sons and of their daughters which they sacrificed to the idols of Chanaan. And the land was polluted with blood,
Psalms	Ps	21	105	39	And was defiled with their works: and they went aside after their own inventions.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	40	And the Lord was exceedingly angry with his people: and he abhorred his inheritance.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	41	And he delivered them into the hands of the nations: and they that hated them had dominion over them.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	42	And their enemies afflicted them: and they were humbled under their hands:
Psalms	Ps	21	105	43	Many times did he deliver them. But they provoked him with their counsel: and they were brought low by their iniquities.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	44	And he saw when they were in tribulation: and he heard their prayer.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	45	And he was mindful of his covenant: and repented according to the multitude of his mercies.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	46	And he gave them unto mercies, in the sight of all those that had made them captives.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	47	Save us, O Lord, our God: and gather us from among nations: That we may give thanks to thy holy name, and may glory in thy praise.
Psalms	Ps	21	105	48	Blessed be the Lord the God of Israel, from everlasting to everlasting: and let all the people say: So be it, so be it.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	1	Give glory to the Lord, for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	2	Let them say so that have been redeemed by the Lord, whom he hath redeemed from the hand of the enemy: and gathered out of the countries.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	3	From the rising and the setting of the sun, from the north and from the sea.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	4	They wandered in a wilderness, in a place without water: they found not the way of a city for their habitation.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	5	They were hungry and thirsty: their soul fainted in them.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	6	And they cried to the Lord in their tribulation: and he delivered them out of their distresses.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	7	And he led them into the right way: that they might go to a city of habitation.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	8	Let the mercies of the Lord give glory to him: and his wonderful works to the children of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	9	For he hath satisfied the empty soul, and hath filled the hungry soul with good things.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	10	Such as sat in darkness and in the shadow of death: bound in want and in iron.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	11	Because they had exasperated the words of God: and provoked the counsel of the most High:
Psalms	Ps	21	106	12	And their heart was humbled with labours: they were weakened, and there was none to help them.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	13	Then they cried to the Lord in their affliction: and he delivered them out of their distresses.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	14	And he brought them out of darkness, and the shadow of death; and broke their bonds in sunder.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	15	Let the mercies of the Lord give glory to him, and his wonderful works to the children of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	16	Because he hath broken gates of brass, and burst the iron bars.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	17	He took them out of the way of their iniquity: for they were brought low for their injustices.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	18	Their soul abhorred all manner of meat: and they drew nigh even to the gates of death.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	19	And they cried to the Lord in their affliction: and he delivered them out of their distresses.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	20	He sent his word, and healed them: and delivered them from their destructions.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	21	Let the mercies of the Lord give glory to him: and his wonderful works to the children of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	22	And let them sacrifice the sacrifice of praise: and declare his works with joy.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	23	They that go down to the sea in ships, doing business in the great waters:
Psalms	Ps	21	106	24	These have seen the works of the Lord, and his wonders in the deep.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	25	He said the word, and there arose a storm of wind: and the waves thereof were lifted up.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	26	They mount up to the heavens, and they go down to the depths: their soul pined away with evils.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	27	They were troubled, and reeled like a drunken man; and all their wisdom was swallowed up.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	28	And they cried to the Lord in their affliction: and he brought them out of their distresses.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	29	And he turned the storm into a breeze: and its waves were still.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	30	And they rejoiced because they were still: and he brought them to the haven which they wished for.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	31	Let the mercies of the Lord give glory to him, and his wonderful works to the children of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	32	And let them exalt him in the church of the people: and praise him in the chair of the ancients.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	33	He hath turned rivers into a wilderness: and the sources of water into dry ground:
Psalms	Ps	21	106	34	A fruitful land into barrenness, for the wickedness of them that dwell therein.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	35	He hath turned a wilderness into pools of water, and a dry land into water springs.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	36	And hath placed there the hungry; and they made a city for their habitation.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	37	And they sowed fields, and planted vineyards: and they yielded fruit of birth.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	38	And he blessed them, and they were multiplied exceedingly: and their cattle he suffered not to decrease.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	39	Then they were brought to be few: and they were afflicted through the trouble of evils and sorrow.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	40	Contempt was poured forth upon their princes: and he caused them to wander where there was no passing, and out of the way.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	41	And he helped the poor out of poverty: and made him families like a flock of sheep.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	42	The just shall see, and shall rejoice, and all iniquity shall stop their mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	106	43	Who is wise, and will keep these things: and will understand the mercies of the Lord?
Psalms	Ps	21	107	1	[A canticle of a psalm for David himself.]
Psalms	Ps	21	107	2	My heart is ready, O God, my heart is ready: I will sing, and will give praise, with my glory.
Psalms	Ps	21	107	3	Arise, my glory; arise, psaltery and harp: I will arise in the morning early.
Psalms	Ps	21	107	4	I will praise thee, O Lord, among the people: and I will sing unto thee among the populations.
Psalms	Ps	21	107	5	For thy mercy is great above the heavens: and thy truth even unto the clouds.
Psalms	Ps	21	107	6	Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens, and thy glory over all the earth:
Psalms	Ps	21	107	7	That thy beloved may be delivered. Save with thy right hand and hear me.
Psalms	Ps	21	107	8	God hath spoken in his holiness. I will rejoice, and I will divide Sichem and I will mete out the vale of tabernacles.
Psalms	Ps	21	107	9	Galaad is mine, and Manasses is mine and Ephraim the protection of my head. Juda is my king:
Psalms	Ps	21	107	10	Moab the pot of my hope. Over Edom I will stretch out my shoe: the aliens are become my friends.
Psalms	Ps	21	107	11	Who will bring me into the strong city? who will lead me into Edom?
Psalms	Ps	21	107	12	Wilt not thou, O God, who hast cast us off? and wilt not thou, O God, go forth with our armies?
Psalms	Ps	21	107	13	O grant us help from trouble: for vain is the help of man.
Psalms	Ps	21	107	14	Through God we shall do mightily: and he will bring our enemies to nothing.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	108	2	O God, be not thou silent in my praise: for the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of the deceitful man is opened against me.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	3	They have spoken against me with deceitful tongues; and they have compassed me about with words of hatred; and have fought against me without cause.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	4	Instead of making me a return of love, they detracted me: but I gave myself to prayer.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	5	And they repaid me evil for good: and hatred for my love.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	6	Set thou the sinner over him: and may the devil stand at his right hand.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	7	When he is judged, may he go out condemned; and may his prayer be turned to sin.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	8	May his days be few: and his bishopric let another take.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	9	May his children be fatherless, and his wife a widow.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	10	Let his children be carried about vagabonds, and beg; and let them be cast out of their dwellings.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	11	May the usurer search all his substance: and let strangers plunder his labours.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	12	May there be none to help him: nor none to pity his fatherless offspring.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	13	May his posterity be cut off; in one generation may his name be blotted out.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	14	May the iniquity of his fathers be remembered in the sight of the Lord: and let not the sin of his mother be blotted out.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	15	May they be before the Lord continually, and let the memory of them perish from the earth:
Psalms	Ps	21	108	16	because he remembered not to shew mercy,
Psalms	Ps	21	108	17	But persecuted the poor man and the beggar; and the broken in heart, to put him to death.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	18	And he loved cursing, and it shall come unto him: and he would not have blessing, and it shall be far from him. And he put on cursing, like a garment: and it went in like water into his entrails, and like oil in his bones.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	19	May it be unto him like a garment which covereth him; and like a girdle with which he is girded continually.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	20	This is the work of them who detract me before the Lord; and who speak evils against my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	21	But thou, O Lord, do with me for thy name's sake: because thy mercy is sweet. Do thou deliver me,
Psalms	Ps	21	108	22	for I am poor and needy, and my heart is troubled within me.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	23	I am taken away like the shadow when it declineth: and I am shaken off as locusts.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	24	My knees are weakened through fasting: and my flesh is changed for oil.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	25	And I am become a reproach to them: they saw me and they shaked their heads,
Psalms	Ps	21	108	26	Help me, O Lord my God; save me according to thy mercy.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	27	And let them know that this is thy hand: and that thou, O Lord, hast done it.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	28	They will curse and thou will bless: let them that rise up against me be confounded: but thy servant shall rejoice.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	29	Let them that detract me be clothed with shame: and let them be covered with their confusion as with a double cloak.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	30	I will give great thanks to the Lord with my mouth: and in the midst of many I will praise him.
Psalms	Ps	21	108	31	Because he hath stood at the right hand of the poor, to save my soul from persecutors.
Psalms	Ps	21	109	1	The Lord said to my Lord: Sit thou at my right hand: Until I make thy enemies thy footstool.
Psalms	Ps	21	109	2	The Lord will send forth the sceptre of thy power out of Sion: rule thou in the midst of thy enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	109	3	With thee is the principality in the day of thy strength: in the brightness of the saints: from the womb before the day star I begot thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	109	4	The Lord hath sworn, and he will not repent: Thou art a priest for ever according to the order of Melchisedech.
Psalms	Ps	21	109	5	The Lord at thy right hand hath broken kings in the day of his wrath.
Psalms	Ps	21	109	6	He shall judge among nations, he shall fill ruins: he shall crush the heads in the land of the many.
Psalms	Ps	21	109	7	He shall drink of the torrent in the way: therefore shall he lift up the head.
Psalms	Ps	21	110	1	I will praise thee, O Lord, with my whole heart; in the council of the just: and in the congregation.
Psalms	Ps	21	110	2	Great are the works of the Lord: sought out according to all his wills.
Psalms	Ps	21	110	3	His work is praise and magnificence: and his justice continueth for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	110	4	He hath made a remembrance of his wonderful works, being a merciful and gracious Lord:
Psalms	Ps	21	110	5	He hath given food to them that fear him. He will be mindful for ever of his covenant:
Psalms	Ps	21	110	6	He will shew forth to his people the power of his works.
Psalms	Ps	21	110	7	That he may give them the inheritance of the Gentiles: the works of his hands are truth and judgment.
Psalms	Ps	21	110	8	All his commandments are faithful: confirmed for ever and ever, made in truth and equity.
Psalms	Ps	21	110	9	He hath sent redemption to his people: he hath commanded his covenant for ever. Holy and terrible is his name:
Psalms	Ps	21	110	10	The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom. A good understanding to all that do it: his praise continueth for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	111	1	Blessed is the man that feareth the Lord: he shall delight exceedingly in his commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	111	2	His seed shall be mighty upon earth: the generation of the righteous shall be blessed.
Psalms	Ps	21	111	3	Glory and wealth shall be in his house: and his justice remaineth for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	111	4	To the righteous a light is risen up in darkness: he is merciful, and compassionate and just.
Psalms	Ps	21	111	5	Acceptable is the man that sheweth mercy and lendeth: he shall order his words with judgment:
Psalms	Ps	21	111	6	Because he shall not be moved for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	111	7	The just shall be in everlasting remembrance: he shall not fear the evil hearing. His heart is ready to hope in the Lord:
Psalms	Ps	21	111	8	His heart is strengthened, he shall not be moved until he look over his enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	111	9	He hath distributed, he hath given to the poor: his justice remaineth for ever and ever: his horn shall be exalted in glory.
Psalms	Ps	21	111	10	The wicked shall see, and shall be angry, he shall gnash with his teeth and pine away: the desire of the wicked shall perish.
Psalms	Ps	21	112	1	Praise the Lord, ye children: praise ye the name of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	112	2	Blessed be the name of the Lord, from henceforth now and for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	112	3	From the rising of the sun unto the going down of the same, the name of the Lord is worthy of praise.
Psalms	Ps	21	112	4	The Lord is high above all nations; and his glory above the heavens.
Psalms	Ps	21	112	5	Who is as the Lord our God, who dwelleth on high:
Psalms	Ps	21	112	6	And looketh down on the low things in heaven and in earth?
Psalms	Ps	21	112	7	Raising up the needy from the earth, and lifting up the poor out of the dunghill:
Psalms	Ps	21	112	8	That he may place him with princes, with the princes of his people.
Psalms	Ps	21	112	9	Who maketh a barren woman to dwell in a house, the joyful mother of children.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	1	When Israel went out of Egypt, the house of Jacob from a barbarous people:
Psalms	Ps	21	113	2	Judea was made his sanctuary, Israel his dominion.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	3	The sea saw and fled: Jordan was turned back.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	4	The mountains skipped like rams, and the hills like the lambs of the flock.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	5	What ailed thee, O thou sea, that thou didst flee: and thou, O Jordan, that thou wast turned back?
Psalms	Ps	21	113	6	Ye mountains, that ye skipped like rams, and ye hills, like lambs of the flock?
Psalms	Ps	21	113	7	At the presence of the Lord the earth was moved, at the presence of the God of Jacob:
Psalms	Ps	21	113	8	Who turned the rock into pools of water, and the stony hill into fountains of waters.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	9	Not to us, O Lord, not to us; but to thy name give glory.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	10	For thy mercy, and for thy truth's sake: lest the gentiles should say: Where is their God?
Psalms	Ps	21	113	11	But our God is in heaven: he hath done all things whatsoever he would.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	12	The idols of the gentiles are silver and gold, the works of the hands of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	13	They have mouths and speak not: they have eyes and see not.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	14	They have ears and hear not: they have noses and smell not.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	15	They have hands and feel not: they have feet and walk not: neither shall they cry out through their throat.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	16	Let them that make them become like unto them: and all such as trust in them.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	17	The house of Israel hath hoped in the Lord: he is their helper and their protector.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	18	The house of Aaron hath hoped in the Lord: he is their helper and their protector.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	19	They that fear the Lord hath hoped in the Lord: he is their helper and their protector.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	20	The Lord hath been mindful of us, and hath blessed us. He hath blessed the house of Israel: he hath blessed the house of Aaron.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	21	He hath blessed all that fear the Lord, both little and great.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	22	May the Lord add blessings upon you: upon you, and upon your children.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	23	Blessed be you of the Lord, who made heaven and earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	24	The heaven of heaven is the Lord's: but the earth he has given to the children of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	25	The dead shall not praise thee, O Lord: nor any of them that go down to hell.
Psalms	Ps	21	113	26	But we that live bless the Lord: from this time now and for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	114	1	I have loved, because the Lord will hear the voice of my prayer.
Psalms	Ps	21	114	2	Because he hath inclined his ear unto me: and in my days I will call upon him.
Psalms	Ps	21	114	3	The sorrows of death have encompassed me: and the perils of hell have found me. I met with trouble and sorrow:
Psalms	Ps	21	114	4	And I called upon the name of the Lord. O Lord, deliver my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	114	5	The Lord is merciful and just, and our God sheweth mercy.
Psalms	Ps	21	114	6	The Lord is the keeper of little ones: I was little and he delivered me.
Psalms	Ps	21	114	7	Turn, O my soul, into thy rest: for the Lord hath been bountiful to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	114	8	For he hath delivered my soul from death: my eyes from tears, my feet from falling.
Psalms	Ps	21	114	9	I will please the Lord in the land of the living.
Psalms	Ps	21	115	1	I have believed, therefore have I spoken; but I have been humbled exceedingly.
Psalms	Ps	21	115	2	I said in my excess: Every man is a liar.
Psalms	Ps	21	115	3	What shall I render to the Lord, for all the things he hath rendered unto me?
Psalms	Ps	21	115	4	I will take the chalice of salvation; and I will call upon the name of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	115	5	I will pay my vows to the Lord before all his people:
Psalms	Ps	21	115	6	Precious in the sight of the Lord is the death of his saints.
Psalms	Ps	21	115	7	O Lord, for I am thy servant: I am thy servant, and the son of thy handmaid. Thou hast broken my bonds:
Psalms	Ps	21	115	8	I will sacrifice to thee the sacrifice of praise, and I will call upon the name of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	115	9	I will pay my vows to the Lord in the sight of all his people:
Psalms	Ps	21	115	10	In the courts of the house of the Lord, in the midst of thee, O Jerusalem.
Psalms	Ps	21	116	1	O praise the Lord, all ye nations: praise him, all ye people.
Psalms	Ps	21	116	2	For his mercy is confirmed upon us: and the truth of the Lord remaineth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	1	Give praise to the Lord, for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	2	Let Israel now say that he is good: that his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	3	Let the house of Aaron now say, that his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	4	Let them that fear the Lord now say, that his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	5	In my trouble I called upon the Lord: and the Lord heard me, and enlarged me.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	6	The Lord is my helper, I will not fear what man can do unto me.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	7	The Lord is my helper: and I will look over my enemies.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	8	It is good to confide in the Lord, rather than to have confidence in man.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	9	It is good to trust in the Lord, rather than to trust in princes.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	10	All nations compassed me about; and in the name of the Lord I have been revenged on them.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	11	Surrounding me they compassed me about: and in the name of the Lord I have been revenged on them.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	12	They surrounded me like bees, and they burned like fire among thorns: and in the name of the Lord I was revenged on them.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	13	Being pushed I was overturned that I might fall: but the Lord supported me.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	14	The Lord is my strength and my praise: and he is become my salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	15	The voice of rejoicing and of salvation is in the tabernacles of the just.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	16	The right hand of the Lord hath wrought strength: the right hand of the Lord hath exulted me: the right hand of the Lord hath wrought strength.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	17	I shall not die, but live: and shall declare the works of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	18	The Lord chastising hath chastised me: but he hath not delivered me over to death.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	19	Open ye to me the gates of justice: I will go into them, and give praise to the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	20	This is the gate of the Lord, the just shall enter into it.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	21	I will give glory to thee because thou hast heard me: and art become my salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	22	The stone which the builders rejected; the same is become the head of the corner.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	23	This is the Lord's doing: and it is wonderful in our eyes.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	24	This is the day which the Lord hath made: let us be glad and rejoice therein.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	25	O Lord, save me: O Lord, give good success.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	26	Blessed be he that cometh in the name Lord. We have blessed you out of the house of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	27	The Lord is God, and he hath shone upon us. Appoint a solemn day, with shady boughs, even to the horn of the altar.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	28	Thou art my God, and I will praise thee: thou art my God, and I will exalt thee. I will praise thee, because thou hast heard me, and art become my salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	117	29	O praise ye the Lord, for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	1	<Aleph>Blessed are the undefiled in the way, who walk in the law of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	2	Blessed are they who search his testimonies: that seek him with their whole heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	3	For they that work iniquity, have not walked in his ways.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	4	Thou hast commanded thy commandments to be kept most diligently.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	5	O! that my ways may be directed to keep thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	6	Then shall I not be confounded, when I shall look into all thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	7	I will praise thee with uprightness of heart, when I shall have learned the judgments of thy justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	8	I will keep thy justifications: O! do not thou utterly forsake me.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	9	<Beth>By what doth a young man correct his way? by observing thy words.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	10	With my whole heart have I sought after thee: let me not stray from thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	11	Thy words have I hidden in my heart, that I may not sin against thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	12	Blessed art thou, O Lord: teach me thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	13	With my lips I have pronounced all the judgments of thy mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	14	I have been delighted in the way of thy testimonies, as in all riches.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	15	I will meditate on thy commandments: and I will consider thy ways.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	16	I will think of thy justifications: I will not forget thy words.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	17	<Gimel>Give bountifully to thy servant, enliven me: and I shall keep thy words.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	18	Open thou my eyes: and I will consider the wondrous things of thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	19	I am a sojourner on the earth: hide not thy commandments from me.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	20	My soul hath coveted to long for thy justifications, at all times.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	21	Thou hast rebuked the proud: they are cursed who decline from thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	22	Remove from me reproach and contempt: because I have sought after thy testimonies.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	23	For princes sat, and spoke against me: but thy servant was employed in thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	24	For thy testimonies are my meditation: and thy justifications my counsel.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	25	<Daleth>My soul hath cleaved to the pavement: quicken thou me according to thy word.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	26	I have declared my ways, and thou hast heard me: teach me thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	27	Make me to understand the way of thy justifications: and I shall be exercised in thy wondrous works.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	28	My soul hath slumbered through heaviness: strengthen thou me in thy words.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	29	Remove from me the way of iniquity: and out of thy law have mercy on me.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	30	I have chosen the way of truth: thy judgments I have not forgotten.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	31	I have stuck to thy testimonies, O Lord: put me not to shame.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	32	I have run the way of thy commandments, when thou didst enlarge my heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	33	<He>Set before me for a law the way of thy justifications, O Lord: and I will always seek after it.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	34	Give me understanding, and I will search thy law; and I will keep it with my whole heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	35	Lead me into the path of thy commandments; for this same I have desired.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	36	Incline my heart into thy testimonies and not to covetousness.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	37	Turn away my eyes that they may not behold vanity: quicken me in thy way.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	38	Establish thy word to thy servant, in thy fear.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	39	Turn away my reproach, which I have apprehended: for thy judgments are delightful.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	40	Behold I have longed after thy precepts: quicken me in thy justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	41	<Vau>Let thy mercy also come upon me, O Lord: thy salvation according to thy word.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	42	So shall I answer them that reproach me in any thing; that I have trusted in thy words.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	43	And take not thou the word of truth utterly out of my mouth: for in thy words have I hoped exceedingly.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	44	So shall I always keep thy law, for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	45	And I walked at large: because I have sought after thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	46	And I spoke of thy testimonies before kings: and I was not ashamed.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	47	I meditated also on thy commandments, which I loved.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	48	And I lifted up my hands to thy commandments, which I loved: and I was exercised in thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	49	<Zain>Be thou mindful of thy word to thy servant, in which thou hast given me hope.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	50	This hath comforted me in my humiliation: because thy word hath enlivened me.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	51	The proud did iniquitously altogether: but I declined not from thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	52	I remembered, O Lord, thy judgments of old: and I was comforted.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	53	A fainting hath taken hold of me, because of the wicked that forsake thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	54	Thy justifications were the subject of my song, in the place of my pilgrimage.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	55	In the night I have remembered thy name, O Lord: and have kept thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	56	This happened to me: because I sought after thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	57	<Heth>O Lord, my portion, I have said, I would keep thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	58	I entreated thy face with all my heart: have mercy on me according to thy word.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	59	I have thought on my ways: and turned my feet unto thy testimonies.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	60	I am ready, and am not troubled: that I may keep thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	61	The cords of the wicked have encompassed me: but I have not forgotten thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	62	I rose at midnight to give praise to thee; for the judgments of thy justification.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	63	I am a partaker with all them that fear thee, and that keep thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	64	The earth, O Lord, is full of thy mercy: teach me thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	65	<Teth>Thou hast done well with thy servant, O Lord, according to thy word.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	66	Teach me goodness and discipline and knowledge; for I have believed thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	67	Before I was humbled I offended; therefore have I kept thy word.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	68	Thou art good; and in thy goodness teach me thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	69	The iniquity of the proud hath been multiplied over me: but I will seek thy commandments with my whole heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	70	Their heart is curdled like milk: but I have meditated on thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	71	It is good for me that thou hast humbled me, that I may learn thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	72	The law of thy mouth is good to me, above thousands of gold and silver.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	73	<Jod>Thy hands have made me and formed me: give me understanding, and I will learn thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	74	They that fear thee shall see me, and shall be glad: because I have greatly hoped in thy words.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	75	I know, O Lord, that thy judgments are equity: and in thy truth thou hast humbled me.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	76	O! let thy mercy be for my comfort, according to thy word unto thy servant.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	77	Let thy tender mercies come unto me, and I shall live: for thy law is my meditation.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	78	Let the proud be ashamed, because they have done unjustly towards me: but I will be employed in thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	79	Let them that fear thee turn to me and they that know thy testimonies.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	80	Let my heart be undefiled in thy justifications, that I may not be confounded.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	81	<Caph>My soul hath fainted after thy salvation: and in thy word I have very much hoped.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	82	My eyes have failed for thy word, saying: When wilt thou comfort me?
Psalms	Ps	21	118	83	For I am become like a bottle in the frost: I have not forgotten thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	84	How many are the days of thy servant: when wilt thou execute judgment on them that persecute me?
Psalms	Ps	21	118	85	The wicked have told me fables: but not as thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	86	All thy statutes are truth: they have persecuted me unjustly, do thou help me.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	87	They had almost made an end of me upon earth: but I have not forsaken thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	88	Quicken thou me according to thy mercy: and I shall keep the testimonies of thy mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	89	<Lamed>For ever, O Lord, thy word standeth firm in heaven.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	90	Thy truth unto all generations: thou hast founded the earth, and it continueth.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	91	By thy ordinance the day goeth on: for all things serve thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	92	Unless thy law had been my meditation, I had then perhaps perished in my abjection.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	93	Thy justifications I will never forget: for by them thou hast given me life.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	94	I am thine, save thou me: for I have sought thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	95	The wicked have waited for me to destroy me: but I have understood thy testimonies.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	96	I have seen an end to all persecution: thy commandment is exceeding broad.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	97	<Mem>O how have I loved thy law, O Lord! it is my meditation all the day.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	98	Through thy commandment, thou hast made me wiser than my enemies: for it is ever with me.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	99	I have understood more than all my teachers: because thy testimonies are my meditation.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	100	I have had understanding above ancients: because I have sought thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	101	I have restrained my feet from every evil way: that I may keep thy words.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	102	I have not declined from thy judgments, because thou hast set me a law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	103	How sweet are thy words to my palate! more than honey to my mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	104	By thy commandments I have had understanding: therefore have I hated every way of iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	105	<Nun>Thy word is a lamp to my feet, and a light to my paths.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	106	I have sworn and am determined to keep the judgments of thy justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	107	I have been humbled, O Lord, exceedingly: quicken thou me according to thy word.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	108	The free offerings of my mouth make acceptable, O Lord: and teach me thy judgments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	109	My soul is continually in my hands: and I have not forgotten thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	110	Sinners have laid a snare for me: but I have not erred from thy precepts.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	111	I have purchased thy testimonies for an inheritance for ever: because they are a joy to my heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	112	I have inclined my heart to do thy justifications for ever, for the reward.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	113	<Samech>I have hated the unjust: and have loved thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	114	Thou art my helper and my protector: and in thy word I have greatly hoped.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	115	Depart from me, ye malignant: and I will search the commandments of my God.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	116	Uphold me according to thy word, and I shall live: and let me not be confounded in my expectation.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	117	Help me, and I shall be saved: and I will meditate always on thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	118	Thou hast despised all them that fall off from thy judgments; for their thought is unjust.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	119	I have accounted all the sinners of the earth prevaricators: therefore have I loved thy testimonies.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	120	Pierce thou my flesh with thy fear: for I am afraid of thy judgments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	121	<Ain>I have done judgment and justice: give me not up to them that slander me.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	122	Uphold thy servant unto good: let not the proud calumniate me.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	123	My eyes have fainted after thy salvation: and for the word of thy justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	124	Deal with thy servant according to thy mercy: and teach me thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	125	I am thy servant: give me understanding that I may know thy testimonies.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	126	It is time, O Lord, to do: they have dissipated thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	127	Therefore have I loved thy commandments above gold and the topaz.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	128	Therefore was I directed to all thy commandments: I have hated all wicked ways.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	129	<Phe>Thy testimonies are wonderful: therefore my soul hath sought them.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	130	The declaration of thy words giveth light: and giveth understanding to little ones.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	131	I opened my mouth and panted: because I longed for thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	132	Look thou upon me, and have mercy on me, according to the judgment of them that love thy name.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	133	Direct my steps according to thy word: and let no iniquity have dominion over me.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	134	Redeem me from the calumnies of men: that I may keep thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	135	Make thy face to shine upon thy servant: and teach me thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	136	My eyes have sent forth springs of water: because they have not kept thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	137	<Sade>Thou art just, O Lord: and thy judgment is right.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	138	Thou hast commanded justice thy testimonies: and thy truth exceedingly.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	139	My zeal hath made me pine away: because my enemies forgot thy words.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	140	Thy word is exceedingly refined: and thy servant hath loved it.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	141	I am very young and despised; but I forgot not thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	142	Thy justice is justice for ever: and thy law is the truth.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	143	Trouble and anguish have found me: thy commandments are my meditation.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	144	Thy testimonies are justice for ever: give me understanding, and I shall live.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	145	<Coph>I cried with my whole heart, hear me, O Lord: I will seek thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	146	I cried unto thee, save me: that I may keep thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	147	I prevented the dawning of the day, and cried: because in thy words I very much hoped.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	148	My eyes to thee have prevented the morning: that I might meditate on thy words.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	149	Hear thou my voice, O Lord, according to thy mercy: and quicken me according to thy mercy.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	150	They that persecute me have drawn nigh to iniquity; but they are gone far off from thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	151	Thou art near, O Lord: and all thy ways are truth.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	152	I have known from the beginning concerning thy testimonies: that thou hast founded them for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	153	<Res>See my humiliation and deliver me: for I have not forgotten thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	154	Judge my judgment and redeem me: quicken thou me for thy word's sake.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	155	Salvation is far from sinners; because they have not sought thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	156	Many, O Lord, are thy mercies: quicken me according to thy judgment.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	157	Many are they that persecute me, and afflict me; but I have not declined from thy testimonies.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	158	I beheld the transgressors, and I pined away; because they kept not thy word.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	159	Behold I have loved thy commandments, O Lord; quicken me thou in thy mercy.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	160	The beginning of thy words is truth: all the judgments of thy justice are for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	161	<Sin>Princes have persecuted me without cause: and my heart hath been in awe of thy words.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	162	I will rejoice at thy words, as one that hath found great spoil.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	163	I have hated and abhorred iniquity; but I have loved thy law.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	164	Seven times a day I have given praise to thee, for the judgments of thy justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	165	Much peace have they that love thy law, and to them there is no stumbling block.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	166	I looked to thy salvation, O Lord: and I loved thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	167	My soul hath kept thy testimonies: and hath loved them exceedingly.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	168	I have kept thy commandments and thy testimonies: because all my ways are in thy sight.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	169	<Tau>Let my supplication, O Lord, come near in thy sight: give me understanding according to thy word.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	170	Let my request come in before thee; deliver thou me according to thy word.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	171	My lips shall utter a hymn, when thou shalt teach me thy justifications.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	172	My tongue shall pronounce thy word: because all thy commandments are justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	173	Let thy hand be with me to save me; for I have chosen thy precepts.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	174	I have longed for thy salvation, O Lord; and thy law is my meditation.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	175	My soul shall live and shall praise thee: and thy judgments shall help me.
Psalms	Ps	21	118	176	I have gone astray like a sheep that is lost: seek thy servant, because I have not forgotten thy commandments.
Psalms	Ps	21	119	1	In my trouble I cried to the Lord: and he heard me.
Psalms	Ps	21	119	2	O Lord, deliver my soul from wicked lips, and a deceitful tongue.
Psalms	Ps	21	119	3	What shall be given to thee, or what shall be added to thee, to a deceitful tongue?
Psalms	Ps	21	119	4	The sharp arrows of the mighty, with coals that lay waste.
Psalms	Ps	21	119	5	Woe is me, that my sojourning is prolonged! I have dwelt with the inhabitants of Cedar:
Psalms	Ps	21	119	6	My soul hath been long a sojourner.
Psalms	Ps	21	119	7	With them that hated peace I was peaceable: when I spoke to them they fought against me without cause.
Psalms	Ps	21	120	1	I have lifted up my eyes to the mountains, from whence help shall come to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	120	2	My help is from the Lord, who made heaven and earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	120	3	May he not suffer thy foot to be moved: neither let him slumber that keepeth thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	120	4	Behold he shall neither slumber nor sleep, that keepeth Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	120	5	The Lord is thy keeper, the Lord is thy protection upon thy right hand.
Psalms	Ps	21	120	6	The sun shall not burn thee by day: nor the moon by night.
Psalms	Ps	21	120	7	The Lord keepeth thee from all evil: may the Lord keep thy soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	120	8	May the Lord keep thy coming in and thy going out; from henceforth now and for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	121	1	I rejoiced at the things that were said to me: We shall go into the house of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	121	2	Our feet were standing in thy courts, O Jerusalem.
Psalms	Ps	21	121	3	Jerusalem, which is built as a city, which is compact together.
Psalms	Ps	21	121	4	For thither did the tribes go up, the tribes of the Lord: the testimony of Israel, to praise the name of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	121	5	Because their seats have sat in judgment, seats upon the house of David.
Psalms	Ps	21	121	6	Pray ye for the things that are for the peace of Jerusalem: and abundance for them that love thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	121	7	Let peace be in thy strength: and abundance in thy towers.
Psalms	Ps	21	121	8	For the sake of my brethren, and of my neighbours, I spoke peace of thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	121	9	Because of the house of the Lord our God, I have sought good things for thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	122	1	To thee have I lifted up my eyes, who dwellest in heaven.
Psalms	Ps	21	122	2	Behold as the eyes of servants are on the hands of their masters, As the eyes of the handmaid are on the hands of her mistress: so are our eyes unto the Lord our God, until he have mercy on us.
Psalms	Ps	21	122	3	Have mercy on us, O Lord, have mercy on us: for we are greatly filled with contempt.
Psalms	Ps	21	122	4	For our soul is greatly filled: we are a reproach to the rich, and contempt to the proud.
Psalms	Ps	21	123	1	If it had not been that the Lord was with us, let Israel now say:
Psalms	Ps	21	123	2	If it had not been that the Lord was with us, When men rose up against us,
Psalms	Ps	21	123	3	Perhaps they had swallowed us up alive. When their fury was enkindled against us,
Psalms	Ps	21	123	4	Perhaps the waters had swallowed us up.
Psalms	Ps	21	123	5	Our soul hath passed through a torrent: perhaps our soul had passed through a water insupportable.
Psalms	Ps	21	123	6	Blessed be the Lord, who hath not given us to be a prey to their teeth.
Psalms	Ps	21	123	7	Our soul hath been delivered as a sparrow out of the snare of the fowlers. The snare is broken, and we are delivered.
Psalms	Ps	21	123	8	Our help is in the name of the Lord, who made heaven and earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	124	1	They that trust in the Lord shall be as mount Sion: he shall not be moved for ever that dwelleth
Psalms	Ps	21	124	2	In Jerusalem. Mountains are round about it: so the Lord is round about his people from henceforth now and for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	124	3	For the Lord will not leave the rod of sinners upon the lot of the just: that the just may not stretch forth their hands to iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	124	4	Do good, O Lord, to those that are good, and to the upright of heart.
Psalms	Ps	21	124	5	But such as turn aside into bonds, the Lord shall lead out with the workers of iniquity: peace upon Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	125	1	When the Lord brought back the captivity of Sion, we became like men comforted.
Psalms	Ps	21	125	2	Then was our mouth filled with gladness; and our tongue with joy. Then shall they say among the Gentiles: The Lord hath done great things for them.
Psalms	Ps	21	125	3	The Lord hath done great things for us: we are become joyful.
Psalms	Ps	21	125	4	Turn again our captivity, O Lord, as a stream in the south.
Psalms	Ps	21	125	5	They that sow in tears shall reap in joy.
Psalms	Ps	21	125	6	Going they went and wept, casting their seeds.
Psalms	Ps	21	125	7	But coming they shall come with joyfulness, carrying their sheaves.
Psalms	Ps	21	126	1	Unless the Lord build the house, they labour in vain that build it. Unless the Lord keep the city, he watcheth in vain that keepeth it.
Psalms	Ps	21	126	2	It is vain for you to rise before light, rise ye after you have sitten, you that eat the bread of sorrow. When he shall give sleep to his beloved,
Psalms	Ps	21	126	3	Behold the inheritance of the Lord are children: the reward, the fruit of the womb.
Psalms	Ps	21	126	4	As arrows in the hand of the mighty, so the children of them that have been shaken.
Psalms	Ps	21	126	5	Blessed is the man that hath filled the desire with them; he shall not be confounded when he shall speak to his enemies in the gate.
Psalms	Ps	21	127	1	Blessed are all they that fear the Lord: that walk in his ways.
Psalms	Ps	21	127	2	For thou shalt eat the labours of thy hands: blessed art thou, and it shall be well with thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	127	3	Thy wife as a fruitful vine, on the sides of thy house. Thy children as olive plants, round about thy table.
Psalms	Ps	21	127	4	Behold, thus shall the man be blessed that feareth the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	127	5	May the Lord bless thee out of Sion: and mayest thou see the good things of Jerusalem all the days of thy life.
Psalms	Ps	21	127	6	And mayest thou see thy children's children, peace upon Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	128	1	Often have they fought against me from my youth, let Israel now say.
Psalms	Ps	21	128	2	Often have they fought against me from my youth: but they could not prevail over me.
Psalms	Ps	21	128	3	The wicked have wrought upon my back: they have lengthened their iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	128	4	The Lord who is just will cut the necks of sinners:
Psalms	Ps	21	128	5	Let them all be confounded and turned back that hate Sion.
Psalms	Ps	21	128	6	Let them be as grass on the tops of houses: which withered before it be plucked up:
Psalms	Ps	21	128	7	Wherewith the mower filleth not his hand: nor he that gathereth sheaves his bosom.
Psalms	Ps	21	128	8	And they that have passed by have not said: The blessing of the Lord be upon you: we have blessed you in the name of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	129	1	Out of the depths I have cried to thee, O Lord:
Psalms	Ps	21	129	2	Lord, hear my voice. Let thy ears be attentive to the voice of my supplication.
Psalms	Ps	21	129	3	If thou, O Lord, wilt mark iniquities: Lord, who shall stand it.
Psalms	Ps	21	129	4	For with thee there is merciful forgiveness: and by reason of thy law, I have waited for thee, O Lord. My soul hath relied on his word:
Psalms	Ps	21	129	5	My soul hath hoped in the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	129	6	From the morning watch even until night, let Israel hope in the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	129	7	Because with the Lord there is mercy: and with him plentiful redemption.
Psalms	Ps	21	129	8	And he shall redeem Israel from all his iniquities.
Psalms	Ps	21	130	1	Lord, my heart is not exalted: nor are my eyes lofty. Neither have I walked in great matters, nor in wonderful things above me.
Psalms	Ps	21	130	2	If I was not humbly minded, but exalted my soul: As a child that is weaned is towards his mother, so reward in my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	130	3	Let Israel hope in the Lord, from henceforth now and for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	1	O Lord, remember David, and all his meekness.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	2	How he swore to the Lord, he vowed a vow to the God of Jacob:
Psalms	Ps	21	131	3	If I shall enter into the tabernacle of my house: if I shall go up into the bed wherein I lie:
Psalms	Ps	21	131	4	If I shall give sleep to my eyes, or slumber to my eyelids,
Psalms	Ps	21	131	5	Or rest to my temples: until I find out a place for the Lord, a tabernacle for the God of Jacob.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	6	Behold we have heard of it in Ephrata: we have found it in the fields of the wood.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	7	We will go into his tabernacle: We will adore in the place where his feet stood.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	8	Arise, O Lord, into thy resting place: thou and the ark, which thou hast sanctified.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	9	Let thy priests be clothed with justice: and let thy saints rejoice.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	10	For thy servant David's sake, turn not away the face of thy anointed.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	11	The Lord hath sworn truth to David, and he will not make it void: of the fruit of thy womb I will set upon thy throne.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	12	If thy children will keep thy covenant, and these my testimonies which I shall teach them: Their children also for evermore shall sit upon thy throne.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	13	For the Lord hath chosen Sion: he hath chosen it for his dwelling.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	14	This is my rest for ever and ever: here will I dwell, for I have chosen it.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	15	Blessing, I will bless her widow: I will satisfy her poor with bread.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	16	I will clothe her priests with salvation: and her saints shall rejoice with exceeding great joy.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	17	There will I bring forth a horn to David: I have prepared a lamp for my anointed.
Psalms	Ps	21	131	18	His enemies I will clothe with confusion: but upon him will my sanctification flourish.
Psalms	Ps	21	132	1	Behold how good and how pleasant it is for brethren to dwell in unity.
Psalms	Ps	21	132	2	Like the precious ointment on the head, that ran down upon the beard, the beard of Aaron, Which ran down to the skirt of his garment:
Psalms	Ps	21	132	3	As the dew of Hermon, which descendeth upon mount Sion. For there the Lord hath commandeth blessing, and life for evermore.
Psalms	Ps	21	133	1	Behold now bless ye the Lord, all ye servants of the Lord: Who stand in the house of the Lord, in the courts of the house of our God.
Psalms	Ps	21	133	2	In the nights lift up your hands to the holy places, and bless ye the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	133	3	May the Lord out of Sion bless thee, he that made heaven and earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	1	Praise ye the name of the Lord: O you his servants, praise the Lord:
Psalms	Ps	21	134	2	You that stand in the house of the Lord, in the courts of the house of our God.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	3	Praise ye the Lord, for the Lord is good: sing ye to his name, for it is sweet.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	4	For the Lord hath chosen Jacob unto himself: Israel for his own possession.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	5	For I have known that the Lord is great, and our God is above all gods.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	6	Whatsoever the Lord hath pleased he hath done, in heaven, in earth, in the sea, and in all the deeps.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	7	He bringeth up clouds from the end of the earth: he hath made lightnings for the rain. He bringeth forth winds out of his stores:
Psalms	Ps	21	134	8	He slew the firstborn of Egypt from man even unto beast.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	9	He sent forth signs and wonders in the midst of thee, O Egypt: upon Pharao, and upon all his servants.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	10	He smote many nations, and slew mighty kings:
Psalms	Ps	21	134	11	Sehon king of the Amorrhites, and Og king of Basan, and all the kingdoms of Chanaan.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	12	And gave their land for an inheritance, for an inheritance to his people Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	13	Thy name, O Lord, is for ever: thy memorial, O Lord, unto all generations.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	14	For the Lord will judge his people, and will be entreated in favour of his servants.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	15	The idols of the Gentiles are silver and gold, the works of men's hands.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	16	They have a mouth, but they speak not: they have eyes, but they see not.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	17	They have ears, but they hear not: neither is there any breath in their mouths.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	18	Let them that make them be like to them: and every one that trusteth in them.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	19	Bless the Lord, O house of Israel: bless the Lord, O house of Aaron.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	20	Bless the Lord, O house of Levi: you that fear the Lord, bless the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	134	21	Blessed be the Lord out of Sion, who dwelleth in Jerusalem.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	1	Praise the Lord, for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	2	Praise ye the God of gods: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	3	Praise ye the Lord of lords: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	4	Who alone doth great wonders: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	5	Who made the heavens in understanding: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	6	Who established the earth above the waters: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	7	Who made the great lights: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	8	The sun to rule over the day: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	9	The moon and the stars to rule the night: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	10	Who smote Egypt with their firstborn: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	11	Who brought out Israel from among them: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	12	With a mighty hand and a stretched out arm: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	13	Who divided the Red Sea into parts: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	14	And brought out Israel through the midst thereof: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	15	And overthrew Pharao and his host in the Red Sea: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	16	Who led his people through the desert: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	17	Who smote great kings: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	18	And slew strong kings: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	19	Sehon king of the Amorrhites: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	20	And Og king of Basan: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	21	And he gave their land for an inheritance: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	22	For an inheritance to his servant Israel: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	23	For he was mindful of us in our affliction: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	24	And he redeemed us from our enemies: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	25	Who giveth food to all flesh: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	26	Give glory to the God of heaven: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	135	27	Give glory to the Lord of lords: for his mercy endureth for ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	136	1	Upon the rivers of Babylon, there we sat and wept: when we remembered Sion:
Psalms	Ps	21	136	2	On the willows in the midst thereof we hung up our instruments.
Psalms	Ps	21	136	3	For there they that led us into captivity required of us the words of songs. And they that carried us away, said: Sing ye to us a hymn of the songs of Sion.
Psalms	Ps	21	136	4	How shall we sing the song of the Lord in a strange land?
Psalms	Ps	21	136	5	If I forget thee, O Jerusalem, let my right hand be forgotten.
Psalms	Ps	21	136	6	Let my tongue cleave to my jaws, if I do not remember thee: If I make not Jerusalem the beginning of my joy.
Psalms	Ps	21	136	7	Remember, O Lord, the children of Edom, in the day of Jerusalem: Who say: Rase it, rase it, even to the foundation thereof.
Psalms	Ps	21	136	8	O daughter of Babylon, miserable: blessed shall he be who shall repay thee thy payment which thou hast paid us.
Psalms	Ps	21	136	9	Blessed be he that shall take and dash thy little ones against the rock.
Psalms	Ps	21	137	1	I will praise thee, O Lord, with my whole heart: for thou hast heard the words of my mouth. I will sing praise to thee in the sight of his angels:
Psalms	Ps	21	137	2	I will worship towards thy holy temple, and I will give glory to thy name. For thy mercy, and for thy truth: for thou hast magnified thy holy name above all.
Psalms	Ps	21	137	3	In what day soever I shall call upon thee, hear me: thou shall multiply strength in my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	137	4	May all the kings of the earth give glory to thee: for they have heard all the words of thy mouth.
Psalms	Ps	21	137	5	And let them sing in the ways of the Lord: for great is the glory of the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	137	6	For the Lord is high, and looketh on the low: and the high he knoweth afar off.
Psalms	Ps	21	137	7	If I shall walk in the midst of tribulation, thou wilt quicken me: and thou hast stretched forth thy hand against the wrath of my enemies: and thy right hand hath saved me.
Psalms	Ps	21	137	8	The Lord will repay for me: thy mercy, O Lord, endureth for ever: O despise not the work of thy hands.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	1	Lord, thou hast proved me, and known me:
Psalms	Ps	21	138	2	Thou hast known my sitting down, and my rising up.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	3	Thou hast understood my thoughts afar off: my path and my line thou hast searched out.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	4	And thou hast foreseen all my ways: for there is no speech in my tongue.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	5	Behold, O Lord, thou hast known all things, the last and those of old: thou hast formed me, and hast laid thy hand upon me.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	6	Thy knowledge is become wonderful to me: it is high, and I cannot reach to it.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	7	Whither shall I go from thy spirit? or whither shall I flee from thy face?
Psalms	Ps	21	138	8	If I ascend into heaven, thou art there: if I descend into hell, thou art present.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	9	If I take my wings early in the morning, and dwell in the uttermost parts of the sea:
Psalms	Ps	21	138	10	Even there also shall thy hand lead me: and thy right hand shall hold me.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	11	And I said: Perhaps darkness shall cover me: and night shall be my light in my pleasures.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	12	But darkness shall not be dark to thee, and night shall be light as day: the darkness thereof, and the light thereof are alike to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	13	For thou hast possessed my reins: thou hast protected me from my mother's womb.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	14	I will praise thee, for thou art fearfully magnified: wonderful are thy works, and my soul knoweth right well.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	15	My bone is not hidden from thee, which thou hast made in secret: and my substance in the lower parts of the earth.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	16	Thy eyes did see my imperfect being, and in thy book all shall be written: days shall be formed, and no one in them.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	17	But to me thy friends, O God, are made exceedingly honourable: their principality is exceedingly strengthened.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	18	I will number them, and they shall be multiplied above the sand: I rose up and am still with thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	19	If thou wilt kill the wicked, O God: ye men of blood, depart from me:
Psalms	Ps	21	138	20	Because you say in thought: They shall receive thy cities in vain.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	21	Have I not hated them, O Lord, that hated thee: and pine away because of thy enemies?
Psalms	Ps	21	138	22	I have hated them with a perfect hatred: and they are become enemies to me.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	23	Prove me, O God, and know my heart: examine me, and know my paths.
Psalms	Ps	21	138	24	And see if there be in me the way of iniquity: and lead me in the eternal way.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	1	[Unto the end, a psalm for David.]
Psalms	Ps	21	139	2	Deliver me, O Lord, from the evil man: rescue me from the unjust man.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	3	Who have devised iniquities in their hearts: all the day long they designed battles.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	4	They have sharpened their tongues like a serpent: the venom of asps is under their lips.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	5	Keep me, O Lord, from the hand of the wicked: and from unjust men deliver me. Who have proposed to supplant my steps.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	6	The proud have hidden a net for me. And they have stretched out cords for a snare: they have laid for me a stumblingblock by the wayside.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	7	I said to the Lord: Thou art my God: hear, O Lord, the voice of my supplication.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	8	O Lord, Lord, the strength of my salvation: thou hast overshadowed my head in the day of battle.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	9	Give me not up, O Lord, from my desire to the wicked: they have plotted against me; do not thou forsake me, lest they should triumph.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	10	The head of them compassing me about: the labour of their lips shall overwhelm them.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	11	Burning coals shall fall upon them; thou wilt cast them down into the fire: in miseries they shall not be able to stand.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	12	A man full of tongue shall not be established in the earth: evil shall catch the unjust man unto destruction.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	13	I know that the Lord will do justice to the needy, and will revenge the poor.
Psalms	Ps	21	139	14	But as for the just, they shall give glory to thy name: and the upright shall dwell with thy countenance.
Psalms	Ps	21	140	1	I have cried to thee, O Lord, hear me: hearken to my voice, when I cry to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	140	2	Let my prayer be directed as incense in thy sight; the lifting up of my hands, as evening sacrifice.
Psalms	Ps	21	140	3	Set a watch, O Lord, before my mouth: and a door round about my lips.
Psalms	Ps	21	140	4	Incline not my heart to evil words; to make excuses in sins. With men that work iniquity: and I will not communicate with the choicest of them.
Psalms	Ps	21	140	5	The just shall correct me in mercy, and shall reprove me: but let not the oil of the sinner fatten my head. For my prayer also shall still be against the things with which they are well pleased:
Psalms	Ps	21	140	6	Their judges falling upon the rock have been swallowed up. They shall hear my words, for they have prevailed:
Psalms	Ps	21	140	7	As when the thickness of the earth is broken up upon the ground: Our bones are scattered by the side of hell.
Psalms	Ps	21	140	8	But o to thee, O Lord, Lord, are my eyes: in thee have I put my trust, take not away my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	140	9	Keep me from the snare, which they have laid for me, and from the stumblingblocks of them that work iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	140	10	The wicked shall fall in his net: I am alone until I pass.
Psalms	Ps	21	141	1	[Of understanding for David. A prayer when he was in the cave.]
Psalms	Ps	21	141	2	I cried to the Lord with my voice: with my voice I made supplication to the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	141	3	In his sight I pour out my prayer, and before him I declare my trouble:
Psalms	Ps	21	141	4	When my spirit failed me, then thou knewest my paths. In this way wherein I walked, they have hidden a snare for me.
Psalms	Ps	21	141	5	I looked on my right hand, and beheld, and there was no one that would know me. Flight hath failed me: and there is no one that hath regard to my soul.
Psalms	Ps	21	141	6	I cried to thee, O Lord: I said: Thou art my hope, my portion in the land of the living.
Psalms	Ps	21	141	7	Attend to my supplication: for I am brought very low. Deliver me from my persecutors; for they are stronger than I.
Psalms	Ps	21	141	8	Bring my soul out of prison, that I may praise thy name: the just wait for me, until thou reward me.
Psalms	Ps	21	142	1	Hear, O Lord, my prayer: give ear to my supplication in thy truth: hear me in thy justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	142	2	And enter not into judgment with thy servant: for in thy sight no man living shall be justified.
Psalms	Ps	21	142	3	For the enemy hath persecuted my soul: he hath brought down my life to the earth. He hath made me to dwell in darkness as those that have been dead of old:
Psalms	Ps	21	142	4	And my spirit is in anguish within me: my heart within me is troubled.
Psalms	Ps	21	142	5	I remembered the days of old, I meditated on all thy works: I meditated upon the works of thy hands.
Psalms	Ps	21	142	6	I stretched forth my hands to thee: my soul is as earth without water unto thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	142	7	Hear me speedily, O Lord: my spirit hath fainted away. Turn not away thy face from me, lest I be like unto them that go down into the pit.
Psalms	Ps	21	142	8	Cause me to hear thy mercy in the morning; for in thee have I hoped. Make the way known to me, wherein I should walk: for I have lifted up my soul to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	142	9	Deliver me from my enemies, O Lord, to thee have I fled:
Psalms	Ps	21	142	10	Teach me to do thy will, for thou art my God. Thy good spirit shall lead me into the right land:
Psalms	Ps	21	142	11	For thy name's sake, O Lord, thou wilt quicken me in thy justice. Thou wilt bring my soul out of trouble:
Psalms	Ps	21	142	12	And in thy mercy thou wilt destroy my enemies. And thou wilt cut off all them that afflict my soul: for I am thy servant.
Psalms	Ps	21	143	1	Blessed be the Lord my God, who teacheth my hands to fight, and my fingers to war.
Psalms	Ps	21	143	2	My mercy, and my refuge: my support, and my deliverer: My protector, and I have hoped in him: who subdueth my people under me.
Psalms	Ps	21	143	3	Lord, what is man, that thou art made known to him? or the son of man, that thou makest account of him?
Psalms	Ps	21	143	4	Man is like to vanity: his days pass away like a shadow.
Psalms	Ps	21	143	5	Lord, bow down thy heavens and descend: touch the mountains and they shall smoke.
Psalms	Ps	21	143	6	Send forth lightning, and thou shalt scatter them: shoot out thy arrows, and thou shalt trouble them.
Psalms	Ps	21	143	7	Put forth thy hand from on high, take me out, and deliver me from many waters: from the hand of strange children:
Psalms	Ps	21	143	8	Whose mouth hath spoken vanity: and their right hand is the right hand of iniquity.
Psalms	Ps	21	143	9	To thee, O God, I will sing a new canticle: on the psaltery and an instrument of ten strings I will sing praises to thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	143	10	Who givest salvation to kings: who hast redeemed thy servant David from the malicious sword:
Psalms	Ps	21	143	11	Deliver me, And rescue me out of the hand of strange children; whose mouth hath spoken vanity: and their right hand is the right hand of iniquity:
Psalms	Ps	21	143	12	Whose sons are as new plants in their youth: Their daughters decked out, adorned round about after the similitude of a temple:
Psalms	Ps	21	143	13	Their storehouses full, flowing out of this into that. Their sheep fruitful in young, abounding in their goings forth:
Psalms	Ps	21	143	14	Their oxen fat. There is no breach of wall, nor passage, nor crying out in their streets.
Psalms	Ps	21	143	15	They have called the people happy, that hath these things: but happy is that people whose God is the Lord.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	1	I will extol thee, O God my king: and I will bless thy name for ever; yea, for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	2	Every day I will bless thee: and I will praise thy name for ever; yea, for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	3	Great is the Lord, and greatly to be praised: and of his greatness there is no end.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	4	Generation and generation shall praise thy works: and they shall declare thy power.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	5	They shall speak of the magnificence of the glory of thy holiness: and shall tell thy wondrous works.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	6	And they shall speak of the might of thy terrible acts: and shall declare thy greatness.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	7	They shall publish the memory of the abundance of thy sweetness: and shall rejoice in thy justice.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	8	The Lord is gracious and merciful: patient and plenteous in mercy.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	9	The Lord is sweet to all: and his tender mercies are over all his works.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	10	Let all thy works, O lord, praise thee: and let thy saints bless thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	11	They shall speak of the glory of thy kingdom: and shall tell of thy power:
Psalms	Ps	21	144	12	To make thy might known to the sons of men: and the glory of the magnificence of thy kingdom.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	13	Thy kingdom is a kingdom of all ages: and thy dominion endureth throughout all generations. The Lord is faithful in all his words: and holy in all his works.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	14	The Lord lifteth up all that fall: and setteth up all that are cast down.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	15	The eyes of all hope in thee, O Lord: and thou givest them meat in due season.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	16	Thou openest thy hand, and fillest with blessing every living creature.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	17	The Lord is just in all his ways: and holy in all his works.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	18	The Lord is nigh unto all them that call upon him: to all that call upon him in truth.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	19	He will do the will of them that fear him: and he will hear their prayer, and save them.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	20	The Lord keepeth all them that love him; but all the wicked he will destroy.
Psalms	Ps	21	144	21	My mouth shall speak the praise of the Lord: and let all flesh bless thy holy name for ever; yea, for ever and ever.
Psalms	Ps	21	145	1	[Alleluia, of Aggeus and Zacharias.]
Psalms	Ps	21	145	2	Praise the Lord, O my soul, in my life I will praise the Lord: I will sing to my God as long as I shall be. Put not your trust in princes:
Psalms	Ps	21	145	3	In the children of men, in whom there is no salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	145	4	His spirit shall go forth, and he shall return into his earth: in that day all their thoughts shall perish.
Psalms	Ps	21	145	5	Blessed is he who hath the God of Jacob for his helper, whose hope is in the Lord his God:
Psalms	Ps	21	145	6	Who made heaven and earth, the sea, and all things that are in them.
Psalms	Ps	21	145	7	Who keepeth truth for ever: who executeth judgment for them that suffer wrong: who giveth food to the hungry. The Lord looseth them that are fettered:
Psalms	Ps	21	145	8	The Lord enlighteneth the blind. The Lord lifteth up them that are cast down: the Lord loveth the just.
Psalms	Ps	21	145	9	The Lord keepeth the strangers, he will support the fatherless and the widow: and the ways of sinners he will destroy.
Psalms	Ps	21	145	10	The Lord shall reign for ever: thy God, O Sion, unto generation and generation.
Psalms	Ps	21	146	1	Praise ye the Lord, because psalm is good: to our God be joyful and comely praise.
Psalms	Ps	21	146	2	The Lord buildeth up Jerusalem: he will gather together the dispersed of Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	146	3	Who healeth the broken of heart, and bindeth up their bruises.
Psalms	Ps	21	146	4	Who telleth the number of the stars: and calleth them all by their names.
Psalms	Ps	21	146	5	Great is our Lord, and great is his power: and of his wisdom there is no number.
Psalms	Ps	21	146	6	The Lord lifteth up the meek, and bringeth the wicked down even to the ground.
Psalms	Ps	21	146	7	Sing ye to the Lord with praise: sing to our God upon the harp.
Psalms	Ps	21	146	8	Who covereth the heaven with clouds, and prepareth rain for the earth. Who maketh grass to grow on the mountains, and herbs for the service of men.
Psalms	Ps	21	146	9	Who giveth to beasts their food: and to the young ravens that call upon him.
Psalms	Ps	21	146	10	He shall not delight in the strength of the horse: nor take pleasure in the legs of a man.
Psalms	Ps	21	146	11	The Lord taketh pleasure in them that fear him: and in them that hope in his mercy.
Psalms	Ps	21	147	12	Praise the Lord, O Jerusalem: praise thy God, O Sion.
Psalms	Ps	21	147	13	Because he hath strengthened the bolts of thy gates, he hath blessed thy children within thee.
Psalms	Ps	21	147	14	Who hath placed peace in thy borders: and filleth thee with the fat of corn.
Psalms	Ps	21	147	15	Who sendeth forth his speech to the earth: his word runneth swiftly.
Psalms	Ps	21	147	16	Who giveth snow like wool: scattereth mists like ashes.
Psalms	Ps	21	147	17	He sendeth his crystal like morsels: who shall stand before the face of his cold?
Psalms	Ps	21	147	18	He shall send out his word, and shall melt them: his wind shall blow, and the waters shall run.
Psalms	Ps	21	147	19	Who declareth his word to Jacob: his justices and his judgments to Israel.
Psalms	Ps	21	147	20	He hath not done in like manner to every nation: and his judgments he hath not made manifest to them. Alleluia.
Psalms	Ps	21	148	1	Praise ye the Lord from the heavens: praise ye him in the high places.
Psalms	Ps	21	148	2	Praise ye him, all his angels: praise ye him, all his hosts.
Psalms	Ps	21	148	3	Praise ye him, O sun and moon: praise him, all ye stars and light.
Psalms	Ps	21	148	4	Praise him, ye heavens of heavens: and let all the waters that are above the heavens
Psalms	Ps	21	148	5	Praise the name of the Lord. For he spoke, and they were made: he commanded, and they were created.
Psalms	Ps	21	148	6	He hath established them for ever, and for ages of ages: he hath made a decree, and it shall not pass away.
Psalms	Ps	21	148	7	Praise the Lord from the earth, ye dragons, and all ye deeps:
Psalms	Ps	21	148	8	Fire, hail, snow, ice, stormy winds which fulfill his word:
Psalms	Ps	21	148	9	Mountains and all hills, fruitful trees and all cedars:
Psalms	Ps	21	148	10	Beasts and all cattle: serpents and feathered fowls:
Psalms	Ps	21	148	11	Kings of the earth and all people: princes and all judges of the earth:
Psalms	Ps	21	148	12	Young men and maidens: let the old with the younger, praise the name of the Lord:
Psalms	Ps	21	148	13	For his name alone is exalted.
Psalms	Ps	21	148	14	The praise of him is above heaven and earth: and he hath exalted the horn of his people. A hymn to all his saints: to the children of Israel, a people approaching to him. Alleluia.
Psalms	Ps	21	149	1	Sing ye to the Lord a new canticle: let his praise be in the church of the saints.
Psalms	Ps	21	149	2	Let Israel rejoice in him that made him: and let the children of Sion be joyful in their king.
Psalms	Ps	21	149	3	Let them praise his name in choir: let them sing to him with the timbrel and the psaltery.
Psalms	Ps	21	149	4	For the Lord is well pleased with his people: and he will exalt the meek unto salvation.
Psalms	Ps	21	149	5	The saints shall rejoice in glory: they shall be joyful in their beds.
Psalms	Ps	21	149	6	The high praise of God shall be in their mouth: and two-edged swords in their hands:
Psalms	Ps	21	149	7	To execute vengeance upon the nations, chastisements among the people:
Psalms	Ps	21	149	8	To bind their kings with fetters, and their nobles with manacles of iron.
Psalms	Ps	21	149	9	To execute upon them the judgment that is written: this glory is to all his saints. Alleluia.
Psalms	Ps	21	150	1	Praise ye the Lord in his holy places: praise ye him in the firmament of his power.
Psalms	Ps	21	150	2	Praise ye him for his mighty acts: praise ye him according to the multitude of his greatness.
Psalms	Ps	21	150	3	Praise him with sound of trumpet: praise him with psaltery and harp.
Psalms	Ps	21	150	4	Praise him with timbrel and choir: praise him with strings and organs.
Psalms	Ps	21	150	5	Praise him on high sounding cymbals: praise him on cymbals of joy: let every spirit praise the Lord. Alleluia.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	1	The parables of Solomon, the son of David, king of Israel.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	2	To know wisdom, and instruction:
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	3	To understand the words of prudence: and to receive the instruction of doctrine, justice, and judgment, and equity:
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	4	To give subtilty to little ones, to the young man knowledge and understanding.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	5	A wise man shall hear and shall be wiser: and he that understandeth, shall possess governments.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	6	He shall understand a parable, and the interpretation, the words of the wise, and their mysterious sayings.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	7	The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom. Fools despise wisdom and instruction.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	8	My son, hear the instruction of thy father, and forsake not the law of thy mother:
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	9	That grace may be added to thy head, and a chain of gold to thy neck.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	10	My son, if sinners shall entice thee, consent not to them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	11	If they shall say: Come with us, let us lie in wait for blood, let us hide snares for the innocent without cause:
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	12	Let us swallow him up alive like hell, and whole as one that goeth down into the pit.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	13	We shall find all precious substance, we shall fill our houses with spoils.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	14	Cast in thy lot with us, let us all have one purse.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	15	My son, walk not thou with them, restrain thy foot from their paths.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	16	For their feet run to evil, and make haste to shed blood.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	17	But a net is spread in vain before the eyes of them that have wings.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	18	And they themselves lie in wait for their own blood, and practise deceits against their own souls.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	19	So the wage of every covetous man destroy the souls of the possessors.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	20	Wisdom preacheth abroad, she uttereth her voice in the streets:
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	21	At the head of multitudes she crieth out, in the entrance of the gates of the city she uttereth her words, saying:
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	22	O children, how long will you love childishness, and fools covet those things which are hurtful to themselves, and the unwise hate knowledge?
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	23	Turn ye at my reproof: behold I will utter my spirit to you, and will shew you my words.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	24	Because I called, and you refused: I stretched out my hand, and there was none that regarded.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	25	You have despised all my counsel, and have neglected my reprehensions.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	26	I also will laugh in your destruction, and will mock when that shall come to you which you feared.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	27	When sudden calamity shall fall on you, and destruction, as a tempest, shall be at hand: when tribulation and distress shall come upon you:
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	28	Then shall they call upon me, and I will not hear: they shall rise in the morning and shall not find me:
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	29	Because they have hated instruction and received not the fear of the Lord,
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	30	Nor consented to my counsel, but despised all my reproof.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	31	Therefore they shall eat the fruit of their own way, and shall be filled with their own devices.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	32	The turning away of little ones shall kill them, and the prosperity of fools shall destroy them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	1	33	But he that shall hear me, shall rest without terror, and shall enjoy abundance, without fear of evils.
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	1	My son, if thou wilt receive my words, and wilt hide my commandments with thee,
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	2	That thy ear may hearken to wisdom: Incline thy heart to know prudence:
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	3	For if thou shalt call for wisdom, and incline thy heart to prudence:
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	4	If thou shalt seek her as money, and shalt dig for her as for a treasure:
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	5	Then shalt thou understand the fear of the Lord, and shalt find the knowledge of God.
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	6	Because the Lord giveth wisdom: and out of his mouth cometh prudence and knowledge.
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	7	He will keep the salvation of the righteous, and protect them that walk in simplicity.
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	8	Keeping the paths of justice, and guarding the ways of saints.
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	9	Then shalt thou understand justice, and judgment, and equity, and every good path.
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	10	If wisdom shall enter into thy heart, and knowledge please thy soul:
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	11	Counsel shall keep thee, and prudence shall preserve thee,
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	12	That thou mayst be delivered from the evil way, and from the man that speaketh perverse things:
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	13	Who leave the right way, and walk by dark ways:
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	14	Who are glad when they have done evil, and rejoice in most wicked things:
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	15	Whose ways are perverse, and their steps infamous.
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	16	That thou mayst be delivered from the strange women, and from the stranger, who softeneth her words:
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	17	And forsaketh the guide of her youth,
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	18	And hath forgotten the covenant of her God: for her house inclineth unto death, and her paths to hell.
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	19	None that go in unto her shall return again, neither shall they take hold of the paths of life,
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	20	That thou mayst walk in a good way: and mayst keep the paths of the just.
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	21	For they that are upright shall dwell in the earth, and the simple shall continue in it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	2	22	But the wicked shall be destroyed from the earth: and they that do unjustly shall be taken away from it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	1	My son, forget not my law, and let thy heart keep my commandments.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	2	For they shall add to thee length of days, and years of life and peace.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	3	Let not mercy and truth leave thee, put them about thy neck, and write them in the tables of thy heart:
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	4	And thou shalt find grace and good understanding before God and men.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	5	Have confidence in the Lord with all thy heart, and lean not upon thy own prudence.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	6	In all thy ways think on him, and he will direct thy steps.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	7	Be not wise in thy own conceit: fear God, and depart from evil:
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	8	For it shall be health to thy navel, and moistening to thy bones.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	9	Honour the Lord with thy substance, and give him of the first of all thy fruits:
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	10	And thy barns shall be filled with abundance, and thy presses shall run over with wine.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	11	My son, reject not the correction of the Lord: and do not faint when thou art chastised by him:
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	12	For whom the Lord loveth, he chastiseth: and as a father in the son he pleaseth himself.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	13	Blessed is the man that findeth wisdom and is rich in prudence:
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	14	The purchasing thereof is better than the merchandise of silver, and her fruit than the chiefest and purest gold:
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	15	She is more precious than all riches: and all the things that are desired, are not to be compared with her.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	16	Length of days is in her right hand, and in her left hand riches and glory.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	17	Her ways are beautiful ways, and all her paths are peaceable.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	18	She is a tree of life to them that lay hold on her: and he that shall retain her is blessed.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	19	The Lord by wisdom hath founded the earth, hath established the heavens by prudence.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	20	By his wisdom the depths have broken out, and the clouds grow thick with dew.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	21	My son, let not these things depart from thy eyes: keep the law and counsel:
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	22	And there shall be life to thy soul, and grace to thy mouth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	23	Then shalt thou walk confidently in thy way, and thy foot shall not stumble:
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	24	If thou sleep, thou shalt not fear: thou shalt rest, and thy sleep shall be sweet.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	25	Be not afraid of sudden fear, nor of the power of the wicked falling upon thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	26	For the Lord will be at thy side, and will keep thy foot that thou be not taken.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	27	Do not withhold him from doing good, who is able: if thou art able, do good thyself also.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	28	Say not to thy friend: Go, and come again: and tomorrow I will give to thee: when thou canst give at present.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	29	Practise not evil against thy friend, when he hath confidence in thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	30	Strive not against a man without cause, when he hath done thee no evil.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	31	Envy not the unjust man, and do not follow his ways:
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	32	For every mocker is an abomination to the Lord, and his communication is with the simple.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	33	Want is from the Lord in the house of the wicked: but the habitations of the just shall be blessed.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	34	He shall scorn the scorners, and to the meek he will give grace.
Proverbs	Prv	22	3	35	The wise shall possess glory: the promotion of fools is disgrace.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	1	Hear, ye children, the instruction of a father, and attend that you may know prudence.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	2	I will give you a good gift, forsake not my law.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	3	For I also was my father's son, tender and as an only son in the sight of my mother:
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	4	And he taught me, and said: Let thy heart receive my words, keep my commandments, and thou shalt live.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	5	Get wisdom, get prudence: forget not, neither decline from the words of my mouth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	6	Forsake her not, and she shall keep thee: love her, and she shall preserve thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	7	The beginning of wisdom, get wisdom, and with all thy possession purchase prudence.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	8	Take hold on her, and she shall exalt thee: thou shalt be glorified by her, when thou shalt embrace her.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	9	She shall give to thy head increase of graces, and protect thee with a noble crown.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	10	Hear, O my son, and receive my words, that years of life may be multiplied to thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	11	I will shew thee the way of wisdom, I will lead thee by the paths of equity:
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	12	Which when thou shalt have entered, thy steps shall not be straitened, and when thou runnest thou shalt not meet a stumblingblock.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	13	Take hold on instruction, leave it not: keep it, because it is thy life.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	14	Be not delighted in the paths of the wicked, neither let the way of evil men please thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	15	Flee from it, pass not by it: go aside, and forsake it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	16	For they sleep not except they have done evil: and their sleep is taken away unless they have made some to fall.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	17	They eat the bread of wickedness, and drink the wine of iniquity.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	18	But the path of the just, as a shining light, goeth forwards and increaseth even to perfect day.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	19	The way of the wicked is darksome: they know not where they fall.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	20	My son, hearken to my words, and incline thy ear to my sayings.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	21	Let them not depart from thy eyes, keep them in the midst of thy heart:
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	22	For they are life to those that find them, and health to all flesh.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	23	With all watchfulness keep thy heart, because life issueth out from it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	24	Remove from thee a froward mouth, and let detracting lips be far from thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	25	Let thy eyes look straight on, and let thy eyelids go before thy steps.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	26	Make straight the path for thy feet, and all thy ways shall be established.
Proverbs	Prv	22	4	27	Decline not to the right hand, nor to the left: turn away thy foot from evil. For the Lord knoweth the ways that are on the right hand: but those are perverse which are on the left hand. But he will make thy courses straight, he will bring forward thy ways in peace.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	1	My son, attend to my wisdom, and incline thy ear to my prudence.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	2	That thou mayst keep thoughts, and thy lips may preserve instruction. Mind not the deceit of a woman.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	3	For the lips of a harlot are like a honeycomb dropping, and her throat is smoother than oil.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	4	But her end is bitter as wormwood, and sharp as a two-edged sword.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	5	Her feet go down into death, and her steps go in as far as hell.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	6	They walk not by the path of life, her steps are wandering, and unaccountable.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	7	Now therefore, my son, hear me, and depart not from the words of my mouth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	8	Remove thy way far from her, and come not nigh the doors of her house.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	9	Give not thy honour to strangers, and thy years to the cruel.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	10	Lest strangers be filled with thy strength, and thy labours be in another man's house,
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	11	And thou mourn it the last, when thou shalt have spent thy flesh and thy body, and say:
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	12	Why have I hated instruction, and my heart consented not to reproof,
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	13	And have not heard the voice of them that taught me, and have not inclined my ear to masters?
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	14	I have almost been in all evil, in the midst of the church and of the congregation.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	15	Drink water out of thy own cistern, and the streams of thy own well:
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	16	Let thy fountains be conveyed abroad, and in the streets divide thy waters.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	17	Keep them to thyself alone, neither let strangers be partakers with thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	18	Let thy vein be blessed, and rejoice with the wife of thy youth:
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	19	Let her be thy dearest hind, and most agreeable fawn: let her breasts inebriate thee at all times; be thou delighted continually with her love.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	20	Why art thou seduced, my son, by a strange woman, and art cherished in the bosom of another?
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	21	The Lord beholdeth the ways of man, and considereth all his steps.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	22	His own iniquities catch the wicked, and he is fast bound with the ropes of his own sins.
Proverbs	Prv	22	5	23	He shall die, because he hath not received instruction, and in the multitude of his folly he shall be deceived.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	1	My son, if thou be surety for thy friend, thou hast engaged fast thy hand to a stranger.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	2	Thou art ensnared with the words of thy mouth, and caught with thy own words.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	3	Do therefore, my son, what I say, and deliver thyself: because thou art fallen into the hand of thy neighbour. Run about, make haste, stir up thy friend:
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	4	Give not sleep to thy eyes, neither let thy eyelids slumber.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	5	Deliver thyself as a doe from the hand, and as a bird from the hand of the fowler.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	6	Go to the ant, O sluggard, and consider her ways, and learn wisdom:
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	7	Which, although she hath no guide, nor master, nor captain,
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	8	Provideth her meat for herself in the summer, and gathereth her food in the harvest.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	9	How long wilt thou sleep, O sluggard? when wilt thou rise out of thy sleep?
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	10	Thou wilt sleep a little, thou wilt slumber a little, thou wilt fold thy hands a little to sleep:
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	11	And want shall come upon thee, as a traveller, and poverty as a man armed. But if thou be diligent, thy harvest shall come as a fountain, and want shall flee far from thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	12	A man that is an apostate, an unprofitable man, walketh with a perverse mouth,
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	13	He winketh with the eyes, presseth with the foot, speaketh with the finger.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	14	With a wicked heart he deviseth evil, and at all times he soweth discord.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	15	To such a one his destruction shall presently come, and he shall suddenly be destroyed, and shall no longer have any remedy.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	16	Six things there are, which the Lord hateth, and the seventh his soul detesteth:
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	17	Haughty eyes, a lying tongue, hands that shed innocent blood,
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	18	A heart that deviseth wicked plots, feet that are swift to run into mischief,
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	19	A deceitful witness that uttereth lies, and him that soweth discord among brethren.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	20	My son, keep the commandments of thy father, and forsake not the law of thy mother.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	21	Bind them in thy heart continually, and put them about thy neck.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	22	When thou walkest, let them go with thee: when thou sleepest, let them keep thee; and when thou awakest, talk with them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	23	Because the commandment is a lamp, and the law a light, and reproofs of instruction are the way of life:
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	24	That they may keep thee from the evil woman, and from the flattering tongue of the stranger.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	25	Let not thy heart covet her beauty, be not caught with her winks:
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	26	For the price of a harlot is scarce one loaf: but the woman catcheth the precious soul of a man.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	27	Can a man hide fire in his bosom, and his garments not burn?
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	28	Or can he walk upon hot coals, and his feet not be burnt?
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	29	So he that goeth in to his neighbour's wife, shall not be clean when he shall touch her.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	30	The fault is not so great when a man hath stolen: for he stealeth to fill his hungry soul:
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	31	And if he be taken he shall restore sevenfold, and shall give up all the substance of his house.
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	32	But he that is an adulterer, for the folly of his heart shall destroy his own soul:
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	33	He gathereth to himself shame and dishonour, and his reproach shall not be blotted out:
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	34	Because the jealousy and rage of the husband will not spare in the day of revenge,
Proverbs	Prv	22	6	35	Nor will he yield to any man's prayers, nor will he accept for satisfaction ever so many gifts.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	1	My son, keep my words, and lay up my precepts with thee. Son,
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	2	Keep my commandments, and thou shalt live: and my law as the apple of thy eye:
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	3	Bind it upon thy fingers, write it upon the tables of thy heart.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	4	Say to wisdom: Thou art my sister: and call prudence thy friend,
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	5	That she may keep thee from the woman that is not thine, and from the stranger who sweeteneth her words.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	6	For I look out of the window of my house through the lattice,
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	7	And I see little ones, I behold a foolish young man,
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	8	Who passeth through the street by the corner, and goeth nigh the way of her house.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	9	In the dark, when it grows late, in the darkness and obscurity of the night,
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	10	And behold a woman meeteth him in harlot's attire prepared to deceive souls; talkative and wandering,
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	11	Not bearing to be quiet, not able to abide still at home,
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	12	Now abroad, now in the streets, now lying in wait near the corners.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	13	And catching the young man, she kisseth him, and with an impudent face, flattereth, saying:
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	14	I vowed victims for prosperity, this day I have paid my vows.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	15	Therefore I am come out to meet thee, desirous to see thee, and I have found thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	16	I have woven my bed with cords, I have covered it with painted tapestry, brought from Egypt.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	17	I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	18	Come, let us be inebriated with the breasts, and let us enjoy the desired embraces, till the day appear.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	19	For my husband is not at home, he is gone a very long journey.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	20	He took with him a bag of money: he will return home the day of the full moon.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	21	She entangled him with many words, and drew him away with the flattery of her lips.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	22	Immediately he followeth her as an ox led to be a victim, and as a lamb playing the wanton, and not knowing that he is drawn like a fool to bonds,
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	23	Till the arrow pierce his liver: as if a bird should make haste to the snare, and knoweth not that his life is in danger.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	24	Now therefore, my son, hear me, and attend to the words of my mouth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	25	Let not thy mind be drawn away in her ways: neither be thou deceived with her paths.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	26	For she hath cast down many wounded, and the strongest have been slain by her.
Proverbs	Prv	22	7	27	Her house is the way to hell, reaching even to the inner chambers of death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	1	Doth not wisdom cry aloud, and prudence put forth her voice?
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	2	Standing in the top of the highest places by the way, in the midst of the paths.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	3	Beside the gates of the city, in the very doors she speaketh, saying:
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	4	O ye men, to you I call, and my voice is to the sons of men.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	5	O little ones, understand subtilty, and ye unwise, take notice.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	6	Hear, for I will speak of great things: and my lips shall be opened to preach right things.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	7	My mouth shall meditate truth, and my lips shall hate wickedness.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	8	All my words are just, there is nothing wicked nor perverse in them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	9	They are right to them that understand, and just to them that find knowledge.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	10	Receive my instruction, and not money: choose knowledge rather than gold.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	11	For wisdom is better than all the most precious things: and whatsoever may be desired cannot be compared to it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	12	I wisdom dwell in counsel, and am present in learned thoughts.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	13	The fear of the Lord hateth evil: I hate arrogance, and pride, and every wicked way, and a mouth with a double tongue.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	14	Counsel and equity is mine, prudence is mine, strength is mine.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	15	By me kings reign, and lawgivers decree just things,
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	16	By me princes rule, and the mighty decree justice.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	17	I love them that love me: and they that in the morning early watch for me, shall find me.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	18	With me are riches and glory, glorious riches and justice.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	19	For my fruit is better than gold and the precious stone, and my blossoms than choice silver.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	20	I walk in the way of justice, in the midst of the paths of judgment,
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	21	That I may enrich them that love me, and may fill their treasures.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	22	The Lord possessed me in the beginning of his ways, before he made any thing from the beginning.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	23	I was set up from eternity, and of old before the earth was made.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	24	The depths were not as yet, and I was already conceived. neither had the fountains of waters as yet sprung out:
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	25	The mountains with their huge bulk had not as yet been established: before the hills I was brought forth:
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	26	He had not yet made the earth, nor the rivers, nor the poles of the world.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	27	When he prepared the heavens, I was present: when with a certain law and compass he enclosed the depths:
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	28	When he established the sky above, and poised the fountains of waters:
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	29	When he compassed the sea with its bounds, and set a law to the waters that they should not pass their limits: when he balanced the foundations of the earth;
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	30	I was with him forming all things: and was delighted every day, playing before him at all times;
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	31	Playing in the world: and my delights were to be with the children of men.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	32	Now therefore, ye children, hear me: Blessed are they that keep my ways.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	33	Hear instruction and be wise, and refuse it not.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	34	Blessed is the man that heareth me, and that watcheth daily at my gates, and waiteth at the posts of my doors.
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	35	He that shall find me, shall find life, and shall have salvation from the Lord:
Proverbs	Prv	22	8	36	But he that shall sin against me, shall hurt his own soul. All that hate me love death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	1	Wisdom hath built herself a house, she hath hewn her out seven pillars.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	2	She hath slain her victims, mingled her wine, and set forth her table.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	3	She hath sent her maids to invite to the tower, and to the walls of the city:
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	4	Whosoever is a little one, let him come to me. And to the unwise she said:
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	5	Come, eat my bread, and drink the wine which I have mingled for you.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	6	Forsake childishness, and live, and walk by the ways of prudence.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	7	He that teacheth a scorner, doth an injury to himself: and he that rebuketh a wicked man, getteth himself a blot.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	8	Rebuke not a scorner lest he hate thee. Rebuke a wise man, and he will love thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	9	Give an occasion to a wise man, and wisdom shall be added to him. Teach a just man, and he shall make haste to receive it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	10	The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom: and the knowledge of the holy is prudence.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	11	For by me shall thy days be multiplied, and years of life shall be added to thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	12	If thou be wise, thou shalt be so to thyself: and if a scorner, thou alone shalt bear the evil.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	13	A foolish woman and clamorous, and full of allurements, and knowing nothing at all,
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	14	Sat at the door of her house, upon a seat, in a high place of the city,
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	15	To call them that pass by the way, and go on their journey:
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	16	He that is a little one, let him turn to me. And to the fool she said:
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	17	Stolen waters are sweeter, and hidden bread is more pleasant.
Proverbs	Prv	22	9	18	And he did not know that giants are there, and that her guests are in the depths of hell.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	1	A wise son maketh the father glad: but a foolish son is the sorrow of his mother.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	2	Treasures of wickedness shall profit nothing: but justice shall deliver from death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	3	The Lord will not afflict the soul of the just with famine, and he will disappoint the deceitful practices of the wicked.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	4	The slothful hand hath wrought poverty: but the hand of the industrious getteth riches. He that trusteth to lies feedeth the winds: and the same runneth after birds that fly away.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	5	He that gathered in the harvest is a wise son: but he that snorteth in the summer, is the son of confusion.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	6	The blessing of the Lord is upon the head of the just: but iniquity covereth the mouth of the wicked.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	7	The memory of the just is with praises: and the name of the wicked shall rot.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	8	The wise of heart receiveth precepts: a fool is beaten with lips.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	9	He that walketh sincerely, walketh confidently: but he that perverteth his ways, shall be manifest.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	10	He that winketh with the eye shall cause sorrow: and the foolish in lips shall be beaten.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	11	The mouth of the just is a vein of life: and the mouth of the wicked covereth iniquity.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	12	Hatred stirreth up strifes: and charity covereth all sins.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	13	In the lips of the wise is wisdom found: and a rod on the back of him that wanteth sense.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	14	Wise men lay up knowledge: but the mouth of the fool is next to confusion.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	15	The substance of a rich man is the city of his strength: the fear of the poor is their poverty.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	16	The work of the just is unto life: but the fruit of the wicked, unto sin.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	17	The way of life, to him that observeth correction: but he that forsaketh reproofs goeth astray.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	18	Lying lips hide hatred: he that uttereth reproach is foolish.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	19	In the multitude of words there shall not want sin: but he that refraineth his lips is most wise.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	20	The tongue of the just is as choice silver: but the heart of the wicked is nothing worth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	21	The lips of the just teach many: but they that are ignorant, shall die in the want of understanding.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	22	The blessing of the Lord maketh men rich: neither shall affliction be joined to them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	23	A fool worketh mischief as it were for sport: but wisdom is prudence to a man.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	24	That which the wicked feareth, shall come upon him: to the just their desire shall be given.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	25	As a tempest that passeth, so the wicked shall be no more: but the just is as an everlasting foundation.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	26	As vinegar to the teeth, and smoke to the eyes, so is the sluggard to them that sent him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	27	The fear of the Lord shall prolong days: and the years of the wicked shall be shortened.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	28	The expectation of the just is joy; but the hope of the wicked shall perish.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	29	The strength of the upright is the way of the Lord: and fear to them that work evil.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	30	The just shall never be moved: but the wicked shall not dwell on the earth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	31	The mouth of the just shall bring forth wisdom: the tongue of the perverse shall perish.
Proverbs	Prv	22	10	32	The lips of the just consider what is acceptable: and the mouth of the wicked uttereth perverse things.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	1	A deceitful balance is an abomination before the Lord: and a just weight is his will.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	2	Where pride is, there also shall be reproach: but where humility is, there also is wisdom.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	3	The simplicity of the just shall guide them: and the deceitfulness of the wicked shall destroy them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	4	Riches shall not profit in the day of revenge: but justice shall deliver from death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	5	The justice of the upright shall make his way prosperous: and the wicked man shall fall by his own wickedness.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	6	The justice of the righteous shall deliver them: and the unjust shall be caught in their own snares.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	7	When the wicked man is dead, there shall be no hope any more: and the expectation of the solicitous shall perish.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	8	The just is delivered out of distress: and the wicked shall be given up for him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	9	The dissembler with his mouth deceiveth his friend: but the just shall be delivered by knowledge.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	10	When it goeth well with the just the city shall rejoice: and when the wicked perish there shall be praise.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	11	By the blessing of the just the city shall be exalted: and by the mouth of the wicked it shall be overthrown.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	12	He that despiseth his friend, is mean of heart: but the wise man will hold his peace.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	13	He that walketh deceitfully, revealeth secrets: but he that is faithful, concealeth the thing committed to him by his friend.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	14	Where there is no governor, the people shall fall: but there is safety where there is much counsel.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	15	He shall be afflicted with evil, that is surety for a stranger: but he that is aware of the snares, shall be secure.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	16	A gracious woman shall find glory: and the strong shall have riches.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	17	A merciful man doth good to his own soul: but he that is cruel casteth off even his own kindred.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	18	The wicked maketh an unsteady work: but to him that soweth justice, there is a faithful reward.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	19	Clemency prepareth life: and the pursuing of evil things, death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	20	A perverse heart is abominable to the Lord: and his will is in them that walk sincerely.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	21	Hand in hand the evil man shall not be innocent: but the seed of the just shall be saved.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	22	A golden ring in a swine's snout, a woman fair and foolish.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	23	The desire of the just is all good: the expectation of the wicked is indignation.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	24	Some distribute their own goods, and grow richer: others take away what is not their own, and are always in want.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	25	The soul which blesseth, shall be made fat: and he that inebriateth, shall be inebriated also himself.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	26	He that hideth up corn, shall be cursed among the people: but a blessing upon the head of them that sell.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	27	Well doth he rise early who seeketh good things; but he that seeketh after evil things shall be oppressed by them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	28	He that trusteth in his riches shall fall: but the just shall spring up as a green leaf.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	29	He that troubleth his own house, shall inherit the winds: and the fool shall serve the wise.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	30	The fruit of the just man is a tree of life: and he that gaineth souls, is wise.
Proverbs	Prv	22	11	31	If the just man receive in the earth, how much more the wicked and the sinner.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	1	He that loveth correction, loveth knowledge: but he that hateth reproof is foolish.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	2	He that is good, shall draw grace from the Lord: but he that trusteth in his own devices doth wickedly.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	3	Men shall not be strengthened by wickedness: and the root of the just shall not be moved.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	4	A diligent woman is a crown to her husband: and she that doth things worthy of confusion, is a rottenness in his bones.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	5	The thoughts of the just are judgments: and the counsels of the wicked are deceitful.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	6	The words of the wicked lie in wait for blood: the mouth of the just shall deliver them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	7	Turn the wicked, and they shall not be: but the house of the just shall stand firm.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	8	A man shall be known by his learning: but he that is vain and foolish, shall be exposed to contempt.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	9	Better is the poor man that provideth for himself, than he that is glorious and wanteth bread.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	10	The just regardeth the lives of his beasts: but the bowels of the wicked are cruel.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	11	He that tilleth his land shall be satisfied with bread: but he that pursueth idleness is very foolish. He that is delighted in passing his time over wine, leaveth a reproach in his strong holds.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	12	The desire of the wicked is the fortification of evil men: but the root of the just shall prosper.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	13	For the sins of the lips ruin draweth nigh to the evil man: but the just shall escape out of distress.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	14	By the fruit of his own mouth shall a man be filled with good things, and according to the works of his hands it shall be repaid him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	15	The way of a fool is right in his own eyes: but he that is wise hearkeneth unto counsels.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	16	A fool immediately sheweth his anger: but he that dissembleth injuries is wise.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	17	He that speaketh that which he knoweth, sheweth forth justice: but he that lieth, is a deceitful witness.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	18	There is that promiseth, and is pricked as it were with a sword of conscience: but the tongue of the wise is health.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	19	The lip of truth shall be steadfast for ever: but he that is a hasty witness, frameth a lying tongue.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	20	Deceit is in the heart of them that think evil things: but joy followeth them that take counsels of peace.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	21	Whatsoever shall befall the just man. it shall not make him sad: but the wicked shall be filled with mischief.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	22	Lying lips are an abomination to the Lord: but they that deal faithfully please him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	23	A cautious man concealeth knowledge: and the heart of fools publisheth folly.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	24	The hand of the valiant shall bear rule: but that which is slothful, shall be under tribute.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	25	Grief in the heart of a man shall bring him low, but with a good word he shall be made glad.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	26	He that neglecteth a loss for the sake of a friend, is just: but the way of the wicked shall deceive them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	27	The deceitful man shall not find gain: but the substance of a just man shall be precious gold.
Proverbs	Prv	22	12	28	In the path of justice is life: but the by-way leadeth to death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	1	A wise son heareth the doctrine of his father: but he that is a scorner, beareth not when he is reproved.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	2	Of the fruit of his own mouth shall a man be filled with good things: but the soul of transgressors is wicked.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	3	He that keepeth his mouth, keepeth his soul: but he that hath no guard on his speech shall meet with evils.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	4	The sluggard willeth and willeth not: but the soul of them that work, shall be made fat.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	5	The just shall hate a lying word: but the wicked confoundeth, and shall be confounded.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	6	Justice keepeth the way of the innocent: but wickedness overthroweth the sinner.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	7	One is as it were rich, when he hath nothing: and another is as it were poor, when he hath great riches.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	8	The ransom of a man's life are his riches: but he that is poor beareth not reprehension.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	9	The light of the just giveth joy: but the lamp of the wicked shall be put out.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	10	Among the proud there are always contentions: but they that do all things with counsel, are ruled by wisdom.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	11	Substance got in haste shall be diminished: but that which by little and little is gathered with the hand shall increase.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	12	Hope that is deferred afflicteth the soul: desire when it cometh is a tree of life.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	13	Whosoever speaketh ill of any thing, bindeth himself for the time to come: but he that feareth the commandment, shall dwell in peace. Deceitful souls go astray in sins: the just are merciful, and shew mercy.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	14	The law of the wise is a fountain of life, that he may decline from the ruin of death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	15	Good instruction shall give grace: in the way of scorners is a deep pit.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	16	The prudent man doth all things with counsel: but he that is a fool, layeth open his folly.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	17	The messenger of the wicked shall fall into mischief: but a faithful ambassador is health.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	18	Poverty and shame to him that refuseth instruction: but he that yieldeth to reproof, shall be glorified.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	19	The desire that is accomplished, delighteth the soul: fools hate them that flee from evil things.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	20	He that walketh with the wise, shall be wise: a friend of fools shall become like to them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	21	Evil pursueth sinners: and to the just good shall be repaid.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	22	The good man leaveth heirs, sons, and grandsons: and the substance of the sinner is kept for the just.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	23	Much food is in the tillage of fathers: but for others it is gathered with out judgment.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	24	He that spareth the rod hateth his son: but he that loveth him correcteth him betimes.
Proverbs	Prv	22	13	25	The just eateth and filleth his soul: but the belly of the wicked is never to be filled.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	1	A wise woman buildeth her house: but the foolish will pull down with her hands that also which is built.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	2	He that walketh in the right way, and feareth God, is despised by him that goeth by an infamous way.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	3	In the mouth of a fool is the rod of pride: but the lips of the wise preserve them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	4	Where there are no oxen, the crib is empty: but where there is much corn, there the strength of the ox is manifest.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	5	A faithful witness will not lie: but a deceitful witness uttereth a lie.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	6	A scorner seeketh wisdom, and findeth it not: the learning of the wise is easy.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	7	Go against a foolish man, and he knoweth not the lips of prudence.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	8	The wisdom of a discreet man is to understand his way: and the imprudence of fools erreth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	9	A fool will laugh at sin, but among the just grace shall abide.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	10	The heart that knoweth the bitterness of his own soul, in his joy the stranger shall not intermeddle.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	11	The house of the wicked shall be destroyed: but the tabernacles of the just shall flourish.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	12	There is a way which seemeth just to a man: but the ends thereof lead to death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	13	Laughter shall be mingled with sorrow, and mourning taketh hold of the end of joy.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	14	A fool shall be filled with his own ways, and the good man shall be above him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	15	The innocent believeth every word: the discreet man considereth his steps. No good shall come to the deceitful son: but the wise servant shall prosper in his dealings, and his way shall be made straight.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	16	A wise man feareth and declineth from evil: the fool leapeth over and is confident.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	17	The impatient man shall work folly: and the crafty man is hateful.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	18	The childish shall possess folly, and the prudent, shall look for knowledge.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	19	The evil shall fall down before the good: and the wicked before the gates of the just.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	20	The poor man shall be hateful even to his own neighbour: but the friends of the rich are many.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	21	He that despiseth his neighbour, sinneth: but he that sheweth mercy to the poor, shall be blessed. He that believeth in the Lord, loveth mercy.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	22	They err that work evil: but mercy and truth prepare good things.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	23	In much work there shall be abundance: but where there are many words, there is oftentimes want.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	24	The crown of the wise is their riches: the folly of fools, imprudence.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	25	A faithful witness delivereth souls: and the double dealer uttereth lies.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	26	In the fear of the Lord is confidence of strength, and there shall be hope for his children.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	27	The fear of the Lord is a fountain of life, to decline from the ruin of death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	28	In the multitude of people is the dignity of the king: and in the small number of people the dishonour of the prince.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	29	He that is patient, is governed with much wisdom: but he that is impatient, exalteth his folly.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	30	Soundness of heart is the life of the flesh: but envy is the rottenness of the bones.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	31	He that oppresseth the poor, upbraideth his Maker: but he that hath pity on the poor, honoureth him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	32	The wicked man shall be driven out in his wickedness: but the just hath hope in his death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	33	In the heart of the prudent resteth wisdom, and it shall instruct all the ignorant.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	34	Justice exalteth a nation: but sin maketh nations miserable.
Proverbs	Prv	22	14	35	A wise servant is acceptable to the king: he that is good for nothing shall feel his anger.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	1	A mild answer breaketh wrath: but a harsh word stirreth up fury.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	2	The tongue of the wise adorneth knowledge: but the mouth of fools bubbleth out folly.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	3	The eyes of the Lord in every place behold the good and the evil.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	4	A peaceable tongue is a tree of life: but that which is immoderate, shall crush the spirit.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	5	A fool laugheth at the instruction of his father: but he that regardeth reproofs shall become prudent. In abundant justice there is the greatest strength: but the devices of the wicked shall be rooted out.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	6	The house of the just is very much strength: and in the fruits of the wicked is trouble.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	7	The lips of the wise shall disperse knowledge: the heart of fools shall be unlike.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	8	The victims of the wicked are abominable to the Lord: the vows of the just are acceptable.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	9	The way of the wicked is an abomination to the Lord: he that followeth justice is beloved by him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	10	Instruction is grievous to him that forsaketh the way of life: he that hateth reproof shall die.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	11	Hell and destruction are before the Lord: how much more the hearts of the children of men?
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	12	A corrupt man loveth not one that reproveth him: nor will he go to the wise.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	13	A glad heart maketh a cheerful countenance: but by grief of mind the spirit is cast down.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	14	The heart of the wise seeketh instruction: and the mouth of fools feedeth on foolishness.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	15	All the days of the poor are evil: a secure mind is like a continual feast.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	16	Better is a little with the fear of the Lord, than great treasures without content,
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	17	It is better to be invited to herbs with love, than to a fatted calf with hatred.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	18	A passionate man stirreth up strifes: he that is patient appeaseth those that are stirred up.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	19	The way of the slothful is as a hedge of thorns; the way of the just is without offence.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	20	A wise son maketh a father joyful: but the foolish man despiseth his mother.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	21	Folly is joy to the fool: and the wise man maketh straight his steps.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	22	Designs are brought to nothing where there is no counsel: but where there are many counsellors, they are established.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	23	A man rejoiceth in the sentence of his mouth: and a word in due time is best.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	24	The path of life is above for the wise, that he may decline from the lowest hell.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	25	The Lord will destroy the house of the proud: and will strengthen the borders of the widow.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	26	Evil thoughts are an abomination to the Lord: and pure words most beautiful shall be confirmed by him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	27	He that is greedy of gain troubleth his own house: but he that hateth bribes shall live. By mercy and faith sins are purged away: and by the fear of the Lord every one declineth from evil.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	28	The mind of the just studieth obedience: the mouth of the wicked over floweth with evils.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	29	The Lord is far from the wicked: and he will hear the prayers of the just.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	30	The light of the eyes rejoiceth the soul: a good name maketh the bones fat.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	31	The ear that heareth the reproofs of life, shall abide in the midst of the wise.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	32	He that rejecteth instruction, despiseth his own soul: but he that yieldeth to reproof possesseth understanding.
Proverbs	Prv	22	15	33	The fear of the Lord is the lesson of wisdom: and humility goeth before glory.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	1	It is the part of man to prepare the soul: and of the Lord to govern the tongue.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	2	All the ways of a man are open to his eyes: the Lord is the weigher of spirits.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	3	Lay open thy works to the Lord: and thy thoughts shall be directed.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	4	The Lord hath made all things for himself: the wicked also for the evil day.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	5	Every proud man is an abomination to the Lord: though hand should be joined to hand, he is not innocent. The beginning of a good way is to do justice; and this is more acceptable with God, than to offer sacrifices.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	6	By mercy and truth iniquity is redeemed: and by the fear of the Lord men depart from evil.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	7	When the ways of man shall please the Lord, he will convert even his enemies to peace.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	8	Better is a little with justice, than great revenues with iniquity.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	9	The heart of man disposeth his way: but the Lord must direct his steps.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	10	Divination is in the lips of the king, his mouth shall not err in judgment.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	11	Weight and balance are judgments of the Lord: and his work all the weights of the bag.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	12	They that act wickedly are abominable to the king: for the throne is established by justice.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	13	Just lips are the delight of kings: he that speaketh right things shall be loved.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	14	The wrath of a king is as messengers of death: and the wise man will pacify it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	15	In the cheerfulness of the king's countenance is life: and his clemency is like the latter rain.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	16	Get wisdom, because it is better than gold: and purchase prudence, for it is more precious than silver.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	17	The path of the just departeth from evils: he that keepeth his soul keepeth his way.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	18	Pride goeth before destruction: and the spirit is lifted up before a fall.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	19	It is better to be humbled with the meek, than to divide spoils with the proud.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	20	The learned in word shall find good things: and he that trusteth in the Lord is blessed.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	21	The wise in heart shall be called prudent: and he that is sweet in words shall attain to greater things.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	22	Knowledge is a fountain of life to him that possesseth it: the instruction of fools is foolishness.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	23	The heart of the wise shall instruct his mouth: and shall add grace to his lips.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	24	Well ordered words are as a honeycomb: sweet to the soul, and health to the bones.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	25	There is a way that seemeth to a man right: and the ends thereof lead to death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	26	The soul of him that laboureth, laboureth for himself, because his mouth hath obliged him to it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	27	The wicked man diggeth evil, and in his lips is a burning fire.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	28	A perverse man stirreth up quarrels: and one full of words separateth princes.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	29	An unjust man allureth his friend: and leadeth him into a way that is not good.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	30	He that with fixed eyes deviseth wicked things, biting his lips, bringeth: evil to pass.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	31	Old age is a crown of dignity, when it is found in the ways of justice.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	32	The patient man is better than the valiant: and he that ruleth his spirit than he that taketh cities.
Proverbs	Prv	22	16	33	Lots are cast into the lap, but they are disposed of by the Lord.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	1	Better is a dry morsel with joy, than a house full of victims with strife.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	2	A wise servant shall rule over foolish sons, and shall divide the inheritance among the brethren.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	3	As silver is tried by fire, and gold in the furnace: so the Lord trieth the hearts.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	4	The evil man obeyeth an unjust tongue: and the deceitful hearkeneth to lying lips.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	5	He that despiseth the poor, reproacheth his Maker; and he that rejoiceth at another man's ruin, shall not be unpunished.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	6	Children's children are the crown of old men: and the glory of children are their fathers.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	7	Eloquent words do not become a fool, nor lying lips a prince.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	8	The expectation of him that expecteth, is a most acceptable jewel: whithersoever he turneth himself, he understandeth wisely.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	9	He that concealeth a transgression. seeketh friendships: he that repeateth it again, separateth friends.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	10	A reproof availeth more with a wise man, than a hundred stripes with a fool.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	11	An evil man always seeketh quarrels: but a cruel angel shall be sent against him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	12	It is better to meet a bear robbed of her whelps, than a fool trusting in his own folly.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	13	He that rendereth evil for good, evil shall not depart from his house.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	14	The beginning of quarrels is as when one letteth out water: before he suffereth reproach he forsaketh judgment.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	15	He that justifieth the wicked, and he that condemneth the just, both are abominable before God.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	16	What doth it avail a fool to have riches, seeing he cannot buy wisdom? He that maketh his house high, seeketh a downfall: and he that refuseth to learn, shall fall into evils.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	17	He that is a friend loveth at all times: and a brother is proved in distress.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	18	A foolish man will clap hands, when he is surety for his friend.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	19	He that studieth discords, loveth quarrels: and he that exalteth his door, seeketh ruin.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	20	He that is of a perverse heart, shall not find good: and he that perverteth his tongue, shall fall into evil.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	21	A fool is born to his own disgrace: and even his father shall not rejoice in a fool.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	22	A joyful mind maketh age flourishing: a sorrowful spirit drieth up the bones.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	23	The wicked man taketh gifts out of the bosom, that he may pervert the paths of judgment.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	24	Wisdom shineth in the face of the wise: the eyes of fools are in the ends of the earth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	25	A foolish son is the anger of the father: and the sorrow of the mother that bore him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	26	It is no good thing to do hurt to the just: nor to strike the prince, who judgeth right.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	27	He that setteth bounds to his words. is knowing and wise: and the man of understanding is of a precious spirit.
Proverbs	Prv	22	17	28	Even a fool, if he will hold his peace shall be counted wise: and if he close his lips, a man of understanding.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	1	He that hath a mind to depart from a friend seeketh occasions: he shall ever be subject to reproach.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	2	A fool receiveth not the words of prudence: unless thou say those things which are in his heart.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	3	The wicked man when he is come into the depth of sins, contemneth: but ignominy and reproach follow him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	4	Words from the mouth of a man are as deep water: and the fountain of wisdom as an overflowing stream.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	5	It is not good to accept the person of the wicked, to decline from the truth of judgment.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	6	The lips of a fool intermeddle with strife: and his mouth provoketh quarrels.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	7	The mouth of a fool is his destruction: and his lips are the ruin of his soul.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	8	The words of the double tongued are as if they were harmless: and they reach even to the inner parts of the bowels. Fear casteth down the slothful: and the souls of the effeminate shall be hungry.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	9	He that is loose and slack in his work, is the brother of him that wasteth his own works.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	10	The name of the Lord is a strong tower: the just runneth to it, and shall be exalted.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	11	The substance of the rich man is the city of his strength, and as a strong wall compassing him about.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	12	Before destruction, the heart of a man is exalted: and before he be glorified, it is humbled.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	13	He that answereth before he heareth sheweth himself to be a fool, and worthy of confusion.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	14	The spirit of a man upholdeth his infirmity: but a spirit that is easily angered, who can bear?
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	15	A wise heart shall acquire knowledge: and the ear of the wise seeketh instruction.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	16	A man's gift enlargeth his way, and maketh him room before princes.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	17	The just is first accuser of himself: his friend cometh, and shall search him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	18	The lot suppresseth contentions, and determineth even between the mighty.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	19	A brother that is helped by his brother, is like a strong city: and judgments are like the bars of cities.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	20	Of the fruit of a man's mouth shall his belly be satisfied: and the offspring of his lips shall fill him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	21	Death and life are in the power of the tongue: they that love it, shall eat the fruits thereof.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	22	He that hath found a good wife, hath found a good thing, and shall receive a pleasure from the Lord. He that driveth away a good wife, driveth away a good thing: but he that keepeth an adulteress, is foolish and wicked.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	23	The poor will speak with supplications, and the rich will speak roughly.
Proverbs	Prv	22	18	24	A man amiable in society, shall be more friendly than a brother.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	1	Better is the poor man, that walketh in his simplicity, than a rich man that is perverse in his lips, and unwise.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	2	Where there is no knowledge of the soul, there is no good: and he that is hasty with his feet shall stumble.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	3	The folly of a man supplanteth his steps: and he fretteth in his mind against God.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	4	Riches make many friends: but from the poor man, even they whom he had, depart.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	5	A false witness shall not be unpunished: and he that speaketh lies shall not escape.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	6	Many honour the person of him that is mighty, and are friends of him that giveth gifts.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	7	The brethren of the poor man hate him: moreover also his friends have departed far from him. He that followeth after words only, shall have nothing.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	8	But he that possesseth a mind, loveth his own soul, and he that keepeth prudence shall find good things.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	9	A false witness shall not be unpunished: and he that speaketh lies, shall perish.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	10	Delicacies are not seemly for a fool: nor for a servant to have rule over princes.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	11	The learning of a man is known by patience and his glory is to pass over wrongs.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	12	As the roaring of a lion, so also is the anger of a king: and his cheerfulness as the dew upon the grass.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	13	A foolish son is the grief of his father: and a wrangling wife is like a roof continually dropping through.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	14	House and riches are given by parents: but a prudent wife is properly from the Lord.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	15	Slothfulness casteth into a deep sleep, and an idle soul shall suffer hunger.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	16	He that keepeth the commandment, keepeth his own soul: but he that neglecteth his own way, shall die.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	17	He that hath mercy on the poor, lendeth to the Lord: and he will repay him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	18	Chastise thy son, despair not: but to the killing of him set not thy soul.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	19	He that is impatient, shall suffer damage: and when he shall take away he shall add another thing.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	20	Hear counsel, and receive instruction, that thou mayst be wise in thy latter end.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	21	There are many thoughts in the heart of a man: but the will of the Lord shall stand firm.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	22	A needy man is merciful: and better is the poor than the lying man.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	23	The fear of the Lord is unto life: and he shall abide in fulness without being visited with evil.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	24	The slothful hideth his hand under his armpit, and will not so much as bring it to his mouth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	25	The wicked man being; scourged, the fool shall be wiser: but if thou rebuke a wise man he will understand discipline.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	26	He that afflicteth his father, and chaseth away his mother, is infamous and unhappy.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	27	Cease not, O my son, to hear instruction, and be not ignorant of the words of knowledge.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	28	An unjust witness scorneth judgment: and the mouth of the wicked devoureth iniquity.
Proverbs	Prv	22	19	29	Judgments are prepared for scorners: and striking hammers for the bodies of fools.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	1	Wine is a luxurious thing, and drunkenness riotous: whosoever is delighted therewith shall not be wise.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	2	As the roaring of a lion, so also is the dread of a king: he that provoketh him, sinneth against his own soul.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	3	It is an honour for a man to separate himself from quarrels: but all fools are meddling with reproaches.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	4	Because of the cold the sluggard would not plough: he shall beg therefore in the summer, and it shall not be given him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	5	Counsel in the heart of a man is like deep water: but a wise man will draw it out.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	6	Many men are called merciful: but who shall find a faithful man?
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	7	The just that walketh in his simplicity, shall leave behind him blessed children.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	8	The king, that sitteth on the throne of judgment, scattereth away all evil with his look.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	9	Who can say: My heart is clean, I am pure from sin?
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	10	Diverse weights and diverse measures, both are abominable before God.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	11	By his inclinations a child is known, if his works be clean and right.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	12	The hearing ear, and the seeing eye, the Lord hath made them both.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	13	Love not sleep, lest poverty oppress thee: open thy eyes, and be filled with bread.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	14	It is nought, it is nought, saith every buyer: and when he is gone away, then he will boast.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	15	There is gold, and a multitude of jewels: but the lips of knowledge are a precious vessel.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	16	Take away the garment of him that is surety for a stranger, and take a pledge from him for strangers.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	17	The bread of lying is sweet to a man: but afterwards his mouth shall be filled with gravel.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	18	Designs are strengthened by counsels: and wars are to be managed by governments.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	19	Meddle not with him that revealeth secrets, and walketh deceitfully, and openeth wide his lips.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	20	He that curseth his father, and mother, his lamp shall be put out in the midst of darkness.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	21	The inheritance gotten hastily in the beginning, in the end shall be without a blessing.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	22	Say not: I will return evil: wait for the Lord and he will deliver thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	23	Diverse weights are an abomination before the Lord: a deceitful balance is not good.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	24	The steps of man are guided by the Lord: but who is the man that can understand his own way?
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	25	It is ruin to a man to devour holy ones, and after vows to retract.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	26	A wise king scattereth the wicked, and bringeth over them the wheel.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	27	The spirit of a man is the lamp of the Lord, which searcheth all the hidden things of the bowels.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	28	Mercy and truth preserve the king, and his throne is strengthened by clemency.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	29	The joy of young men is their strength: and the dignity of old men, their grey hairs.
Proverbs	Prv	22	20	30	The blueness of a wound shall wipe away evils: and stripes in the more inward parts of the belly.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	1	As the divisions of waters, so the heart of the king is in the hand of the Lord: whithersoever he will he shall turn it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	2	Every way of a man seemeth right to himself: but the Lord weigheth the hearts.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	3	To do mercy and judgment, pleaseth the Lord more than victims.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	4	Haughtiness of the eyes is the enlarging of the heart: the lamp of the wicked is sin.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	5	The thoughts of the industrious always bring forth abundance: but every sluggard is always in want.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	6	He that gathereth treasures by a lying tongue, is vain and foolish, and shall stumble upon the snares of death.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	7	The robberies of the wicked shall be their downfall, because they would not do judgment.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	8	The perverse way of a man is strange: but as for him that is pure, his work is right.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	9	It is better to sit in a corner of the housetop, than with a brawling woman, and in a common house.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	10	The soul of the wicked desireth evil, he will not have pity on his neighbour.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	11	When a pestilent man is punished, the little one will be wiser: and if he follow the wise, he will receive knowledge.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	12	The just considereth seriously the house of the wicked, that he may withdraw the wicked from evil.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	13	He that stoppeth his ear against the cry of the poor, shall also cry himself and shall not be heard.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	14	A secret present quencheth anger: and a gift in the bosom the greatest wrath.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	15	It is joy to the just to do judgment: and dread to them that work iniquity.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	16	A man that shall wander out of the way of doctrine, shall abide in the company of the giants.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	17	He that loveth good cheer, shall be in want: he that loveth wine, and fat things, shall not be rich.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	18	The wicked is delivered up for the just: and the unjust for the righteous.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	19	It is better to dwell in a wilderness, than with a quarrelsome and passionate woman.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	20	There is a treasure to be desired, and oil in the dwelling of the just: and the foolish man shall spend it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	21	He that followeth justice and mercy, shall find life, justice, and glory.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	22	The wise man hath scaled the city of the strong, and hath cast down the strength of the confidence thereof.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	23	He that keepeth his mouth and his tongue, keepeth his soul from distress.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	24	The proud and the arrogant is called ignorant, who in anger worketh pride.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	25	Desires kill the slothful: for his hands have refused to work at all.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	26	He longeth and desireth all the day: but he that is just, will give, and will not cease.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	27	The sacrifices of the wicked are abominable, because they are offered of wickedness.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	28	A lying witness shall perish: an obedient man shall speak of victory.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	29	The wicked man impudently hardeneth his face: but he that is righteous, correcteth his way.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	30	There is no wisdom, there is no prudence, there is no counsel against the Lord.
Proverbs	Prv	22	21	31	The horse is prepared for the day of battle: but the Lord giveth safety.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	1	A good name is better than great riches: and good favour is above silver and gold.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	2	The rich and poor have met one another: the Lord is the maker of them both.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	3	The prudent man saw the evil, and hid himself: the simple passed on, and suffered loss.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	4	The fruit of humility is the fear of the Lord, riches and glory and life.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	5	Arms and swords are in the way of the perverse: but he that keepeth his own soul departeth far from them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	6	It is a proverb: A young man according to his way, even when he is old he will not depart from it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	7	The rich ruleth over the poor: and the borrower is servant to him that lendeth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	8	He that soweth iniquity shall reap evils, and with the rod of his anger he shall be consumed.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	9	He that is inclined to mercy shall be blessed: for of his bread he hath given to the poor. He that maketh presents shall purchase victory and honour: but he carrieth away the souls of the receivers.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	10	Cast out the scoffer, and contention shall go out with him, and quarrels and reproaches shall cease.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	11	He that loveth cleanness of heart, for the grace of his lips shall have the king for his friend.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	12	The eyes of the Lord preserve knowledge: and the words of the unjust are overthrown.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	13	The slothful man saith: There is a lion without, I shall be slain in the midst of the streets.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	14	The mouth of a strange woman is a deep pit: he whom the Lord is angry with, shall fall into it.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	15	Folly is bound up in the heart of a child, and the rod of correction shall drive it away.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	16	He that oppresseth the poor, to increase his own riches, shall himself give to one that is richer, and shall be in need.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	17	Incline thy ear, and hear the words of the wise: and apply thy heart to my doctrine:
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	18	Which shall be beautiful for thee, if thou keep it in thy bowels, and it shall flow in thy lips:
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	19	That thy trust may be in the Lord, wherefore I have also shewn it to thee this day.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	20	Behold I have described it to thee three manner of ways, in thoughts and knowledge:
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	21	That I might shew thee the certainty, and the words of truth, to answer out of these to them that sent thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	22	Do no violence to the poor, because he is poor: and do not oppress the needy in the gate:
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	23	Because the Lord will judge his cause, and will afflict them that have afflicted his soul.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	24	Be not a friend to an angry man, and do not walk with a furious man:
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	25	Lest perhaps thou learn his ways, and take scandal to thy soul.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	26	Be not with them that fasten down their hands, and that offer themselves sureties for debts:
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	27	For if thou have not wherewith to restore, what cause is there, that he should take the covering from thy bed?
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	28	Pass not beyond the ancient bounds which thy fathers have set.
Proverbs	Prv	22	22	29	Hast thou seen a man swift in his work? he shall stand before kings, and shall not be before those that are obscure.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	1	When thou shalt sit to eat with a prince, consider diligently what is set before thy face.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	2	And put a knife to thy throat, if it be so that thou have thy soul in thy own power.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	3	Be not desirous of his meats, in which is the bread of deceit.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	4	Labour not to be rich: but set bounds to thy prudence.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	5	Lift not up thy eyes to riches which thou canst not have: because they shall make themselves wings like those of an eagle, and shall fly towards heaven.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	6	Eat not with an envious man, and desire not his meats:
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	7	Because like a soothsayer, and diviner, he thinketh that which he knoweth not. Eat and drink, will he say to thee: and his mind is not with thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	8	The meats which thou hadst eaten, thou shalt vomit up: and shalt loose thy beautiful words.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	9	Speak not in the ears of fools: because they will despise the instruction of thy speech.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	10	Touch not the bounds of little ones: and enter not into the field of the fatherless:
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	11	For their near kinsman is strong: and he will judge their cause against thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	12	Let thy heart apply itself to instruction: and thy ears to words of knowledge.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	13	Withhold not correction from a child: for if thou strike him with the rod, he shall not die.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	14	Thou shalt beat him with the rod, and deliver his soul from hell.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	15	My son, if thy mind be wise, my heart shall rejoice with thee:
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	16	And my reins shall rejoice, when thy lips shall speak what is right.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	17	Let not thy heart envy sinners: but be thou in the fear of the Lord all the day long:
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	18	Because thou shalt have hope in the latter end, and thy expectation shall not be taken away.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	19	Hear thou, my son, and be wise: and guide thy mind in the way.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	20	Be not in the feasts of great drinkers, nor in their revellings, who contribute flesh to eat:
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	21	Because they that give themselves to drinking, and that club together shall be consumed; and drowsiness shall be clothed with rags.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	22	Hearken to thy father, that beget thee: and despise not thy mother when she is old.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	23	Buy truth, and do not sell wisdom, and instruction, and understanding.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	24	The father of the just rejoiceth greatly: he that hath begotten a wise son, shall have joy in him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	25	Let thy father, and thy mother be joyful, and let her rejoice that bore thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	26	My son, give me thy heart: and let thy eyes keep my ways.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	27	For a harlot is a deep ditch: and a strange woman is a narrow pit.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	28	She lieth in wait in the way as a robber, and him whom she shall see unwary, she will kill.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	29	Who hath woe? whose father hath woe? who hath contentions? who falls into pits? who hath wounds without cause? who hath redness of eyes?
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	30	Surely they that pass their time in wine, and study to drink of their cups.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	31	Look not upon the wine when it is yellow, when the colour thereof shineth in the glass: it goeth in pleasantly,
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	32	But in the end, it will bite like a snake, and will spread abroad poison like a basilisk.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	33	Thy eyes shall behold strange women, and thy heart shall utter perverse things.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	34	And thou shalt be as one sleeping in the midst of the sea, and as a pilot fast asleep, when the stern is lost.
Proverbs	Prv	22	23	35	And thou shalt say: They have beaten me, but I was not sensible of pain: they drew me, and I felt not: when shall I awake, and find wine again?
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	1	Seek not to be like evil men, neither desire to be with them:
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	2	Because their mind studieth robberies, and their lips speak deceits.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	3	By wisdom the house shall be built, and by prudence it shall be strengthened.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	4	By instruction the storerooms shall be filled with all precious and most beautiful wealth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	5	A wise man is strong: and a knowing man, stout and valiant.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	6	Because war is managed by due ordering: and there shall be safety where there are many counsels.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	7	Wisdom is too high for a fool, in the gate he shall not open his mouth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	8	He that deviseth to do evils, shall be called a fool.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	9	The thought of a fool is sin: and the detracter is the abomination of men.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	10	If thou lose hope being weary in the day of distress, thy strength shall be diminished.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	11	Deliver them that are led to death: and those that are drawn to death forbear not to deliver.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	12	If thou say: I have not strength enough: he that seeth into the heart, he understandeth, and nothing deceiveth the keeper of thy soul, and he shall render to a man according to his works.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	13	Eat honey, my son, because it is good, and the honeycomb most sweet to thy throat:
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	14	So also is the doctrine of wisdom to thy soul: which when thou hast found, thou shalt have hope in the end, and thy hope shall not perish.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	15	Lie not in wait, nor seek after wickedness in the house of the just, nor spoil his rest.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	16	For a just man shall fall seven times and shall rise again: but the wicked shall fall down into evil.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	17	When thy enemy shall fall, be not glad, and in his ruin let not thy heart rejoice:
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	18	Lest the Lord see, and it displease him, and he turn away his wrath from him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	19	Contend not with the wicked, nor seek to be like the ungodly:
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	20	For evil men have no hope of things to come, and the lamp of the wicked shall be put out.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	21	My son, fear the Lord and the king: and have nothing to do with detracters.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	22	For their destruction shall rise suddenly: and who knoweth the ruin of both?
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	23	These things also to the wise: It is not good to have respect to persons in judgment.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	24	They that say to the wicked man: Thou art just: shall be cursed by the people, and the tribes shall abhor them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	25	They that rebuke him, shall be praised: and a blessing shall come upon them.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	26	He shall kiss the lips, who answereth right words.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	27	Prepare thy work without, and diligently till thy ground: that afterward thou mayst build thy house.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	28	Be not witness without cause against thy neighbour: and deceive not any man with thy lips.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	29	Say not: I will do to him as he hath done to me: I will render to every one according to his work.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	30	I passed by the field of the slothful man, and by the vineyard of the foolish man:
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	31	And behold it was all filled with nettles, and thorns had covered the face thereof, and the stone wall was broken down.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	32	Which when I had seen, I laid it up in my heart, and by the example I received instruction.
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	33	Thou wilt sleep a little, said I, thou wilt slumber a little, thou wilt fold thy hands a little to rest:
Proverbs	Prv	22	24	34	And poverty shall come to thee as a runner, and beggary as an armed man.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	1	These are also parables of Solomon, which the men of Ezechias king of Juda copied out.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	2	It is the glory of God to conceal the word, and the glory of kings to search out the speech.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	3	The heaven above, and the earth beneath, and the heart of kings is unsearchable.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	4	Take away the rust from silver, and there shall come forth a most pure vessel:
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	5	Take away wickedness from the face of the king, and his throne shall be established with justice.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	6	Appear not glorious before the king, and stand not in the place of great men.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	7	For it is better that it should be said to thee: Come up hither; than that thou shouldst be humbled before the prince.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	8	The things which thy eyes have seen, utter not hastily in a quarrel: lest afterward thou mayst not be able to make amends, when thou hast dishonoured thy friend.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	9	Treat thy cause with thy friend, and discover not the secret to a stranger:
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	10	Lest he insult over thee, when he hath heard it, and cease not to upbraid thee. Grace and friendship deliver a man: keep these for thyself, lest thou fall under reproach.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	11	To speak a word in due time, is like apples of gold on beds of silver.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	12	As an earring of gold and a bright pearl, so is he that reproveth the wise, and the obedient ear.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	13	As the cold of snow in the time of harvest, so is a faithful messenger to him that sent him, for he refresheth his soul.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	14	As clouds, and wind, when no rain followeth, so is the man that boasteth, and doth not fulfill his promises.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	15	By patience a prince shall be appeased, and a soft tongue shall break hardness.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	16	Thou hast found honey, eat what is sufficient for thee, lest being glutted therewith thou vomit it up.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	17	Withdraw thy foot from the house of thy neighbour, lest having his fill he hate thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	18	A man that beareth false witness against his neighbour, is like a dart and a sword and a sharp arrow.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	19	To trust to an unfaithful man in the time of trouble, is like a rotten tooth, and weary foot,
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	20	And one that looseth his garment in cold weather. As vinegar upon nitre, so is he that singeth songs to a very evil heart. As a moth doth by a garment, and a worm by the wood: so the sadness of a man consumeth the heart.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	21	If thy enemy be hungry, give him to eat: if he thirst, give him water to drink:
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	22	For thou shalt heap hot coals upon his head, and the Lord will reward thee.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	23	The north wind driveth away rain, as doth a sad countenance a backbiting tongue.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	24	It is better to sit in a corner of the housetop, than with a brawling woman, and in a common house.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	25	As cold water to a thirsty soul, so is good tidings from a far country.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	26	A just man falling down before the wicked, is as a fountain troubled with the foot, and a corrupted spring.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	27	As it is not good for a man to eat much honey, so he that is a searcher of majesty, shall be overwhelmed by glory.
Proverbs	Prv	22	25	28	As a city that lieth open and is not compassed with walls, so is a man that cannot refrain his own spirit in speaking.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	1	As snow in summer, and rain in harvest, so glory is not seemly for a fool.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	2	As a bird flying to other places, and a sparrow going here or there: so a curse uttered without cause shall come upon a man.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	3	A whip for a horse, and a snaffle for an ass, and a rod for the back of fools.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	4	Answer not a fool according to his folly, lest thou be made like him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	5	Answer a fool according to his folly, lest he imagine himself to be wise.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	6	He that sendeth words by a foolish messenger, is lame of feet and drinketh iniquity.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	7	As a lame man hath fair legs in vain: so a parable is unseemly in the mouth of fools.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	8	As he that casteth a stone into the heap of Mercury: so is he that giveth honour to a fool.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	9	As if a thorn should grow in the hand of a drunkard: so is a parable in the mouth of fools.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	10	Judgment determineth causes: and he that putteth a fool to silence, appeaseth anger.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	11	As a dog that returneth to his vomit, so is the fool that repeateth his folly.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	12	Hast thou seen a man wise in his own conceit? there shall be more hope of a fool than of him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	13	The slothful man saith: There is a lion in the way, and a lioness in the roads.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	14	As the door turneth upon its hinges, so doth the slothful upon his bed.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	15	The slothful hideth his hand under his armpit, and it grieveth him to turn it to his mouth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	16	The sluggard is wiser in his own conceit, than seven men that speak sentences.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	17	As he that taketh a dog by the ears, so is he that passeth by in anger, and meddleth with another man's quarrel.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	18	As he is guilty that shooteth arrows, and lances unto death:
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	19	So is the man that hurteth his friend deceitfully: and when he is taken, saith: I did it in jest.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	20	When the wood faileth, the fire shall go out: and when the talebearer is taken away, contentions shall cease.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	21	As coals are to burning coals, and wood to fire, so an angry man stirreth up strife.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	22	The words of a talebearer are as it were simple, but they reach to the innermost parts of the belly.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	23	Swelling lips joined with a corrupt heart, are like an earthen vessel adorned with silver dross.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	24	An enemy is known by his lips, when in his heart he entertaineth deceit.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	25	When he shall speak low, trust him not: because there are seven mischiefs in his heart.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	26	He that covereth hatred deceitfully, his malice shall be laid open in the public assembly.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	27	He that diggeth a pit, shall fall into it: and he that rolleth a stone, it shall return to him.
Proverbs	Prv	22	26	28	A deceitful tongue loveth not truth: and a slippery mouth worketh ruin.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	1	Boast not for tomorrow, for thou knowest not what the day to come may bring forth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	2	Let another praise thee, and not thy own mouth: a stranger, and not thy own lips.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	3	A stone is heavy, and sand weighty: but the anger of a fool is heavier than them both.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	4	Anger hath no mercy, nor fury when it breaketh forth: and who can bear the violence of one provoked?
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	5	Open rebuke is better than hidden love.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	6	Better are the wounds of a friend, than the deceitful kisses of an enemy.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	7	A soul that is full shall tread upon the honeycomb: and a soul that is hungry shall take even bitter for sweet.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	8	As a bird that wandereth from her nest, so is a man that leaveth his place.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	9	Ointment and perfumes rejoice the heart: and the good counsels of a friend are sweet to the soul.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	10	Thy own friend, and thy father's friend forsake not: and go not into thy brother's house in the day of thy affliction. Better is a neighbour that is near, than a brother afar off.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	11	Study wisdom, my son, and make my heart joyful, that thou mayst give an answer to him that reproacheth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	12	The prudent man seeing evil hideth himself: little ones passing on have suffered losses.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	13	Take away his garment that hath been surety for a stranger: and take from him a pledge for strangers.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	14	He that blesseth his neighbour with a loud voice, rising in the night, shall be like to him that curseth.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	15	Roofs dropping through in a cold day, and a contentious woman are alike.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	16	He that retaineth her, is as he that would hold the wind, and shall call in the oil of his right hand.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	17	Iron sharpeneth iron, so a man sharpeneth the countenance of his friend.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	18	He that keepeth the fig tree, shall eat the fruit thereof: and he that is the keeper of his master, shall be glorified.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	19	As the faces of them that look therein, shine in the water, so-the hearts of men are laid open to the wise.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	20	Hell and destruction are never filled: so the eyes of men are never satisfied.
Proverbs	Prv	22	27	21	As silver is tried in the fining-pot and gold in the furnace: so a man is tried by the mouth of him that praiseth. The heart of the wicked seeketh after evils, but the righteous heart seeketh after knowledge.
